{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RUvMmKjhWNCp9j4RRQSaiY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01K2is4GPidHTa6QErXDkWXh","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n\nCard: **The Dawning Archaic** — `{10}` — Legendary Creature — Avatar — 7/7.\n\nOracle text and the clauses each test covers:\n\n1. *\"This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in\n   your graveyard.\"* — a **cost-reduction** mechanic via the engine\n   `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` hook (clamped to the generic portion by\n   `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n2. *\"Reach\"* — a keyword.\n3. *\"Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or\n   sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost.\"* — an\n   **attack trigger** (`AttacksTriggeredEvent`) whose optional effect free-casts\n   a chosen instant/sorcery from the controller's graveyard (mirrors the\n   reference card Etali, Primal Storm / FDN 194, which uses\n   `engine.casting.cast_spell_free`).\n4. *\"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"* — a\n   **zone-replacement** rider: the free-cast spell, once it resolves, must end\n   up in exile rather than the graveyard.\n\nAll tests are in `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`. They were authored TDD-first: the\ncurrent stub (`CardImpl` with `pass`) fails 23/27, and a plausible reference\nimplementation passes all 27 (verified out-of-band), confirming the contract is\nboth correct against the spec and achievable.\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicProperties (static data)\n- `test_name` — name is \"The Dawning Archaic\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost is `{10}`.\n- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature` / has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T is 7/7.\n- `test_legendary` — has `Supertype.LEGENDARY`.\n- `test_avatar_subtype` — has the \"Avatar\" subtype.\n- `test_has_reach` — has `Keyword.REACH`.\n- `test_is_colorless` — `{10}` carries no colored or hybrid pips (the card is\n  colorless, matching the empty `colors` list in the spec).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicCostReduction\nValidates clause (1): reduction equals the count of instant + sorcery cards in\n*the controller's* graveyard.\n- `test_no_reduction_with_empty_graveyard` — 0 with an empty graveyard.\n- `test_one_instant_reduces_by_one` / `test_one_sorcery_reduces_by_one` — each\n  instant/sorcery contributes 1.\n- `test_mixed_instants_and_sorceries_sum` — 3 instants + 2 sorceries → 5.\n- `test_creatures_in_graveyard_do_not_reduce` — creatures are not counted.\n- `test_only_instant_sorcery_among_mixed_graveyard_count` — only the\n  instant/sorcery subset of a mixed graveyard counts (1 + 1 → 2).\n- `test_opponent_graveyard_does_not_reduce` — only \"your\" graveyard counts.\n- `test_engine_clamps_reduction_to_generic` — with >10 spells the engine clamps\n  the reduction to the `{10}` generic via `get_cost_reduction`.\n- `test_cast_with_reduction_succeeds_with_reduced_mana` — integration: 4\n  instant/sorcery in graveyard → effective `{6}`; 6 colorless mana casts and\n  resolves it onto the battlefield.\n- `test_cast_without_enough_reduction_fails` — negative integration: empty\n  graveyard requires the full `{10}`; 6 mana raises `CastingError` matching\n  \"insufficient mana\" (the match string guards against the cast failing for an\n  incidental reason rather than the cost).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicTriggerRegistration\nValidates clause (3) wiring.\n- `test_registers_an_attacks_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds exactly one\n  trigger for `AttacksTriggeredEvent` keyed to this creature as source.\n- `test_trigger_condition_matches_this_creature` — the trigger's condition\n  returns `True` only when *this* creature attacks and `False` for a different\n  attacker (so it does not fire for unrelated creatures).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicAttackEffect\nValidates clause (3) effect: optional free-cast of a graveyard instant/sorcery.\nThe shared helper registers the trigger, fires `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, and\nresolves the single pushed trigger StackObject, seeding the controller's\ndeterministic-player script with the \"may\" yes/no and the chosen card.\n- `test_chosen_instant_leaves_graveyard_onto_stack` — chosen instant leaves the\n  graveyard and appears on the stack (free cast).\n- `test_free_cast_does_not_spend_mana` — the controller's mana pool is untouched\n  (\"without paying its mana cost\").\n- `test_chosen_sorcery_can_be_cast` — works for a sorcery too.\n- `test_may_declining_leaves_graveyard_untouched` — declining (\"you may\") leaves\n  the graveyard unchanged and adds nothing to the stack.\n- `test_empty_graveyard_is_a_safe_noop` — with no instant/sorcery available the\n  trigger resolves cleanly and casts nothing (no exception).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicExileReplacement\nValidates clause (4): the free-cast spell is exiled, not put in the graveyard.\nThe helper free-casts the chosen spell and then resolves the spell itself.\n- `test_resolved_free_cast_instant_goes_to_exile` — resolved instant ends in\n  exile and is NOT in the graveyard.\n- `test_resolved_free_cast_sorcery_goes_to_exile` — same for a sorcery.\n\n## Edge cases covered (and why)\n- Optional (\"you may\") path — declining must be a clean no-op.\n- Empty graveyard — the trigger must not crash with no legal target.\n- Opponent's graveyard and non-instant/sorcery cards must not affect the\n  reduction (common implementation mistakes).\n- Engine-level clamp of the reduction to the generic cost.\n- Mana-pool untouched on the free cast (the defining property of \"without\n  paying its mana cost\").\n- Exile-instead replacement asserted on observable end zone, independent of how\n  the implementer routes the zone change.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (out of scope)\n- Full combat integration via `declare_attackers_step`: the engine's\n  `declare_attackers_step` does not itself fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (no\n  engine path constructs that event during combat), so the attack-trigger tests\n  fire the event directly through the `trigger_manager`, matching the pattern\n  used by the FDN reference cards (Etali / Ruby). Testing whether combat fires\n  the event is an engine concern, not this card's contract.\n- Targeting legality/UI for choosing the graveyard spell (which exact prompt is\n  used) — tested only at the observable level (a card is chosen and cast).\n- Legend-rule / \"summoning sickness can't attack\" interactions — generic engine\n  behavior, not specific to this card.\n- Reach combat behavior (blocking fliers) — covered by engine combat tests; here\n  we only assert the keyword is present.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":539,"cache_read_input_tokens":140890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":539,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01M6QwNHGRh57GZfrPn9to8x","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"e1b8a9c6-4371-4c87-9c37-3783c48c3b66","request_id":"req_011CbdRwqUTwEvrwetbm3TGE","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_1"}
