{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GotmMhshLedCbbZBEMnugd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n2\t\n3\tCard: **The Dawning Archaic** — `{10}` — Legendary Creature — Avatar — 7/7.\n4\t\n5\tOracle text and the clauses each test covers:\n6\t\n7\t1. *\"This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in\n8\t   your graveyard.\"* — a **cost-reduction** mechanic via the engine\n9\t   `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` hook (clamped to the generic portion by\n10\t   `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n11\t2. *\"Reach\"* — a keyword.\n12\t3. *\"Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or\n13\t   sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost.\"* — an\n14\t   **attack trigger** (`AttacksTriggeredEvent`) whose optional effect free-casts\n15\t   a chosen instant/sorcery from the controller's graveyard (mirrors the\n16\t   reference card Etali, Primal Storm / FDN 194, which uses\n17\t   `engine.casting.cast_spell_free`).\n18\t4. *\"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"* — a\n19\t   **zone-replacement** rider: the free-cast spell, once it resolves, must end\n20\t   up in exile rather than the graveyard.\n21\t\n22\tAll tests are in `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`. They were authored TDD-first: the\n23\tcurrent stub (`CardImpl` with `pass`) fails 23/27, and a plausible reference\n24\timplementation passes all 27 (verified out-of-band), confirming the contract is\n25\tboth correct against the spec and achievable.\n26\t\n27\t## File: `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n28\t\n29\t### TestTheDawningArchaicProperties (static data)\n30\t- `test_name` — name is \"The Dawning Archaic\".\n31\t- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost is `{10}`.\n32\t- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature` / has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n33\t- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T is 7/7.\n34\t- `test_legendary` — has `Supertype.LEGENDARY`.\n35\t- `test_avatar_subtype` — has the \"Avatar\" subtype.\n36\t- `test_has_reach` — has `Keyword.REACH`.\n37\t- `test_is_colorless` — `{10}` carries no colored or hybrid pips (the card is\n38\t  colorless, matching the empty `colors` list in the spec).\n39\t\n40\t### TestTheDawningArchaicCostReduction\n41\tValidates clause (1): reduction equals the count of instant + sorcery cards in\n42\t*the controller's* graveyard.\n43\t- `test_no_reduction_with_empty_graveyard` — 0 with an empty graveyard.\n44\t- `test_one_instant_reduces_by_one` / `test_one_sorcery_reduces_by_one` — each\n45\t  instant/sorcery contributes 1.\n46\t- `test_mixed_instants_and_sorceries_sum` — 3 instants + 2 sorceries → 5.\n47\t- `test_creatures_in_graveyard_do_not_reduce` — creatures are not counted.\n48\t- `test_only_instant_sorcery_among_mixed_graveyard_count` — only the\n49\t  instant/sorcery subset of a mixed graveyard counts (1 + 1 → 2).\n50\t- `test_opponent_graveyard_does_not_reduce` — only \"your\" graveyard counts.\n51\t- `test_engine_clamps_reduction_to_generic` — with >10 spells the engine clamps\n52\t  the reduction to the `{10}` generic via `get_cost_reduction`.\n53\t- `test_cast_with_reduction_succeeds_with_reduced_mana` — integration: 4\n54\t  instant/sorcery in graveyard → effective `{6}`; 6 colorless mana casts and\n55\t  resolves it onto the battlefield.\n56\t- `test_cast_without_enough_reduction_fails` — negative integration: empty\n57\t  graveyard requires the full `{10}`; 6 mana raises `CastingError` matching\n58\t  \"insufficient mana\" (the match string guards against the cast failing for an\n59\t  incidental reason rather than the cost).\n60\t\n61\t### TestTheDawningArchaicTriggerRegistration\n62\tValidates clause (3) wiring.\n63\t- `test_registers_an_attacks_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds exactly one\n64\t  trigger for `AttacksTriggeredEvent` keyed to this creature as source.\n65\t- `test_trigger_condition_matches_this_creature` — the trigger's condition\n66\t  returns `True` only when *this* creature attacks and `False` for a different\n67\t  attacker (so it does not fire for unrelated creatures).\n68\t\n69\t### TestTheDawningArchaicAttackEffect\n70\tValidates clause (3) effect: optional free-cast of a graveyard instant/sorcery.\n71\tThe shared helper registers the trigger, fires `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, and\n72\tresolves the single pushed trigger StackObject, seeding the controller's\n73\tdeterministic-player script with the \"may\" yes/no and the chosen card.\n74\t- `test_chosen_instant_leaves_graveyard_onto_stack` — chosen instant leaves the\n75\t  graveyard and appears on the stack (free cast).\n76\t- `test_free_cast_does_not_spend_mana` — the controller's mana pool is untouched\n77\t  (\"without paying its mana cost\").\n78\t- `test_chosen_sorcery_can_be_cast` — works for a sorcery too.\n79\t- `test_may_declining_leaves_graveyard_untouched` — declining (\"you may\") leaves\n80\t  the graveyard unchanged and adds nothing to the stack.\n81\t- `test_empty_graveyard_is_a_safe_noop` — with no instant/sorcery available the\n82\t  trigger resolves cleanly and casts nothing (no exception).\n83\t\n84\t### TestTheDawningArchaicExileReplacement\n85\tValidates clause (4): the free-cast spell is exiled, not put in the graveyard.\n86\tThe helper free-casts the chosen spell and then resolves the spell itself.\n87\t- `test_resolved_free_cast_instant_goes_to_exile` — resolved instant ends in\n88\t  exile and is NOT in the graveyard.\n89\t- `test_resolved_free_cast_sorcery_goes_to_exile` — same for a sorcery.\n90\t\n91\t## Edge cases covered (and why)\n92\t- Optional (\"you may\") path — declining must be a clean no-op.\n93\t- Empty graveyard — the trigger must not crash with no legal target.\n94\t- Opponent's graveyard and non-instant/sorcery cards must not affect the\n95\t  reduction (common implementation mistakes).\n96\t- Engine-level clamp of the reduction to the generic cost.\n97\t- Mana-pool untouched on the free cast (the defining property of \"without\n98\t  paying its mana cost\").\n99\t- Exile-instead replacement asserted on observable end zone, independent of how\n100\t  the implementer routes the zone change.\n101\t\n102\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (out of scope)\n103\t- Full combat integration via `declare_attackers_step`: the engine's\n104\t  `declare_attackers_step` does not itself fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (no\n105\t  engine path constructs that event during combat), so the attack-trigger tests\n106\t  fire the event directly through the `trigger_manager`, matching the pattern\n107\t  used by the FDN reference cards (Etali / Ruby). Testing whether combat fires\n108\t  the event is an engine concern, not this card's contract.\n109\t- Targeting legality/UI for choosing the graveyard spell (which exact prompt is\n110\t  used) — tested only at the observable level (a card is chosen and cast).\n111\t- Legend-rule / \"summoning sickness can't attack\" interactions — generic engine\n112\t  behavior, not specific to this card.\n113\t- Reach combat behavior (blocking fliers) — covered by engine combat tests; here\n114\t  we only assert the keyword is present.\n115\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"1ce1f16f-3fef-4b0f-98ac-a366ccf8581c","timestamp":"2026-06-01T23:46:56.827Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n\nCard: **The Dawning Archaic** — `{10}` — Legendary Creature — Avatar — 7/7.\n\nOracle text and the clauses each test covers:\n\n1. *\"This spell costs {1} less to cast for each instant and sorcery card in\n   your graveyard.\"* — a **cost-reduction** mechanic via the engine\n   `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` hook (clamped to the generic portion by\n   `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n2. *\"Reach\"* — a keyword.\n3. *\"Whenever The Dawning Archaic attacks, you may cast target instant or\n   sorcery card from your graveyard without paying its mana cost.\"* — an\n   **attack trigger** (`AttacksTriggeredEvent`) whose optional effect free-casts\n   a chosen instant/sorcery from the controller's graveyard (mirrors the\n   reference card Etali, Primal Storm / FDN 194, which uses\n   `engine.casting.cast_spell_free`).\n4. *\"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead.\"* — a\n   **zone-replacement** rider: the free-cast spell, once it resolves, must end\n   up in exile rather than the graveyard.\n\nAll tests are in `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`. They were authored TDD-first: the\ncurrent stub (`CardImpl` with `pass`) fails 23/27, and a plausible reference\nimplementation passes all 27 (verified out-of-band), confirming the contract is\nboth correct against the spec and achievable.\n\n## File: `cards/sos/sos_1/tests.py`\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicProperties (static data)\n- `test_name` — name is \"The Dawning Archaic\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost is `{10}`.\n- `test_is_creature` — is a `Creature` / has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T is 7/7.\n- `test_legendary` — has `Supertype.LEGENDARY`.\n- `test_avatar_subtype` — has the \"Avatar\" subtype.\n- `test_has_reach` — has `Keyword.REACH`.\n- `test_is_colorless` — `{10}` carries no colored or hybrid pips (the card is\n  colorless, matching the empty `colors` list in the spec).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicCostReduction\nValidates clause (1): reduction equals the count of instant + sorcery cards in\n*the controller's* graveyard.\n- `test_no_reduction_with_empty_graveyard` — 0 with an empty graveyard.\n- `test_one_instant_reduces_by_one` / `test_one_sorcery_reduces_by_one` — each\n  instant/sorcery contributes 1.\n- `test_mixed_instants_and_sorceries_sum` — 3 instants + 2 sorceries → 5.\n- `test_creatures_in_graveyard_do_not_reduce` — creatures are not counted.\n- `test_only_instant_sorcery_among_mixed_graveyard_count` — only the\n  instant/sorcery subset of a mixed graveyard counts (1 + 1 → 2).\n- `test_opponent_graveyard_does_not_reduce` — only \"your\" graveyard counts.\n- `test_engine_clamps_reduction_to_generic` — with >10 spells the engine clamps\n  the reduction to the `{10}` generic via `get_cost_reduction`.\n- `test_cast_with_reduction_succeeds_with_reduced_mana` — integration: 4\n  instant/sorcery in graveyard → effective `{6}`; 6 colorless mana casts and\n  resolves it onto the battlefield.\n- `test_cast_without_enough_reduction_fails` — negative integration: empty\n  graveyard requires the full `{10}`; 6 mana raises `CastingError` matching\n  \"insufficient mana\" (the match string guards against the cast failing for an\n  incidental reason rather than the cost).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicTriggerRegistration\nValidates clause (3) wiring.\n- `test_registers_an_attacks_trigger` — `register_triggers` adds exactly one\n  trigger for `AttacksTriggeredEvent` keyed to this creature as source.\n- `test_trigger_condition_matches_this_creature` — the trigger's condition\n  returns `True` only when *this* creature attacks and `False` for a different\n  attacker (so it does not fire for unrelated creatures).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicAttackEffect\nValidates clause (3) effect: optional free-cast of a graveyard instant/sorcery.\nThe shared helper registers the trigger, fires `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, and\nresolves the single pushed trigger StackObject, seeding the controller's\ndeterministic-player script with the \"may\" yes/no and the chosen card.\n- `test_chosen_instant_leaves_graveyard_onto_stack` — chosen instant leaves the\n  graveyard and appears on the stack (free cast).\n- `test_free_cast_does_not_spend_mana` — the controller's mana pool is untouched\n  (\"without paying its mana cost\").\n- `test_chosen_sorcery_can_be_cast` — works for a sorcery too.\n- `test_may_declining_leaves_graveyard_untouched` — declining (\"you may\") leaves\n  the graveyard unchanged and adds nothing to the stack.\n- `test_empty_graveyard_is_a_safe_noop` — with no instant/sorcery available the\n  trigger resolves cleanly and casts nothing (no exception).\n\n### TestTheDawningArchaicExileReplacement\nValidates clause (4): the free-cast spell is exiled, not put in the graveyard.\nThe helper free-casts the chosen spell and then resolves the spell itself.\n- `test_resolved_free_cast_instant_goes_to_exile` — resolved instant ends in\n  exile and is NOT in the graveyard.\n- `test_resolved_free_cast_sorcery_goes_to_exile` — same for a sorcery.\n\n## Edge cases covered (and why)\n- Optional (\"you may\") path — declining must be a clean no-op.\n- Empty graveyard — the trigger must not crash with no legal target.\n- Opponent's graveyard and non-instant/sorcery cards must not affect the\n  reduction (common implementation mistakes).\n- Engine-level clamp of the reduction to the generic cost.\n- Mana-pool untouched on the free cast (the defining property of \"without\n  paying its mana cost\").\n- Exile-instead replacement asserted on observable end zone, independent of how\n  the implementer routes the zone change.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (out of scope)\n- Full combat integration via `declare_attackers_step`: the engine's\n  `declare_attackers_step` does not itself fire `AttacksTriggeredEvent` (no\n  engine path constructs that event during combat), so the attack-trigger tests\n  fire the event directly through the `trigger_manager`, matching the pattern\n  used by the FDN reference cards (Etali / Ruby). Testing whether combat fires\n  the event is an engine concern, not this card's contract.\n- Targeting legality/UI for choosing the graveyard spell (which exact prompt is\n  used) — tested only at the observable level (a card is chosen and cast).\n- Legend-rule / \"summoning sickness can't attack\" interactions — generic engine\n  behavior, not specific to this card.\n- Reach combat behavior (blocking fliers) — covered by engine combat tests; here\n  we only assert the keyword is present.\n","numLines":115,"startLine":1,"totalLines":115}}}
