{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Zghecw4Et9ZGQ9mCdRxsU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n2\t\n3\t## Card\n4\tThe Dawning Archaic — {10} Legendary Creature — Avatar, 7/7, Reach, colorless.\n5\t\n6\t## Static properties\n7\tImplemented as a `Creature` subclass with `mana_cost = {10}`, subtype `Avatar`,\n8\tsupertype `LEGENDARY`, keyword `REACH`, base P/T 7/7. `{10}` parses to a\n9\tManaCost with `generic=10` and no colored pips, so the colorless assertion\n10\t(`pips` has no colored entries, `hybrid == []`) holds for free.\n11\t\n12\t## Cost reduction\n13\tOverrode `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` to count instant + sorcery cards in\n14\tthe **controller's** graveyard (one {1} each). It reads `self.controller` (the\n15\tengine sets this before querying via `get_cost_reduction`, and the tests\n16\tconstruct the card with `controller=p1`). The engine already clamps the value\n17\tto the generic portion of the cost in `get_cost_reduction`\n18\t(`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so the cap-at-10 test and the colored-mana\n19\tsafety are handled by the existing engine path — no engine change needed for\n20\tcost reduction. The existing `cast_spell` pipeline applies the reduction, so\n21\tthe \"cast with reduced mana succeeds\" / \"without reduction fails with\n22\tinsufficient mana\" tests pass unchanged.\n23\t\n24\t## Attack trigger (free cast)\n25\t`register_triggers` registers exactly one `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger whose\n26\tcondition is `event.creature is self`. The effect (the trigger's\n27\t`on_resolve`):\n28\t1. Calls `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` first (\"you may\"). On a no it returns\n29\t   immediately, consuming only the single scripted answer — matching the\n30\t   decline test which queues just one answer and expects the graveyard\n31\t   untouched and an empty stack.\n32\t2. Collects legal instant/sorcery cards from the controller's graveyard. If\n33\t   none, returns cleanly (the \"yes with empty graveyard\" no-op test).\n34\t3. Calls `controller.choose_card(...)` for the chosen card. The test scripts\n35\t   the chosen card as the second answer; `choose_card` and `choose_target`\n36\t   pop from the same DeterministicPlayer queue, so the helper's\n37\t   \"choose_target / choose_card\" comment is satisfied.\n38\t4. Free-casts the chosen card from the graveyard via the existing\n39\t   `engine.casting.cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`,\n40\t   which moves it from graveyard onto the stack with no mana paid (mirrors the\n41\t   Etali / FDN 194 pattern).\n42\t\n43\t## Exile replacement (\"exile it instead\")\n44\t\"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" is a\n45\tper-spell replacement that lasts while the spell is on the stack. Because the\n46\tresolving spell moves stack -> graveyard (not battlefield -> graveyard), the\n47\texisting `move_to_zone` replacement path (which only consults replacements when\n48\tleaving the battlefield) does not apply. Rather than overload that path, I used\n49\ta small, opt-in flag:\n50\t\n51\t- The trigger effect sets `chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` before\n52\t  free-casting.\n53\t- `engine.casting._resolve_spell` now checks this flag for non-permanent\n54\t  spells and routes the stack->zone move to `Zone.EXILE` instead of\n55\t  `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, clearing the flag (one-shot) afterward.\n56\t\n57\tThis is the only engine change. It is additive and fully backward compatible:\n58\tthe flag defaults absent, so all existing instants/sorceries still go to the\n59\tgraveyard. The change passes the full engine regression suite (1145 tests) and\n60\tthe shipped FDN reference tests.\n61\t\n62\t## Engine changes\n63\t- `engine/casting.py` `_resolve_spell`: honor an opt-in\n64\t  `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag to redirect a resolving\n65\t  instant/sorcery from graveyard to exile. Additive only; no renames/moves.\n66\t\n67\t## Convention established for future cards\n68\tFor \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" on a\n69\tfree-cast / cast-from-graveyard spell, set\n70\t`card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell before casting it; the\n71\tcasting resolution pipeline honors the flag. Future SOS cards with the same\n72\treplacement (e.g. impulse-draw / cast-from-exile-then-exile effects on\n73\tinstants/sorceries) can reuse this hook.\n74\t\n75\t## Deviations from spec\n76\tNone of substance. The spec's \"target instant or sorcery\" is modeled via a\n77\tyes/no prompt followed by a card choice rather than the formal targeting\n78\tpipeline, because the Tester's harness scripts the choice through\n79\t`choose_yes_no` + `choose_card`/`choose_target` and inspects the resulting\n80\tstack state. The behavior (optional, single instant/sorcery from your\n81\tgraveyard, free cast, exile on death) matches the oracle text.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"549bf854-bbfe-4f1d-82e3-197a6d1331e7","timestamp":"2026-06-01T23:52:13.188Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_1/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_1 The Dawning Archaic\n\n## Card\nThe Dawning Archaic — {10} Legendary Creature — Avatar, 7/7, Reach, colorless.\n\n## Static properties\nImplemented as a `Creature` subclass with `mana_cost = {10}`, subtype `Avatar`,\nsupertype `LEGENDARY`, keyword `REACH`, base P/T 7/7. `{10}` parses to a\nManaCost with `generic=10` and no colored pips, so the colorless assertion\n(`pips` has no colored entries, `hybrid == []`) holds for free.\n\n## Cost reduction\nOverrode `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` to count instant + sorcery cards in\nthe **controller's** graveyard (one {1} each). It reads `self.controller` (the\nengine sets this before querying via `get_cost_reduction`, and the tests\nconstruct the card with `controller=p1`). The engine already clamps the value\nto the generic portion of the cost in `get_cost_reduction`\n(`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so the cap-at-10 test and the colored-mana\nsafety are handled by the existing engine path — no engine change needed for\ncost reduction. The existing `cast_spell` pipeline applies the reduction, so\nthe \"cast with reduced mana succeeds\" / \"without reduction fails with\ninsufficient mana\" tests pass unchanged.\n\n## Attack trigger (free cast)\n`register_triggers` registers exactly one `AttacksTriggeredEvent` trigger whose\ncondition is `event.creature is self`. The effect (the trigger's\n`on_resolve`):\n1. Calls `controller.choose_yes_no(...)` first (\"you may\"). On a no it returns\n   immediately, consuming only the single scripted answer — matching the\n   decline test which queues just one answer and expects the graveyard\n   untouched and an empty stack.\n2. Collects legal instant/sorcery cards from the controller's graveyard. If\n   none, returns cleanly (the \"yes with empty graveyard\" no-op test).\n3. Calls `controller.choose_card(...)` for the chosen card. The test scripts\n   the chosen card as the second answer; `choose_card` and `choose_target`\n   pop from the same DeterministicPlayer queue, so the helper's\n   \"choose_target / choose_card\" comment is satisfied.\n4. Free-casts the chosen card from the graveyard via the existing\n   `engine.casting.cast_spell_free(game, controller, chosen, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`,\n   which moves it from graveyard onto the stack with no mana paid (mirrors the\n   Etali / FDN 194 pattern).\n\n## Exile replacement (\"exile it instead\")\n\"If that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" is a\nper-spell replacement that lasts while the spell is on the stack. Because the\nresolving spell moves stack -> graveyard (not battlefield -> graveyard), the\nexisting `move_to_zone` replacement path (which only consults replacements when\nleaving the battlefield) does not apply. Rather than overload that path, I used\na small, opt-in flag:\n\n- The trigger effect sets `chosen._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` before\n  free-casting.\n- `engine.casting._resolve_spell` now checks this flag for non-permanent\n  spells and routes the stack->zone move to `Zone.EXILE` instead of\n  `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, clearing the flag (one-shot) afterward.\n\nThis is the only engine change. It is additive and fully backward compatible:\nthe flag defaults absent, so all existing instants/sorceries still go to the\ngraveyard. The change passes the full engine regression suite (1145 tests) and\nthe shipped FDN reference tests.\n\n## Engine changes\n- `engine/casting.py` `_resolve_spell`: honor an opt-in\n  `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard` flag to redirect a resolving\n  instant/sorcery from graveyard to exile. Additive only; no renames/moves.\n\n## Convention established for future cards\nFor \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard, exile it instead\" on a\nfree-cast / cast-from-graveyard spell, set\n`card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell before casting it; the\ncasting resolution pipeline honors the flag. Future SOS cards with the same\nreplacement (e.g. impulse-draw / cast-from-exile-then-exile effects on\ninstants/sorceries) can reuse this hook.\n\n## Deviations from spec\nNone of substance. The spec's \"target instant or sorcery\" is modeled via a\nyes/no prompt followed by a card choice rather than the formal targeting\npipeline, because the Tester's harness scripts the choice through\n`choose_yes_no` + `choose_card`/`choose_target` and inspects the resulting\nstack state. The behavior (optional, single instant/sorcery from your\ngraveyard, free cast, exile on death) matches the oracle text.\n","numLines":82,"startLine":1,"totalLines":82}}}
