{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019K55Wz2F1rmvUe5JMF96DH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n2\t\n3\t## Card under test\n4\t\n5\t**Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery (colorless).\n6\t\n7\t> Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any\n8\t> target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to\n9\t> cast this spell.\n10\t\n11\t### Mechanics\n12\t\n13\t- **Converge**: X equals the number of *distinct colors* of mana spent to cast\n14\t  the spell. The cast pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) records this on the card as\n15\t  `colors_spent` — a list of `engine.types.Color` derived from\n16\t  `ManaPool.last_payment_colors`. Colorless mana is not a color and does not\n17\t  contribute. So an all-colorless `{6}` payment yields X = 0; paying with W+U+B\n18\t  plus 3 colorless yields X = 3; WUBRG-style payment yields X = 5.\n19\t- **Two targets, applied in one resolution**:\n20\t  1. *Target player* draws X cards (a player-only target).\n21\t  2. *Any target* (creature/player/planeswalker per rule 115.4) is dealt X damage.\n22\t  3. *You* (the controller) gain X life — untargeted.\n23\t\n24\tThe implementation contract mirrors the FDN converge reference\n25\t(`cards/fdn/fdn_205`): `colors_spent` is set by the cast pipeline (or by tests),\n26\tand `on_resolve` reads it. Targeting follows `cards/fdn/fdn_13` and\n27\t`cards/fdn/fdn_192` (Burst Lightning's \"any target\" filter): `get_targets`\n28\treturns `TargetRequirement`s and the pipeline populates `chosen_targets` in the\n29\tsame order the requirements are returned.\n30\t\n31\t## Test file\n32\t\n33\t`cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n34\t\n35\t### TestTogetherAsOneProperties — static card data\n36\t- `test_is_sorcery` — card is a `Sorcery` and has `CardType.SORCERY`.\n37\t- `test_name` — name is \"Together as One\".\n38\t- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost parses to `{6}`.\n39\t- `test_not_a_creature` — it is a noncreature spell (guards against a wrong base\n40\t  class). *(Passes against the empty stub because `CardImpl` is not a `Creature`;\n41\t  retained as a meaningful guard for any future impl.)*\n42\t\n43\t### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting — \"target player\" and \"any target\"\n44\t- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — `get_targets` returns exactly two\n45\t  `TargetRequirement`s (one per targeted clause).\n46\t- `test_first_requirement_accepts_players_only` — the \"target player\" filter\n47\t  accepts a player and rejects a creature.\n48\t- `test_second_requirement_accepts_any_target` — the \"any target\" filter accepts\n49\t  both a player and a creature.\n50\t- `test_any_target_rejects_noncreature_nonplayer` — a noncreature, nonplayer\n51\t  object is not a legal \"any target\" (rule 115.4 excludes noncreature artifacts\n52\t  etc.).\n53\t\n54\t### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeDraw — \"target player draws X cards\"\n55\t- `test_zero_colors_draws_nothing` — X = 0 (empty `colors_spent`) draws nothing.\n56\t- `test_two_colors_target_player_draws_two` — two distinct colors → targeted\n57\t  player draws 2.\n58\t- `test_five_colors_target_player_draws_five` — five colors → targeted player\n59\t  draws 5.\n60\t- `test_draw_goes_to_chosen_player_not_controller` — when the chosen target\n61\t  player is the opponent, the opponent draws and the controller does not. This\n62\t  verifies the draw clause targets the *chosen player*, not \"you\".\n63\t\n64\t### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeDamage — \"deals X damage to any target\"\n65\t- `test_damage_to_player` — X damage reduces a targeted player's life.\n66\t- `test_damage_to_creature` — X damage marks `damage_marked` on a targeted\n67\t  creature.\n68\t- `test_zero_colors_deals_no_damage` — X = 0 deals no damage.\n69\t\n70\t### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeLifeGain — \"you gain X life\"\n71\t- `test_controller_gains_life_equal_to_colors` — controller's life increases by X.\n72\t- `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` — life goes to the\n73\t  controller (\"you\"), even when the *target player* who draws is the opponent.\n74\t- `test_zero_colors_no_life_gain` — X = 0 gives no life.\n75\t\n76\t### TestTogetherAsOneCombinedResolution\n77\t- `test_all_three_effects_in_one_resolution` — a single `on_resolve` applies all\n78\t  three clauses together (draw X, deal X damage, gain X life) with the same X.\n79\t\n80\t### TestTogetherAsOneResolveSafety — robustness\n81\t- `test_no_colors_spent_attribute_is_noop` — if `colors_spent` was never set\n82\t  (X treated as 0), resolution is a safe no-op and does not raise.\n83\t- `test_no_targets_does_not_raise` — with no `chosen_targets`, resolution does\n84\t  not raise (targeted clauses fizzle; untargeted life gain may still apply).\n85\t\n86\t### TestTogetherAsOneEndToEnd — real cast pipeline\n87\tThese ground the converge wiring in real mana payment (the pipeline sets\n88\t`colors_spent` from `last_payment_colors`).\n89\t- `test_cast_with_three_colors_applies_x_equals_three` — pay `{6}` with W+U+B+3\n90\t  colorless → X = 3: target player (controller) draws 3, opponent takes 3 damage,\n91\t  controller gains 3 life.\n92\t- `test_cast_with_all_colorless_is_x_zero` — all-colorless payment → X = 0 and no\n93\t  effects.\n94\t- `test_spell_goes_to_graveyard_after_resolution` — as a sorcery, it is placed in\n95\t  its owner's graveyard after resolving.\n96\t\n97\t## Edge cases covered and why\n98\t- **X = 0 (all-colorless payment)** across all three clauses and end-to-end —\n99\t  converge counts *colors*, not mana, so a fully colorless payment must be inert.\n100\t- **Target player ≠ controller** — distinguishes \"target player draws\" from\n101\t  \"you gain life\", which would be conflated by a naive impl that always uses the\n102\t  controller.\n103\t- **Any target = player vs creature** — both legal target shapes for the damage\n104\t  clause.\n105\t- **Resolution safety with unset targets / colors** — defensive no-op behavior.\n106\t\n107\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope)\n108\t- **Player choosing how to pay generic mana to maximize converge color count** —\n109\t  `engine/casting.py` explicitly defers this (\"TODO: Phase 3 — support player\n110\t  choice for generic mana payment to optimize Converge color count\"); the auto-pay\n111\t  path determines colors spent. Testing player-optimized payment would test engine\n112\t  behavior the engine does not yet expose, not this card.\n113\t- **Hexproof / ward / protection interactions with the targets** — these are\n114\t  generic targeting-legality concerns handled by the engine's cast pipeline and\n115\t  covered by engine tests, not specific to this card.\n116\t- **Planeswalker / battle as the \"any target\"** — the engine's modeled \"any\n117\t  target\" surface in reference cards is players + creatures; planeswalkers/battles\n118\t  are not part of the test fixtures used by the reference cards.\n119\t- **Drawing from an empty library / decking out** — that is engine state-based\n120\t  behavior covered by `engine_tests`, not this card's contract.\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"d216b8cf-eef7-493d-a24d-e057835bd2ad","timestamp":"2026-06-01T23:56:00.159Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_4/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n\n## Card under test\n\n**Together as One** — `{6}` Sorcery (colorless).\n\n> Converge — Target player draws X cards, Together as One deals X damage to any\n> target, and you gain X life, where X is the number of colors of mana spent to\n> cast this spell.\n\n### Mechanics\n\n- **Converge**: X equals the number of *distinct colors* of mana spent to cast\n  the spell. The cast pipeline (`engine/casting.py`) records this on the card as\n  `colors_spent` — a list of `engine.types.Color` derived from\n  `ManaPool.last_payment_colors`. Colorless mana is not a color and does not\n  contribute. So an all-colorless `{6}` payment yields X = 0; paying with W+U+B\n  plus 3 colorless yields X = 3; WUBRG-style payment yields X = 5.\n- **Two targets, applied in one resolution**:\n  1. *Target player* draws X cards (a player-only target).\n  2. *Any target* (creature/player/planeswalker per rule 115.4) is dealt X damage.\n  3. *You* (the controller) gain X life — untargeted.\n\nThe implementation contract mirrors the FDN converge reference\n(`cards/fdn/fdn_205`): `colors_spent` is set by the cast pipeline (or by tests),\nand `on_resolve` reads it. Targeting follows `cards/fdn/fdn_13` and\n`cards/fdn/fdn_192` (Burst Lightning's \"any target\" filter): `get_targets`\nreturns `TargetRequirement`s and the pipeline populates `chosen_targets` in the\nsame order the requirements are returned.\n\n## Test file\n\n`cards/sos/sos_4/tests.py`\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneProperties — static card data\n- `test_is_sorcery` — card is a `Sorcery` and has `CardType.SORCERY`.\n- `test_name` — name is \"Together as One\".\n- `test_mana_cost` — mana cost parses to `{6}`.\n- `test_not_a_creature` — it is a noncreature spell (guards against a wrong base\n  class). *(Passes against the empty stub because `CardImpl` is not a `Creature`;\n  retained as a meaningful guard for any future impl.)*\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneTargeting — \"target player\" and \"any target\"\n- `test_returns_two_target_requirements` — `get_targets` returns exactly two\n  `TargetRequirement`s (one per targeted clause).\n- `test_first_requirement_accepts_players_only` — the \"target player\" filter\n  accepts a player and rejects a creature.\n- `test_second_requirement_accepts_any_target` — the \"any target\" filter accepts\n  both a player and a creature.\n- `test_any_target_rejects_noncreature_nonplayer` — a noncreature, nonplayer\n  object is not a legal \"any target\" (rule 115.4 excludes noncreature artifacts\n  etc.).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeDraw — \"target player draws X cards\"\n- `test_zero_colors_draws_nothing` — X = 0 (empty `colors_spent`) draws nothing.\n- `test_two_colors_target_player_draws_two` — two distinct colors → targeted\n  player draws 2.\n- `test_five_colors_target_player_draws_five` — five colors → targeted player\n  draws 5.\n- `test_draw_goes_to_chosen_player_not_controller` — when the chosen target\n  player is the opponent, the opponent draws and the controller does not. This\n  verifies the draw clause targets the *chosen player*, not \"you\".\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeDamage — \"deals X damage to any target\"\n- `test_damage_to_player` — X damage reduces a targeted player's life.\n- `test_damage_to_creature` — X damage marks `damage_marked` on a targeted\n  creature.\n- `test_zero_colors_deals_no_damage` — X = 0 deals no damage.\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneConvergeLifeGain — \"you gain X life\"\n- `test_controller_gains_life_equal_to_colors` — controller's life increases by X.\n- `test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` — life goes to the\n  controller (\"you\"), even when the *target player* who draws is the opponent.\n- `test_zero_colors_no_life_gain` — X = 0 gives no life.\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneCombinedResolution\n- `test_all_three_effects_in_one_resolution` — a single `on_resolve` applies all\n  three clauses together (draw X, deal X damage, gain X life) with the same X.\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneResolveSafety — robustness\n- `test_no_colors_spent_attribute_is_noop` — if `colors_spent` was never set\n  (X treated as 0), resolution is a safe no-op and does not raise.\n- `test_no_targets_does_not_raise` — with no `chosen_targets`, resolution does\n  not raise (targeted clauses fizzle; untargeted life gain may still apply).\n\n### TestTogetherAsOneEndToEnd — real cast pipeline\nThese ground the converge wiring in real mana payment (the pipeline sets\n`colors_spent` from `last_payment_colors`).\n- `test_cast_with_three_colors_applies_x_equals_three` — pay `{6}` with W+U+B+3\n  colorless → X = 3: target player (controller) draws 3, opponent takes 3 damage,\n  controller gains 3 life.\n- `test_cast_with_all_colorless_is_x_zero` — all-colorless payment → X = 0 and no\n  effects.\n- `test_spell_goes_to_graveyard_after_resolution` — as a sorcery, it is placed in\n  its owner's graveyard after resolving.\n\n## Edge cases covered and why\n- **X = 0 (all-colorless payment)** across all three clauses and end-to-end —\n  converge counts *colors*, not mana, so a fully colorless payment must be inert.\n- **Target player ≠ controller** — distinguishes \"target player draws\" from\n  \"you gain life\", which would be conflated by a naive impl that always uses the\n  controller.\n- **Any target = player vs creature** — both legal target shapes for the damage\n  clause.\n- **Resolution safety with unset targets / colors** — defensive no-op behavior.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope)\n- **Player choosing how to pay generic mana to maximize converge color count** —\n  `engine/casting.py` explicitly defers this (\"TODO: Phase 3 — support player\n  choice for generic mana payment to optimize Converge color count\"); the auto-pay\n  path determines colors spent. Testing player-optimized payment would test engine\n  behavior the engine does not yet expose, not this card.\n- **Hexproof / ward / protection interactions with the targets** — these are\n  generic targeting-legality concerns handled by the engine's cast pipeline and\n  covered by engine tests, not specific to this card.\n- **Planeswalker / battle as the \"any target\"** — the engine's modeled \"any\n  target\" surface in reference cards is players + creatures; planeswalkers/battles\n  are not part of the test fixtures used by the reference cards.\n- **Drawing from an empty library / decking out** — that is engine state-based\n  behavior covered by `engine_tests`, not this card's contract.\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}}}
