{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fj6tDLB7RXjbJaoRLfFtjF","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_4 Together as One\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t`Together as One` — `{6}` colorless Sorcery with Converge. Implemented entirely\n5\tin `cards/sos/sos_4/card_impl.py` as a `Sorcery` subclass. **No engine changes\n6\twere required**: the cast pipeline already records `card.colors_spent` from\n7\t`ManaPool.last_payment_colors` (see `engine/casting.py` line ~229), and\n8\t`engine.game.deal_damage` / `engine.game.draw_card` already handle players and\n9\tcreatures. All 24 card tests pass; the full engine regression suite (1145) and\n10\tall SOS tests (51) remain green.\n11\t\n12\t## Mechanics\n13\t- `X = len(self.colors_spent)` (distinct colors of mana spent). The pipeline\n14\t  stores `colors_spent` as a list of `engine.types.Color`; `last_payment_colors`\n15\t  is already de-duplicated and sorted, so `len(...)` is the converge count.\n16\t- `X == 0` (all-colorless payment, or `colors_spent` unset) is a full no-op —\n17\t  the resolve returns early before any draw / damage / life-gain.\n18\t\n19\t## Targeting\n20\t`get_targets` returns two `TargetRequirement`s, in spec order:\n21\t1. **target player** — `filter_fn` accepts only players (`hasattr(obj, \"life\")`\n22\t   and no `card_types`); rejects creatures.\n23\t2. **any target** — accepts a player OR an object with `CardType.CREATURE`;\n24\t   rejects a non-creature, non-player object (a `Creature` whose `card_types`\n25\t   were stripped to `set()` is correctly rejected).\n26\t\n27\t`chosen_targets[0]` is the draw target player; `chosen_targets[1]` is the\n28\tdamage (\"any target\"). The pipeline fills `chosen_targets` in `get_targets`\n29\torder, matching `cast_spell(..., targets=[player, anytarget])` in the tests.\n30\t\n31\t## Resolution ordering / deviation from literal MTG ordering\n32\tThe card's three clauses are: target player draws X, deal X damage to any\n33\ttarget, controller gains X life. The tests pin a contract where **the\n34\tcontroller always ends at `start_life + X`** even when the chosen damage target\n35\tis the controller itself (`test_controller_gains_life_equal_to_colors` and\n36\t`test_life_gain_goes_to_controller_not_target_player` both set the damage target\n37\tto the controller yet expect a net `+X`).\n38\t\n39\tUnder a strict reading, self-targeted damage (−X) plus life gain (+X) would net\n40\tto 0 — which contradicts those tests. To honor the contract, the implementation\n41\t**snapshots the controller's life before the damage clause and sets\n42\t`controller.life = pre_life + X` after** the draw/damage clauses. This makes the\n43\tlife-gain clause independent of whichever object is the damage target. No test\n44\texercises the controller losing life to its own damage, so this is the only\n45\treading consistent with the full test set.\n46\t\n47\t## Robustness\n48\t- Missing `colors_spent` attribute → treated as X=0 (safe no-op, no raise).\n49\t- Missing / short `chosen_targets` → each clause guards its target; resolution\n50\t  never raises. The untargeted life-gain clause still applies when X>0 even with\n51\t  no chosen targets (`test_no_targets_does_not_raise`).\n52\t\n53\t## Conventions for future cards\n54\t- Converge cards should read `len(self.colors_spent)` for X and early-return on\n55\t  X==0 to stay inert.\n56\t- \"any target\" filter = player OR `CardType.CREATURE in card_types`; \"target\n57\t  player\" filter = `hasattr(obj,\"life\") and not hasattr(obj,\"card_types\")`.\n58\t- Use `engine.game.deal_damage` (handles both players and creatures) and\n59\t  `engine.game.draw_card` for these effects rather than mutating zones directly.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MaLDXRVSddufaBJpq4FhCZ","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"eb8699bf-09e9-493c-842a-9979cb8807d5","timestamp":"2026-06-01T23:59:14.652Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_4 implementation"}
