{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SPQ7DL22qGNxwdMMXXdjjJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_13\",\n4\t    \"requirement\": \"While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it. (CR 722.3c — casting a copy of the prepare spell, Swords to Plowshares, from exile while the creature is prepared, which then removes the prepared designation.)\",\n5\t    \"why_untestable\": \"The engine has no preparation-card / 'Prepared' designation support and no pipeline for creating a copy of a spell in exile and casting it from there. There is no public API to (a) place a prepare-spell copy into exile when the creature becomes prepared, (b) cast that copy, or (c) observe the unprepare transition triggered by casting it.\",\n6\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An engine surface for preparation cards: e.g. when a permanent 'becomes prepared', create a castable copy of its prepare spell in the controller's exile zone, expose a way to cast that copy (without paying mana per the reminder text), and clear the 'prepared' designation when the copy is cast. With that, tests could assert: the exiled copy exists while prepared, casting it resolves Swords to Plowshares, and the source creature is no longer prepared afterward.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"card_id\": \"sos_13\",\n10\t    \"requirement\": \"Swords to Plowshares: 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.' (the inset prepare spell's resolution effect)\",\n11\t    \"why_untestable\": \"Covered only by skip-guarded tests (TestSwordsToPlowshares) because the engine mandates no API for constructing the inset prepare spell. The tests probe for make_prepare_spell / get_prepare_spell / prepare_spell / create_copy and skip if none is exposed, so the exile-and-lifegain behavior is not enforced as a hard contract unless the Implementer adopts one of those construction surfaces.\",\n12\t    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A defined, documented way to obtain a castable Swords to Plowshares spell object from the card (e.g. a card.make_prepare_spell(game) factory or a standalone class), so the resolution effect (exile target creature; that creature's controller gains life equal to its power) can be asserted directly rather than skipped.\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"9f448945-f67d-4c0c-9905-85357eb451b7","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:04:58.129Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/untestable.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_13\",\n    \"requirement\": \"While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it. (CR 722.3c — casting a copy of the prepare spell, Swords to Plowshares, from exile while the creature is prepared, which then removes the prepared designation.)\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"The engine has no preparation-card / 'Prepared' designation support and no pipeline for creating a copy of a spell in exile and casting it from there. There is no public API to (a) place a prepare-spell copy into exile when the creature becomes prepared, (b) cast that copy, or (c) observe the unprepare transition triggered by casting it.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"An engine surface for preparation cards: e.g. when a permanent 'becomes prepared', create a castable copy of its prepare spell in the controller's exile zone, expose a way to cast that copy (without paying mana per the reminder text), and clear the 'prepared' designation when the copy is cast. With that, tests could assert: the exiled copy exists while prepared, casting it resolves Swords to Plowshares, and the source creature is no longer prepared afterward.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"card_id\": \"sos_13\",\n    \"requirement\": \"Swords to Plowshares: 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.' (the inset prepare spell's resolution effect)\",\n    \"why_untestable\": \"Covered only by skip-guarded tests (TestSwordsToPlowshares) because the engine mandates no API for constructing the inset prepare spell. The tests probe for make_prepare_spell / get_prepare_spell / prepare_spell / create_copy and skip if none is exposed, so the exile-and-lifegain behavior is not enforced as a hard contract unless the Implementer adopts one of those construction surfaces.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock_it\": \"A defined, documented way to obtain a castable Swords to Plowshares spell object from the card (e.g. a card.make_prepare_spell(game) factory or a standalone class), so the resolution effect (exile target creature; that creature's controller gains life equal to its power) can be asserted directly rather than skipped.\"\n  }\n]\n","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":15}}}
