{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014yxDPBP93yYXzxze6YVhm2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n2\t\n3\t## Card mechanics\n4\t\n5\tThis is a **preparation card** (CR 722), a two-part card:\n6\t\n7\t- **Front face — Emeritus of Truce**: `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3 white Creature — Cat Cleric.\n8\t  - ETB trigger: *\"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white\n9\t    and black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls\n10\t    more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\"*\n11\t- **Inset \"prepare spell\" — Swords to Plowshares**: `{W}` Instant — *\"Exile\n12\t  target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\"*\n13\t  - While the creature is prepared, its controller may cast a copy of the\n14\t    prepare spell from exile; doing so unprepares it (CR 722.3c).\n15\t\n16\tThe engine has **no native \"Prepared\" designation, no preparation-card frame,\n17\tand no split-card support**. The Implementer therefore has latitude over the\n18\tinternal representation. The tests assert *observable behaviour* and probe the\n19\tlikely attribute/method shapes tolerantly (e.g. `card.prepared` /\n20\t`card.is_prepared`, a token's `colors` / `subtypes`, a prepare-spell factory).\n21\t\n22\t## Test file\n23\t\n24\t`cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`\n25\t\n26\t### `TestEmeritusProperties` — printed front-face characteristics\n27\t- `test_is_creature` — it is a `Creature` and has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n28\t- `test_name` — name matches the spec (`Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares`).\n29\t- `test_mana_cost` — `{1}{W}{W}`.\n30\t- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T 3/3.\n31\t- `test_creature_subtypes` — Cat Cleric.\n32\t- `test_is_white` — white color identity (`colors` contains `\"W\"`).\n33\t\n34\tThese pin the static data implied by `type_line`, `mana_cost`, and P/T.\n35\t\n36\t### `TestEmeritusEtbRegistration` — trigger wiring\n37\t- `test_register_triggers_adds_etb` — `register_triggers` registers exactly one\n38\t  `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` trigger for the card. Validates the \"When\n39\t  this creature enters …\" clause is an ETB trigger (not a static/etc. ability).\n40\t\n41\t### `TestEmeritusTokenCreation` — first ETB clause\n42\tValidates *\"target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling creature token\n43\twith flying.\"* The ETB is driven through the trigger system (with an `on_resolve`\n44\tfallback) with the target player set via `chosen_targets`.\n45\t- `test_target_player_gets_one_token` — exactly one Inkling appears under the\n46\t  chosen target player's control.\n47\t- `test_token_goes_to_chosen_player_not_caster` — when the opponent is targeted,\n48\t  the caster receives no token (verifies \"target *player*\", not \"you\").\n49\t- `test_controller_may_target_self` — the controller is a legal target and may\n50\t  take the token.\n51\t- `test_token_is_one_one` — token base P/T is 1/1.\n52\t- `test_token_has_flying` — token has `Keyword.FLYING`.\n53\t- `test_token_is_white_and_black` — token colors include both W and B.\n54\t- `test_token_is_an_inkling` — token has the `Inkling` subtype.\n55\t- `test_token_is_marked_as_token` — token's `is_token` flag is set (so SBAs treat\n56\t  it correctly).\n57\t\n58\t### `TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared` — second ETB clause\n59\tValidates *\"Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature\n60\tbecomes prepared.\"* The comparison is over creatures on the battlefield, and the\n61\ttoken (clause 1) is created **before** the comparison, so it can affect counts.\n62\t- `test_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures` — opponent has strictly more\n63\t  creatures → prepared.\n64\t- `test_not_prepared_when_counts_equal` — equal counts → NOT prepared (strict\n65\t  \"more than\"); also asserts the token was still created so the negative case\n66\t  cannot be satisfied by a no-op implementation.\n67\t- `test_not_prepared_when_controller_has_more` — controller has more → NOT\n68\t  prepared; likewise guards against a no-op.\n69\t- `test_token_under_opponent_can_flip_the_comparison` — directing the token to\n70\t  the opponent (created before the check) tips the opponent into \"more\n71\t  creatures\", making the creature prepared. Verifies ordering of the two\n72\t  clauses.\n73\t\n74\t### `TestSwordsToPlowshares` — the prepare spell (partial / skip-guarded)\n75\tValidates *\"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its\n76\tpower.\"* These tests probe for a prepare-spell construction surface\n77\t(`make_prepare_spell` / `get_prepare_spell` / `prepare_spell` / `create_copy`)\n78\tand `pytest.skip` if none is exposed, because the engine mandates no specific\n79\tAPI for the inset spell.\n80\t- `test_exiles_target_creature` — the targeted creature leaves the battlefield\n81\t  and lands in its owner's exile zone.\n82\t- `test_controller_gains_life_equal_to_power` — the exiled creature's\n83\t  *controller* (not the caster) gains life equal to the creature's power.\n84\t- `test_caster_does_not_gain_life_for_opponents_creature` — exiling an\n85\t  opponent's creature gives the caster no life (the controller does).\n86\t- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — resolving with no chosen target must not raise or\n87\t  change life.\n88\t\n89\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n90\t- **Casting a copy of the prepare spell from exile / \"doing so unprepares it\"**\n91\t  (CR 722.3c): requires a preparation-card / cast-copy-from-exile pipeline that\n92\t  the engine does not provide. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n93\t- **The full alternative-characteristics copy semantics** (CR 722.3c, that the\n94\t  exiled copy has only the prepare spell's characteristics): no engine surface\n95\t  to construct/inspect the exile copy. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n96\t- **Sorcery-speed/timing legality of the ETB token target** — that's engine\n97\t  targeting/priority behaviour, out of scope for this card.\n98\t- **Token's exact white/black color *and* not-other-colors** beyond W and B\n99\t  presence: the engine's `colors` representation for tokens is implementation\n100\t  defined; asserting only the presence of W and B keeps the contract robust.\n101\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"dbae94bd-df83-4a15-9a4d-acb9a8f4ef96","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:04:58.434Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_13 Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares\n\n## Card mechanics\n\nThis is a **preparation card** (CR 722), a two-part card:\n\n- **Front face — Emeritus of Truce**: `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3 white Creature — Cat Cleric.\n  - ETB trigger: *\"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white\n    and black Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls\n    more creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\"*\n- **Inset \"prepare spell\" — Swords to Plowshares**: `{W}` Instant — *\"Exile\n  target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\"*\n  - While the creature is prepared, its controller may cast a copy of the\n    prepare spell from exile; doing so unprepares it (CR 722.3c).\n\nThe engine has **no native \"Prepared\" designation, no preparation-card frame,\nand no split-card support**. The Implementer therefore has latitude over the\ninternal representation. The tests assert *observable behaviour* and probe the\nlikely attribute/method shapes tolerantly (e.g. `card.prepared` /\n`card.is_prepared`, a token's `colors` / `subtypes`, a prepare-spell factory).\n\n## Test file\n\n`cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`\n\n### `TestEmeritusProperties` — printed front-face characteristics\n- `test_is_creature` — it is a `Creature` and has `CardType.CREATURE`.\n- `test_name` — name matches the spec (`Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares`).\n- `test_mana_cost` — `{1}{W}{W}`.\n- `test_power_toughness` — base P/T 3/3.\n- `test_creature_subtypes` — Cat Cleric.\n- `test_is_white` — white color identity (`colors` contains `\"W\"`).\n\nThese pin the static data implied by `type_line`, `mana_cost`, and P/T.\n\n### `TestEmeritusEtbRegistration` — trigger wiring\n- `test_register_triggers_adds_etb` — `register_triggers` registers exactly one\n  `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent` trigger for the card. Validates the \"When\n  this creature enters …\" clause is an ETB trigger (not a static/etc. ability).\n\n### `TestEmeritusTokenCreation` — first ETB clause\nValidates *\"target player creates a 1/1 white and black Inkling creature token\nwith flying.\"* The ETB is driven through the trigger system (with an `on_resolve`\nfallback) with the target player set via `chosen_targets`.\n- `test_target_player_gets_one_token` — exactly one Inkling appears under the\n  chosen target player's control.\n- `test_token_goes_to_chosen_player_not_caster` — when the opponent is targeted,\n  the caster receives no token (verifies \"target *player*\", not \"you\").\n- `test_controller_may_target_self` — the controller is a legal target and may\n  take the token.\n- `test_token_is_one_one` — token base P/T is 1/1.\n- `test_token_has_flying` — token has `Keyword.FLYING`.\n- `test_token_is_white_and_black` — token colors include both W and B.\n- `test_token_is_an_inkling` — token has the `Inkling` subtype.\n- `test_token_is_marked_as_token` — token's `is_token` flag is set (so SBAs treat\n  it correctly).\n\n### `TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared` — second ETB clause\nValidates *\"Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature\nbecomes prepared.\"* The comparison is over creatures on the battlefield, and the\ntoken (clause 1) is created **before** the comparison, so it can affect counts.\n- `test_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures` — opponent has strictly more\n  creatures → prepared.\n- `test_not_prepared_when_counts_equal` — equal counts → NOT prepared (strict\n  \"more than\"); also asserts the token was still created so the negative case\n  cannot be satisfied by a no-op implementation.\n- `test_not_prepared_when_controller_has_more` — controller has more → NOT\n  prepared; likewise guards against a no-op.\n- `test_token_under_opponent_can_flip_the_comparison` — directing the token to\n  the opponent (created before the check) tips the opponent into \"more\n  creatures\", making the creature prepared. Verifies ordering of the two\n  clauses.\n\n### `TestSwordsToPlowshares` — the prepare spell (partial / skip-guarded)\nValidates *\"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its\npower.\"* These tests probe for a prepare-spell construction surface\n(`make_prepare_spell` / `get_prepare_spell` / `prepare_spell` / `create_copy`)\nand `pytest.skip` if none is exposed, because the engine mandates no specific\nAPI for the inset spell.\n- `test_exiles_target_creature` — the targeted creature leaves the battlefield\n  and lands in its owner's exile zone.\n- `test_controller_gains_life_equal_to_power` — the exiled creature's\n  *controller* (not the caster) gains life equal to the creature's power.\n- `test_caster_does_not_gain_life_for_opponents_creature` — exiling an\n  opponent's creature gives the caster no life (the controller does).\n- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — resolving with no chosen target must not raise or\n  change life.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n- **Casting a copy of the prepare spell from exile / \"doing so unprepares it\"**\n  (CR 722.3c): requires a preparation-card / cast-copy-from-exile pipeline that\n  the engine does not provide. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **The full alternative-characteristics copy semantics** (CR 722.3c, that the\n  exiled copy has only the prepare spell's characteristics): no engine surface\n  to construct/inspect the exile copy. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **Sorcery-speed/timing legality of the ETB token target** — that's engine\n  targeting/priority behaviour, out of scope for this card.\n- **Token's exact white/black color *and* not-other-colors** beyond W and B\n  presence: the engine's `colors` representation for tokens is implementation\n  defined; asserting only the presence of W and B keeps the contract robust.\n","numLines":101,"startLine":1,"totalLines":101}}}
