{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01LgkiGBm8DmbQXfJjpzmvSa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DqRrGT3e6vnefGAH5ufqMX","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Implement sos_13 with preparation API","subagent_type":"Implementer","prompt":"You are implementing a single Magic: The Gathering card (TDD green phase) AND adding a small engine/card API surface that the coordinator has directed.\n\nCARD: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares — a \"preparation card\", CR 722)\n- Spec: `cards/sos/sos_13/card_spec.json`\n- Implementation file to complete: `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py`\n- Tests you MUST make pass are listed in `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-files.txt` (currently `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`).\n- **REQUIRED READING: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/coordinator-directives.md`** — it mandates exact API names you must expose (`prepared`, `make_prepare_spell`, a cast-while-prepared method). Follow it precisely; the coordinator will re-run the Tester against this API afterward.\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- You MUST NOT modify any test file listed in `test-files.txt`, nor anything under `engine_tests/`, nor any `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`. If a test is genuinely wrong/impossible, do NOT edit it — return DISPUTE.\n- Engine changes are ALLOWED and expected here: add methods/classes/helpers or modify existing function bodies inside `engine/`. You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete existing engine symbols.\n- Read `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_MAP.md`, `KEY_DECISIONS.md` first.\n\nREFERENCE MATERIAL:\n- FDN reference impls for ETB triggers, token creation, and free casting: read `cards/fdn/fdn_*/card_impl.py` (look for `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, token creation helpers, and `cast_spell_free`).\n- Engine source: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/zones.py`, `engine/types.py`.\n- For the preparation mechanic, grep `RULEBOOK.txt` for rule \"722\".\n\nTASK:\n1. Read the directives, spec, tests, and relevant engine/FDN code.\n2. Implement Emeritus of Truce front face: ETB trigger creating a 1/1 white+black flying Inkling token for the TARGET player (token created before the prepared check; `is_token` set), then \"becomes prepared\" iff an opponent controls strictly more creatures than you.\n3. Expose the mandated API: `prepared` boolean, `make_prepare_spell(game)` factory (Swords to Plowshares: exile target creature, its controller gains life equal to its power; no-target = safe no-op), and a cast-while-prepared method that requires prepared, resolves the prepare spell, and unprepares (sets prepared=False).\n4. Run `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py -q` until all NON-skipped tests pass and the previously skip-guarded Swords-to-Plowshares tests now RUN and pass (because `make_prepare_spell` is exposed).\n5. Regression check: `pytest engine_tests/ -q`.\n\nOUTPUT (into $CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13`):\n- `impl.diff` — `git diff` of all changes.\n- `impl-rationale.md` — what you implemented, the preparation API you exposed (exact method/attribute names + signatures), engine changes and why, design decisions / spec deviations.\n- `impl-files.txt` — files created/modified, one per line.\n- Upsert this card's entry into `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` (match by `card: \"sos_13\"`; replace in place if present). Entry shape:\n  {\"card\": \"sos_13\", \"tests\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\"}], \"implementation\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\"}]}\n\nReturn ONLY:\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: <N>\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: <one-line, INCLUDING the exact API names you exposed>\n\nOR:\nDISPUTE\ntests_failing: <N>\ndisputed_tests: <list>\ndispute_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-dispute.md\nnotes: <one-line>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"