{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PNbaXCSR9qYCtb35tQysYP","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n2\t\n3\tThis is a **preparation card** (CR 722). The engine has no native preparation\n4\tsupport. You are expected to add a minimal, additive engine/card surface so the\n5\tmechanic is functional AND testable. Do NOT rename/move/delete existing engine\n6\tsymbols.\n7\t\n8\t## Card (verify against `cards/sos/sos_13/card_spec.json`)\n9\t- Front face — **Emeritus of Truce**: `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3 white Creature — Cat Cleric.\n10\t  - ETB: \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black\n11\t    Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more\n12\t    creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\"\n13\t  - The token is created BEFORE the \"more creatures than you\" comparison, so it\n14\t    affects the count.\n15\t- Inset prepare spell — **Swords to Plowshares**: `{W}` Instant —\n16\t  \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\"\n17\t- \"While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.\"\n18\t  (CR 722.3c — grep RULEBOOK.txt for rule 722 if unsure.)\n19\t\n20\t## Required, concretely-named API (so the Tester's probes resolve to hard tests)\n21\tImplement ALL of the following on the card class (names are mandated — the\n22\tpre-written tests probe for these exact shapes):\n23\t\n24\t1. **`prepared` designation**: expose a boolean attribute `self.prepared`\n25\t   (default `False`). Also accept `is_prepared` as an alias/property if cheap.\n26\t   Set `prepared = True` during ETB resolution only when an opponent controls\n27\t   strictly more creatures than the controller (after the token is created).\n28\t\n29\t2. **`make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory**: return a castable Swords to\n30\t   Plowshares spell object (an `Instant` subclass instance) whose resolution\n31\t   exiles its chosen target creature and gives THAT creature's controller life\n32\t   equal to the exiled creature's power. Use `chosen_targets` for the target.\n33\t   No-target resolution must be a safe no-op (no raise, no life change). This is\n34\t   the canonical name — the Tester probes `make_prepare_spell` first.\n35\t\n36\t3. **Cast-while-prepared + unprepare**: expose a method (e.g.\n37\t   `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, ...)`) that:\n38\t   - requires `self.prepared is True` (raise or return falsy if not prepared),\n39\t   - casts/resolves a copy of the prepare spell (Swords to Plowshares),\n40\t   - sets `self.prepared = False` afterward (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n41\t   Per the reminder text the copy is cast \"without paying its mana cost\" — model\n42\t   it as a free cast (mirror the cast_spell_free pattern if convenient).\n43\t\n44\t## Implementation expectations\n45\t- Front-face static data, ETB token creation (1/1 W+B flying Inkling for the\n46\t  TARGET player, `is_token` set), and the becomes-prepared comparison are already\n47\t  covered by `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` — make those pass.\n48\t- Add only additive engine support if needed (e.g. a token-creation helper or a\n49\t  prepared-designation field). Prefer existing helpers used by FDN reference\n50\t  cards for token creation and free casting.\n51\t\n52\tAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to extend the\n53\ttest file (hardening the skip-guarded Swords-to-Plowshares tests and adding an\n54\tunprepare-on-cast test) against the API above. Then you'll get a final green\n55\tpass. Keep the API stable.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DqRrGT3e6vnefGAH5ufqMX","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"297e2156-a0f0-4363-8198-6960ec0c0ba0","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:06:40.111Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_13 with preparation API"}
