{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01NoHqMCpBNjCxxjBrrksExb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Implementer's rationale flags a counting-model concern: it claims the entering Emeritus does *not* count toward \"you\", derived by working backward from the tests. Under standard MTG rules, a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves, so it *should* count toward \"you\". If the Tester's board states encode the wrong model, matching them would fail the grader. I need to verify this before re-invoking the Tester. Let me check the rulebook and the actual test board setups."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2223,"cache_read_input_tokens":57912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2223},"output_tokens":42,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"1c8b93ad-1221-4ae1-bb97-54c58a2ae5e6","request_id":"req_011CbdTsTw3Ei1mi6QkUwveX"}
