th the token to the\ncontroller (opp 3 > controller 2). Keep the test's intent (opp-more → prepared)\nand keep the token-created-before-check ordering. The other three\nbecomes-prepared tests already pass under standard counting — leave them.\n\nIMPLEMENTER (final pass): the becomes-prepared check must count the entering\nEmeritus toward the controller (standard rules). Remove any \"subtract the\nentering creature\" adjustment.\n\n## B. Extend coverage for the two previously-untestable requirements\nThe card now exposes (keep these exact names stable):\n- `prepared: bool` (+ `is_prepared` read-only alias)\n- `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` → castable Swords to Plowshares instance\n- `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)` → requires prepared, free-casts a\n  copy, then sets `prepared = False`.\n\nTESTER: extend `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` to:\n1. Harden the previously skip-guarded Swords-to-Plowshares tests — they now run\n   because `make_prepare_spell` is exposed (no behavior change needed; just make\n   sure they assert exile + victim-controller lifegain as hard tests).\n2. Add a test for the unprepare-on-cast transition: prepare the creature\n   (`prepared = True`), put a target creature on the battlefield, call\n   `cast_prepare_spell(game, target=...)`, then assert (a) the target was exiled\n   and its controller gained life, and (b) `card.prepared is False` afterward\n   (CR 722.3c). Also assert calling `cast_prepare_spell` when NOT prepared\n   raises / is rejected.\n\nUpdate `test-rationale.md` and `test-files.txt` accordingly. Do NOT touch\n`engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":55,"newStart":1,"newLines":53,"lines":["-# Coordinator directives — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)","+# Coordinator directives — sos_13 (round 2: Tester extension + counting fix)"," ","-This is a **preparation card** (CR 722). The engine has no native preparation","-support. You are expected to add a