s than the controller (after the token is created).","+The test `TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared::test_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures`","+currently sets opponent=2 creatures and targets the Inkling token to the","+CONTROLLER, then asserts `prepared is True`. Under standard counting that board","+is controller = Emeritus + token = 2 vs opponent = 2 → NOT more → NOT prepared,","+so the assertion is wrong (the test comment \"controller controls only Emeritus","+(1)\" overlooked that the controller's own token bumps the count)."," ","-2. **`make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory**: return a castable Swords to","-   Plowshares spell object (an `Instant` subclass instance) whose resolution","-   exiles its chosen target creature and gives THAT creature's controller life","-   equal to the exiled creature's power. Use `chosen_targets` for the target.","-   No-target resolution must be a safe no-op (no raise, no life change). This is","-   the canonical name — the Tester probes `make_prepare_spell` first.","+TESTER: fix ONLY that one test's board so the \"prepared\" case is genuinely","+\"opponent strictly more than you\" under standard counting. Simplest fix: target","+the Inkling token to the OPPONENT (so opp = 2 bears + token = 3 vs controller =","+Emeritus = 1 → prepared), or give the opponent 3 bears with the token to the","+controller (opp 3 > controller 2). Keep the test's intent (opp-more → prepared)","+and keep the token-created-before-check ordering. The other three","+becomes-prepared tests already pass under standard counting — leave them."," ","-3. **Cast-while-prepared + unprepare**: expose a method (e.g.","-   `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, ...)`) that:","-   - requires `self.prepared is True` (raise or return falsy if not prepared),","-   - casts/resolves a copy of the prepare spell (Swords to Plowshares),","-   - sets `self.prepared = False` afterward (unprepare per CR 722.3c).","-   Per the reminder text the copy is cast \"without paying its mana cost\" — model","-   it as a free cast (mirror the cast_spell_free pattern if convenient).","+IMPLEMENTER (final pass): the becomes-prepared check must count the entering","+Emeritus toward the controller (standard rules). Remove any \"subtract the","+entering creature\" adjustment."," ","-## Implementation expectations","-- Front-face static data, ETB token creation (1/1 W+B flying Inkling for the","-  TARGET player, `is_token` set), and the becomes-prepared comparison are already","-  covered by `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` — make those pass.","-- Add only additive engine support if needed (e.g. a token-creation helper or a","-  prepared-designation field). Prefer existing helpers used by FDN reference","-  cards for token creation and free casting.","+## B. Extend coverage for the two previously-untestable requirements","+The card now exposes (keep these exact names stable):","+- `prepared: bool` (+ `is_prepared` read-only alias)","+- `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` → castable Swords to Plowshares instance","+- `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)` → requires prepared, free-casts a","+  copy, then sets `prepared = False`."," ","-After you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to extend the","-test file (hardening the skip-guarded Swords-to-Plowshares tests and adding an","-unprepare-on-cast test) against the API above. Then you'll get a final green","-pass. Keep the API stable.","+TESTER: extend `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` to:","+1. Harden the previously skip-guarded Swords-to-Plowshares tests — they now run","+   because `make_prepare_spell` is exposed (no behavior change needed; just make","+   sure they assert exile + victim-controller lifegain as hard tests).","+2. Add a test for the unprepare-on-cast transition: prepare the creature","+   (`prepared = True`), put a target creature on the battlefield, call","+   `cast_prepare_spell(game, target=...)`, then assert (a) the target was exiled","+   and its controller gained life, and (b) `card.prepared is False` afterward","+   (CR 722.3c). Also assert calling `cast_prepare_spell` when NOT prepared","+   raises / is rejected.","+","+Update `test-rationale.md` and `test-files.txt` accordingly. Do NOT touch","+`engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`."]}],"originalFile":"# Coordinator directives — sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares)\n\nThis is a **preparation card** (CR 722). The engine has no native preparation\nsupport. You are expected to add a minimal, additive engine/card surface so the\nmechanic is functional AND testable. Do NOT rename/move/delete existing engine\nsymbols.\n\n## Card (verify against `cards/sos/sos_13/card_spec.json`)\n- Front face — **Emeritus of Truce**: `{1}{W}{W}`, 3/3 white Creature — Cat Cleric.\n  - ETB: \"When this creature enters, target player creates a 1/1 white and black\n    Inkling creature token with flying. Then if an opponent controls more\n    creatures than you, this creature becomes prepared.\"\n  - The token is created BEFORE the \"more creatures than you\" comparison, so it\n    affects the count.\n- Inset prepare spell — **Swords to Plowshares**: `{W}` Instant —\n  \"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.\"\n- \"While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so unprepares it.\"\n  (CR 722.3c — grep RULEBOOK.txt for rule 722 if unsure.)\n\n## Required, concretely-named API (so the Tester's probes resolve to hard tests)\nImplement ALL of the following on the card class (names are mandated — the\npre-written tests probe for these exact shapes):\n\n1. **`prepared` designation**: expose a boolean attribute `self.prepared`\n   (default `False`). Also accept `is_prepared` as an alias/property if cheap.\n   Set `prepared = True` during ETB resolution only when an opponent controls\n   strictly more creatures than the controller (after the token is created).\n\n2. **`make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory**: return a castable Swords to\n   Plowshares spell object (an `Instant` subclass instance) whose resolution\n   exiles its chosen target creature and gives THAT creature's controller life\n   equal to the exiled creature's power. Use `chosen_targets` for the target.\n   No-target resolution must be a safe no-op (no raise, no life change). This is\n   the canonical name — the Tester probes `make_prepare_spell` first.\n\n3. **Cast-while-prepared + unprepare**: expose a method (e.g.\n   `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, ...)`) that:\n   - requires `self.prepared is True` (raise or return falsy if not prepared),\n   - casts/resolves a copy of the prepare spell (Swords to Plowshares),\n   - sets `self.prepared = False` afterward (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n   Per the reminder text the copy is cast \"without paying its mana cost\" — model\n   it as a free cast (mirror the cast_spell_free pattern if convenient).\n\n## Implementation expectations\n- Front-face static data, ETB token creation (1/1 W+B flying Inkling for the\n  TARGET player, `is_token` set), and the becomes-prepared comparison are already\n  covered by `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` — make those pass.\n- Add only additive engine support if needed (e.g. a token-creation helper or a\n  prepared-designation field). Prefer existing helpers used by FDN reference\n  cards for token creation and free casting.\n\nAfter you finish, the coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to extend the\ntest file (hardening the skip-guarded Swords-to-Plowshares tests and adding an\nunprepare-on-cast test) against the API above. Then you'll get a final green\npass. Keep the API stable.\n","userModified":false}}
