{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01LZtSP492ajJzk7puc7X9pH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014XeaoWYfsVtkKELfbWWq5K","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Extend & fix tests for sos_13","subagent_type":"Tester","prompt":"You are extending and correcting your existing pytest tests for one MTG card. The implementation now exposes a concrete API, and the coordinator has identified one buggy board state to fix.\n\nCARD: sos_13 (Emeritus of Truce // Swords to Plowshares — a CR 722 \"preparation card\")\n- Spec: `cards/sos/sos_13/card_spec.json`\n- Test file you OWN and will edit: `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`\n- Implementation already in place: `cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py` (read it to see the exposed API).\n- **REQUIRED READING: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/coordinator-directives.md`** — it specifies (A) a counting-model correction for one existing test and (B) coverage to add. Follow it exactly.\n\nEXPOSED API (stable; assert against these names):\n- `prepared: bool` (+ `is_prepared` alias)\n- `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` → castable Swords to Plowshares instance (resolves via `chosen_targets`: exile target creature, its controller gains life equal to its power; no-target = safe no-op)\n- `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)` → requires `prepared` is True (raises ValueError otherwise), free-casts a copy, then sets `prepared = False`.\n\nTASKS:\n1. **Fix the counting bug** in `TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared::test_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures`: under STANDARD MTG counting the entering Emeritus counts toward \"you\", and the Inkling token counts for whoever controls it. The current board (opp=2, token→controller) is 2-vs-2 = NOT prepared, contradicting the assertion. Adjust ONLY that test's board so the \"prepared\" case is genuinely \"opponent strictly more than you\" under standard counting (e.g. target the token to the OPPONENT, or give the opponent 3 creatures). Preserve the test's intent and the token-created-before-check ordering. Do not weaken the other three becomes-prepared tests (they already pass under standard counting).\n2. **Harden the skip-guarded Swords-to-Plowshares tests**: they now run because `make_prepare_spell` exists; ensure they assert exile + victim-controller lifegain as hard (non-skipped) tests.\n3. **Add an unprepare-on-cast test**: set `prepared = True`, put a target creature on the battlefield, call `cast_prepare_spell(game, target=...)`, then assert (a) the target was exiled and its controller gained life equal to power, and (b) `card.prepared is False` afterward. Also assert that calling `cast_prepare_spell` when NOT prepared is rejected (raises).\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Edit ONLY `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py`. Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n- Tests must reflect STANDARD MTG rules (entering creature counts toward you).\n- Read `test_utils.py`/`test_utils.md` and existing FDN test conventions as needed.\n\nVERIFY: run `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py -q`. With standard counting the implementation currently SUBTRACTS the entering creature (it will be fixed in a follow-up Implementer pass), so the becomes-prepared tests may not all pass yet — that's expected. The key requirement: your tests must be CORRECT under standard counting and the new prepare-spell API. Confirm the new/hardened prepare-spell tests pass (the API supports them).\n\nOUTPUT (into $CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13`):\n- Update `cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py` in place.\n- Update `test-rationale.md` (note the counting correction and new tests).\n- Ensure `test-files.txt` still lists the test file path(s).\n- Remove or empty `untestable.json` if everything is now testable.\n\nReturn ONLY a short status summary: total test_cases now, which tests you fixed/added, and untestable_count (0 if none)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1313,"cache_read_input_tokens":78323,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1313},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"71d8be8e-2d44-4e7d-ac64-5d4c52c95ed8","request_id":"req_011CbdU6nwtuT6FQioNtzcTU"}
