{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a71e7fc7ce363eef3","tool_use_id":"toolu_014XeaoWYfsVtkKELfbWWq5K","description":"Editing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Tester","usage":{"total_tokens":46532,"tool_uses":21,"duration_ms":103879},"last_tool_name":"Edit","uuid":"797d2097-9851-4822-b4d0-059edeb24b31","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019tM3CPNHxGxAwuv3s19yk2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M42MehtAGvs9pueRfFWJQe","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_13/test-rationale.md","old_string":"### `TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared` — second ETB clause\nValidates *\"Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature\nbecomes prepared.\"* The comparison is over creatures on the battlefield, and the\ntoken (clause 1) is created **before** the comparison, so it can affect counts.\n- `test_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures` — opponent has strictly more\n  creatures → prepared.\n- `test_not_prepared_when_counts_equal` — equal counts → NOT prepared (strict\n  \"more than\"); also asserts the token was still created so the negative case\n  cannot be satisfied by a no-op implementation.\n- `test_not_prepared_when_controller_has_more` — controller has more → NOT\n  prepared; likewise guards against a no-op.\n- `test_token_under_opponent_can_flip_the_comparison` — directing the token to\n  the opponent (created before the check) tips the opponent into \"more\n  creatures\", making the creature prepared. Verifies ordering of the two\n  clauses.\n\n### `TestSwordsToPlowshares` — the prepare spell (partial / skip-guarded)\nValidates *\"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its\npower.\"* These tests probe for a prepare-spell construction surface\n(`make_prepare_spell` / `get_prepare_spell` / `prepare_spell` / `create_copy`)\nand `pytest.skip` if none is exposed, because the engine mandates no specific\nAPI for the inset spell.\n- `test_exiles_target_creature` — the targeted creature leaves the battlefield\n  and lands in its owner's exile zone.\n- `test_controller_gains_life_equal_to_power` — the exiled creature's\n  *controller* (not the caster) gains life equal to the creature's power.\n- `test_caster_does_not_gain_life_for_opponents_creature` — exiling an\n  opponent's creature gives the caster no life (the controller does).\n- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — resolving with no chosen target must not raise or\n  change life.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n- **Casting a copy of the prepare spell from exile / \"doing so unprepares it\"**\n  (CR 722.3c): requires a preparation-card / cast-copy-from-exile pipeline that\n  the engine does not provide. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **The full alternative-characteristics copy semantics** (CR 722.3c, that the\n  exiled copy has only the prepare spell's characteristics): no engine surface\n  to construct/inspect the exile copy. Recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **Sorcery-speed/timing legality of the ETB token target** — that's engine","new_string":"### `TestEmeritusBecomesPrepared` — second ETB clause\nValidates *\"Then if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature\nbecomes prepared.\"* The comparison is over creatures on the battlefield, and the\ntoken (clause 1) is created **before** the comparison, so it can affect counts.\n\n**STANDARD MTG counting (round-2 correction).** The entering Emeritus is on the\nbattlefield when its own ETB resolves, so it **counts toward \"you\"** (the\ncontroller); it is NOT subtracted. Tokens count for whoever controls them, and\n\"more than\" is strict `>`.\n- `test_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures` — **counting bug fixed.** The\n  previous board (opp = 2 bears, token to controller) was you = Emeritus + token\n  = 2 vs opp = 2 → NOT more → the old `prepared is True` assertion was wrong\n  under standard counting. The board now gives the opponent **3 bears** with the\n  token still directed to the **controller**, so you = Emeritus + token = 2 vs\n  opp = 3 → 3 > 2 → prepared. The test still asserts the token was created\n  before the check (preserving clause ordering and the original \"opp-more →\n  prepared\" intent).\n- `test_not_prepared_when_counts_equal` — token to self, you = Emeritus + token\n  = 2 vs opp = 1 → NOT more → NOT prepared (strict \"more than\"); also asserts the\n  token was still created so the negative case cannot be satisfied by a no-op.\n- `test_not_prepared_when_controller_has_more` — controller has more → NOT\n  prepared; likewise guards against a no-op.\n- `test_token_under_opponent_can_flip_the_comparison` — directing the token to\n  the opponent (created before the check) tips the opponent into \"more\n  creatures\" (you = Emeritus = 1 vs opp = bear + token = 2), making the creature\n  prepared. Verifies ordering of the two clauses.\n\n### `TestSwordsToPlowshares` — the prepare spell (now a HARD contract)\nValidates *\"Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its\npower.\"* The card now exposes a stable `make_prepare_spell(game)` factory, so\nthese tests are **no longer skip-guarded**: the helper hard-asserts that the\nfactory exists, is callable, and returns a spell object.\n- `test_exiles_target_creature` — the targeted creature leaves the battlefield\n  and lands in its owner's exile zone.\n- `test_controller_gains_life_equal_to_power` — the exiled creature's\n  *controller* (not the caster) gains life equal to the creature's power.\n- `test_caster_does_not_gain_life_for_opponents_creature` — exiling an\n  opponent's creature gives the caster no life (the controller does).\n- `test_no_target_is_a_noop` — resolving with no chosen target must not raise or\n  change life.\n\n### `TestCastPrepareSpellUnprepares` — cast-while-prepared transition (CR 722.3c)\nValidates *\"While it's prepared, you may cast a copy of its spell. Doing so\nunprepares it.\"* via the stable `cast_prepare_spell(game, target=...)` API.\n- `test_cast_while_prepared_exiles_grants_life_and_unprepares` — with\n  `prepared = True`, casting the prepare spell against a battlefield creature\n  exiles it, grants that creature's controller life equal to its power, and\n  then clears the prepared designation (`card.prepared is False`).\n- `test_cast_when_not_prepared_is_rejected` — calling `cast_prepare_spell` when\n  the creature is NOT prepared raises `ValueError`, and the rejected attempt\n  leaves the would-be victim on the battlefield with life unchanged.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n- **The full alternative-characteristics copy semantics** (CR 722.3c, that the\n  exiled copy has only the prepare spell's characteristics): no engine surface\n  to construct/inspect a card-in-exile copy with split-card characteristics.\n  The card-local `make_prepare_spell` / `cast_prepare_spell` model is asserted\n  for its observable effects (exile + lifegain + unprepare) instead.\n- **Sorcery-speed/timing legality of the ETB token target** — that's engine"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":323,"cache_read_input_tokens":45831,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":323,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014XeaoWYfsVtkKELfbWWq5K","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"94aa28d1-e489-4a08-88ae-e8b6a7f860e1","request_id":"req_011CbdUDLtBhD44EHworsmTa","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend & fix tests for sos_13"}
