{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GrHvYQfneB6nGkFp83ppHB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_13 — final pass rationale (counting-model correction)\n2\t\n3\t## Change\n4\tCorrected the \"becomes prepared\" comparison in\n5\t`cards/sos/sos_13/card_impl.py::EmeritusOfTruceSwordsToPlowshares._opponent_controls_more_creatures`\n6\tto use **standard MTG counting** (per coordinator directives, section A).\n7\t\n8\tPreviously the method subtracted the entering Emeritus from the controller's\n9\tcreature total:\n10\t\n11\t```python\n12\tmy_count = self._creature_count(game, controller)\n13\tif game.get_battlefield(controller).contains(self):\n14\t    my_count -= 1\n15\t```\n16\t\n17\tThat extra subtraction was removed. The controller's count is now simply:\n18\t\n19\t```python\n20\tmy_count = self._creature_count(game, controller)\n21\t```\n22\t\n23\t## Why this is rules-correct\n24\tThe card's ETB resolves while Emeritus is already on the battlefield (CR 722.3a\n25\tis evaluated at resolution). Under standard MTG counting:\n26\t\n27\t- The entering **Emeritus counts toward \"you\"** (its controller) — no subtraction.\n28\t- The just-created **Inkling token counts for whoever controls it** (the\n29\t  targeted player). The token is still created *before* the comparison, so a\n30\t  token given to an opponent bumps that opponent's count and a token given to\n31\t  the controller bumps the controller's count.\n32\t- **\"More than\" is strict `>`** — equal counts do not prepare the creature.\n33\t\n34\tSo the predicate is now: some opponent's full creature count is strictly greater\n35\tthan the controller's full creature count (Emeritus + any controlled tokens\n36\tincluded).\n37\t\n38\t## API stability\n39\tNo public surface changed. The exposed names remain:\n40\t- `prepared: bool` (+ read-only `is_prepared` alias)\n41\t- `make_prepare_spell(self, game)`\n42\t- `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n43\t\n44\t## Engine impact\n45\tNone. The change is confined to one method body in the card file — no engine\n46\tfiles touched, no renames/moves/deletes.\n47\t\n48\t## Tests\n49\t- `pytest cards/sos/sos_13/tests.py -q` → **25 passed**.\n50\t- `pytest engine_tests/ -q` → **1145 passed** (no regressions).\n51\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018joPD2pbTUDWvHehg7gDJr","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"7edce674-81ca-4250-b045-68706d40b29d","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:18:43.527Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_13 implementation"}
