{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01RViKoiwPuZqnitrWouM9SZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016y8RhCLPkzCyX1WyRhrqFj","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)","new_string":"## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\nThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n\n## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\nThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\nstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\nidentity must be observable.\n\n## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":267,"cache_read_input_tokens":86731,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":267},"output_tokens":38,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"67c6a1a4-6b09-440f-ab3c-8c25830be8ac","request_id":"req_011CbdUXWep7hSAaoAwEAA8S"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016y8RhCLPkzCyX1WyRhrqFj","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"78d2ba46-a0fb-4011-9aa2-4dfeb6381a55","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:20:07.049Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)","newString":"## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\nThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n\n## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\nThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\nstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\nidentity must be observable.\n\n## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)","originalFile":"# Key Decisions\n\nPersistent conventions and decisions across runs. Append-only.\n\n## Engine: \"exile instead of graveyard\" for free-cast spells (sos_1)\nFor a non-permanent spell with \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\nexile it instead\": set `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell\nobject before casting it. `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` honors this opt-in\nflag and routes the resolving instant/sorcery from the stack to `Zone.EXILE`\ninstead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, then clears the flag (one-shot). Additive and\nbackward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /\nimpulse effects with the same rider.\n\n## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)\nOverride `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine\nclamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in\n`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so no manual\nclamping is needed. The hook may read `self.controller` (engine sets it before\nquerying).\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":6,"newStart":11,"newLines":27,"lines":[" backward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /"," impulse effects with the same rider."," ","+## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)","+The engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card","+(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:","+- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same","+  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.","+- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`","+  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a","+  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`","+  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a","+  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`","+  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).","+- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG","+  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,","+  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is","+  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.","+","+## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)","+The engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter","+strings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color","+identity must be observable.","+"," ## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)"," Override `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine"," clamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
