{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KbQKEs4DKokeRpgQ59272c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent conventions and decisions across runs. Append-only.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: \"exile instead of graveyard\" for free-cast spells (sos_1)\n6\tFor a non-permanent spell with \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\n7\texile it instead\": set `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell\n8\tobject before casting it. `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` honors this opt-in\n9\tflag and routes the resolving instant/sorcery from the stack to `Zone.EXILE`\n10\tinstead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, then clears the flag (one-shot). Additive and\n11\tbackward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /\n12\timpulse effects with the same rider.\n13\t\n14\t## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\n15\tThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n16\t(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n17\t- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n18\t  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n19\t- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n20\t  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n21\t  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n22\t  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n23\t  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n24\t  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n25\t- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n26\t  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n27\t  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n28\t  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n29\t\n30\t## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\n31\tThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\n32\tstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\n33\tidentity must be observable.\n34\t\n35\t## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)\n36\tOverride `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine\n37\tclamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in\n38\t`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so no manual\n39\tclamping is needed. The hook may read `self.controller` (engine sets it before\n40\tquerying).\n41\t\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qrf5JZhvK5T5bxqEcxyS5K","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"5b7c22e8-b6de-4daf-9496-092b1e3b0b27","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:20:25.708Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_57"}
