{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GDatUkYTmf4Z1P11UPnYZN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_57 (Mana Sculpt)\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant. \"Counter target spell. If you\n4\tcontrol a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast\n5\tthat spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n6\t\n7\tThe Tester flagged two requirements as needing new engine surface. You are\n8\texpected to build BOTH additively (no rename/move/delete of existing engine\n9\tsymbols), and pass full engine regression (`pytest engine_tests/ -q`).\n10\t\n11\t## Item 2 — total mana spent tracking (needed for the {C} amount)\n12\tAdd additive tracking of the TOTAL amount of mana spent to cast a spell, set\n13\tduring `engine/casting.py` payment, analogous to the existing `colors_spent` /\n14\t`last_payment_colors`. Suggested: set `card.mana_spent = <int>` on the spell\n15\twhen it is cast (the converted amount actually paid, after cost reduction). Mana\n16\tSculpt reads this off the COUNTERED spell to compute the deferred {C} amount.\n17\tThe pre-written tests already read back the recorded pending amount, so this\n18\tgoes green once the field + card logic exist.\n19\t\n20\t## Item 1 — deferred {C} at the beginning of your next main phase\n21\tThe engine has no \"beginning of main phase\" event and no delayed/one-shot\n22\tdeferred-effect mechanism. Add them additively:\n23\t1. A new triggered event, e.g. `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, in\n24\t   `engine/events.py`, carrying at least the active player / controller and a\n25\t   phase indicator (precombat main). Fire it from `engine/turn.py` when entering\n26\t   the precombat main phase. Keep existing turn behavior intact (mana pools may\n27\t   still empty at step transitions — {C} added at the START of the main phase\n28\t   persists through that phase, which is correct).\n29\t2. A delayed/one-shot deferred-effect mechanism so an effect can schedule \"do X\n30\t   at the controller's next precombat main phase, once\". Simplest robust design:\n31\t   a per-game (or per-player) list of pending one-shot callbacks keyed to the\n32\t   controller, consumed (and removed) when that controller's\n33\t   BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent fires. Use existing trigger infrastructure\n34\t   if it fits; otherwise add a small additive registry. Document the exact\n35\t   surface in your rationale.\n36\t3. On resolution, Mana Sculpt: (a) always counters the target spell (→ owner's\n37\t   graveyard, never resolves); (b) if the controller controls a creature with\n38\t   the `Wizard` subtype, schedule a one-shot that adds `mana_spent` worth of {C}\n39\t   (colorless) to the controller's mana pool at the controller's next precombat\n40\t   main phase. It must NOT add the {C} immediately at resolution.\n41\t\n42\t## After you finish\n43\tThe coordinator will re-invoke the Tester ONCE to add a DETERMINISTIC delivery\n44\ttest that fires `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` directly via\n45\t`game.trigger_manager` (mirroring how existing tests fire ETB events) and\n46\tasserts the controller's {C} pool gains exactly `mana_spent` once. So:\n47\t- Make the new event + delivery mechanism observable/firable from a test the\n48\t  same way ETB events are (via `trigger_manager.fire_event`).\n49\t- Document in `impl-rationale.md` the EXACT event class name, its constructor\n50\t  args, and how a test should fire it and read the resulting {C} pool, so the\n51\t  Tester can write against a stable surface.\n52\t\n53\tMake the existing 21 tests pass too (targeting, counter, wizard gate, pending\n54\tamount, not-immediate). Do NOT modify any test file, `engine_tests/`, or\n55\t`cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JTbhNLSWJjXmqSfa6WnMu3","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"12ff302f-3378-4494-8952-c8e1df03475a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:27:04.403Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_57 with delayed-trigger engine support"}
