{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011xihJNpBv489b7K9dVLqYX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PROJECT_MAP.md — Directory Layout\n2\t\n3\t```\n4\tAGENTS.md          — Workspace orientation and rules\n5\tPROJECT_MAP.md     — This file; directory summary\n6\tRULEBOOK.txt       — The entire MTG comprehensive rules. Grep — do not read whole.\n7\tprompt.md          — Per-run task prompt (written at stage time)\n8\trun_manifest.json  — Per-run manifest written by the harness: `{timeout_seconds, deadline_utc}`. Harness-owned — do not edit.\n9\tpytest.ini         — Pytest configuration for the workspace\n10\tconftest.py        — Pytest fixtures shared across the workspace\n11\ttest_utils.py      — Shared test helpers (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, …)\n12\ttest_utils.md      — API reference for `test_utils.py`\n13\t.gitignore         — Git ignore rules\n14\tengine/            — Canonical game engine source. Imported as `engine`.\n15\tengine_tests/      — Engine regression tests (do not modify).\n16\tcards/             — Card implementations.\n17\t  cards/fdn/       — Completed FDN reference cards (do not modify their tests).\n18\t  cards/sos/       — SOS card stubs to implement.\n19\tskills/            — Workspace-local skills (e.g. `grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n20\t```\n21\t\n22\t## Card paths\n23\t\n24\tFor an SOS card with collector number `N`:\n25\t\n26\t```\n27\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/card_spec.json   — card metadata (name, mana_cost, oracle_text, P/T, keywords, …)\n28\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py     — implementation stub you complete\n29\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py         — your tests for this card (you create this)\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\tFor an FDN reference card:\n33\t\n34\t```\n35\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/card_spec.json   — card metadata\n36\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/card_impl.py     — completed reference implementation (read for examples)\n37\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/tests.py         — only present for the cards listed below; read as test examples\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t### FDN cards that ship with a `tests.py`\n41\t\n42\tThis is the canonical list — agent prompts refer back here instead of duplicating it.\n43\tDiscover the current set at any time with:\n44\t\n45\t```bash\n46\tfind cards/fdn -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -name tests.py -printf '%h\\n' | sort -V\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tAs of the latest workspace stage, the list is: `fdn_13`, `fdn_142`, `fdn_205`, `fdn_215`, `fdn_244`. If you suspect the list has grown, re-run the `find` command above — it is authoritative.\n50\t\n51\t## Imports\n52\t\n53\tThe workspace root is on `sys.path`, so use bare package imports:\n54\t\n55\t```python\n56\tfrom cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl import TheDawningArchaic\n57\tfrom engine.card import CardImpl, Creature, Instant\n58\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone\n59\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n60\t```\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JTbhNLSWJjXmqSfa6WnMu3","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"20345572-07c6-44c1-a281-56682d3ff4e5","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:27:05.299Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_57 with delayed-trigger engine support"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Lztinh8HVWtEggWJxuTCD","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent conventions and decisions across runs. Append-only.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: \"exile instead of graveyard\" for free-cast spells (sos_1)\n6\tFor a non-permanent spell with \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\n7\texile it instead\": set `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell\n8\tobject before casting it. `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` honors this opt-in\n9\tflag and routes the resolving instant/sorcery from the stack to `Zone.EXILE`\n10\tinstead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, then clears the flag (one-shot). Additive and\n11\tbackward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /\n12\timpulse effects with the same rider.\n13\t\n14\t## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\n15\tThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n16\t(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n17\t- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n18\t  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n19\t- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n20\t  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n21\t  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n22\t  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n23\t  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n24\t  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n25\t- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n26\t  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n27\t  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n28\t  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n29\t\n30\t## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\n31\tThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\n32\tstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\n33\tidentity must be observable.\n34\t\n35\t## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)\n36\tOverride `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine\n37\tclamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in\n38\t`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so no manual\n39\tclamping is needed. The hook may read `self.controller` (engine sets it before\n40\tquerying).\n41\t\n42\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01JTbhNLSWJjXmqSfa6WnMu3","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"d75da8a8-b1b2-40eb-940c-7585abb52884","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:27:05.300Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_57 with delayed-trigger engine support"}
