{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CEDducuJV52nQ9GueY5txJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_57 — Mana Sculpt implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant. \"Counter target spell. If you\n4\tcontrol a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast\n5\tthat spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n6\t\n7\tAll 21 pre-written card tests pass; full engine regression (`engine_tests/`,\n8\t1145 tests) still passes. No test files were modified.\n9\t\n10\t## Exact engine surface added (stable contract for the Tester)\n11\t\n12\t### 1. Total mana-spent tracking — `card.mana_spent: int`\n13\t- Set in `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` immediately after payment:\n14\t  `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (the converted amount actually paid,\n15\t  i.e. AFTER cost reduction). Mirrors the existing `card.colors_spent` exactly.\n16\t- Cleared at the start of each cast (alongside `colors_spent`) so a reused card\n17\t  object never carries a stale value.\n18\t- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell_free` sets `card.mana_spent = 0` (free casts\n19\t  pay no mana).\n20\t- Additive / backward-compatible: the attribute is simply absent on objects that\n21\t  were never cast; readers use `getattr(card, \"mana_spent\", 0)`.\n22\t\n23\t### 2. Beginning-of-main-phase event — `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n24\tDefined in `engine/events.py` (a `TriggeredEvent` subclass / dataclass):\n25\t\n26\t```python\n27\tBeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(\n28\t    player=<Player>,        # active player whose main phase begins\n29\t    controller=<Player>,    # alias of player (matches other events' naming)\n30\t    precombat=<bool>,       # True = precombat main, False = postcombat main\n31\t)\n32\t```\n33\t\n34\tAll three fields default to `None`/`True`, so it can be constructed with no\n35\targs. It is fired from `engine/turn.py::run_turn` when entering the\n36\t`PRECOMBAT_MAIN` (precombat=True) and `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN` (precombat=False) phases,\n37\tvia `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(...)`.\n38\t\n39\t**How a test fires it and reads the {C} pool (deterministic delivery):**\n40\t```python\n41\tfrom engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\n42\tfrom engine.types import ManaType\n43\tgame.active_player_index = game.players.index(controller)   # optional\n44\tgame.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n45\t    game,\n46\t    BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller, controller=controller, precombat=True),\n47\t)\n48\tassert controller.mana_pool.get(ManaType.COLORLESS) == expected   # gains mana_spent once\n49\t```\n50\tFiring it again is a no-op (the scheduled effect is one-shot and removed on\n51\tdelivery), so the pool does not grow on a second fire.\n52\t\n53\t### 3. Delayed / one-shot deferred-effect mechanism\n54\t- `GameState.main_phase_deferred_effects: list[dict]` — a per-game registry.\n55\t- `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(controller, callback, *, precombat=True)`\n56\t  — appends a one-shot entry `{controller, callback, precombat}`. `callback`\n57\t  takes the game state.\n58\t- `engine/deferred.py::deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects(game, event)` — runs\n59\t  and removes every entry whose `controller` matches the event's\n60\t  controller/player (and, if the entry requested `precombat`, only when the\n61\t  event is precombat). It rewrites the registry to the surviving entries first,\n62\t  then invokes the matched callbacks (so callbacks may schedule new effects\n63\t  safely).\n64\t- Wired into `engine/triggers.py::TriggerManager.fire_event`: when the fired\n65\t  event is a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, delivery runs **synchronously\n66\t  inside `fire_event`** (not via the stack). This is why simply firing the event\n67\t  makes the {C} observable immediately, matching the Tester's ETB-direct-fire\n68\t  pattern. Existing trigger behaviour is untouched for every other event type.\n69\t\n70\t## Card implementation (`cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`)\n71\t`ManaSculpt(Instant)` — modelled on the FDN counter cards (`fdn_48` Refute,\n72\t`fdn_160` An Offer You Can't Refuse):\n73\t- `can_cast`: true only when a non-self spell is on the stack.\n74\t- `get_targets`: one `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK)` whose `filter_fn`\n75\t  accepts any spell (creature OR noncreature — `card_types - {LAND}` non-empty)\n76\t  and rejects self (handed either the raw card or its wrapping `StackObject`).\n77\t- `on_resolve`:\n78\t  1. Read the countered spell's `mana_spent` BEFORE countering (the spell leaves\n79\t     the stack during the counter).\n80\t  2. Counter unconditionally (remove the `StackObject`, route the card to its\n81\t     owner's graveyard — local `_counter_spell` helper).\n82\t  3. Wizard gate: `_controls_wizard` checks the controller's battlefield for a\n83\t     creature whose `subtypes` contains `\"Wizard\"`. If absent, set\n84\t     `pending_colorless = 0` and stop — no {C} scheduled.\n85\t  4. With a Wizard, set `self.pending_colorless = mana_spent` (the amount the\n86\t     tests read back) and schedule a one-shot via\n87\t     `game.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(controller, _reimburse, precombat=True)`\n88\t     that adds `mana_spent` {C} to the controller's pool. **Nothing is added to\n89\t     the pool at resolution time** — strictly deferred.\n90\t- Exposes `self.pending_colorless: int` (default 0). The Tester's\n91\t  `_read_pending_colorless` accepts this attribute name.\n92\t- Sets `self.colors = [\"U\"]` per the established explicit-colors convention\n93\t  (KEY_DECISIONS sos_13).\n94\t\n95\t## Design decisions / notes\n96\t- **`mana_spent == effective_cost.cmc`** rather than counting individual pips\n97\t  drained from the pool: this is \"the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\"\n98\t  (CR 118-style mana value of the actual payment, after reduction) and matches\n99\t  both test expectations ({1}{R} from a 3-red pool → 2; {3}{G}{G} from 5 green →\n100\t  5). It deliberately ignores extra mana floating in the pool that wasn't spent.\n101\t- **Synchronous delivery inside `fire_event`** (vs pushing a stack object): the\n102\t  directive's deterministic delivery test fires the event and asserts the pool\n103\t  immediately, without resolving the stack. A delayed trigger that merely pushed\n104\t  a StackObject would require an extra resolve step and wouldn't match that\n105\t  contract. Synchronous delivery is additive and confined to the new event type.\n106\t- **Precombat gating**: the rider says \"your next main phase\"; real MTG delayed\n107\t  triggers of this form fire on the next main phase (precombat). The scheduler\n108\t  defaults `precombat=True` so it fires on the controller's precombat main and\n109\t  the postcombat event is ignored. The {C} added at the start of that phase\n110\t  persists through it (pools only empty on step transitions), which is correct.\n111\t- **No spec deviation.** Behaviour matches the oracle text. The only modelling\n112\t  choice is the deferred-delivery surface, which is what the coordinator\n113\t  mandated.\n114\t\n115\t## Reusable conventions for future cards\n116\t- `card.mana_spent` is now available alongside `card.colors_spent` for any\n117\t  \"mana spent to cast\" mechanic.\n118\t- `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(controller, callback, *, precombat=...)`\n119\t  + `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` are the general mechanism for \"at the\n120\t  beginning of your next main phase, do X (once)\" riders.\n121\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"f7d02764-243f-4f87-9500-d640ae871e0a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:31:47.030Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-rationale.md","content":"# sos_57 — Mana Sculpt implementation rationale\n\nCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant. \"Counter target spell. If you\ncontrol a Wizard, add an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast\nthat spell at the beginning of your next main phase.\"\n\nAll 21 pre-written card tests pass; full engine regression (`engine_tests/`,\n1145 tests) still passes. No test files were modified.\n\n## Exact engine surface added (stable contract for the Tester)\n\n### 1. Total mana-spent tracking — `card.mana_spent: int`\n- Set in `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` immediately after payment:\n  `card.mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` (the converted amount actually paid,\n  i.e. AFTER cost reduction). Mirrors the existing `card.colors_spent` exactly.\n- Cleared at the start of each cast (alongside `colors_spent`) so a reused card\n  object never carries a stale value.\n- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell_free` sets `card.mana_spent = 0` (free casts\n  pay no mana).\n- Additive / backward-compatible: the attribute is simply absent on objects that\n  were never cast; readers use `getattr(card, \"mana_spent\", 0)`.\n\n### 2. Beginning-of-main-phase event — `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\nDefined in `engine/events.py` (a `TriggeredEvent` subclass / dataclass):\n\n```python\nBeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(\n    player=<Player>,        # active player whose main phase begins\n    controller=<Player>,    # alias of player (matches other events' naming)\n    precombat=<bool>,       # True = precombat main, False = postcombat main\n)\n```\n\nAll three fields default to `None`/`True`, so it can be constructed with no\nargs. It is fired from `engine/turn.py::run_turn` when entering the\n`PRECOMBAT_MAIN` (precombat=True) and `POSTCOMBAT_MAIN` (precombat=False) phases,\nvia `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(...)`.\n\n**How a test fires it and reads the {C} pool (deterministic delivery):**\n```python\nfrom engine.events import BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent\nfrom engine.types import ManaType\ngame.active_player_index = game.players.index(controller)   # optional\ngame.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n    game,\n    BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=controller, controller=controller, precombat=True),\n)\nassert controller.mana_pool.get(ManaType.COLORLESS) == expected   # gains mana_spent once\n```\nFiring it again is a no-op (the scheduled effect is one-shot and removed on\ndelivery), so the pool does not grow on a second fire.\n\n### 3. Delayed / one-shot deferred-effect mechanism\n- `GameState.main_phase_deferred_effects: list[dict]` — a per-game registry.\n- `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(controller, callback, *, precombat=True)`\n  — appends a one-shot entry `{controller, callback, precombat}`. `callback`\n  takes the game state.\n- `engine/deferred.py::deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects(game, event)` — runs\n  and removes every entry whose `controller` matches the event's\n  controller/player (and, if the entry requested `precombat`, only when the\n  event is precombat). It rewrites the registry to the surviving entries first,\n  then invokes the matched callbacks (so callbacks may schedule new effects\n  safely).\n- Wired into `engine/triggers.py::TriggerManager.fire_event`: when the fired\n  event is a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, delivery runs **synchronously\n  inside `fire_event`** (not via the stack). This is why simply firing the event\n  makes the {C} observable immediately, matching the Tester's ETB-direct-fire\n  pattern. Existing trigger behaviour is untouched for every other event type.\n\n## Card implementation (`cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`)\n`ManaSculpt(Instant)` — modelled on the FDN counter cards (`fdn_48` Refute,\n`fdn_160` An Offer You Can't Refuse):\n- `can_cast`: true only when a non-self spell is on the stack.\n- `get_targets`: one `TargetRequirement(zone=Zone.STACK)` whose `filter_fn`\n  accepts any spell (creature OR noncreature — `card_types - {LAND}` non-empty)\n  and rejects self (handed either the raw card or its wrapping `StackObject`).\n- `on_resolve`:\n  1. Read the countered spell's `mana_spent` BEFORE countering (the spell leaves\n     the stack during the counter).\n  2. Counter unconditionally (remove the `StackObject`, route the card to its\n     owner's graveyard — local `_counter_spell` helper).\n  3. Wizard gate: `_controls_wizard` checks the controller's battlefield for a\n     creature whose `subtypes` contains `\"Wizard\"`. If absent, set\n     `pending_colorless = 0` and stop — no {C} scheduled.\n  4. With a Wizard, set `self.pending_colorless = mana_spent` (the amount the\n     tests read back) and schedule a one-shot via\n     `game.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(controller, _reimburse, precombat=True)`\n     that adds `mana_spent` {C} to the controller's pool. **Nothing is added to\n     the pool at resolution time** — strictly deferred.\n- Exposes `self.pending_colorless: int` (default 0). The Tester's\n  `_read_pending_colorless` accepts this attribute name.\n- Sets `self.colors = [\"U\"]` per the established explicit-colors convention\n  (KEY_DECISIONS sos_13).\n\n## Design decisions / notes\n- **`mana_spent == effective_cost.cmc`** rather than counting individual pips\n  drained from the pool: this is \"the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\"\n  (CR 118-style mana value of the actual payment, after reduction) and matches\n  both test expectations ({1}{R} from a 3-red pool → 2; {3}{G}{G} from 5 green →\n  5). It deliberately ignores extra mana floating in the pool that wasn't spent.\n- **Synchronous delivery inside `fire_event`** (vs pushing a stack object): the\n  directive's deterministic delivery test fires the event and asserts the pool\n  immediately, without resolving the stack. A delayed trigger that merely pushed\n  a StackObject would require an extra resolve step and wouldn't match that\n  contract. Synchronous delivery is additive and confined to the new event type.\n- **Precombat gating**: the rider says \"your next main phase\"; real MTG delayed\n  triggers of this form fire on the next main phase (precombat). The scheduler\n  defaults `precombat=True` so it fires on the controller's precombat main and\n  the postcombat event is ignored. The {C} added at the start of that phase\n  persists through it (pools only empty on step transitions), which is correct.\n- **No spec deviation.** Behaviour matches the oracle text. The only modelling\n  choice is the deferred-delivery surface, which is what the coordinator\n  mandated.\n\n## Reusable conventions for future cards\n- `card.mana_spent` is now available alongside `card.colors_spent` for any\n  \"mana spent to cast\" mechanic.\n- `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(controller, callback, *, precombat=...)`\n  + `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` are the general mechanism for \"at the\n  beginning of your next main phase, do X (once)\" riders.\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}}}
