e,\n/workspace/engine/turn.py-221-                BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(\n/workspace/engine/turn.py-222-                    player=game.active_player,\n--\n/workspace/engine/deferred.py-3-The engine schedules one-shot effects that should run \"at the beginning of a\n/workspace/engine/deferred.py-4-player's next (precombat) main phase\" on\nengine/deferred.py-5-:attr:`GameState.main_phase_deferred_effects` via\nengine/deferred.py:6::meth:`GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect`.\n/workspace/engine/deferred.py-7-\n/workspace/engine/deferred.py-8-This module delivers those effects when the matching\nengine/deferred.py-9-:class:`~engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` fires.  Delivery is\nengine/deferred.py:10:invoked from :meth:`engine.triggers.TriggerManager.fire_event` so that firing\n/workspace/engine/deferred.py-11-the event (the way tests fire ETB events) runs the scheduled callbacks directly\n/workspace/engine/deferred.py-12-and removes them — they are one-shot.\n/workspace/engine/deferred.py-13-\"\"\"\n--\n/workspace/engine/triggers.py-54-    Triggers are registered when a permanent enters the battlefield (or\n/workspace/engine/triggers.py-55-    via other game actions) and unregistered when the source leaves.\n/workspace/engine/triggers.py-56-\nengine/triggers.py:57:    :meth:`fire_event` checks all registered triggers of a matching\n/workspace/engine/triggers.py-58-    event type, evaluates their conditions, and pushes matching triggers\nengine/triggers.py-59-    onto the game stack as :class:`StackObject` instances.  Triggers are\nengine/triggers.py-60-    ordered according to APNAP (Active Player, Non-Active Player):\n--\n/workspace/engine/triggers.py-78-        \"\"\"Remove all triggers registered by *source* (identity-based).\"\"\"\n/workspace/engine/triggers.py-79-        self._triggers = [t for t in self._triggers if t.source is not source]\n/workspace/engine/triggers.py-80-\nengine/triggers.py:81:    def fire_event(self, g