{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JrHCCCdYVb5pX9VipVvLaM","type":"tool_result","content":"total 60\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 node node  4096 Jun  2 00:31 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 node node  4096 Jun  2 00:20 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  3403 Jun  2 00:26 coordinator-directives.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node   139 Jun  2 00:31 impl-files.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  6825 Jun  2 00:31 impl-rationale.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node 16516 Jun  2 00:30 impl.diff\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node    37 Jun  2 00:25 test-files.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  5648 Jun  2 00:25 test-rationale.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  1912 Jun  2 00:25 untestable.json\n---FILES---\n/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py\n---UNTESTABLE---\n[\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"add an amount of {C} ... at the beginning of your next main phase\",\n    \"reason\": \"The engine has no native 'beginning of (your next) main phase' triggered event and no delayed-trigger / one-shot deferred-effect mechanism. Mana pools are also emptied at step transitions. There is no deterministic, implementation-agnostic way to drive the turn loop and observe the {C} actually appear in the pool at the controller's next main phase. The tests instead verify (a) the deferred amount the spell records and (b) that no {C} is added at resolution time.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock\": \"An engine-level delayed/one-shot trigger registered for a new 'beginning of main phase' event (e.g. a BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent fired by turn.py when entering PRECOMBAT_MAIN), plus a test helper to advance to the controller's next main phase and fire that event. Then a test could assert the controller's {C} pool gains the recorded amount exactly once at that phase.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"requirement\": \"an amount of {C} equal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell\",\n    \"reason\": \"The casting pipeline currently records only the distinct colors spent (mana_pool.last_payment_colors), not the total amount of mana spent on a spell. With no such surface the 'amount spent' cannot be read by Mana Sculpt yet. The amount tests assert the contract assuming the Implementer adds mana-spent tracking during payment, and so they correctly fail in the red phase.\",\n    \"what_would_unblock\": \"Additive engine tracking of the total mana spent to cast a spell (e.g. setting card.mana_spent during cast_spell payment, analogous to the existing colors_spent), which Mana Sculpt can then read from the countered spell to compute the deferred {C} amount. Tests are written to read this back via a plausible pending-amount attribute so they pass once both the engine field and the card are implemented.\"\n  }\n]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01T8WgoRHFrkSL8YETG73Xex","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"3bfd736b-ced6-47b8-add1-9bb1223b3d31","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:32:30.629Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Add delivery test for sos_57"}
