{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RMCFKMQhVaNVFiM32442Bn","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_57 Mana Sculpt\n2\t\n3\tCard: **Mana Sculpt** — `{1}{U}{U}` Instant.\n4\tOracle: *\"Counter target spell. If you control a Wizard, add an amount of {C}\n5\tequal to the amount of mana spent to cast that spell at the beginning of your\n6\tnext main phase.\"*\n7\t\n8\t## Mechanics decomposed\n9\t\n10\t1. **Counter target spell** — targets *any* spell on the stack (creature\n11\t   spells included, unlike \"counter target noncreature spell\"). On resolution\n12\t   the targeted spell is removed from the stack and put into its owner's\n13\t   graveyard; it never resolves.\n14\t2. **Wizard gate** — the deferred {C} benefit only happens if the controller\n15\t   controls a creature with the `Wizard` subtype at resolution. The counter\n16\t   itself is unconditional.\n17\t3. **Deferred {C}** — amount equals the mana actually spent to cast the\n18\t   countered spell (CR \"amount of mana spent to cast that spell\"), added at the\n19\t   beginning of the controller's *next* main phase (not immediately).\n20\t\n21\t## Test file\n22\t\n23\t`cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py`\n24\t\n25\t### TestManaSculptProperties — static data\n26\t- `test_name` — name is \"Mana Sculpt\".\n27\t- `test_is_instant` — is an `Instant` and has `CardType.INSTANT`.\n28\t- `test_mana_cost` — cost parses to `{1}{U}{U}`.\n29\t- `test_is_not_a_permanent_type` — guard: not a creature/land (resolves to\n30\t  graveyard, never battlefield). Passes on the empty stub but pins the contract\n31\t  once typed.\n32\t\n33\t### TestManaSculptTargeting — \"Counter target spell\"\n34\t- `test_get_targets_returns_one_requirement` — exactly one target requirement.\n35\t- `test_target_requirement_zone_is_stack` — legal targets live in `Zone.STACK`.\n36\t- `test_target_filter_accepts_creature_spell` — a creature spell IS a legal\n37\t  target (distinguishes Mana Sculpt from noncreature-only counters).\n38\t- `test_target_filter_accepts_noncreature_spell` — an instant is also legal.\n39\t- `test_target_filter_rejects_self` — a spell cannot counter itself; the filter\n40\t  rejects a stack object whose source is this Mana Sculpt (and the raw card).\n41\t- `test_cannot_cast_with_empty_stack` — no spell on the stack ⇒ no legal target\n42\t  ⇒ `can_cast` is False. (Discriminates against the base `can_cast=True`.)\n43\t- `test_can_cast_with_spell_on_stack` — a spell on the stack ⇒ `can_cast` True.\n44\t  Paired with the previous test to pin the can_cast contract; passes on the stub\n45\t  only because the base default is True, so it is meaningful only together with\n46\t  its negative twin.\n47\t\n48\t### TestManaSculptCounter — counter resolution\n49\t- `test_counters_instant_to_graveyard` — countered instant ends in its owner's\n50\t  graveyard and leaves the owner's stack zone.\n51\t- `test_countered_spell_removed_from_stack` — the StackObject is gone from the\n52\t  stack.\n53\t- `test_countered_creature_does_not_enter_battlefield` — a countered creature\n54\t  spell never reaches the battlefield (goes to graveyard).\n55\t- `test_counters_sorcery` — a sorcery is also countered to graveyard.\n56\t- `test_no_target_is_noop` — resolving with no chosen target does not raise\n57\t  (robustness; guards a fizzle/no-op path).\n58\t\n59\t### TestManaSculptWizardManaGate — Wizard gate + deferred {C}\n60\t- `test_no_wizard_no_mana_added_immediately` — without a Wizard, resolution does\n61\t  not add {C} to the controller's pool (benefit gated off) but still counters.\n62\t- `test_counter_happens_even_without_wizard` — counter is unconditional.\n63\t- `test_wizard_sets_up_deferred_mana` — with a Wizard, the spell records a\n64\t  pending {C} amount equal to the mana spent on the countered spell. The bolt\n65\t  costs `{1}{R}` (2 mana); paid from 3 red, exactly 2 mana is spent ⇒ pending\n66\t  amount 2. Read via a small set of plausible attribute names so the test\n67\t  asserts the recorded *amount* (behaviour) rather than a single private field.\n68\t- `test_deferred_amount_tracks_larger_spend` — a `{3}{G}{G}` spell (5 mana,\n69\t  paid from 5 green) ⇒ pending amount 5, proving the amount scales with mana\n70\t  spent.\n71\t- `test_mana_not_added_immediately_even_with_wizard` — even with a Wizard the\n72\t  {C} is NOT in the pool the instant Mana Sculpt resolves (it is deferred to the\n73\t  next main phase). Guards against an implementation that pays immediately.\n74\t\n75\t## Edge cases covered\n76\t- Creature vs. noncreature target legality (the defining trait vs. noncreature\n77\t  counters).\n78\t- Self-targeting rejection.\n79\t- Empty-stack / no-target fizzle and no-op resolution.\n80\t- Wizard present vs. absent gating, with the counter unconditional in both.\n81\t- \"Amount of mana spent\" == mana actually deducted (cost `{1}{R}` = 2, not the\n82\t  pool size of 3), and scaling to a larger spell.\n83\t- Deferred timing: not added at resolution.\n84\t\n85\t## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n86\t- **Exact delivery of the {C} at the beginning of the controller's next main\n87\t  phase.** The engine has no native \"beginning of (your next) main phase\"\n88\t  triggered event and no delayed-trigger / one-shot-deferred-effect mechanism;\n89\t  the priority/turn loop also resets mana pools at step transitions. Driving the\n90\t  full turn loop to observe the {C} appear is non-deterministic against an\n91\t  as-yet-unchosen implementation strategy. Recorded in `untestable.json`. The\n92\t  *amount* and the *not-immediate* properties are tested instead.\n93\t- **Engine-level \"amount of mana spent\" tracking is itself new surface.** The\n94\t  pipeline currently records only `last_payment_colors` (colors), not the total\n95\t  amount spent. The amount tests require the Implementer to add mana-spent\n96\t  tracking during payment; this is the intended TDD contract (red now, green\n97\t  after the additive engine change). Noted in `untestable.json` as a dependency.\n98\t- **Multiplayer / split-second / can't-be-countered interactions** — out of\n99\t  scope for this two-player engine and this card.\n100\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01T8WgoRHFrkSL8YETG73Xex","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"1edcf60c-f923-4899-96d6-c9d2fa2aa9b3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:33:14.057Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Add delivery test for sos_57"}
