{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EQccZ2EznC9sZnom5Pm7q7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LAgwRmGVTujdt84KhvtpAK","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/test-rationale.md","old_string":"- \"Amount of mana spent\" == mana actually deducted (cost `{1}{R}` = 2, not the\n  pool size of 3), and scaling to a larger spell.\n- Deferred timing: not added at resolution.\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n- **Exact delivery of the {C} at the beginning of the controller's next main\n  phase.** The engine has no native \"beginning of (your next) main phase\"\n  triggered event and no delayed-trigger / one-shot-deferred-effect mechanism;\n  the priority/turn loop also resets mana pools at step transitions. Driving the\n  full turn loop to observe the {C} appear is non-deterministic against an\n  as-yet-unchosen implementation strategy. Recorded in `untestable.json`. The\n  *amount* and the *not-immediate* properties are tested instead.\n- **Engine-level \"amount of mana spent\" tracking is itself new surface.** The\n  pipeline currently records only `last_payment_colors` (colors), not the total\n  amount spent. The amount tests require the Implementer to add mana-spent\n  tracking during payment; this is the intended TDD contract (red now, green\n  after the additive engine change). Noted in `untestable.json` as a dependency.\n- **Multiplayer / split-second / can't-be-countered interactions** — out of\n  scope for this two-player engine and this card.","new_string":"- \"Amount of mana spent\" == mana actually deducted (cost `{1}{R}` = 2, not the\n  pool size of 3), and scaling to a larger spell.\n- Deferred timing: not added at resolution.\n- **Deterministic delivery** at the beginning of the controller's next main\n  phase via `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, including amount equality with\n  `mana_spent`, scaling, one-shot consumption, and the no-Wizard no-op. (Both\n  formerly-untestable requirements are now covered — see\n  `TestManaSculptDeferredDelivery`; `untestable.json` is now empty.)\n\n## Edge cases deliberately NOT covered (and why)\n- **Mana-pool emptying across real phase transitions.** The delivery tests fire\n  the `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` directly (the engine's documented,\n  synchronous delivery path) rather than advancing the whole turn loop, so they\n  do not also re-verify the engine's pool-emptying behaviour at step\n  boundaries — that is engine-owned behaviour covered by `engine_tests/`.\n- **Multiplayer / split-second / can't-be-countered interactions** — out of\n  scope for this two-player engine and this card."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1044,"cache_read_input_tokens":44464,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1044,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":66,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01T8WgoRHFrkSL8YETG73Xex","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"5e470c37-6201-42e7-841e-ff3f455aa015","request_id":"req_011CbdVZBZH81MtSGHJFxKK4","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Add delivery test for sos_57"}
