{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_018SYvy4CdQ5wDQcinTdu1tN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Gqe6nmCSgzsoRzUUx67VM","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review sos_57 implementation","subagent_type":"Reviewer","prompt":"You are reviewing the implementation diff for a single MTG card plus its supporting engine changes.\n\nCARD: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt — {1}{U}{U} Instant)\n- Diff to review: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl.diff`\n- Implementer's rationale: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-rationale.md`\n- Spec: `cards/sos/sos_57/card_spec.json`\n- Prior-card conventions accepted this run: `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`\n- Persistent conventions: `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`\n\nCONTEXT the coordinator already mandated (do NOT re-litigate these design choices):\n- Add `card.mana_spent` (total mana paid after reduction), analogous to `colors_spent`.\n- Add `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (fired by turn.py on entering main phases) + a one-shot deferred-effect registry (`GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect`), with synchronous delivery inside `TriggerManager.fire_event` for that event type. This deferred-delivery surface is an approved coordinator decision.\n\nREVIEW FOR (within those decisions):\n- Correctness vs spec/MTG rules: counter is unconditional (target spell → owner's graveyard, never resolves); targets any spell incl. creature spells; rejects self; needs a spell on the stack. Wizard gate (creature with `Wizard` subtype under controller). Deferred {C} == countered spell's mana_spent, added at controller's NEXT precombat main, NOT immediately, one-shot.\n- REAL BUGS in the engine changes: does firing `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` synchronously inside fire_event risk re-entrancy, double-delivery, or wrong-controller delivery? Does the deferred registry leak or mis-key entries? Does turn.py firing the event change existing turn behavior or break mana-pool emptying? Is `mana_spent` cleared correctly so a reused card object never carries a stale value? Are all engine changes additive (no rename/move/delete of existing symbols)?\n- Missed edge cases and convention violations VISIBLE IN THE DIFF.\n\nIMPORTANT SCOPING:\n- Do NOT flag the approved design choices above (mana_spent, the new event, synchronous delivery, the deferred registry) as \"wrong approach\" — only flag genuine BUGS within them.\n- Do NOT flag patterns from earlier cards (FILES_MODIFIED.json) or KEY_DECISIONS.md.\n- Do NOT demand test rewrites — tests were arbitrated. Test-quality concerns are `advisory` only.\n\nOUTPUT:\n- Write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json` — JSON array of {\"severity\": \"strict\"|\"advisory\", \"file\": \"...\", \"line\": <n>, \"comment\": \"...\"}. `strict` only for must-fix correctness/bug/contract issues (especially engine regressions or delivery bugs). [] if none.\n\nReturn ONLY:\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2576,"cache_read_input_tokens":103727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2576},"output_tokens":36,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"9d1b3665-a710-4bca-929e-e4a7009598b2","request_id":"req_011CbdVbJou7Niu1paaSAnmQ"}
