{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011L3mEz1qxwu29fVfVXDhv7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 30,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"_is_spell() cannot distinguish a spell from an activated/triggered ability on the stack. In this engine, ability StackObjects reuse their source permanent's card_types (see engine/abilities.py:222-228 and engine/triggers.py:130: source=trigger.source / ability.source). So for an ability put on the stack by a creature, _stack_source().card_types is {CREATURE}, and `card_types - {LAND}` is non-empty -> _is_spell returns True. The intended guard `getattr(obj, 'is_spell', None) is False` is dead code: no StackObject in the engine ever sets an `is_spell` attribute (grep finds none). Result: ManaSculpt.can_cast() and get_targets() will treat abilities on the stack as legal 'spells', allowing Mana Sculpt to target/counter an ability, which violates 'Counter target spell'. Distinguish spells from abilities (e.g. only treat a StackObject as a spell when its source card currently resides in a STACK zone / is an actual cast spell, not an ability whose source is a battlefield permanent).\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 61,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"_counter_spell reaches into the private game.stack._items list to remove the target StackObject because Stack exposes no public 'remove arbitrary object' API (only push/pop/peek/objects). This works today but is brittle if Stack internals change. If a public removal helper is added to engine/stack.py later, prefer it. Not a bug given the current API surface.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"engine/casting.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 237,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc treats {X} as 0 (ManaCost.cmc ignores x_count, engine/types.py:164-169). For an X-spell, 'the amount of mana spent to cast that spell' should include the X payment, so the deferred {C} would under-count by X. Not exercised by the arbitrated tests and consistent with the coordinator-approved cmc-based mana_spent surface, but worth noting for future 'mana spent' consumers.\"\n19\t  },\n20\t  {\n21\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n22\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n23\t    \"line\": 193,\n24\t    \"comment\": \"Delivery is gated to precombat=True only, so a Mana Sculpt resolved during the controller's OWN precombat main delivers on next turn's precombat main, skipping the same turn's postcombat main (real MTG 'your next main phase' would be that postcombat main). This matches the coordinator's explicit 'next precombat main' directive, so flagging only as advisory.\"\n25\t  }\n26\t]\n27\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"6c0b17a7-3630-4ff3-b127-142d1d94c7f1","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:36:52.097Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 30,\n    \"comment\": \"_is_spell() cannot distinguish a spell from an activated/triggered ability on the stack. In this engine, ability StackObjects reuse their source permanent's card_types (see engine/abilities.py:222-228 and engine/triggers.py:130: source=trigger.source / ability.source). So for an ability put on the stack by a creature, _stack_source().card_types is {CREATURE}, and `card_types - {LAND}` is non-empty -> _is_spell returns True. The intended guard `getattr(obj, 'is_spell', None) is False` is dead code: no StackObject in the engine ever sets an `is_spell` attribute (grep finds none). Result: ManaSculpt.can_cast() and get_targets() will treat abilities on the stack as legal 'spells', allowing Mana Sculpt to target/counter an ability, which violates 'Counter target spell'. Distinguish spells from abilities (e.g. only treat a StackObject as a spell when its source card currently resides in a STACK zone / is an actual cast spell, not an ability whose source is a battlefield permanent).\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 61,\n    \"comment\": \"_counter_spell reaches into the private game.stack._items list to remove the target StackObject because Stack exposes no public 'remove arbitrary object' API (only push/pop/peek/objects). This works today but is brittle if Stack internals change. If a public removal helper is added to engine/stack.py later, prefer it. Not a bug given the current API surface.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"engine/casting.py\",\n    \"line\": 237,\n    \"comment\": \"mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc treats {X} as 0 (ManaCost.cmc ignores x_count, engine/types.py:164-169). For an X-spell, 'the amount of mana spent to cast that spell' should include the X payment, so the deferred {C} would under-count by X. Not exercised by the arbitrated tests and consistent with the coordinator-approved cmc-based mana_spent surface, but worth noting for future 'mana spent' consumers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py\",\n    \"line\": 193,\n    \"comment\": \"Delivery is gated to precombat=True only, so a Mana Sculpt resolved during the controller's OWN precombat main delivers on next turn's precombat main, skipping the same turn's postcombat main (real MTG 'your next main phase' would be that postcombat main). This matches the coordinator's explicit 'next precombat main' directive, so flagging only as advisory.\"\n  }\n]\n","numLines":27,"startLine":1,"totalLines":27}}}
