{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01GiioskR6uKQLHvzyqdDnrJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xz9soUWLCTMcPcRwWPo6u7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# sos_57 Mana Sculpt — revision rationale\n\n## Strict fix (review.json index 0): distinguish a cast spell from an ability on the stack\n\n### Problem\n`_is_spell()` previously decided \"is this a counterable spell?\" from the\nStackObject's `card_types`: `bool(card_types - {CardType.LAND})`. In this engine\nan activated/triggered ability's `StackObject` reuses its **source permanent's**\n`card_types` (see `engine/abilities.py` `_activate_regular_ability`,\n`engine/triggers.py` `fire_event`, both of which build\n`StackObject(source=ability.source / trigger.source, ...)`). So an ability whose\nsource is a creature has `card_types == {CREATURE}`, and the old test wrongly\nreturned `True` — letting Mana Sculpt illegally target/counter an *ability*.\nThe guard `getattr(obj, \"is_spell\", None) is False` was dead code: no\nStackObject in the engine ever set an `is_spell` attribute.\n\n### Fix — additive `is_spell` marker on spell StackObjects\nI added an **additive** boolean field `is_spell: bool = False` to the\n`StackObject` dataclass (`engine/stack.py`). It defaults to `False`, so every\nexisting construction site (abilities in `engine/abilities.py`, triggers in\n`engine/triggers.py`, and all engine_tests that build StackObjects) is\nunchanged — abilities remain `is_spell=False`.\n\nThe casting pipeline now marks genuine cast spells:\n- `engine/casting.py` `cast_spell` → `StackObject(..., is_spell=True)`\n- `engine/casting.py` `cast_spell_free` → `StackObject(..., is_spell=True)`\n- `engine/stack.py` `copy_spell` → `StackObject(..., is_spell=True)` (a spell\n  copy is itself a spell).\n\n`_is_spell()` in `cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` now requires\n`getattr(obj, \"is_spell\", False) is True` (so abilities — which never set the\nflag — are rejected), and *additionally* keeps the non-land card-type check so a\nhypothetical bare-land StackObject would not count as a spell.\n\n### Why a marker rather than a zone probe\nThe directive offered two options: probe \"is the source card currently in a\nSTACK zone?\" or add an additive marker. The marker is the more robust signal:\n- It is stable at filter/resolve time regardless of any later zone churn.\n- It is set exactly at the moment of casting (the canonical \"this became a\n  spell\" event), mirroring how the engine already records `card.mana_spent`\n  there.\n- It cannot be confused by an ability whose source permanent happens to share\n  identity quirks, and it doesn't depend on iterating zones.\n\n### Behaviours preserved (all 26 tests still pass)\n- Self-rejection: handled before `_is_spell` by `obj is self` /\n  `_stack_source(obj) is self` in both the `get_targets` filter and `can_cast`.\n  The self-rejection test passes both a raw card and a bare\n  `StackObject(source=sculpt)` (no marker) — both are rejected.\n- Creature-spell acceptance, noncreature-spell acceptance, sorcery counter, and\n  empty-stack `can_cast() is False` are all unchanged; the test spells are cast\n  through the real `engine_cast_spell` pipeline, so they now carry\n  `is_spell=True`.\n\n## Tests\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py -q` → 26 passed.\n- `pytest engine_tests/ -q` → 1145 passed (no regressions).\n- `pytest cards/ -q` → 141 passed (no cross-card regressions from the\n  `StackObject` field addition).\n\n## Optional X advisory (review.json index 2) — NOT applied\nThe advisory notes `mana_spent = effective_cost.cmc` treats `{X}` as 0\n(`ManaCost.cmc` ignores `x_count`), so an X-spell would under-count by X.\nI did **not** change this:\n- The current payment pipeline (`player.mana_pool.pay(effective_cost)`) does not\n  surface the chosen X amount anywhere I can read cleanly; `effective_cost` has\n  `x_count` but not the *value* paid for each X. There is no low-risk, clearly\n  correct additive way to recover \"mana actually spent on X\" without changing\n  the payment model.\n- The advisory itself states it is \"not exercised by the arbitrated tests and\n  consistent with the coordinator-approved cmc-based `mana_spent` surface.\"\n  Touching `mana_spent` semantics risks other consumers and the approved\n  surface, which fails the \"low-risk and clearly correct\" bar for optional work.\n\nAdvisories index 1 (private `stack._items` access) and index 3 (precombat-only\ndelivery) were explicitly out of scope per the task and are not changed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":53527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":311,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_0117GXqJ3qNucMV54hnuyWVy","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"ff3132d8-07b5-46a0-957d-8e09354f131d","request_id":"req_011CbdVz6GEXqGkvmrs5LJGv","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_57 spell/ability distinction"}
