{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0117GXqJ3qNucMV54hnuyWVy","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is in order. The strict correctness fix is applied, all 26 card tests and 1145 engine tests pass, output files are written, and FILES_MODIFIED.json is upserted in place.\n\nSummary of the strict fix: I added an additive `is_spell: bool = False` field to `StackObject` (`/workspace/engine/stack.py`), set `is_spell=True` only in the casting pipeline (`cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free` in `/workspace/engine/casting.py`, and `copy_spell` in `/workspace/engine/stack.py`), and changed `_is_spell()` in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` to require that marker. Abilities (whose `StackObject.source` is a battlefield permanent reusing its `card_types`) never set the flag, so Mana Sculpt can no longer illegally target an ability. The X advisory (index 2) was not applied because the payment pipeline exposes no clean signal for the X amount actually paid, and changing `mana_spent` semantics fails the \"low-risk and clearly correct\" bar.\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/disagreements.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ae17924e9c4218ddc (use SendMessage with to: 'ae17924e9c4218ddc' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 59569\ntool_uses: 33\nduration_ms: 157183</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"759827f5-b1d0-4b96-a2f2-8a67bedeab32","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:39:59.981Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are applying review feedback to a card you implemented. One STRICT correctness issue must be fixed; advisories are optional.\n\nCARD: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt — {1}{U}{U} Instant, \"Counter target spell. ...\")\n- Implementation: `cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py`\n- Tests (do NOT modify, must keep all passing): `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` (26 tests)\n- Review: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/review.json`\n- Prior diff: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl.diff`\n\nSTRICT comment to fix (review.json index 0):\n`_is_spell()` cannot distinguish a spell from an activated/triggered ABILITY on the stack. In this engine, ability StackObjects reuse their source permanent's `card_types` (see `engine/abilities.py`, `engine/triggers.py` where `source=ability.source`/`trigger.source`), so an ability whose source is a creature has `card_types == {CREATURE}` and your `card_types - {LAND}` test wrongly returns True. The `getattr(obj, 'is_spell', None) is False` guard is dead code (no StackObject sets `is_spell`). Result: Mana Sculpt would illegally treat an ability on the stack as a counterable \"spell\", violating \"Counter target spell\".\n\nREQUIRED FIX:\n- Make `_is_spell()` (and therefore `can_cast`/`get_targets`/the target filter) treat a StackObject as a legal target ONLY when it is an actual cast SPELL, not an activated/triggered ability. Inspect the engine to find a reliable distinction — e.g. a spell's source card currently resides in a STACK zone (it was cast and is on the stack), whereas an ability's source permanent is on the battlefield; or another robust signal you find in `engine/stack.py` / `engine/abilities.py` / `engine/triggers.py` / `engine/card.py`. Read those modules before deciding. If a clean public signal does not exist, add a small ADDITIVE marker (e.g. set an attribute on spell StackObjects when a spell is cast in `engine/casting.py`, defaulting absent for abilities) — additive only, no rename/move/delete, no breaking existing behavior.\n- Keep self-rejection, creature-spell acceptance, noncreature-spell acceptance, and empty-stack behavior intact.\n\nOPTIONAL (advisories — apply only if low-risk and clearly correct): index 2 notes `mana_spent` ignores X (so {X} spells under-count by X). You MAY improve `mana_spent` to include the X payment if you can do so cleanly and additively; otherwise leave it. Ignore advisories 1 and 3.\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Do NOT modify any test file, `engine_tests/`, or `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n- Engine changes additive-only; no rename/move/delete of existing symbols; keep existing behavior.\n- If you genuinely disagree with the strict comment, record it instead of silently ignoring it.\n\nTASK:\n1. Read the relevant engine modules and the review.\n2. Apply the fix.\n3. `pytest cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py -q` — all 26 must still pass.\n4. `pytest engine_tests/ -q` — no regressions.\n\nOUTPUT (into $CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57`):\n- `impl-revised.diff` — `git diff` of all current changes for this card.\n- `impl-revised-rationale.md` — what you changed for the strict fix (the exact spell/ability distinction you used), whether you applied the X advisory, and why.\n- `disagreements.json` — JSON array of {\"review_comment_index\": <n>, \"reviewer_comment\": \"...\", \"implementer_justification\": \"...\"} for any strict comment you did NOT fully apply. Empty `[]` if you applied everything.\n- Keep `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` entry for `sos_57` accurate (upsert in place).\n\nReturn ONLY:\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: <N>\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/disagreements.json","agentId":"ae17924e9c4218ddc","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is in order. The strict correctness fix is applied, all 26 card tests and 1145 engine tests pass, output files are written, and FILES_MODIFIED.json is upserted in place.\n\nSummary of the strict fix: I added an additive `is_spell: bool = False` field to `StackObject` (`/workspace/engine/stack.py`), set `is_spell=True` only in the casting pipeline (`cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free` in `/workspace/engine/casting.py`, and `copy_spell` in `/workspace/engine/stack.py`), and changed `_is_spell()` in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_57/card_impl.py` to require that marker. Abilities (whose `StackObject.source` is a battlefield permanent reusing its `card_types`) never set the flag, so Mana Sculpt can no longer illegally target an ability. The X advisory (index 2) was not applied because the payment pipeline exposes no clean signal for the X amount actually paid, and changing `mana_spent` semantics fails the \"low-risk and clearly correct\" bar.\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_57/disagreements.json"}],"totalDurationMs":157183,"totalTokens":59569,"totalToolUseCount":33,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":581,"cache_read_input_tokens":58539,"output_tokens":447,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":581},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":447,"cache_read_input_tokens":58539,"cache_creation_input_tokens":581,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":581,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":10,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":15,"editFileCount":7,"linesAdded":157,"linesRemoved":62,"otherToolCount":0}}}
