{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UTqGu96uM67KzieH2G3YGv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MVb4oC4BJkL7j2ALHuzuRG","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n\nLegendary Planeswalker — Ral, `{1}{B}{B}`, starting loyalty 3. Four loyalty\nabilities (verify against `cards/sos/sos_97/card_spec.json`):\n- **+1**: Surveil 2.\n- **−1**: Any number of target players each discard a card.\n- **−2**: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your\n  graveyard to the battlefield.\n- **−7**: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is\n  the number of coins that came up heads.\n\n## Conventions to FOLLOW (the tests were written against these)\nMatch the FDN planeswalker convention (read `cards/fdn/fdn_44`, `fdn_234`,\n`fdn_176` impls) and the names the Tester assumed:\n- `RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)` with `starting_loyalty=3`,\n  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, `\"Ral\"` subtype, `{1}{B}{B}`.\n- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect,\n  description)` with costs `+1, −1, −2, −7`; each `effect` is `(game) -> None`\n  reading `pw.controller`.\n- Targeted abilities read `pw._resolve_target` (single object; −2 and −7) and\n  `pw._resolve_targets` (list; the multi-target −1).\n- Surveil keep/bin decisions use the controller's `choose_yes_no`.\n- Set `self.colors` explicitly per KEY_DECISIONS (e.g. `[\"U\",\"R\"]` or per spec —\n  match the spec's color identity; the cost is {1}{B}{B} so include the colored\n  pips' colors).\nIf any assumed attribute name is genuinely unworkable, return DISPUTE rather than\nsilently diverging.\n\n## Engine support to BUILD (additive only; no rename/move/delete; full regression must pass)\n\n### Coin-flip primitive (for the −7)\nAdd a deterministic, injectable coin-flip helper, e.g. a `GameState`/`engine.game`\nfunction `flip_coins(game, n) -> int` returning the number of heads, using an RNG\nthat tests can control deterministically. Document the EXACT injection point so a\ntest can force results (options: an injectable `game.rng = random.Random(seed)`,\nor honoring a pre-seeded list like `game._forced_coin_flips`, or monkeypatch\ntarget). Also record the heads count from the −7 on the card, e.g.\n`pw._last_heads: int`, so a test can assert X directly.\n\n### Skip-turn support (for the −7)\nAdd native skip-turn support: a per-player counter (e.g. `Player.skipped_turns`\nor `GameState`-tracked) that the turn rotation / `advance_phase` (engine/turn.py)\nhonors so a player's next N turns are actually skipped (decrementing as each is\nskipped). The −7 increments the TARGET OPPONENT's skipped-turns by X (the heads\ncount). Keep `extra_turns` behavior intact and pass full engine regression.\nDocument how a test advances turns and observes the opponent's turns being\nskipped X times.\n\n## After you finish\nThe coordinator re-invokes the Tester ONCE to:\n- Force a deterministic coin-flip result and assert X == heads (read `pw._last_heads`\n  and/or the scheduled skip count).\n- Advance turns and assert the target opponent's next X turns are skipped.\nDocument the exact, stable surface (helper signatures, attribute names, how to\nforce flips, how to advance/observe skipped turns) in `impl-rationale.md`.\n\nMake the existing 27 tests pass (properties, ability shape, +1 surveil, −1\ndiscard, −2 reanimate MV≤3, −7 runs-without-raising). Do NOT modify any test\nfile, `engine_tests/`, or `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":984,"cache_read_input_tokens":124457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":984},"output_tokens":54,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"f168676d-b2d0-444c-a904-da0e98564149","request_id":"req_011CbdWZgGJ4EC9wkgFn2yy5"}
