 name is genuinely unworkable, return DISPUTE rather than\nsilently diverging.\n\n## Engine support to BUILD (additive only; no rename/move/delete; full regression must pass)\n\n### Coin-flip primitive (for the −7)\nAdd a deterministic, injectable coin-flip helper, e.g. a `GameState`/`engine.game`\nfunction `flip_coins(game, n) -> int` returning the number of heads, using an RNG\nthat tests can control deterministically. Document the EXACT injection point so a\ntest can force results (options: an injectable `game.rng = random.Random(seed)`,\nor honoring a pre-seeded list like `game._forced_coin_flips`, or monkeypatch\ntarget). Also record the heads count from the −7 on the card, e.g.\n`pw._last_heads: int`, so a test can assert X directly.\n\n### Skip-turn support (for the −7)\nAdd native skip-turn support: a per-player counter (e.g. `Player.skipped_turns`\nor `GameState`-tracked) that the turn rotation / `advance_phase` (engine/turn.py)\nhonors so a player's next N turns are actually skipped (decrementing as each is\nskipped). The −7 increments the TARGET OPPONENT's skipped-turns by X (the heads\ncount). Keep `extra_turns` behavior intact and pass full engine regression.\nDocument how a test advances turns and observes the opponent's turns being\nskipped X times.\n\n## After you finish\nThe coordinator re-invokes the Tester ONCE to:\n- Force a deterministic coin-flip result and assert X == heads (read `pw._last_heads`\n  and/or the scheduled skip count).\n- Advance turns and assert the target opponent's next X turns are skipped.\nDocument the exact, stable surface (helper signatures, attribute names, how to\nforce flips, how to advance/observe skipped turns) in `impl-rationale.md`.\n\nMake the existing 27 tests pass (properties, ability shape, +1 surveil, −1\ndiscard, −2 reanimate MV≤3, −7 runs-without-raising). Do NOT modify any test\nfile, `engine_tests/`, or `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
