{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K98gEEzk6Zrhs4yWd7jj4C","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n2\t\n3\tLegendary Planeswalker — Ral, `{1}{B}{B}`, starting loyalty 3. Four loyalty\n4\tabilities (verify against `cards/sos/sos_97/card_spec.json`):\n5\t- **+1**: Surveil 2.\n6\t- **−1**: Any number of target players each discard a card.\n7\t- **−2**: Return target creature card with mana value 3 or less from your\n8\t  graveyard to the battlefield.\n9\t- **−7**: Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, where X is\n10\t  the number of coins that came up heads.\n11\t\n12\t## Conventions to FOLLOW (the tests were written against these)\n13\tMatch the FDN planeswalker convention (read `cards/fdn/fdn_44`, `fdn_234`,\n14\t`fdn_176` impls) and the names the Tester assumed:\n15\t- `RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)` with `starting_loyalty=3`,\n16\t  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, `\"Ral\"` subtype, `{1}{B}{B}`.\n17\t- `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect,\n18\t  description)` with costs `+1, −1, −2, −7`; each `effect` is `(game) -> None`\n19\t  reading `pw.controller`.\n20\t- Targeted abilities read `pw._resolve_target` (single object; −2 and −7) and\n21\t  `pw._resolve_targets` (list; the multi-target −1).\n22\t- Surveil keep/bin decisions use the controller's `choose_yes_no`.\n23\t- Set `self.colors` explicitly per KEY_DECISIONS (e.g. `[\"U\",\"R\"]` or per spec —\n24\t  match the spec's color identity; the cost is {1}{B}{B} so include the colored\n25\t  pips' colors).\n26\tIf any assumed attribute name is genuinely unworkable, return DISPUTE rather than\n27\tsilently diverging.\n28\t\n29\t## Engine support to BUILD (additive only; no rename/move/delete; full regression must pass)\n30\t\n31\t### Coin-flip primitive (for the −7)\n32\tAdd a deterministic, injectable coin-flip helper, e.g. a `GameState`/`engine.game`\n33\tfunction `flip_coins(game, n) -> int` returning the number of heads, using an RNG\n34\tthat tests can control deterministically. Document the EXACT injection point so a\n35\ttest can force results (options: an injectable `game.rng = random.Random(seed)`,\n36\tor honoring a pre-seeded list like `game._forced_coin_flips`, or monkeypatch\n37\ttarget). Also record the heads count from the −7 on the card, e.g.\n38\t`pw._last_heads: int`, so a test can assert X directly.\n39\t\n40\t### Skip-turn support (for the −7)\n41\tAdd native skip-turn support: a per-player counter (e.g. `Player.skipped_turns`\n42\tor `GameState`-tracked) that the turn rotation / `advance_phase` (engine/turn.py)\n43\thonors so a player's next N turns are actually skipped (decrementing as each is\n44\tskipped). The −7 increments the TARGET OPPONENT's skipped-turns by X (the heads\n45\tcount). Keep `extra_turns` behavior intact and pass full engine regression.\n46\tDocument how a test advances turns and observes the opponent's turns being\n47\tskipped X times.\n48\t\n49\t## After you finish\n50\tThe coordinator re-invokes the Tester ONCE to:\n51\t- Force a deterministic coin-flip result and assert X == heads (read `pw._last_heads`\n52\t  and/or the scheduled skip count).\n53\t- Advance turns and assert the target opponent's next X turns are skipped.\n54\tDocument the exact, stable surface (helper signatures, attribute names, how to\n55\tforce flips, how to advance/observe skipped turns) in `impl-rationale.md`.\n56\t\n57\tMake the existing 27 tests pass (properties, ability shape, +1 surveil, −1\n58\tdiscard, −2 reanimate MV≤3, −7 runs-without-raising). Do NOT modify any test\n59\tfile, `engine_tests/`, or `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CEQK4iuzVq89pcNhCfuf9F","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"e145ae2f-5f96-4bce-b27a-a17a4f319a9b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:47:22.587Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_97 planeswalker + engine support"}
