ck on top; keep/bin via controller `choose_yes_no`).\n- −1: Any number of target players each discard a card (reads `pw._resolve_targets`, a list).\n- −2: Return target creature card with mana value (mana_cost.cmc) 3 or less from YOUR graveyard to the battlefield (reads `pw._resolve_target`).\n- −7: Flip five coins; target opponent (`pw._resolve_target`) skips their next X turns, X = heads. Record heads on `pw._last_heads`.\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Do NOT modify any test file in `test-files.txt`, nor `engine_tests/`, nor `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`. If a Tester assumption is genuinely unworkable, return DISPUTE.\n- Engine changes ALLOWED and expected (coin-flip helper, skip-turn support); add methods/classes/helpers/files; modify existing function bodies (incl. `engine/turn.py`, `engine/game.py`/`engine/game_state.py`, `engine/player.py`). You MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols. Keep ALL existing engine behavior intact and pass full regression.\n- Read `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_MAP.md`, `KEY_DECISIONS.md` first (reuse established conventions; e.g. explicit `self.colors`).\n\nREFERENCE: FDN planeswalkers `cards/fdn/fdn_44` (Kaito), `cards/fdn/fdn_234` (Vivien), `cards/fdn/fdn_176` (Liliana) for `Planeswalker`/`LoyaltyAbility`/`get_loyalty_abilities`/`_resolve_target` patterns. Engine: `engine/card.py` (Planeswalker, LoyaltyAbility), `engine/turn.py`, `engine/game_state.py`, `engine/player.py`, `engine/zones.py`, `engine/types.py`. Grep RULEBOOK.txt for surveil (701.x) and skip-turn (614.10) if needed.\n\nTASK:\n1. Read directives, spec, tests, FDN planeswalkers, engine source.\n2. Build the coin-flip primitive (deterministic/injectable RNG; record `pw._last_heads`) and skip-turn support (per-player skipped-turns counter honored by turn rotation). Document EXACT signatures/attribute names + how a test forces flips and observes skipped turns, in the rationale.\n3. Implement Ral Zarek and all four loyalty abilities.\n4. `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py -q` until all