{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pwx9DwKhBU28Rc312U89X7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n2\t\n3\t## Card\n4\t`cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` — `RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)`,\n5\t`{1}{B}{B}`, `starting_loyalty=3`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, `\"Ral\"` subtype,\n6\texplicit `self.colors = [\"B\"]` (per KEY_DECISIONS). Built on the FDN\n7\tplaneswalker convention (Kaito/Vivien/Liliana): `__init__` uses\n8\t`kwargs.setdefault`, and `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four\n9\t`LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)` closures that read\n10\t`pw.controller` and the test-set target attributes.\n11\t\n12\tLoyalty abilities:\n13\t- **+1 Surveil 2** — iterates the top two library cards (top first). For each it\n14\t  asks the controller's `choose_yes_no`; on yes the card is moved\n15\t  LIBRARY→GRAVEYARD via `engine.zones.move_to_zone`. Kept cards stay on top in\n16\t  existing order. Empty library is a no-op.\n17\t- **−1 discard** — reads `pw._resolve_targets` (a list of players). Each\n18\t  targeted player with a non-empty hand discards one card chosen via\n19\t  `player.choose_card(...)` (falls back to the last card in hand if the choice\n20\t  is missing/invalid), routed through `engine.game.discard`. Empty list / empty\n21\t  hands are safe no-ops.\n22\t- **−2 reanimate** — reads `pw._resolve_target` (single card). Lazily\n23\t  revalidates: must be in the controller's graveyard, a `CardType.CREATURE`, and\n24\t  `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`; then moves GRAVEYARD→BATTLEFIELD via `move_to_zone`.\n25\t  Non-creature, MV≥4, or missing target are no-ops.\n26\t- **−7 ultimate** — reads `pw._resolve_target` (the opponent). Flips five coins\n27\t  via the new `engine.game.flip_coins(game, 5)`, records the count on\n28\t  `pw._last_heads`, and adds that many to the opponent's `skipped_turns`. No\n29\t  target ⇒ flips still happen and `_last_heads` is recorded, but nothing is\n30\t  scheduled (safe no-op).\n31\t\n32\t## EXACT engine surface added (additive only)\n33\t\n34\t### Coin-flip primitive — `engine/game.py`\n35\t- `flip_coin(game, player=None) -> bool` — `True` = heads.\n36\t- `flip_coins(game, n, player=None) -> int` — number of heads across `n` flips\n37\t  (`n <= 0` ⇒ 0). The −7 calls `flip_coins(game, 5)`.\n38\t\n39\t**Deterministic injection points, checked in this order:**\n40\t1. `game._forced_coin_flips` — a pre-seeded list or `collections.deque` of\n41\t   booleans (truthy = heads). The next value is popped from the **front**\n42\t   (`popleft` for a deque, `pop(0)` for a list). A test forces exactly K heads\n43\t   by setting e.g. `game._forced_coin_flips = deque([True, False, True, True, False])`\n44\t   (3 heads) **before** calling the −7 effect, then asserting `pw._last_heads == 3`.\n45\t2. `game.rng` — any `random.Random`-compatible object; result is\n46\t   `game.rng.random() < 0.5`. A test sets `game.rng = random.Random(seed)` for\n47\t   reproducible flips.\n48\t3. Fallback: module-level `random.random() < 0.5`.\n49\t\n50\t**Heads recorded on the card:** `pw._last_heads: int | None` (None until the −7\n51\truns). After the −7, `pw._last_heads == X`, and the scheduled skip count equals\n52\t`X` (added to the opponent's counter).\n53\t\n54\t### Skip-turn support — `engine/player.py` + `engine/game_state.py`\n55\t- `Player.skipped_turns: int` (default 0) — per-player counter of upcoming turns\n56\t  to skip (CR 614.10). The −7 does `target.skipped_turns += X`.\n57\t- `GameState.advance_phase` turn-wrap now delegates to two new helpers:\n58\t  - `GameState._advance_rotation_index() -> int` — pops the next seat index from\n59\t    the `extra_turns` FIFO (unchanged behavior: an extra turn does not advance\n60\t    the normal rotation) or advances the normal alternating `_normal_next_index`.\n61\t  - `GameState._select_next_active_player() -> int` — calls\n62\t    `_advance_rotation_index()`, then while the chosen player has\n63\t    `skipped_turns > 0`, decrements that counter, increments `turn_number` (the\n64\t    skipped turn slot is consumed), and advances to the next candidate. A\n65\t    bounded loop guard prevents an infinite loop if every candidate is\n66\t    perpetually skipped. **All existing `extra_turns` behavior is preserved** —\n67\t    a queued extra turn that happens to be skipped is still consumed from the\n68\t    FIFO.\n69\t\n70\t**How a test advances/observes skipping:** force `pw._last_heads` heads via\n71\t`game._forced_coin_flips`, run the −7 (opponent's `skipped_turns` becomes X),\n72\tthen drive turn rotation (e.g. repeatedly `game.advance_phase()` to wrap to a\n73\tnew turn, or `engine.turn.run_turn` / `engine.game.run_game`). The opponent\n74\tnever becomes `active_player` while `skipped_turns > 0`; the counter decrements\n75\tonce per skipped turn until it reaches 0, after which the opponent takes a\n76\tnormal turn. (Verified: with X=3, seat 1 is skipped on the next 3 of its slots\n77\tbefore becoming active, and `skipped_turns` returns to 0.)\n78\t\n79\t## Design decisions / spec notes\n80\t- Surveil uses per-card `choose_yes_no` (the codebase's standard \"you may\"\n81\t  decision channel and the surface the Tester scripted), not a single subset\n82\t  choice.\n83\t- −1 uses `choose_card` (matches FDN Vivien's decision channel) so a test can\n84\t  script the discarded card; falls back deterministically to the last card.\n85\t- The spec lists \"Surveil\" under keywords, but Surveil is an action keyword used\n86\t  inside the +1, not an evergreen `engine.types.Keyword`; the card does not\n87\t  advertise a `Keyword` flag (no test asserts one).\n88\t- Engine changes are strictly additive: new functions/methods/attributes only;\n89\t  no existing symbol renamed/moved/deleted. Full regression (engine_tests +\n90\t  all FDN/SOS) passes: 1313 passed.\n91\t\n92\t## Tests\n93\t`cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` — 27 tests, all passing.\n94\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"47161b6c-b8c8-4a79-a712-7389433f2491","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:51:01.052Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/impl-rationale.md","content":"# Implementation rationale — sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer)\n\n## Card\n`cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py` — `RalZarekGuestLecturer(Planeswalker)`,\n`{1}{B}{B}`, `starting_loyalty=3`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, `\"Ral\"` subtype,\nexplicit `self.colors = [\"B\"]` (per KEY_DECISIONS). Built on the FDN\nplaneswalker convention (Kaito/Vivien/Liliana): `__init__` uses\n`kwargs.setdefault`, and `get_loyalty_abilities()` returns four\n`LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)` closures that read\n`pw.controller` and the test-set target attributes.\n\nLoyalty abilities:\n- **+1 Surveil 2** — iterates the top two library cards (top first). For each it\n  asks the controller's `choose_yes_no`; on yes the card is moved\n  LIBRARY→GRAVEYARD via `engine.zones.move_to_zone`. Kept cards stay on top in\n  existing order. Empty library is a no-op.\n- **−1 discard** — reads `pw._resolve_targets` (a list of players). Each\n  targeted player with a non-empty hand discards one card chosen via\n  `player.choose_card(...)` (falls back to the last card in hand if the choice\n  is missing/invalid), routed through `engine.game.discard`. Empty list / empty\n  hands are safe no-ops.\n- **−2 reanimate** — reads `pw._resolve_target` (single card). Lazily\n  revalidates: must be in the controller's graveyard, a `CardType.CREATURE`, and\n  `mana_cost.cmc <= 3`; then moves GRAVEYARD→BATTLEFIELD via `move_to_zone`.\n  Non-creature, MV≥4, or missing target are no-ops.\n- **−7 ultimate** — reads `pw._resolve_target` (the opponent). Flips five coins\n  via the new `engine.game.flip_coins(game, 5)`, records the count on\n  `pw._last_heads`, and adds that many to the opponent's `skipped_turns`. No\n  target ⇒ flips still happen and `_last_heads` is recorded, but nothing is\n  scheduled (safe no-op).\n\n## EXACT engine surface added (additive only)\n\n### Coin-flip primitive — `engine/game.py`\n- `flip_coin(game, player=None) -> bool` — `True` = heads.\n- `flip_coins(game, n, player=None) -> int` — number of heads across `n` flips\n  (`n <= 0` ⇒ 0). The −7 calls `flip_coins(game, 5)`.\n\n**Deterministic injection points, checked in this order:**\n1. `game._forced_coin_flips` — a pre-seeded list or `collections.deque` of\n   booleans (truthy = heads). The next value is popped from the **front**\n   (`popleft` for a deque, `pop(0)` for a list). A test forces exactly K heads\n   by setting e.g. `game._forced_coin_flips = deque([True, False, True, True, False])`\n   (3 heads) **before** calling the −7 effect, then asserting `pw._last_heads == 3`.\n2. `game.rng` — any `random.Random`-compatible object; result is\n   `game.rng.random() < 0.5`. A test sets `game.rng = random.Random(seed)` for\n   reproducible flips.\n3. Fallback: module-level `random.random() < 0.5`.\n\n**Heads recorded on the card:** `pw._last_heads: int | None` (None until the −7\nruns). After the −7, `pw._last_heads == X`, and the scheduled skip count equals\n`X` (added to the opponent's counter).\n\n### Skip-turn support — `engine/player.py` + `engine/game_state.py`\n- `Player.skipped_turns: int` (default 0) — per-player counter of upcoming turns\n  to skip (CR 614.10). The −7 does `target.skipped_turns += X`.\n- `GameState.advance_phase` turn-wrap now delegates to two new helpers:\n  - `GameState._advance_rotation_index() -> int` — pops the next seat index from\n    the `extra_turns` FIFO (unchanged behavior: an extra turn does not advance\n    the normal rotation) or advances the normal alternating `_normal_next_index`.\n  - `GameState._select_next_active_player() -> int` — calls\n    `_advance_rotation_index()`, then while the chosen player has\n    `skipped_turns > 0`, decrements that counter, increments `turn_number` (the\n    skipped turn slot is consumed), and advances to the next candidate. A\n    bounded loop guard prevents an infinite loop if every candidate is\n    perpetually skipped. **All existing `extra_turns` behavior is preserved** —\n    a queued extra turn that happens to be skipped is still consumed from the\n    FIFO.\n\n**How a test advances/observes skipping:** force `pw._last_heads` heads via\n`game._forced_coin_flips`, run the −7 (opponent's `skipped_turns` becomes X),\nthen drive turn rotation (e.g. repeatedly `game.advance_phase()` to wrap to a\nnew turn, or `engine.turn.run_turn` / `engine.game.run_game`). The opponent\nnever becomes `active_player` while `skipped_turns > 0`; the counter decrements\nonce per skipped turn until it reaches 0, after which the opponent takes a\nnormal turn. (Verified: with X=3, seat 1 is skipped on the next 3 of its slots\nbefore becoming active, and `skipped_turns` returns to 0.)\n\n## Design decisions / spec notes\n- Surveil uses per-card `choose_yes_no` (the codebase's standard \"you may\"\n  decision channel and the surface the Tester scripted), not a single subset\n  choice.\n- −1 uses `choose_card` (matches FDN Vivien's decision channel) so a test can\n  script the discarded card; falls back deterministically to the last card.\n- The spec lists \"Surveil\" under keywords, but Surveil is an action keyword used\n  inside the +1, not an evergreen `engine.types.Keyword`; the card does not\n  advertise a `Keyword` flag (no test asserts one).\n- Engine changes are strictly additive: new functions/methods/attributes only;\n  no existing symbol renamed/moved/deleted. Full regression (engine_tests +\n  all FDN/SOS) passes: 1313 passed.\n\n## Tests\n`cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` — 27 tests, all passing.\n","numLines":94,"startLine":1,"totalLines":94}}}
