{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Y7V1sUPXQ3vfFLW4ycV6Cv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RoJ6RPpqSKURXwre4ZKYaZ","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md","old_string":"### TestRalZarekUltimate (3 tests) — the −7\n- The ultimate exists at loyalty cost −7.\n- It runs without raising when a target opponent is supplied (five coin flips +\n  skip scheduling execute).\n- With no target it is a safe no-op and does not corrupt game state.\n\nThe exact value of X (number of heads across five flips) and the *enforcement*\nof skipping the opponent's next X turns are not asserted — see the edge cases\nbelow and `untestable.json`.","new_string":"### TestRalZarekUltimate (3 tests) — the −7 (structural)\n- The ultimate exists at loyalty cost −7.\n- It runs without raising when a target opponent is supplied (five coin flips +\n  skip scheduling execute).\n- With no target it is a safe no-op and does not corrupt game state.\n\n### TestRalZarekUltimateDeterministic (7 tests) — the −7 (deterministic)\nThe implementation now exposes a deterministic surface, so X (heads) and the\nenforced turn-skipping are asserted directly. Coin flips are forced via\n`game._forced_coin_flips` (a `deque` of booleans consumed from the front,\ntruthy == heads); the resolved heads count is read from `pw._last_heads`; the\nscheduled skips are read from the target opponent's `Player.skipped_turns`; and\nturn enforcement is observed through `GameState.advance_phase` /\n`_select_next_active_player` (driven one turn boundary at a time via a small\n`_force_turn_wrap` helper that jumps to ENDING/CLEANUP and advances once).\n\n- **X == heads.** A forced sequence with exactly 3 heads gives `_last_heads == 3`\n  and the opponent's `skipped_turns == 3`.\n- **All heads.** Five heads -> `_last_heads == 5`, opponent `skipped_turns == 5`.\n- **All tails.** Zero heads -> `_last_heads == 0`, opponent `skipped_turns == 0`\n  (the lower boundary; nothing is scheduled).\n- **Additive scheduling.** A second −7 (1 head) on top of an earlier one (2\n  heads) leaves `skipped_turns == 3` — the skip count accumulates rather than\n  overwriting, matching CR 614.10 stacking of skip-turn effects.\n- **Enforcement — opponent stays inactive while owed skips.** With 2 skips owed,\n  the opponent (seat 1) never becomes the active player across the next two turn\n  boundaries; the active player remains seat 0 and `skipped_turns` decrements\n  by one per skipped slot (2 -> 1 -> 0).\n- **Enforcement — normal turn resumes.** After both skipped slots are consumed\n  (`skipped_turns == 0`), the very next turn boundary finally makes the opponent\n  (seat 1) the active player.\n- **No-target deterministic no-op.** With no `pw._resolve_target`, the −7 still\n  flips and records `_last_heads` (3 in the forced sequence) but increments\n  nobody's `skipped_turns` — neither controller nor opponent is scheduled to\n  skip."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":60872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":322,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GnDaDCbHwYtiWkdURk8PBC","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"f94b896a-ba28-43cd-b694-22efca9b4114","request_id":"req_011CbdX3qWwnnGDZoeN5zoyW","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Add −7 X/skip-turn tests for sos_97"}
