{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WzQTmUTDmgHAb2QQLbMtVu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"requirement\": \"−7: Flip five coins ... where X is the number of coins that came up heads.\",\n4\t    \"reason\": \"The engine has no coin-flip primitive (no helper in engine/, confirmed by grep), and the implementer's RNG entry point is unknown. Asserting the exact number of heads (X) would require seeding or monkeypatching an unspecified internal random call, which would over-couple the test to implementation details.\",\n5\t    \"what_would_unblock\": \"An engine-level coin-flip helper (e.g. engine.game.flip_coin(game) or game.flip_coins(n)) with a deterministic/injectable RNG, or a documented card attribute recording the heads count (e.g. pw._last_heads), so the test can assert X.\"\n6\t  },\n7\t  {\n8\t    \"requirement\": \"−7: Target opponent skips their next X turns.\",\n9\t    \"reason\": \"\\\"Skip your next X turns\\\" is a replacement effect (CR 614.10). The engine has no native skip-turn support — only a GameState.extra_turns FIFO, and GameState's own docstring flags 'skip your next turn' as not fully handled. There is no observable, engine-defined surface to assert that the opponent's next X turns are actually skipped via advance_phase.\",\n10\t    \"what_would_unblock\": \"Native skip-turn support: e.g. a per-player skipped_turns counter on GameState/Player honored by advance_phase / turn rotation, so a test can advance turns and observe the opponent's turns being skipped X times.\"\n11\t  }\n12\t]\n13\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GnDaDCbHwYtiWkdURk8PBC","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"9b32f611-19a0-472d-8f41-4790a5332d87","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:53:32.420Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Add −7 X/skip-turn tests for sos_97"}
