{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GnDaDCbHwYtiWkdURk8PBC","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TESTS_REWRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 34\n\n−7 deterministic tests added (new class `TestRalZarekUltimateDeterministic`, 7 cases):\n- `test_x_equals_heads_count_and_schedules_that_many_skips` — forced 3-head sequence → `pw._last_heads == 3` and opponent `skipped_turns == 3`.\n- `test_all_heads_schedules_five_skips` — all heads → X == 5.\n- `test_all_tails_schedules_no_skips` — all tails → X == 0, no skips.\n- `test_skip_counter_is_additive_across_two_ultimates` — second −7 adds to (not overwrites) the skip count (2 + 1 → 3).\n- `test_opponent_is_not_active_while_skip_counter_positive` — opponent never becomes active while owed skips; counter decrements per skipped slot.\n- `test_opponent_takes_a_normal_turn_after_skips_are_exhausted` — once `skipped_turns == 0`, opponent resumes a normal turn.\n- `test_no_target_flips_but_schedules_no_skip` — no `_resolve_target` still records `_last_heads` but increments nobody's `skipped_turns`.\n\nuntestable_count: 0\n\nAll 34 tests pass (27 existing + 7 new). `untestable.json` set to `[]`; `test-rationale.md` updated (new deterministic −7 section + previously-blocked items marked COVERED); `test-files.txt` lists `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`.\n\nRelevant paths:\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-files.txt`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/untestable.json`"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a6b7bd85376c698fd (use SendMessage with to: 'a6b7bd85376c698fd' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 65425\ntool_uses: 25\nduration_ms: 139424</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"df9280a5-dc3e-4b8a-ad89-764701baee57","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:53:45.716Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are adding coverage to your existing tests for one MTG planeswalker. The implementation now exposes a deterministic surface for the previously-untestable −7 ultimate (coin-flip X and skip-turn enforcement).\n\nCARD: sos_97 (Ral Zarek, Guest Lecturer — −7: \"Flip five coins. Target opponent skips their next X turns, X = heads.\")\n- Test file you OWN and will edit: `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`\n- Implementation in place: `cards/sos/sos_97/card_impl.py`\n\nSTABLE SURFACE (now implemented — assert against these):\n- Coin-flip helpers in `engine/game.py`: `flip_coin(game, player=None) -> bool`, `flip_coins(game, n, player=None) -> int` (heads count).\n- **Deterministic injection**: set `game._forced_coin_flips` to a list/`collections.deque` of booleans (truthy = heads) BEFORE running the −7; values are consumed from the FRONT. E.g. `game._forced_coin_flips = deque([True, False, True, True, False])` → 3 heads. (Alternatively `game.rng = random.Random(seed)`.) Prefer `_forced_coin_flips` for exact control.\n- After the −7 effect runs, `pw._last_heads == X` (the heads count).\n- Skip-turn: `Player.skipped_turns: int` (default 0); the −7 adds X to the target opponent's `skipped_turns`. `GameState.advance_phase` / turn rotation honors it: while a player's `skipped_turns > 0`, they don't become active and the counter decrements once per skipped slot until 0.\n\nTASKS — add a new test class covering the −7 deterministically:\n1. **X == heads**: set `game._forced_coin_flips` to a known sequence of 5 booleans with a known heads count (e.g. 3), set `pw.controller` and `pw._resolve_target` = the opponent, run the −7 `effect(game)`, then assert `pw._last_heads == 3` AND the opponent's `skipped_turns == 3`.\n2. **Different head counts**: parametrize or add a second test with a different forced sequence (e.g. all heads → 5, all tails → 0) and assert `pw._last_heads` and `opponent.skipped_turns` match.\n3. **Skip-turn enforcement**: with the opponent's `skipped_turns` set to X (via the −7 or directly), advance the turn rotation (read `engine/turn.py`, `engine/game_state.py`, and `test_utils.py` to find the right call — e.g. repeatedly `game.advance_phase()` to wrap turns, or a turn-advance helper) and assert the opponent does NOT become the active player while `skipped_turns > 0`, that the counter decrements per skipped slot, and that after X skips the opponent can take a normal turn. Keep it deterministic and minimal; if a clean turn-advance call isn't available, fire/advance the minimal surface that exercises `_select_next_active_player`.\n4. **No-target −7**: with no `_resolve_target`, the −7 still flips (records `_last_heads`) but schedules no skip (nobody's `skipped_turns` increases). Safe no-op.\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Edit ONLY `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`. Do NOT touch `engine_tests/` or `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n- Keep all existing 27 tests intact and passing.\n- Read `test_utils.py`, `engine/game.py`, `engine/game_state.py`, `engine/turn.py`, `engine/player.py` to use correct APIs.\n\nVERIFY: `pytest cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py -q` — all tests (existing + new) must pass.\n\nOUTPUT (into $CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97`):\n- Update `cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py` in place.\n- Update `test-rationale.md` (note the new −7 tests).\n- Ensure `test-files.txt` lists the test file.\n- Empty `untestable.json` to `[]` (both requirements now covered).\n\nReturn ONLY a short status summary: total test_cases now, the −7 tests added, and untestable_count (0).","agentId":"a6b7bd85376c698fd","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"TESTS_REWRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 34\n\n−7 deterministic tests added (new class `TestRalZarekUltimateDeterministic`, 7 cases):\n- `test_x_equals_heads_count_and_schedules_that_many_skips` — forced 3-head sequence → `pw._last_heads == 3` and opponent `skipped_turns == 3`.\n- `test_all_heads_schedules_five_skips` — all heads → X == 5.\n- `test_all_tails_schedules_no_skips` — all tails → X == 0, no skips.\n- `test_skip_counter_is_additive_across_two_ultimates` — second −7 adds to (not overwrites) the skip count (2 + 1 → 3).\n- `test_opponent_is_not_active_while_skip_counter_positive` — opponent never becomes active while owed skips; counter decrements per skipped slot.\n- `test_opponent_takes_a_normal_turn_after_skips_are_exhausted` — once `skipped_turns == 0`, opponent resumes a normal turn.\n- `test_no_target_flips_but_schedules_no_skip` — no `_resolve_target` still records `_last_heads` but increments nobody's `skipped_turns`.\n\nuntestable_count: 0\n\nAll 34 tests pass (27 existing + 7 new). `untestable.json` set to `[]`; `test-rationale.md` updated (new deterministic −7 section + previously-blocked items marked COVERED); `test-files.txt` lists `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`.\n\nRelevant paths:\n- `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_97/tests.py`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-rationale.md`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/test-files.txt`\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_97/untestable.json`"}],"totalDurationMs":139424,"totalTokens":65425,"totalToolUseCount":25,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":284,"cache_read_input_tokens":64493,"output_tokens":646,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":284},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":646,"cache_read_input_tokens":64493,"cache_creation_input_tokens":284,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":284,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":10,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":8,"editFileCount":7,"linesAdded":234,"linesRemoved":43,"otherToolCount":0}}}
