{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01SVngo3WrgScaGmvf8oPYwk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019NbgQypM1Fj6rsfvc84VD8","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2841,"cache_read_input_tokens":8113,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2841,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019FjC3Yg4WQJQBFnLquD2dB","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"8648ddf8-c432-404c-abd4-669cd645a129","request_id":"req_011CbdX8LnhCLp5RN5D94EXR","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019NbgQypM1Fj6rsfvc84VD8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent conventions and decisions across runs. Append-only.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: \"exile instead of graveyard\" for free-cast spells (sos_1)\n6\tFor a non-permanent spell with \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\n7\texile it instead\": set `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell\n8\tobject before casting it. `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` honors this opt-in\n9\tflag and routes the resolving instant/sorcery from the stack to `Zone.EXILE`\n10\tinstead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, then clears the flag (one-shot). Additive and\n11\tbackward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /\n12\timpulse effects with the same rider.\n13\t\n14\t## Engine: mana-spent tracking, delayed main-phase triggers, spell/ability marker (sos_57)\n15\t- `card.mana_spent: int` — set by `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` to the\n16\t  converted mana actually paid (after cost reduction, `effective_cost.cmc`),\n17\t  analogous to `card.colors_spent`; `cast_spell_free` sets 0. Read via\n18\t  `getattr(card, \"mana_spent\", 0)`. Use for any \"amount of mana spent to cast\"\n19\t  rider. (Known gap: ignores {X} payments — would under-count X-spells.)\n20\t- `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, controller, precombat=True)` in\n21\t  `engine/events.py`, fired by `engine/turn.py` on entering precombat/postcombat\n22\t  main phases. Paired with `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(\n23\t  controller, callback, *, precombat=True)` (registry on GameState; delivery via\n24\t  `engine/deferred.py::deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects`, run SYNCHRONOUSLY\n25\t  inside `TriggerManager.fire_event` for that event type). This is the general\n26\t  \"at the beginning of your next main phase, do X once\" mechanism. A test fires\n27\t  it directly: `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game,\n28\t  BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=ctrl, controller=ctrl, precombat=True))`.\n29\t  Effects are one-shot (removed on delivery).\n30\t- `StackObject.is_spell: bool` (additive, default False) — set True only in the\n31\t  casting pipeline (`cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free`, `copy_spell`). Abilities on\n32\t  the stack reuse their source permanent's `card_types`, so to distinguish a\n33\t  SPELL from an ability on the stack (e.g. for \"counter target spell\"), check\n34\t  `getattr(stack_obj, \"is_spell\", False)` rather than inspecting `card_types`.\n35\t\n36\t## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\n37\tThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n38\t(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n39\t- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n40\t  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n41\t- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n42\t  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n43\t  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n44\t  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n45\t  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n46\t  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n47\t- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n48\t  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n49\t  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n50\t  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n51\t\n52\t## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\n53\tThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\n54\tstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\n55\tidentity must be observable.\n56\t\n57\t## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)\n58\tOverride `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine\n59\tclamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in\n60\t`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so no manual\n61\tclamping is needed. The hook may read `self.controller` (engine sets it before\n62\tquerying).\n63\t\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019FjC3Yg4WQJQBFnLquD2dB","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"76afb185-bae7-4d40-b37a-011732ffccc5","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:54:06.241Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"abc49dc9e5f803813","tool_use_id":"toolu_019FjC3Yg4WQJQBFnLquD2dB","description":"Reading engine/game_state.py","subagent_type":"Reviewer","usage":{"total_tokens":24715,"tool_uses":6,"duration_ms":7735},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"ddf64891-a946-4c57-a379-836146dccc71","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011vofd86orgf2pXXzUQKLfr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EBqSaCoLBYbQgbCYaUc8K9","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/game_state.py","limit":250},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13713,"cache_read_input_tokens":10954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13713,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019FjC3Yg4WQJQBFnLquD2dB","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"fdd0d270-df82-463b-908c-0df0bc9d6258","request_id":"req_011CbdX8dr7biohyCk3BRLyB","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EBqSaCoLBYbQgbCYaUc8K9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Central game state and turn/phase/step progression.\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\t\n5\tfrom typing import Any\n6\t\n7\tfrom engine.combat import CombatState\n8\tfrom engine.continuous_effects import EffectManager\n9\tfrom engine.player import Player\n10\tfrom engine.replacement_effects import ReplacementManager\n11\tfrom engine.stack import Stack\n12\tfrom engine.triggers import TriggerManager\n13\tfrom engine.types import Phase, Step, Zone\n14\tfrom engine.zones import ZoneContainer\n15\t\n16\t# Ordered list of (Phase, Step | None) representing a full MTG turn.\n17\t_TURN_SEQUENCE: list[tuple[Phase, Step | None]] = [\n18\t    # Beginning phase\n19\t    (Phase.BEGINNING, Step.UNTAP),\n20\t    (Phase.BEGINNING, Step.UPKEEP),\n21\t    (Phase.BEGINNING, Step.DRAW),\n22\t    # Precombat main phase\n23\t    (Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN, None),\n24\t    # Combat phase\n25\t    (Phase.COMBAT, Step.BEGIN_COMBAT),\n26\t    (Phase.COMBAT, Step.DECLARE_ATTACKERS),\n27\t    (Phase.COMBAT, Step.DECLARE_BLOCKERS),\n28\t    (Phase.COMBAT, Step.COMBAT_DAMAGE),\n29\t    (Phase.COMBAT, Step.END_COMBAT),\n30\t    # Postcombat main phase\n31\t    (Phase.POSTCOMBAT_MAIN, None),\n32\t    # Ending phase\n33\t    (Phase.ENDING, Step.END),\n34\t    (Phase.ENDING, Step.CLEANUP),\n35\t]\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tclass GameState:\n39\t    \"\"\"Central game-state object tracking all mutable game information.\n40\t\n41\t    Attributes:\n42\t        players: The list of players in the game.\n43\t        active_player_index: Index of the current active player.\n44\t        priority_player_index: Index of the player who currently has priority.\n45\t        phase: Current phase of the turn.\n46\t        step: Current step within the phase (``None`` for main phases).\n47\t        turn_number: The current turn number (1-indexed).\n48\t        stack: The game stack for spells and abilities.\n49\t        trigger_manager: Central registry for triggered abilities.\n50\t        replacement_manager: Central registry for replacement effects.\n51\t        effect_manager: Manager for continuous effects and the layer system.\n52\t        is_game_over: Whether the game has ended.\n53\t        winner: The winning player, or ``None`` if the game is ongoing / draw.\n54\t    \"\"\"\n55\t\n56\t    def __init__(self, players: list[Player]) -> None:\n57\t        if len(players) < 2:\n58\t            raise ValueError(\"GameState requires at least 2 players\")\n59\t        if len(players) > 2:\n60\t            raise ValueError(\"GameState supports exactly 2 players\")\n61\t\n62\t        self.players: list[Player] = players\n63\t        self.active_player_index: int = 0\n64\t        self.priority_player_index: int = 0\n65\t        self.phase: Phase = Phase.BEGINNING\n66\t        self.step: Step | None = Step.UNTAP\n67\t        self.turn_number: int = 1\n68\t        self.stack: Stack = Stack()\n69\t        self.trigger_manager: TriggerManager = TriggerManager()\n70\t        self.replacement_manager: ReplacementManager = ReplacementManager()\n71\t        self.effect_manager: EffectManager = EffectManager()\n72\t        self.combat_state: CombatState = CombatState()\n73\t        self.is_game_over: bool = False\n74\t        self.winner: Player | None = None\n75\t        # ENGINE LIMITATION: Extra turns queue (FIFO of player seat indices).\n76\t        # Complex interactions ('skip your next turn', multiple extra turns\n77\t        # from different sources) are not fully handled.\n78\t        self.extra_turns: list[int] = []\n79\t        # Tracks normal turn rotation independently of extra turns.\n80\t        # Extra turns are truly *inserted* — they don't advance the\n81\t        # normal rotation.  When extras are exhausted the game picks up\n82\t        # from _normal_next_index.\n83\t        self._normal_next_index: int = 1\n84\t        # Deferred one-shot effects scheduled to run \"at the beginning of a\n85\t        # player's next (precombat) main phase\". Each entry is a dict with\n86\t        # keys: ``controller`` (Player), ``callback`` (callable taking the\n87\t        # game state), and ``precombat`` (bool — restrict to the precombat\n88\t        # main phase). Consumed (and removed) by\n89\t        # :func:`engine.deferred.deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects` when the\n90\t        # matching BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent fires. Additive — see\n91\t        # :func:`schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect`.\n92\t        self.main_phase_deferred_effects: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n93\t\n94\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n95\t    # Deferred one-shot main-phase effects\n96\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n97\t\n98\t    def schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(\n99\t        self,\n100\t        controller: Player,\n101\t        callback: Any,\n102\t        *,\n103\t        precombat: bool = True,\n104\t    ) -> None:\n105\t        \"\"\"Schedule a one-shot effect for *controller*'s next main phase.\n106\t\n107\t        The *callback* (a callable taking the game state) runs exactly once,\n108\t        when the matching :class:`~engine.events.BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`\n109\t        next fires for *controller*. If *precombat* is ``True`` the effect\n110\t        only fires for the precombat main phase.\n111\t\n112\t        This is the engine's delayed/one-shot deferred-effect mechanism for\n113\t        \"do X at the beginning of your next main phase\" riders (e.g. Mana\n114\t        Sculpt). It is additive and does not use the stack.\n115\t        \"\"\"\n116\t        self.main_phase_deferred_effects.append(\n117\t            {\"controller\": controller, \"callback\": callback, \"precombat\": precombat}\n118\t        )\n119\t\n120\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n121\t    # Player properties\n122\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n123\t\n124\t    @property\n125\t    def active_player(self) -> Player:\n126\t        \"\"\"Return the currently active player.\"\"\"\n127\t        return self.players[self.active_player_index]\n128\t\n129\t    @property\n130\t    def priority_player(self) -> Player:\n131\t        \"\"\"Return the player who currently has priority.\"\"\"\n132\t        return self.players[self.priority_player_index]\n133\t\n134\t    @property\n135\t    def non_active_player(self) -> Player:\n136\t        \"\"\"Return the non-active player (2-player assumption for v1).\"\"\"\n137\t        return self.players[1 - self.active_player_index]\n138\t\n139\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n140\t    # Zone accessors\n141\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n142\t\n143\t    def get_battlefield(self, player: Player) -> ZoneContainer:\n144\t        \"\"\"Return the battlefield zone for *player*.\"\"\"\n145\t        return player.zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD]\n146\t\n147\t    def get_hand(self, player: Player) -> ZoneContainer:\n148\t        \"\"\"Return the hand zone for *player*.\"\"\"\n149\t        return player.zones[Zone.HAND]\n150\t\n151\t    def get_graveyard(self, player: Player) -> ZoneContainer:\n152\t        \"\"\"Return the graveyard zone for *player*.\"\"\"\n153\t        return player.zones[Zone.GRAVEYARD]\n154\t\n155\t    def get_library(self, player: Player) -> ZoneContainer:\n156\t        \"\"\"Return the library zone for *player*.\"\"\"\n157\t        return player.zones[Zone.LIBRARY]\n158\t\n159\t    def get_exile(self, player: Player) -> ZoneContainer:\n160\t        \"\"\"Return the exile zone for *player*.\"\"\"\n161\t        return player.zones[Zone.EXILE]\n162\t\n163\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n164\t    # Phase/step progression\n165\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n166\t\n167\t    def advance_phase(self) -> None:\n168\t        \"\"\"Advance to the next phase/step in MTG turn order.\n169\t\n170\t        At the end of CLEANUP, the turn number is incremented and the\n171\t        active player swaps (2-player assumption).  Mana pools are\n172\t        emptied on every transition.\n173\t        \"\"\"\n174\t        current = (self.phase, self.step)\n175\t        idx = _TURN_SEQUENCE.index(current)\n176\t\n177\t        if idx + 1 < len(_TURN_SEQUENCE):\n178\t            # Move to next phase/step within the same turn.\n179\t            next_phase, next_step = _TURN_SEQUENCE[idx + 1]\n180\t            self.phase = next_phase\n181\t            self.step = next_step\n182\t        else:\n183\t            # End of turn — wrap around.\n184\t            self.turn_number += 1\n185\t            self.active_player_index = self._select_next_active_player()\n186\t            self.priority_player_index = self.active_player_index\n187\t            self.phase = _TURN_SEQUENCE[0][0]\n188\t            self.step = _TURN_SEQUENCE[0][1]\n189\t\n190\t        self.empty_mana_pools()\n191\t\n192\t    def _select_next_active_player(self) -> int:\n193\t        \"\"\"Determine the seat index that should take the upcoming turn.\n194\t\n195\t        Resolves the next active player from the extra-turn FIFO / normal\n196\t        rotation, then honors per-player skip-turn counters (CR 614.10): if\n197\t        the would-be active player has ``skipped_turns > 0``, that counter is\n198\t        decremented and their turn is consumed, advancing to the following\n199\t        candidate. This preserves all existing ``extra_turns`` behavior — an\n200\t        extra turn that is skipped is still consumed from the queue.\n201\t\n202\t        A safety guard caps the number of skip iterations so that a state in\n203\t        which both players are perpetually skipped cannot loop forever; once\n204\t        the guard trips, the last candidate takes the turn.\n205\t        \"\"\"\n206\t        # Guard against the (degenerate) case where every candidate is skipped.\n207\t        max_iterations = (len(self.players) * 2) + sum(\n208\t            getattr(p, \"skipped_turns\", 0) for p in self.players\n209\t        ) + 1\n210\t\n211\t        candidate = self._advance_rotation_index()\n212\t        for _ in range(max_iterations):\n213\t            player = self.players[candidate]\n214\t            if getattr(player, \"skipped_turns\", 0) > 0:\n215\t                # This player's turn is skipped — consume one skip and the\n216\t                # turn slot, then move to the next candidate.\n217\t                player.skipped_turns -= 1\n218\t                self.turn_number += 1\n219\t                candidate = self._advance_rotation_index()\n220\t                continue\n221\t            return candidate\n222\t        return candidate\n223\t\n224\t    def _advance_rotation_index(self) -> int:\n225\t        \"\"\"Pop the next seat index from the extra-turn FIFO or normal rotation.\n226\t\n227\t        Mirrors the prior inline logic in :meth:`advance_phase`: an extra turn\n228\t        (if queued) is taken without advancing the normal rotation; otherwise\n229\t        the normal alternating rotation advances.\n230\t        \"\"\"\n231\t        if self.extra_turns:\n232\t            # ENGINE LIMITATION: Extra turns queue (FIFO). Pop the next player\n233\t            # seat index; that player gets the next turn. Normal rotation is\n234\t            # NOT advanced — extra turns are inserted before the normal next\n235\t            # turn.\n236\t            return self.extra_turns.pop(0)\n237\t        index = self._normal_next_index\n238\t        self._normal_next_index = 1 - self._normal_next_index\n239\t        return index\n240\t\n241\t    def empty_mana_pools(self) -> None:\n242\t        \"\"\"Empty all players' mana pools — called on each phase/step transition.\"\"\"\n243\t        for player in self.players:\n244\t            player.mana_pool.empty()\n245\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019FjC3Yg4WQJQBFnLquD2dB","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"ac1b5529-22fa-4cd4-822d-cf973ffba34f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:54:10.064Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"abc49dc9e5f803813","tool_use_id":"toolu_019FjC3Yg4WQJQBFnLquD2dB","description":"Reading engine/card.py","subagent_type":"Reviewer","usage":{"total_tokens":24720,"tool_uses":7,"duration_ms":8047},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"d2aed1c4-6849-4c90-9e0f-c41007fe96a5","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011vofd86orgf2pXXzUQKLfr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FreY5UdJ1CHkj4d5TGGpZH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/card.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13713,"cache_read_input_tokens":10954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13713,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019FjC3Yg4WQJQBFnLquD2dB","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"c6a4817d-0152-4486-bd77-00f48e8ab5c2","request_id":"req_011CbdX8dr7biohyCk3BRLyB","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FreY5UdJ1CHkj4d5TGGpZH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Card base classes, CardImpl interface, and supporting dataclasses.\n2\t\n3\tProvides the core class hierarchy for all Magic: The Gathering card types:\n4\t\n5\t- ``GameObject`` — base for anything that can exist in zones.\n6\t- ``CardImpl(GameObject)`` — abstract card implementation with hooks for\n7\t  casting, resolution, targeting, triggers, and abilities.\n8\t- Concrete subclasses: ``Creature``, ``Instant``, ``Sorcery``,\n9\t  ``Enchantment``, ``Aura``, ``Artifact``, ``ArtifactCreature``,\n10\t  ``Planeswalker``, ``Land``.\n11\t- Supporting dataclasses: ``ActivatedAbility``, ``LoyaltyAbility``,\n12\t  ``ManaAbility``, ``ContinuousEffect``, ``Mode``.\n13\t\"\"\"\n14\t\n15\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n16\t\n17\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n18\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable\n19\t\n20\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, Supertype\n21\t\n22\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n23\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n24\t    from engine.player import Player\n25\t\n26\t\n27\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n28\t# Supporting dataclasses\n29\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n30\t\n31\t@dataclass\n32\tclass Mode:\n33\t    \"\"\"Represents a single mode of a modal spell or ability.\n34\t\n35\t    Attributes:\n36\t        name: Short label for this mode (e.g. ``\"Destroy target creature\"``).\n37\t        description: Detailed rules text for the mode.\n38\t    \"\"\"\n39\t\n40\t    name: str = \"\"\n41\t    description: str = \"\"\n42\t\n43\t\n44\t@dataclass\n45\tclass ActivatedAbility:\n46\t    \"\"\"An activated ability on a permanent.\n47\t\n48\t    Attributes:\n49\t        cost: A callable that checks/pays the cost given the game state.\n50\t        effect: A callable that applies the effect given the game state.\n51\t        description: Human-readable description of the ability.\n52\t    \"\"\"\n53\t\n54\t    cost: Callable[..., Any]\n55\t    effect: Callable[..., Any]\n56\t    description: str = \"\"\n57\t\n58\t\n59\t@dataclass\n60\tclass LoyaltyAbility:\n61\t    \"\"\"A planeswalker loyalty ability.\n62\t\n63\t    Attributes:\n64\t        loyalty_cost: The loyalty cost (positive for ``+``, negative for ``−``).\n65\t        effect: A callable that applies the ability's effect.\n66\t        description: Human-readable description.\n67\t    \"\"\"\n68\t\n69\t    loyalty_cost: int\n70\t    effect: Callable[..., Any]\n71\t    description: str = \"\"\n72\t\n73\t\n74\t@dataclass\n75\tclass ManaAbility:\n76\t    \"\"\"A mana ability (does not use the stack).\n77\t\n78\t    Attributes:\n79\t        cost: A callable that checks/pays the cost.\n80\t        mana_produced: A callable that returns the mana added.\n81\t        description: Human-readable description.\n82\t    \"\"\"\n83\t\n84\t    cost: Callable[..., Any]\n85\t    mana_produced: Callable[..., Any]\n86\t    description: str = \"\"\n87\t\n88\t\n89\t@dataclass\n90\tclass ContinuousEffect:\n91\t    \"\"\"A continuous effect applied by an enchantment or other source.\n92\t\n93\t    Attributes:\n94\t        apply: A callable that applies the effect to the game state.\n95\t        remove: A callable that removes the effect from the game state.\n96\t        description: Human-readable description.\n97\t    \"\"\"\n98\t\n99\t    apply: Callable[..., Any]\n100\t    remove: Callable[..., Any]\n101\t    description: str = \"\"\n102\t\n103\t\n104\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n105\t# GameObject — base class for zone-resident objects\n106\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n107\t\n108\tclass GameObject:\n109\t    \"\"\"Base class for anything that can exist in a zone.\n110\t\n111\t    Each instance receives a unique ``object_id`` via a class-level\n112\t    auto-incrementing counter.\n113\t\n114\t    Attributes:\n115\t        object_id: Unique integer identifier (auto-assigned).\n116\t        owner: The player who owns this object.\n117\t        controller: The player who currently controls this object.\n118\t    \"\"\"\n119\t\n120\t    _next_id: int = 1\n121\t\n122\t    def __init__(self, owner: Player | None = None, controller: Player | None = None) -> None:\n123\t        self.object_id: int = GameObject._next_id\n124\t        GameObject._next_id += 1\n125\t        self.owner: Player | None = owner\n126\t        self.controller: Player | None = controller if controller is not None else owner\n127\t\n128\t    @classmethod\n129\t    def reset_id_counter(cls) -> None:\n130\t        \"\"\"Reset the auto-incrementing counter (useful in tests).\"\"\"\n131\t        cls._next_id = 1\n132\t\n133\t\n134\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n135\t# CardImpl — abstract card implementation\n136\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n137\t\n138\tclass CardImpl(GameObject):\n139\t    \"\"\"Abstract base for all card implementations.\n140\t\n141\t    Subclasses should override the ``can_cast``, ``on_cast``, ``on_resolve``,\n142\t    and other hook methods to implement card-specific behaviour.\n143\t\n144\t    Attributes:\n145\t        name: Card name.\n146\t        mana_cost: The card's mana cost.\n147\t        card_types: Set of :class:`~engine.types.CardType` values.\n148\t        subtypes: Set of subtype strings (e.g. ``{\"Elf\", \"Warrior\"}``).\n149\t        supertypes: Set of :class:`~engine.types.Supertype` values.\n150\t        keywords: Combination of :class:`~engine.types.Keyword` flags.\n151\t        rules_text: The card's rules text string.\n152\t    \"\"\"\n153\t\n154\t    def __init__(\n155\t        self,\n156\t        name: str = \"\",\n157\t        mana_cost: ManaCost | None = None,\n158\t        card_types: set[CardType] | None = None,\n159\t        subtypes: set[str] | None = None,\n160\t        supertypes: set[Supertype] | None = None,\n161\t        keywords: Keyword | None = None,\n162\t        rules_text: str = \"\",\n163\t        owner: Player | None = None,\n164\t        controller: Player | None = None,\n165\t    ) -> None:\n166\t        super().__init__(owner=owner, controller=controller)\n167\t        self.name: str = name\n168\t        self.mana_cost: ManaCost = mana_cost if mana_cost is not None else ManaCost()\n169\t        self.card_types: set[CardType] = card_types if card_types is not None else set()\n170\t        self.subtypes: set[str] = subtypes if subtypes is not None else set()\n171\t        self.supertypes: set[Supertype] = supertypes if supertypes is not None else set()\n172\t        self.keywords: Keyword = keywords if keywords is not None else Keyword(0)\n173\t        self.rules_text: str = rules_text\n174\t        # Snapshot original characteristics for continuous-effect reset.\n175\t        self._original_card_types: frozenset[CardType] = frozenset(self.card_types)\n176\t        self._original_keywords: Keyword = self.keywords\n177\t\n178\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n179\t    # Continuous-effect reset support\n180\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n181\t\n182\t    def _reset_characteristics(self) -> None:\n183\t        \"\"\"Reset mutable characteristics to their original (pre-effect) values.\n184\t\n185\t        Called by :meth:`EffectManager.apply_all` before reapplying effects\n186\t        so that the recalculation is idempotent.\n187\t        \"\"\"\n188\t        self.card_types = set(self._original_card_types)\n189\t        self.keywords = self._original_keywords\n190\t\n191\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n192\t    # Hook methods — override in subclasses / card definitions\n193\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n194\t\n195\t    def can_cast(self, game: GameState) -> bool:\n196\t        \"\"\"Return ``True`` if this card can currently be cast.\"\"\"\n197\t        return True\n198\t\n199\t    def cost_reduction(self, game: GameState) -> int:\n200\t        \"\"\"Return the generic mana reduction for casting this card.\n201\t\n202\t        Override in subclasses to implement cost-reduction mechanics\n203\t        (e.g. Embercleave costs {1} less for each attacking creature).\n204\t        The returned value is clamped so that generic mana cannot go below 0.\n205\t        Only reduces generic mana — colored costs are never reduced.\n206\t\n207\t        Returns:\n208\t            Non-negative integer representing generic mana to subtract.\n209\t        \"\"\"\n210\t        return 0\n211\t\n212\t    def on_cast(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n213\t        \"\"\"Called when the card is cast (before it goes on the stack).\"\"\"\n214\t\n215\t    def on_resolve(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n216\t        \"\"\"Called when the spell resolves from the stack.\n217\t\n218\t        Targets are available via ``self.chosen_targets`` — set at\n219\t        resolve-time by :func:`~engine.casting._resolve_spell` from\n220\t        :attr:`StackObject.targets`, or directly by test code.\n221\t        \"\"\"\n222\t\n223\t    def get_targets(self, game: GameState) -> list[Any]:\n224\t        \"\"\"Return a list of legal targets for this card.\"\"\"\n225\t        return []\n226\t\n227\t    def register_triggers(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n228\t        \"\"\"Register any triggered abilities this card provides.\"\"\"\n229\t\n230\t    def register_replacement_effects(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n231\t        \"\"\"Register any replacement effects this card provides.\"\"\"\n232\t\n233\t    def get_activated_abilities(self) -> list[ActivatedAbility]:\n234\t        \"\"\"Return activated abilities this card provides.\"\"\"\n235\t        return []\n236\t\n237\t    def get_modes(self) -> list[Mode]:\n238\t        \"\"\"Return available modes for modal spells/abilities.\n239\t\n240\t        Non-modal cards return an empty list by default.\n241\t        \"\"\"\n242\t        return []\n243\t\n244\t\n245\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n246\t# Creature\n247\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n248\t\n249\tclass Creature(CardImpl):\n250\t    \"\"\"A creature card.\n251\t\n252\t    Attributes:\n253\t        base_power: The printed power value (rule 208.1). Immutable after init.\n254\t        base_toughness: The printed toughness value. Immutable after init.\n255\t        modified_power: Current power after continuous effects (Layer 7c), before counters.\n256\t            Reset to ``base_power`` each effect cycle; continuous effects write here.\n257\t        modified_toughness: Current toughness after continuous effects, before counters.\n258\t        damage_marked: Amount of damage currently marked on this creature.\n259\t        is_tapped: Whether the creature is tapped.\n260\t        summoning_sick: Whether the creature has summoning sickness.\n261\t        is_attacking: Combat flag — currently declared as an attacker.\n262\t        is_blocking: Combat flag — currently declared as a blocker.\n263\t        plus_one_counters: Number of +1/+1 counters.\n264\t        minus_one_counters: Number of -1/-1 counters.\n265\t        is_token: Whether this object is a token (for SBA checks).\n266\t    \"\"\"\n267\t\n268\t    def __init__(\n269\t        self,\n270\t        name: str = \"\",\n271\t        mana_cost: ManaCost | None = None,\n272\t        card_types: set[CardType] | None = None,\n273\t        subtypes: set[str] | None = None,\n274\t        supertypes: set[Supertype] | None = None,\n275\t        keywords: Keyword | None = None,\n276\t        rules_text: str = \"\",\n277\t        owner: Player | None = None,\n278\t        controller: Player | None = None,\n279\t        base_power: int = 0,\n280\t        base_toughness: int = 0,\n281\t    ) -> None:\n282\t        # Always include CREATURE in card_types.\n283\t        card_types = (card_types or set()) | {CardType.CREATURE}\n284\t        super().__init__(\n285\t            name=name,\n286\t            mana_cost=mana_cost,\n287\t            card_types=card_types,\n288\t            subtypes=subtypes,\n289\t            supertypes=supertypes,\n290\t            keywords=keywords,\n291\t            rules_text=rules_text,\n292\t            owner=owner,\n293\t            controller=controller,\n294\t        )\n295\t        self.base_power: int = base_power\n296\t        self.base_toughness: int = base_toughness\n297\t        self.modified_power: int = base_power\n298\t        self.modified_toughness: int = base_toughness\n299\t        self.damage_marked: int = 0\n300\t        self.is_tapped: bool = False\n301\t        self.summoning_sick: bool = True\n302\t        self.is_attacking: bool = False\n303\t        self.is_blocking: bool = False\n304\t        self.plus_one_counters: int = 0\n305\t        self.minus_one_counters: int = 0\n306\t        self.is_token: bool = False\n307\t        self.dealt_deathtouch_damage: bool = False\n308\t        self._base_plus_one_counters: int = 0\n309\t        self._base_minus_one_counters: int = 0\n310\t\n311\t    def _reset_characteristics(self) -> None:\n312\t        \"\"\"Reset creature characteristics to pre-effect values.\"\"\"\n313\t        super()._reset_characteristics()\n314\t        self.modified_power = self.base_power\n315\t        self.modified_toughness = self.base_toughness\n316\t        self.plus_one_counters = self._base_plus_one_counters\n317\t        self.minus_one_counters = self._base_minus_one_counters\n318\t        # Reset combat-restriction flags set by continuous effects (e.g. Pacifism).\n319\t        # These are reapplied by active effects during apply_all().\n320\t        self._cant_attack: bool = False\n321\t        self._cant_block: bool = False\n322\t        self._cant_be_blocked: bool = False\n323\t        self._cant_activate: bool = False\n324\t        self._max_attackers_blocked: int = 1\n325\t        # Clear granted protections so they are reapplied by active effects.\n326\t        if hasattr(self, \"protections\"):\n327\t            self.protections = []\n328\t\n329\t    @property\n330\t    def counters(self) -> dict[str, int]:\n331\t        \"\"\"Return a dict-like view of counters on this creature.\"\"\"\n332\t        result: dict[str, int] = {}\n333\t        if self.plus_one_counters > 0:\n334\t            result[\"+1/+1\"] = self.plus_one_counters\n335\t        if self.minus_one_counters > 0:\n336\t            result[\"-1/-1\"] = self.minus_one_counters\n337\t        return result\n338\t\n339\t    @property\n340\t    def power(self) -> int:\n341\t        \"\"\"Current power including counter modifications.\"\"\"\n342\t        return self.modified_power + self.plus_one_counters - self.minus_one_counters\n343\t\n344\t    @property\n345\t    def toughness(self) -> int:\n346\t        \"\"\"Current toughness including counter modifications.\"\"\"\n347\t        return self.modified_toughness + self.plus_one_counters - self.minus_one_counters\n348\t\n349\t\n350\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n351\t# Instant / Sorcery\n352\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n353\t\n354\tclass Instant(CardImpl):\n355\t    \"\"\"An instant spell — no extra fields beyond CardImpl.\"\"\"\n356\t\n357\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n358\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.INSTANT}\n359\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n360\t\n361\t\n362\tclass Sorcery(CardImpl):\n363\t    \"\"\"A sorcery spell — no extra fields beyond CardImpl.\"\"\"\n364\t\n365\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n366\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.SORCERY}\n367\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n368\t\n369\t\n370\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n371\t# Enchantment\n372\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n373\t\n374\tclass Enchantment(CardImpl):\n375\t    \"\"\"An enchantment card.\n376\t\n377\t    For auras, use the :class:`Aura` subclass which sets ``is_aura = True``.\n378\t    The base ``Enchantment`` class retains the ``attached_to`` attribute for\n379\t    backwards compatibility but marks ``is_aura = False`` so that state-based\n380\t    actions do not treat a non-aura enchantment as an unattached aura.\n381\t\n382\t    Attributes:\n383\t        attached_to: The object this enchantment is attached to (``None``\n384\t            if not an aura or not yet attached).\n385\t        is_aura: ``False`` for regular enchantments; ``True`` for auras.\n386\t    \"\"\"\n387\t\n388\t    is_aura: bool = False\n389\t\n390\t    def __init__(self, attached_to: Any | None = None, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n391\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.ENCHANTMENT}\n392\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n393\t        self.attached_to: Any | None = attached_to\n394\t\n395\t    def apply_continuous_effect(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n396\t        \"\"\"Apply the enchantment's continuous effect to the game.\"\"\"\n397\t\n398\t    def on_enchant(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n399\t        \"\"\"Called when this enchantment becomes attached to an object.\"\"\"\n400\t\n401\t    def on_detach(self, game: GameState) -> None:\n402\t        \"\"\"Called when this enchantment is detached from its object.\"\"\"\n403\t\n404\t\n405\tclass Aura(Enchantment):\n406\t    \"\"\"An Aura enchantment — attaches to a permanent on the battlefield.\n407\t\n408\t    Sets ``is_aura = True`` so that state-based actions correctly identify\n409\t    this as an aura (and move it to the graveyard when unattached).\n410\t\n411\t    Attributes:\n412\t        is_aura: Always ``True`` for auras.\n413\t    \"\"\"\n414\t\n415\t    is_aura: bool = True\n416\t\n417\t    def __init__(self, attached_to: Any | None = None, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n418\t        super().__init__(attached_to=attached_to, **kwargs)\n419\t\n420\t\n421\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n422\t# Artifact / ArtifactCreature\n423\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n424\t\n425\tclass Artifact(CardImpl):\n426\t    \"\"\"An artifact card.\n427\t\n428\t    Attributes:\n429\t        is_tapped: Whether the artifact is currently tapped.\n430\t    \"\"\"\n431\t\n432\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n433\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.ARTIFACT}\n434\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n435\t        self.is_tapped: bool = False\n436\t\n437\t\n438\tclass ArtifactCreature(Creature):\n439\t    \"\"\"An artifact creature — combines Artifact and Creature types.\n440\t\n441\t    Inherits creature combat stats and behaviour from :class:`Creature`.\n442\t    \"\"\"\n443\t\n444\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n445\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.ARTIFACT, CardType.CREATURE}\n446\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n447\t\n448\t\n449\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n450\t# Planeswalker\n451\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n452\t\n453\tclass Planeswalker(CardImpl):\n454\t    \"\"\"A planeswalker card.\n455\t\n456\t    Attributes:\n457\t        starting_loyalty: The starting loyalty printed on the card.\n458\t        loyalty: Current loyalty counter value.\n459\t    \"\"\"\n460\t\n461\t    def __init__(\n462\t        self,\n463\t        starting_loyalty: int = 0,\n464\t        **kwargs: Any,\n465\t    ) -> None:\n466\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.PLANESWALKER}\n467\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n468\t        self.starting_loyalty: int = starting_loyalty\n469\t        self.loyalty: int = starting_loyalty\n470\t\n471\t    def get_loyalty_abilities(self) -> list[LoyaltyAbility]:\n472\t        \"\"\"Return the planeswalker's loyalty abilities.\"\"\"\n473\t        return []\n474\t\n475\t\n476\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n477\t# Land\n478\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n479\t\n480\tclass Land(CardImpl):\n481\t    \"\"\"A land card.\n482\t\n483\t    Lands are not cast — they are played via a special action. ``can_cast``\n484\t    always returns ``False``.\n485\t\n486\t    Attributes:\n487\t        is_tapped: Whether the land is currently tapped.\n488\t    \"\"\"\n489\t\n490\t    def __init__(self, **kwargs: Any) -> None:\n491\t        kwargs[\"card_types\"] = (kwargs.get(\"card_types\") or set()) | {CardType.LAND}\n492\t        super().__init__(**kwargs)\n493\t        self.is_tapped: bool = False\n494\t\n495\t    def can_cast(self, game: GameState) -> bool:\n496\t        \"\"\"Lands cannot be cast; they are played as a special action.\"\"\"\n497\t        return False\n498\t\n499\t    def get_mana_abilities(self) -> list[ManaAbility]:\n500\t        \"\"\"Return the land's mana abilities.\"\"\"\n501\t        return []\n502\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019FjC3Yg4WQJQBFnLquD2dB","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"3b66f452-d2ea-48e1-b93a-7a21b1430b90","timestamp":"2026-06-02T00:54:10.372Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_97 implementation"}
