{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XUFaNngQiH9GQk6NcaNa87","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is in place. The card stub is untouched (only `tests.py` is new), all output files are written, and the suite is in the correct TDD red phase.\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 24\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md\nfiles_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-files.txt\nuntestable_count: 1\nuntestable_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/untestable.json\nnotes: wrote 24 tests for sos_120 Improvisation Capstone covering exile-until-MV-4, free-cast-from-exile (lands excluded), Paradigm self-exile, and the recurring precombat-main-phase free-copy delayed trigger; validated all 24 pass against a scratch reference impl and 22 fail (red) against the stub (2 are defensive guards). One residual ambiguity (exact multi-select free-cast API) recorded in untestable.json.\n\nThe test file is at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`. Notable design choices:\n- The exile-until-MV-4 loop is the unambiguous core and got 8 boundary tests (exact 4, over 4, {0}-MV non-stop, small/empty library).\n- The \"you may cast\" clause is exercised via the `choose_yes_no` convention from sos_1; the decline path and \"lands can never be cast\" invariant are API-agnostic, while the positive free-cast assumption is flagged in `untestable.json`.\n- Paradigm uses the documented `schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect` + `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` surface (KEY_DECISIONS sos_57) and the `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` pipeline opt-in (sos_1) for self-exile, with a dedicated test verifying the delayed trigger is recurring rather than one-shot."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a7d9c79d140d8ea50 (use SendMessage with to: 'a7d9c79d140d8ea50' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 138932\ntool_uses: 63\nduration_ms: 468433</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4