{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014mWkY7DVpNWNnL7Sv4rpSk","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone\n2\t\n3\t## Card under test\n4\t\n5\t`{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson, mythic, with the **Paradigm** keyword.\n6\t\n7\tOracle text:\n8\t\n9\t> Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total\n10\t> mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them\n11\t> without paying their mana costs.\n12\t> Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this\n13\t> name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at\n14\t> the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n15\t\n16\tThree distinct behaviours, plus the static card identity:\n17\t\n18\t1. **Exile-until-MV-4** — exile cards one at a time off the top of the library,\n19\t   stopping as soon as the cumulative mana value of the exiled pile reaches 4\n20\t   (CR-style \"until\" loop). The boundary card may push the total over 4.\n21\t2. **Free-cast from among the exiled pile** — the controller *may* cast any\n22\t   number of the exiled *spells* (nonland cards) without paying mana costs.\n23\t   Lands cannot be cast. Declining leaves the cards in exile.\n24\t3. **Paradigm** — \"Then exile this spell.\" (the resolved Capstone goes to exile\n25\t   instead of the graveyard), and after the controller first resolves a spell\n26\t   with this name, a delayed effect lets them cast a free copy from exile at\n27\t   the beginning of *each* of their first (precombat) main phases (CR 702.192a).\n28\t\n29\t## Conventions used\n30\t\n31\t- Imports follow the standard SOS shape: card from\n32\t  `cards.sos.sos_120.card_impl`, base classes from `engine.card`, types from\n33\t  `engine.types`, helpers from `test_utils`.\n34\t- `_set_library(game, player, cards)` loads the library with index `-1` as the\n35\t  top (matches `ZoneContainer.add(position=\"top\")` appending — confirmed in\n36\t  `engine/zones.py`).\n37\t- The \"you may cast\" clause is exercised through the `DeterministicPlayer`\n38\t  decision interface (`choose_yes_no` / `choose_card`), matching the\n39\t  established \"you may free-cast\" pattern in `cards/sos/sos_1` (The Dawning\n40\t  Archaic). `_decline_free_casts` pre-scripts a generous run of `False` answers\n41\t  so exile-focused tests are not derailed by the cast-offer prompts.\n42\t- The Paradigm delayed trigger is verified through the engine's documented\n43\t  delayed/one-shot main-phase mechanism (KEY_DECISIONS sos_57):\n44\t  `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect` +\n45\t  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, fired directly in tests.\n46\t- Self-exile of the resolved spell is verified through the full casting\n47\t  pipeline (`test_utils.cast_spell`), which honours the\n48\t  `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` opt-in documented in KEY_DECISIONS sos_1.\n49\t\n50\t## Test file\n51\t\n52\t`cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n53\t\n54\t### `TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties` (static identity)\n55\t\n56\t- `test_name` — name is \"Improvisation Capstone\".\n57\t- `test_is_sorcery` — is a `Sorcery` and carries `CardType.SORCERY`.\n58\t- `test_mana_cost` — cost is `{5}{R}{R}`.\n59\t- `test_has_lesson_subtype` — has the \"Lesson\" subtype (type line).\n60\t- `test_has_paradigm_keyword_or_marker` — advertises Paradigm. Paradigm is not\n61\t  an evergreen `Keyword` flag, so this accepts a card-level marker attribute\n62\t  (`paradigm`/`has_paradigm`) or the word in `rules_text`.\n63\t- `test_is_red` — colors include \"R\" (explicit-colors convention, sos_13).\n64\t- `test_not_a_permanent_type` — a sorcery must not carry permanent card types.\n65\t  (Passes against the stub today — it is a guard that must remain true after\n66\t  implementation, not a red-phase driver.)\n67\t\n68\t### `TestExileUntilManaValueFour` (clause 1)\n69\t\n70\t- `test_exiles_until_total_mana_value_reaches_four` — two MV-2 cards on top hit\n71\t  total 4 exactly; the third (deeper) card is untouched and stays in library.\n72\t- `test_single_high_value_card_stops_immediately` — a single MV-4 card stops\n73\t  the loop after one exile; the next card stays in the library.\n74\t- `test_total_mana_value_can_exceed_four` — the boundary card (MV 5) pushing\n75\t  the total past 4 is correct; the loop stops *after* reaching ≥ 4.\n76\t- `test_exact_three_one_drops_take_four_cards` — four MV-1 cards are needed to\n77\t  reach total 4; a fifth MV-1 card stays in the library.\n78\t- `test_small_library_below_four_is_emptied` — a library totalling < 4 MV is\n79\t  fully exiled and the loop terminates (does not hang or raise).\n80\t- `test_empty_library_is_safe_noop` — empty library exiles nothing, no raise.\n81\t  (Defensive guard; green against the stub by design.)\n82\t- `test_zero_mana_value_card_does_not_stop_the_loop` — a `{0}` card adds 0, so\n83\t  the loop must keep going until cumulative MV actually reaches 4.\n84\t- `test_exiled_cards_leave_the_library` — exiled cards are removed from the\n85\t  library; untouched cards remain.\n86\t\n87\t### `TestFreeCastFromExile` (clause 2)\n88\t\n89\t- `test_declining_leaves_all_cards_in_exile` — declining every cast offer\n90\t  leaves the whole exiled pile in exile and puts nothing on the stack.\n91\t- `test_lands_among_exiled_are_never_cast` — a land in the exiled pile can\n92\t  never be cast (lands are not spells); even accepting every offer leaves the\n93\t  land in exile and never on the battlefield. Robust regardless of the exact\n94\t  selection API.\n95\t- `test_casting_a_chosen_spell_moves_it_out_of_exile` — accepting the offer for\n96\t  an exiled instant casts it for free: the card leaves the library (exiled) and\n97\t  then leaves exile (cast). Assumes the `choose_yes_no` selection convention.\n98\t- `test_free_cast_does_not_require_mana` — the cast costs no mana: with an empty\n99\t  pool the exiled spell is still exiled and then cast.\n100\t\n101\t### `TestParadigmSelfExile` (clause 3 — self-exile)\n102\t\n103\t- `test_resolution_via_full_pipeline_exiles_the_spell` — casting through the\n104\t  real pipeline routes the resolved Capstone to exile, not the graveyard\n105\t  (\"Then exile this spell\").\n106\t\n107\t### `TestParadigmDelayedCopy` (clause 3 — delayed free copy)\n108\t\n109\t- `test_first_resolution_schedules_a_main_phase_effect` — the first resolution\n110\t  registers a deferred main-phase effect for the controller.\n111\t- `test_scheduled_copy_effect_targets_the_precombat_main_phase` — the scheduled\n112\t  effect is for the controller and carries the precombat flag (Paradigm fires\n113\t  at precombat main phases).\n114\t- `test_precombat_main_phase_consults_player_for_a_copy` — firing the\n115\t  controller's precombat main-phase event runs the scheduled effect and\n116\t  consults the controller (\"you may cast a copy\"); declining casts nothing.\n117\t- `test_paradigm_copy_offer_recurs_each_precombat_main_phase` — Paradigm is a\n118\t  *recurring* delayed trigger (\"each of your first main phases\"); after firing\n119\t  one main phase and declining, a scheduled effect for the controller must\n120\t  still be present for the next one (it is not a single-use one-shot).\n121\t\n122\t## Edge cases deliberately covered\n123\t\n124\t- Cumulative-MV boundary: exactly 4, over 4, and a {0}-MV card that must not\n125\t  short-circuit the loop.\n126\t- Library smaller than needed and a fully empty library (no hang, no raise).\n127\t- Lands among the exiled pile cannot be cast.\n128\t- Free cast requires no mana (empty pool).\n129\t- Paradigm self-exile via the resolution pipeline.\n130\t- Paradigm recurrence across multiple main phases (vs one-shot).\n131\t\n132\t## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n133\t\n134\t- **Exact free-cast selection API** — the spec mandates \"you may cast any number\n135\t  of spells from among them,\" but the engine has no canonical surface for a\n136\t  multi-select / repeated cast offer. The positive cast tests assume the\n137\t  `choose_yes_no`-per-eligible-spell convention used by `cards/sos/sos_1`. This\n138\t  residual ambiguity is recorded in `untestable.json`. The decline path and the\n139\t  lands-never-cast invariant are API-agnostic and remain robustly covered.\n140\t- **Whether the Paradigm copy itself self-exiles / re-triggers** — \"create a\n141\t  copy ... cast the copy\" produces a copy that is itself a Capstone-named\n142\t  spell. Whether resolving the copy re-schedules Paradigm a second time is a\n143\t  rules nuance (the original delayed trigger is what recurs); over-asserting it\n144\t  would constrain a reasonable implementation. Recurrence of the *delayed\n145\t  trigger* is covered; the copy's own re-trigger is left out.\n146\t- **Opponent interaction / countering the freed spells on the stack** — out of\n147\t  scope for this card's local behaviour; covered by engine tests.\n148\t- **{X} spells among the exiled pile** — `ManaCost.cmc` treats X as 0\n149\t  (engine-defined), and Improvisation Capstone's own cost has no X; no\n150\t  card-specific behaviour to test here.\n151\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"8bd78947-31c9-460a-a518-a91a08e614c3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:04:16.593Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — SOS 120 Improvisation Capstone\n\n## Card under test\n\n`{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson, mythic, with the **Paradigm** keyword.\n\nOracle text:\n\n> Exile cards from the top of your library until you exile cards with total\n> mana value 4 or greater. You may cast any number of spells from among them\n> without paying their mana costs.\n> Paradigm (Then exile this spell. After you first resolve a spell with this\n> name, you may cast a copy of it from exile without paying its mana cost at\n> the beginning of each of your first main phases.)\n\nThree distinct behaviours, plus the static card identity:\n\n1. **Exile-until-MV-4** — exile cards one at a time off the top of the library,\n   stopping as soon as the cumulative mana value of the exiled pile reaches 4\n   (CR-style \"until\" loop). The boundary card may push the total over 4.\n2. **Free-cast from among the exiled pile** — the controller *may* cast any\n   number of the exiled *spells* (nonland cards) without paying mana costs.\n   Lands cannot be cast. Declining leaves the cards in exile.\n3. **Paradigm** — \"Then exile this spell.\" (the resolved Capstone goes to exile\n   instead of the graveyard), and after the controller first resolves a spell\n   with this name, a delayed effect lets them cast a free copy from exile at\n   the beginning of *each* of their first (precombat) main phases (CR 702.192a).\n\n## Conventions used\n\n- Imports follow the standard SOS shape: card from\n  `cards.sos.sos_120.card_impl`, base classes from `engine.card`, types from\n  `engine.types`, helpers from `test_utils`.\n- `_set_library(game, player, cards)` loads the library with index `-1` as the\n  top (matches `ZoneContainer.add(position=\"top\")` appending — confirmed in\n  `engine/zones.py`).\n- The \"you may cast\" clause is exercised through the `DeterministicPlayer`\n  decision interface (`choose_yes_no` / `choose_card`), matching the\n  established \"you may free-cast\" pattern in `cards/sos/sos_1` (The Dawning\n  Archaic). `_decline_free_casts` pre-scripts a generous run of `False` answers\n  so exile-focused tests are not derailed by the cast-offer prompts.\n- The Paradigm delayed trigger is verified through the engine's documented\n  delayed/one-shot main-phase mechanism (KEY_DECISIONS sos_57):\n  `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect` +\n  `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, fired directly in tests.\n- Self-exile of the resolved spell is verified through the full casting\n  pipeline (`test_utils.cast_spell`), which honours the\n  `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` opt-in documented in KEY_DECISIONS sos_1.\n\n## Test file\n\n`cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n\n### `TestImprovisationCapstoneProperties` (static identity)\n\n- `test_name` — name is \"Improvisation Capstone\".\n- `test_is_sorcery` — is a `Sorcery` and carries `CardType.SORCERY`.\n- `test_mana_cost` — cost is `{5}{R}{R}`.\n- `test_has_lesson_subtype` — has the \"Lesson\" subtype (type line).\n- `test_has_paradigm_keyword_or_marker` — advertises Paradigm. Paradigm is not\n  an evergreen `Keyword` flag, so this accepts a card-level marker attribute\n  (`paradigm`/`has_paradigm`) or the word in `rules_text`.\n- `test_is_red` — colors include \"R\" (explicit-colors convention, sos_13).\n- `test_not_a_permanent_type` — a sorcery must not carry permanent card types.\n  (Passes against the stub today — it is a guard that must remain true after\n  implementation, not a red-phase driver.)\n\n### `TestExileUntilManaValueFour` (clause 1)\n\n- `test_exiles_until_total_mana_value_reaches_four` — two MV-2 cards on top hit\n  total 4 exactly; the third (deeper) card is untouched and stays in library.\n- `test_single_high_value_card_stops_immediately` — a single MV-4 card stops\n  the loop after one exile; the next card stays in the library.\n- `test_total_mana_value_can_exceed_four` — the boundary card (MV 5) pushing\n  the total past 4 is correct; the loop stops *after* reaching ≥ 4.\n- `test_exact_three_one_drops_take_four_cards` — four MV-1 cards are needed to\n  reach total 4; a fifth MV-1 card stays in the library.\n- `test_small_library_below_four_is_emptied` — a library totalling < 4 MV is\n  fully exiled and the loop terminates (does not hang or raise).\n- `test_empty_library_is_safe_noop` — empty library exiles nothing, no raise.\n  (Defensive guard; green against the stub by design.)\n- `test_zero_mana_value_card_does_not_stop_the_loop` — a `{0}` card adds 0, so\n  the loop must keep going until cumulative MV actually reaches 4.\n- `test_exiled_cards_leave_the_library` — exiled cards are removed from the\n  library; untouched cards remain.\n\n### `TestFreeCastFromExile` (clause 2)\n\n- `test_declining_leaves_all_cards_in_exile` — declining every cast offer\n  leaves the whole exiled pile in exile and puts nothing on the stack.\n- `test_lands_among_exiled_are_never_cast` — a land in the exiled pile can\n  never be cast (lands are not spells); even accepting every offer leaves the\n  land in exile and never on the battlefield. Robust regardless of the exact\n  selection API.\n- `test_casting_a_chosen_spell_moves_it_out_of_exile` — accepting the offer for\n  an exiled instant casts it for free: the card leaves the library (exiled) and\n  then leaves exile (cast). Assumes the `choose_yes_no` selection convention.\n- `test_free_cast_does_not_require_mana` — the cast costs no mana: with an empty\n  pool the exiled spell is still exiled and then cast.\n\n### `TestParadigmSelfExile` (clause 3 — self-exile)\n\n- `test_resolution_via_full_pipeline_exiles_the_spell` — casting through the\n  real pipeline routes the resolved Capstone to exile, not the graveyard\n  (\"Then exile this spell\").\n\n### `TestParadigmDelayedCopy` (clause 3 — delayed free copy)\n\n- `test_first_resolution_schedules_a_main_phase_effect` — the first resolution\n  registers a deferred main-phase effect for the controller.\n- `test_scheduled_copy_effect_targets_the_precombat_main_phase` — the scheduled\n  effect is for the controller and carries the precombat flag (Paradigm fires\n  at precombat main phases).\n- `test_precombat_main_phase_consults_player_for_a_copy` — firing the\n  controller's precombat main-phase event runs the scheduled effect and\n  consults the controller (\"you may cast a copy\"); declining casts nothing.\n- `test_paradigm_copy_offer_recurs_each_precombat_main_phase` — Paradigm is a\n  *recurring* delayed trigger (\"each of your first main phases\"); after firing\n  one main phase and declining, a scheduled effect for the controller must\n  still be present for the next one (it is not a single-use one-shot).\n\n## Edge cases deliberately covered\n\n- Cumulative-MV boundary: exactly 4, over 4, and a {0}-MV card that must not\n  short-circuit the loop.\n- Library smaller than needed and a fully empty library (no hang, no raise).\n- Lands among the exiled pile cannot be cast.\n- Free cast requires no mana (empty pool).\n- Paradigm self-exile via the resolution pipeline.\n- Paradigm recurrence across multiple main phases (vs one-shot).\n\n## Edge cases NOT covered (and why)\n\n- **Exact free-cast selection API** — the spec mandates \"you may cast any number\n  of spells from among them,\" but the engine has no canonical surface for a\n  multi-select / repeated cast offer. The positive cast tests assume the\n  `choose_yes_no`-per-eligible-spell convention used by `cards/sos/sos_1`. This\n  residual ambiguity is recorded in `untestable.json`. The decline path and the\n  lands-never-cast invariant are API-agnostic and remain robustly covered.\n- **Whether the Paradigm copy itself self-exiles / re-triggers** — \"create a\n  copy ... cast the copy\" produces a copy that is itself a Capstone-named\n  spell. Whether resolving the copy re-schedules Paradigm a second time is a\n  rules nuance (the original delayed trigger is what recurs); over-asserting it\n  would constrain a reasonable implementation. Recurrence of the *delayed\n  trigger* is covered; the copy's own re-trigger is left out.\n- **Opponent interaction / countering the freed spells on the stack** — out of\n  scope for this card's local behaviour; covered by engine tests.\n- **{X} spells among the exiled pile** — `ManaCost.cmc` treats X as 0\n  (engine-defined), and Improvisation Capstone's own cost has no X; no\n  card-specific behaviour to test here.\n","numLines":151,"startLine":1,"totalLines":151}}}
