{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0149bGzoJm7vGbHTy62K3vJp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent conventions and decisions across runs. Append-only.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: \"exile instead of graveyard\" for free-cast spells (sos_1)\n6\tFor a non-permanent spell with \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\n7\texile it instead\": set `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell\n8\tobject before casting it. `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` honors this opt-in\n9\tflag and routes the resolving instant/sorcery from the stack to `Zone.EXILE`\n10\tinstead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, then clears the flag (one-shot). Additive and\n11\tbackward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /\n12\timpulse effects with the same rider.\n13\t\n14\t## Engine: coin flips + skip-turn support; planeswalker conventions (sos_97)\n15\t- Coin flips: `engine.game.flip_coin(game, player=None) -> bool` (True=heads) and\n16\t  `engine.game.flip_coins(game, n, player=None) -> int` (heads count).\n17\t  Deterministic injection order: (1) `game._forced_coin_flips` (list/deque of\n18\t  booleans, consumed from the FRONT); (2) `game.rng` (random.Random-compatible,\n19\t  `rng.random() < 0.5`); (3) module `random`. Cards record their heads count on\n20\t  an attribute (e.g. `pw._last_heads`) for assertion.\n21\t- Skip turns: `Player.skipped_turns: int` (default 0). Honored by\n22\t  `GameState.advance_phase` via `_select_next_active_player`: while the next\n23\t  player has `skipped_turns > 0`, decrement it, consume the turn slot, and move\n24\t  to the next candidate (bounded guard against infinite skip). `extra_turns`\n25\t  FIFO behavior preserved. Use `target.skipped_turns += X` for \"skips their next\n26\t  X turns\" (CR 614.10).\n27\t- Planeswalkers: subclass `Planeswalker` (engine/card.py); set `starting_loyalty`,\n28\t  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtype, explicit `self.colors`. `get_loyalty_abilities()`\n29\t  returns `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)` closures\n30\t  `(game)->None` reading `pw.controller`. Targeted abilities read\n31\t  `pw._resolve_target` (single) / `pw._resolve_targets` (list). \"You may\" /\n32\t  per-card decisions (e.g. surveil keep/bin) via controller `choose_yes_no`;\n33\t  discards via `choose_card`. (Convention from FDN Kaito/Vivien/Liliana.)\n34\t- Surveil N: look at top N library cards, bin any number (per-card `choose_yes_no`),\n35\t  rest stay on top in order; fewer than N or empty library is a safe no-op.\n36\t\n37\t## Engine: mana-spent tracking, delayed main-phase triggers, spell/ability marker (sos_57)\n38\t- `card.mana_spent: int` — set by `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` to the\n39\t  converted mana actually paid (after cost reduction, `effective_cost.cmc`),\n40\t  analogous to `card.colors_spent`; `cast_spell_free` sets 0. Read via\n41\t  `getattr(card, \"mana_spent\", 0)`. Use for any \"amount of mana spent to cast\"\n42\t  rider. (Known gap: ignores {X} payments — would under-count X-spells.)\n43\t- `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, controller, precombat=True)` in\n44\t  `engine/events.py`, fired by `engine/turn.py` on entering precombat/postcombat\n45\t  main phases. Paired with `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(\n46\t  controller, callback, *, precombat=True)` (registry on GameState; delivery via\n47\t  `engine/deferred.py::deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects`, run SYNCHRONOUSLY\n48\t  inside `TriggerManager.fire_event` for that event type). This is the general\n49\t  \"at the beginning of your next main phase, do X once\" mechanism. A test fires\n50\t  it directly: `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game,\n51\t  BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=ctrl, controller=ctrl, precombat=True))`.\n52\t  Effects are one-shot (removed on delivery).\n53\t- `StackObject.is_spell: bool` (additive, default False) — set True only in the\n54\t  casting pipeline (`cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free`, `copy_spell`). Abilities on\n55\t  the stack reuse their source permanent's `card_types`, so to distinguish a\n56\t  SPELL from an ability on the stack (e.g. for \"counter target spell\"), check\n57\t  `getattr(stack_obj, \"is_spell\", False)` rather than inspecting `card_types`.\n58\t\n59\t## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\n60\tThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n61\t(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n62\t- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n63\t  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n64\t- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n65\t  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n66\t  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n67\t  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n68\t  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n69\t  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n70\t- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n71\t  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n72\t  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n73\t  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n74\t\n75\t## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\n76\tThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\n77\tstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\n78\tidentity must be observable.\n79\t\n80\t## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)\n81\tOverride `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine\n82\tclamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in\n83\t`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so no manual\n84\tclamping is needed. The hook may read `self.controller` (engine sets it before\n85\tquerying).\n86\t\n87\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MgVHaaugGQm27LxaZDymC1","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"ce93e64a-3269-4a50-8054-a6732b5680e0","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:06:37.684Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_120 (retry)"}
