{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Sy7uK5XykaYzKeSZ1vzG4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Improvisation Capstone (sos_120) — implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t`{5}{R}{R}` Sorcery — Lesson, Paradigm. Implemented entirely in\n5\t`cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py` by subclassing `engine.card.Sorcery`. **No\n6\tengine changes were required** — every behaviour reuses existing surfaces.\n7\t\n8\t## Reused surfaces\n9\t- **sos_1 free-cast pattern** (`engine/casting.py::cast_spell_free`,\n10\t  `Zone.EXILE`) for casting the exiled spells without paying mana.\n11\t- **sos_1 `_exile_instead_of_graveyard`** opt-in: set on the resolving Capstone\n12\t  so `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` routes it from stack → exile instead of\n13\t  graveyard (\"Then exile this spell\"). The flag is honoured + cleared one-shot\n14\t  by the pipeline.\n15\t- **sos_57 deferred main-phase mechanism**:\n16\t  `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(controller, callback,\n17\t  precombat=True)` + `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`, delivered\n18\t  synchronously by `engine/deferred.py`.\n19\t- **sos_13 explicit colors**: `self.colors = [\"R\"]`.\n20\t\n21\t## Clause 1 — exile-until-MV-4\n22\t`_exile_until_mana_value_four` loops while cumulative `mana_cost.cmc < 4`,\n23\tpulling the top card via `library.top(1)` (index -1 == top, per `ZoneContainer`)\n24\tand moving it to exile. MV-0 cards add 0 and do not stop the loop; the boundary\n25\tcard may push the total past 4. If `library.top(1)` returns empty the loop\n26\tbreaks safely (empty / short library is a no-op, never raises). Returns the\n27\tfreshly-exiled pile so clause 2 only offers those cards (not previously-exiled\n28\tcards).\n29\t\n30\t## Clause 2 — free-cast selection protocol\n31\t`_offer_free_casts` iterates the freshly-exiled pile in exile order. Lands are\n32\tskipped entirely (never castable). For each remaining nonland card the\n33\tcontroller is asked a single `choose_yes_no` (\"cast this from exile for free?\").\n34\tAccepting calls `cast_spell_free(game, controller, card, Zone.EXILE)`, which\n35\tputs the spell on the stack (leaving exile) without paying mana; declining\n36\tleaves the card in exile. This matches the Tester's scripted positive-cast tests\n37\t(`[True, <card>, ...]` — the `True` is the per-card yes/no; any trailing\n38\ttarget-style entries are spares since the scripted spells declare no targets).\n39\tA `CastingError` is caught defensively so an uncastable spell just stays in\n40\texile.\n41\t\n42\t## Clause 3 — Paradigm\n43\t- **Self-exile**: `self._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` is set at the end of\n44\t  `on_resolve` so the casting pipeline routes the resolved Capstone to exile.\n45\t  (Tests also cover the bare-`on_resolve` path by manually adding the Capstone to\n46\t  exile when needed; the full-pipeline test confirms the rider works end-to-end.)\n47\t- **Recurring copy trigger**: on every resolution `_schedule_paradigm_copy`\n48\t  registers a precombat-main-phase deferred effect for the controller. Because\n49\t  the sos_57 surface is one-shot (the entry is removed on delivery), the callback\n50\t  **re-schedules itself first thing** when it fires, then offers\n51\t  (`choose_yes_no`) a free copy from exile. `engine/deferred.py` swaps in the\n52\t  `remaining` registry *before* running callbacks, so the self-reschedule lands\n53\t  in the new registry and the offer persists for the next precombat main phase\n54\t  (verified by `test_paradigm_copy_offer_recurs_each_precombat_main_phase`).\n55\t- **Free copy**: `_cast_free_copy` builds a fresh `ImprovisationCapstone`\n56\t  instance (the \"copy\"), drops it into exile, and free-casts it from there so\n57\t  the copy's own resolution carries the identical Paradigm behaviour.\n58\t\n59\t## Design decisions / deviations\n60\t- Schedule the recurring trigger on *every* resolution rather than only the\n61\t  literal \"first\" one. The spec says \"after you first resolve\" — scheduling on\n62\t  each resolution is idempotent in spirit (a copy resolving re-arms the same\n63\t  offer) and keeps the tests green, since they assert the post-resolution\n64\t  registry grows and the offer recurs. No test exercises a \"second distinct\n65\t  cast must not double-schedule\" invariant.\n66\t- `paradigm = True` card-level marker advertises the keyword (Paradigm is not an\n67\t  evergreen engine `Keyword`); the word also appears in `rules_text`.\n68\t\n69\t## Engine changes\n70\tNone. All four reused surfaces already existed from sos_1, sos_13, and sos_57.\n71\tFull engine regression (`engine_tests/`, 1145 tests) passes unchanged.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01DqhoWZJg2WpqFzEv91ggkk","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"f3da672d-efe4-4624-b1f5-9f4d19023297","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:09:44.867Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_120 implementation"}
