{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RFxP2yczWp8yqdfWh2Ji1g","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 175,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"Paradigm recurring-offer multiplication bug. _schedule_paradigm_copy is called from on_resolve on EVERY resolution, and the scheduled callback also self-reschedules. This is fine for a single chain, but _cast_free_copy free-casts a brand-new ImprovisationCapstone copy whose own on_resolve (reached when that copy later resolves off the stack) calls _schedule_paradigm_copy AGAIN, registering a second independent self-perpetuating chain. Each accepted copy that resolves adds another chain, so after the mechanism is used the controller is offered the free copy multiple times per precombat main phase and the offers grow without bound across turns. The spec is 'you may cast A COPY ... at the beginning of EACH of your first main phases' (one offer per main phase). Guard against duplicate scheduling per controller (e.g. an idempotent 'already armed' flag on the controller/game, or do not re-arm from a copy's resolution) so exactly one recurring offer exists. The implementer's rationale acknowledges this is unguarded and untested; it is a genuine behavioral divergence, not just a style choice.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 207,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"Rules nuance (not tested, low impact): _cast_free_copy routes the resolved copy to exile via the inherited _exile_instead_of_graveyard rider in its on_resolve. Per CR 707.10/110.5g a copy of a spell ceases to exist as a state-based action when it would leave the stack rather than going to exile, so the copy lingering in exile is technically incorrect. The engine has no 'copy ceases to exist' surface, so this is acceptable for now; just noting it. It also feeds the duplicate-schedule issue flagged above.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 158,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"Minor: the per-card 'still in exile' re-check (game.get_exile(controller).contains(card)) is effectively dead because each freshly-exiled pile entry is distinct and a prior free cast moves a different card out. Harmless defensive code; no change required.\"\n19\t  }\n20\t]\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RzexvBRQZBgTXBf5ZRCymj","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"e1fa9776-2475-4e65-afb3-2ffac248232c","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:11:32.276Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_120 Paradigm scheduling"}
