{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a368bf118be2e6d91","tool_use_id":"toolu_01RzexvBRQZBgTXBf5ZRCymj","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":36462,"tool_uses":15,"duration_ms":75983},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"d8312693-a338-4b42-995f-75bd66195aab","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_013jcqBxFC1waYVDTXrMNnLE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011Y6h4pJYPwp1pAQDv1enbM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# sos_120 Improvisation Capstone — Revision rationale\n\n## Strict bug fixed (review.json index 0): Paradigm recurring-offer multiplication\n\n### Root cause\n`_schedule_paradigm_copy` was called from `on_resolve` on EVERY resolution, and\nthe scheduled callback also self-reschedules. That is correct for a single\nchain, but `_cast_free_copy` free-casts a brand-new `ImprovisationCapstone`\ninstance. When that copy later resolves off the stack, its own `on_resolve`\ncalled `_schedule_paradigm_copy` AGAIN, registering a second, independent,\nself-perpetuating chain. Each resolved copy added another chain, so the\ncontroller was offered the free copy multiple times per precombat main phase,\ngrowing without bound.\n\nThe spec is \"you may cast A COPY ... at the beginning of EACH of your first\nmain phases\" = exactly ONE recurring offer per controller.\n\n### Fix: idempotent per-controller arming guard\n`_schedule_paradigm_copy` now arms the recurring offer exactly once per\ncontroller using an additive, lazily-created guard set stored on the game\nstate:\n\n- Attribute name: `_improvisation_capstone_paradigm_armed`\n  (class constant `ImprovisationCapstone._PARADIGM_ARMED_ATTR`).\n- It holds the `set` of controllers for whom the recurring chain has already\n  been armed.\n\nLogic at the top of `_schedule_paradigm_copy`:\n\n1. Read (or lazily create) the guard set on the game state.\n2. If `controller in armed`, return immediately — do NOT add a second chain.\n3. Otherwise `armed.add(controller)` and proceed to schedule the single\n   self-rescheduling callback.\n\nBecause the guard is keyed by controller and checked before any scheduling:\n\n- The controller's FIRST resolution of a spell with this name arms exactly one\n  recurring chain.\n- Every subsequent resolution — and crucially the resolution of any free copy\n  cast via `_cast_free_copy` (which runs the same `on_resolve` -> \n  `_schedule_paradigm_copy`) — finds the controller already armed and is a\n  no-op for scheduling.\n\nThe single armed callback still re-schedules itself each precombat main phase\n(the deferred surface is one-shot), so the lone offer recurs. This keeps\n`test_paradigm_copy_offer_recurs_each_precombat_main_phase` passing: after\nfiring one precombat main phase and declining, exactly one scheduled effect for\nthe controller remains (the chain re-armed itself once), and it does not grow.\n\n### Why the guard lives on the game state, not the card instance\nEach cast/copy is a distinct `ImprovisationCapstone` instance, so a per-instance\nflag would not be shared across copies and could not prevent a copy's resolution\nfrom arming a second chain. Keying by controller on the shared game state is the\nonly place that survives across the original spell and all of its copies. The\nattribute is created lazily and additively; no engine source was modified.\n\n### Confirmation: exactly one recurring chain per controller\n- `pytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py -q` -> 24 passed (including the recurrence\n  test).\n- `pytest engine_tests/ -q` -> 1145 passed, no regressions.\n- By construction, the number of scheduled entries for a controller never\n  exceeds one: arming is gated by the per-controller guard, and the lone\n  callback removes-then-re-adds exactly one entry when it fires.\n\n## Advisories (not applied — explicitly allowed to skip)\n- Index 1 (copy lingering in exile per CR 707.10/110.5g): the engine has no\n  \"copy ceases to exist\" surface; left as-is, as the review notes it is\n  acceptable for now.\n- Index 2 (dead defensive `still in exile` re-check): harmless; left as-is.\n\nOther behavior (exile-until-MV-4, free-cast selection, Paradigm self-exile)\nis unchanged.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3570,"cache_read_input_tokens":32631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3570,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RzexvBRQZBgTXBf5ZRCymj","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"b8768c78-d55c-4913-a445-dd4fed4f6073","request_id":"req_011CbdYXaaR7uJiJc4uPc6kd","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_120 Paradigm scheduling"}
