{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RzexvBRQZBgTXBf5ZRCymj","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All outputs are in place and verified. The strict bug is fixed with an idempotent per-controller arming guard, all 24 card tests pass, and there are no engine regressions (1145 passed).\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/disagreements.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a368bf118be2e6d91 (use SendMessage with to: 'a368bf118be2e6d91' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 40144\ntool_uses: 19\nduration_ms: 103240</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"a514f69b-28c0-4461-aa2c-fd2843e548f3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:13:11.864Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are applying review feedback to a card you implemented. One STRICT correctness bug must be fixed; advisories are optional.\n\nCARD: sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone)\n- Implementation: `cards/sos/sos_120/card_impl.py`\n- Tests (do NOT modify, must keep all 24 passing): `cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py`\n- Review: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/review.json`\n- Prior diff: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl.diff`\n\nSTRICT bug to fix (review.json index 0) — Paradigm recurring-offer MULTIPLICATION:\n`_schedule_paradigm_copy` is called from `on_resolve` on EVERY resolution, and the scheduled callback also self-reschedules. When an accepted free COPY later resolves, its own `on_resolve` calls `_schedule_paradigm_copy` AGAIN, creating a SECOND independent self-perpetuating chain. Each resolved copy adds another chain, so the controller gets the free-copy offer multiple times per precombat main phase and the number of offers grows without bound. The spec is \"you may cast A COPY ... at the beginning of EACH of your first main phases\" = exactly ONE offer per precombat main phase.\n\nREQUIRED FIX:\n- Make Paradigm arming IDEMPOTENT per controller: arm the recurring offer exactly ONCE (on the controller's first resolution of a spell with this name), so there is exactly ONE recurring chain per controller. Subsequent resolutions — and especially the resolution of free copies — must NOT add another chain.\n- Implement with a per-controller \"already armed\" guard (e.g. a flag/set on the game state or controller, keyed by the card name or this effect). The single recurring chain must still re-schedule itself each precombat main phase (the test `test_paradigm_copy_offer_recurs_each_precombat_main_phase` must still pass: after firing one main phase and declining, a scheduled effect for the controller still exists — exactly one, not growing).\n- Keep all other behavior intact (exile-until-MV-4; free-cast selection; self-exile).\n\nOPTIONAL (advisories — ignore unless trivially safe): index 1 (copy lingering in exile per CR 707.10 — engine has no \"copy ceases to exist\" surface, leave it) and index 2 (dead defensive re-check — harmless, leave it).\n\nCONSTRAINTS:\n- Do NOT modify any test file, `engine_tests/`, or `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n- Engine changes should be unnecessary (guard can live on game state/controller as an additive attribute). If you touch engine, additive-only, no rename/move/delete, keep existing behavior.\n- If you genuinely disagree with the strict comment, record it in disagreements.json rather than silently ignoring it.\n\nTASK:\n1. Apply the idempotent-arming fix.\n2. `pytest cards/sos/sos_120/tests.py -q` — all 24 must still pass (especially the recurrence test).\n3. `pytest engine_tests/ -q` — no regressions.\n\nOUTPUT (into $CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120`):\n- `impl-revised.diff` — `git diff` of all current changes for this card.\n- `impl-revised-rationale.md` — how you made arming idempotent (the guard you used) and confirmation exactly one recurring chain exists per controller.\n- `disagreements.json` — JSON array of {\"review_comment_index\": <n>, \"reviewer_comment\": \"...\", \"implementer_justification\": \"...\"} for any strict comment NOT fully applied. Empty `[]` if you applied everything.\n- Keep `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` entry for `sos_120` accurate (upsert in place).\n\nReturn ONLY:\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: <N>\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/disagreements.json","agentId":"a368bf118be2e6d91","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All outputs are in place and verified. The strict bug is fixed with an idempotent per-controller arming guard, all 24 card tests pass, and there are no engine regressions (1145 passed).\n\nREVISION_DONE\ndisagreement_count: 0\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/impl-revised.diff\ndisagreements_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_120/disagreements.json"}],"totalDurationMs":103240,"totalTokens":40144,"totalToolUseCount":19,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484,"cache_read_input_tokens":39514,"output_tokens":144,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":484},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":144,"cache_read_input_tokens":39514,"cache_creation_input_tokens":484,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":484,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":7,"searchCount":1,"bashCount":8,"editFileCount":3,"linesAdded":115,"linesRemoved":11,"otherToolCount":0}}}
