{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01TEhURwJDot8F6h6oV3S7a7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013tShdw5BWVNVBaZQ53C8x9","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Write tests for sos_201","subagent_type":"Tester","prompt":"You are writing pytest tests (TDD red phase) for a single Magic: The Gathering card implementation.\n\nCARD: sos_201\n- Spec: `cards/sos/sos_201/card_spec.json` (read this for name, mana cost, oracle text, P/T, keywords, etc.)\n- Implementation stub you are testing against: `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`\n- Write your tests to: `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`\n\nCONVENTIONS TO DISCOVER:\n- Read `engine_tests/test_casting.py` and `engine_tests/test_triggers.py` for engine test conventions.\n- Read `test_utils.md` and `test_utils.py` for helpers like `create_game`, `set_board_state`.\n- Read FDN reference tests for style: `cards/fdn/fdn_13/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_142/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_205/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_215/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_244/tests.py`. Also read their `card_spec.json` and `card_impl.py`.\n- For any rules question, grep `RULEBOOK.txt` (see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n\nWORKSPACE RULES:\n- Read `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_MAP.md`, and `KEY_DECISIONS.md` first. KEY_DECISIONS has reusable conventions from earlier cards this run (coin flips/skip turns, mana_spent tracking, delayed/recurring main-phase triggers, StackObject.is_spell marker, planeswalker conventions, preparation cards, explicit colors attribute, exile-instead-of-graveyard, cost_reduction). Reuse those established surfaces where relevant and test against them.\n- Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n- Tests must import the card class from `cards.sos.sos_201.card_impl`.\n\nTASK:\n1. Read the spec and understand every clause of the oracle text.\n2. Write thorough pytest tests covering each distinct behavior/clause. Tests should FAIL before implementation (TDD red) but be correct against the spec and MTG rules.\n3. Follow existing test conventions exactly.\n\nOUTPUT (all into $CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201`):\n- `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` — the test file.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md` — what each test covers and why; note the card's mechanics.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-files.txt` — list of test file path(s), one per line.\n- If any requirement cannot be tested with the current engine/test API, write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/untestable.json` — JSON array of `{\"requirement\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"what_would_unblock\": \"...\"}`. Omit if everything is testable.\n\nReturn ONLY a short status summary: number of tests written, the test file path, and untestable_count (0 if none)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":206,"cache_read_input_tokens":159253,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":206},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"13c16a7f-c299-422b-9960-4a30b14591a0","request_id":"req_011CbdYciDSPKQjf4MAC6GzN"}
