{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013tShdw5BWVNVBaZQ53C8x9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"23 tests collected, all valid. Output files written. Final summary:\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\n- **test_files: 1** — `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`\n- **test_cases: 23** (20 fail in red phase as required; 3 pass trivially against the bare stub but assert correct, spec-faithful behavior that remains valid after implementation — fliers/reach can block a flier, and the loot trigger must not fire on the controller's own upkeep)\n- **rationale_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md`\n- **files_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-files.txt`\n- **untestable_count: 1**\n- **untestable_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/untestable.json`\n\nnotes: Covered static data (R/W legendary Elder Dragon, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5), flying+haste via engine `_can_attack`/`_can_block`, the granted miracle-{2} stamping contract on the controller's instants/sorceries, and the opponent-upkeep \"discard then draw\" trigger (registration, opponent-only condition, yes/no/empty-hand paths). The miracle *draw-time casting* timing is untestable — the engine has no alternative-cost-on-draw pipeline — and is recorded with an unblock path in `untestable.json`. The miracle granting tests assume a `grant_miracle(game)` method plus a `MIRACLE_COST` constant; this assumption is documented in the rationale so the Implementer can align."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab0208b1f81d2bafc (use SendMessage with to: 'ab0208b1f81d2bafc' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 101473\ntool_uses: 47\nduration_ms: 261391</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"7e3ac17d-453e-4765-b515-04fc27083c4f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:18:07.976Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"You are writing pytest tests (TDD red phase) for a single Magic: The Gathering card implementation.\n\nCARD: sos_201\n- Spec: `cards/sos/sos_201/card_spec.json` (read this for name, mana cost, oracle text, P/T, keywords, etc.)\n- Implementation stub you are testing against: `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`\n- Write your tests to: `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`\n\nCONVENTIONS TO DISCOVER:\n- Read `engine_tests/test_casting.py` and `engine_tests/test_triggers.py` for engine test conventions.\n- Read `test_utils.md` and `test_utils.py` for helpers like `create_game`, `set_board_state`.\n- Read FDN reference tests for style: `cards/fdn/fdn_13/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_142/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_205/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_215/tests.py`, `cards/fdn/fdn_244/tests.py`. Also read their `card_spec.json` and `card_impl.py`.\n- For any rules question, grep `RULEBOOK.txt` (see `skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n\nWORKSPACE RULES:\n- Read `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_MAP.md`, and `KEY_DECISIONS.md` first. KEY_DECISIONS has reusable conventions from earlier cards this run (coin flips/skip turns, mana_spent tracking, delayed/recurring main-phase triggers, StackObject.is_spell marker, planeswalker conventions, preparation cards, explicit colors attribute, exile-instead-of-graveyard, cost_reduction). Reuse those established surfaces where relevant and test against them.\n- Do NOT modify anything under `engine_tests/` or any `cards/fdn/**/tests.py`.\n- Tests must import the card class from `cards.sos.sos_201.card_impl`.\n\nTASK:\n1. Read the spec and understand every clause of the oracle text.\n2. Write thorough pytest tests covering each distinct behavior/clause. Tests should FAIL before implementation (TDD red) but be correct against the spec and MTG rules.\n3. Follow existing test conventions exactly.\n\nOUTPUT (all into $CARD_DIR = `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201`):\n- `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` — the test file.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md` — what each test covers and why; note the card's mechanics.\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-files.txt` — list of test file path(s), one per line.\n- If any requirement cannot be tested with the current engine/test API, write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/untestable.json` — JSON array of `{\"requirement\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"what_would_unblock\": \"...\"}`. Omit if everything is testable.\n\nReturn ONLY a short status summary: number of tests written, the test file path, and untestable_count (0 if none).","agentId":"ab0208b1f81d2bafc","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"23 tests collected, all valid. Output files written. Final summary:\n\nTESTS_WRITTEN\n- **test_files: 1** — `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`\n- **test_cases: 23** (20 fail in red phase as required; 3 pass trivially against the bare stub but assert correct, spec-faithful behavior that remains valid after implementation — fliers/reach can block a flier, and the loot trigger must not fire on the controller's own upkeep)\n- **rationale_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-rationale.md`\n- **files_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/test-files.txt`\n- **untestable_count: 1**\n- **untestable_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/untestable.json`\n\nnotes: Covered static data (R/W legendary Elder Dragon, {3}{R}{W}, 5/5), flying+haste via engine `_can_attack`/`_can_block`, the granted miracle-{2} stamping contract on the controller's instants/sorceries, and the opponent-upkeep \"discard then draw\" trigger (registration, opponent-only condition, yes/no/empty-hand paths). The miracle *draw-time casting* timing is untestable — the engine has no alternative-cost-on-draw pipeline — and is recorded with an unblock path in `untestable.json`. The miracle granting tests assume a `grant_miracle(game)` method plus a `MIRACLE_COST` constant; this assumption is documented in the rationale so the Implementer can align."}],"totalDurationMs":261391,"totalTokens":101473,"totalToolUseCount":47,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":308,"cache_read_input_tokens":100628,"ou