{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's explicit request: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`. Each card directory contains a `card_spec.json` with the card's details and a `card_impl.py` template to fill in. Use the completed FDN cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as implementation examples. Refer to `RULEBOOK.txt` for the full deep-reference rules text. For engine API discovery, read the source modules directly — they have rich docstrings: `engine/card.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/replacement_effects.py`, `engine/zones.py`. You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics. The existing code base may not be perfect, you are free to make changes that don't break current behavior.\"\n   \n   CRITICAL CONSTRAINT (verbatim): \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/. These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score — it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are correct.\"\n\n   I am operating as a Coordinator that delegates to Tester/Implementer/Reviewer subagents in a TDD loop, one card at a time.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - MTG engine in Python; cards subclass `Creature`/`Instant`/`Sorcery`/`Planeswalker` from `engine/card.py`.\n   - TDD workflow: Tester (red) → arbitrate untestable items → Implementer (green) → Reviewer → revision rounds → commit.\n   - Engine additive-only rule: may add methods/classes/files and modify function bodies; MUST NOT rename/move/delete existing engine symbols.\n   - `cost_reduction(game)` hook; engine clamps to generic via `get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`).\n   - Converge via `colors_spent`/`last_payment_colors`; total `mana_spent` tracking added.\n   - Triggers: `EntersBattlefieldTriggeredEvent`, `AttacksTriggeredEvent`, `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` (fired with no player arg → read `game.active_player`), new `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`.\n   - `cast_spell_free(game, player, card, zone)` for free casts; `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` opt-in flag.\n   - Delayed/one-shot deferred effects: `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(controller, callback, *, precombat=True)` + `engine/deferred.py`; recurring via self-rescheduling callback (must be idempotently armed).\n   - `StackObject.is_spell` marker to distinguish spells from abilities.\n   - Coin flips: `flip_coin/flip_coins` with deterministic injection (`game._forced_coin_flips`, then `game.rng`).\n   - Skip turns: `Player.skipped_turns` honored by `_select_next_active_player`.\n   - Planeswalker conventions: `get_loyalty_abilities()` → `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)`; `pw._resolve_target`/`pw._resolve_targets`; `choose_yes_no` decisions.\n   - Preparation cards (CR 722): `prepared`/`is_prepared`, `make_prepare_spell(game)`, `cast_prepare_spell(game, target)`.\n   - Explicit `self.colors` (engine has no native colors field).\n   - Standard MTG counting: an entering creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB resolves (counts toward \"you\").\n   - Use `python3` (not `python`); run `pytest cards/sos/sos_N/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` to verify.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md` — per-run decision log; contains untestable resolutions for sos_13, sos_57, sos_97, sos_120, and (just added) sos_201. Most recent edit added the sos_201 miracle decision.\n   - `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` — persistent conventions (append-only). Contains entries for: exile-instead-of-graveyard + cost_reduction (sos_1); recurring main-phase delayed trigger + Paradigm (sos_120); coin flips + skip-turn + planeswalker + surveil (sos_97); mana-spent + delayed main-phase triggers + StackObject.is_spell (sos_57); preparation cards (CR 722) + explicit colors (sos_13).\n   - `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` — `{\"cards\": [...]}`; each card upserts an entry. Externally modified for sos_1 (intentional, not to revert).\n   - `engine/casting.py` — modified: `_resolve_spell` honors `_exile_instead_of_graveyard`; `mana_spent` tracking; `is_spell` set in cast_spell/cast_spell_free.\n   - `engine/events.py` — added `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, controller, precombat=True)`.\n   - `engine/game_state.py` — `schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect`, `_select_next_active_player` (honors skipped_turns), `_advance_rotation_index`.\n   - `engine/deferred.py` — new file `deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects`.\n   - `engine/triggers.py` — synchronous delivery for BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent in `fire_event`.\n   - `engine/turn.py` — fires BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent on entering main phases.\n   - `engine/stack.py` — added `StackObject.is_spell` (default False).\n   - `engine/game.py` — `flip_coin`/`flip_coins`; `Player.cards_drawn_this_turn` exists.\n   - `engine/player.py` — `Player.skipped_turns`.\n   - Committed cards: sos_1, sos_4, sos_13, sos_57, sos_97, sos_120 (all in `cards/sos/sos_N/card_impl.py` + `tests.py`).\n   - sos_201 files (in progress): `cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` written (23 tests); `cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py` is still the stub.\n   - `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/` — contains test-rationale.md, test-files.txt (`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`), untestable.json (1 item: miracle draw-time casting).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - sos_13 counting-model bug: Implementer's first pass used a non-standard \"entering creature doesn't count\" model to satisfy a buggy Tester test. Fixed by reading the test file directly, determining standard MTG counting is correct, directing the Tester (re-invocation) to fix the buggy board state (opp=3) and the Implementer (final pass) to remove the subtraction. All passed.\n   - sos_57 strict review finding: `_is_spell()` couldn't distinguish spells from abilities on the stack (abilities reuse source card_types). Fixed via revision round: Implementer added additive `StackObject.is_spell` flag set only in casting pipeline.\n   - sos_120 \"API Error: Overloaded\" on first Implementer invocation (0 tool uses, nothing ran). Fixed by retrying with a fresh self-contained Implementer invocation (treated as transient, not a subagent failure). Retry succeeded.\n   - sos_120 strict review finding: Paradigm offer multiplication (every resolution + resolved copies arm new self-perpetuating chains → unbounded offers). Fixed via revision round: idempotent per-controller arming guard.\n   - Stray `FILES_MODIFIED.json.tmp` files left by Implementer subagents — cleaned with `rm -f FILES_MODIFIED.json.tmp` before committing (sos_13, sos_57, sos_97).\n   - `python: command not found` — switched to `python3` for all pytest runs.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Successfully implemented 6 of 10 cards with full engine support added for: exile-instead-of-graveyard, mana_spent tracking, beginning-of-main-phase events, delayed/recurring deferred effects, StackObject.is_spell, coin flips, skip-turns, planeswalker abilities, preparation cards. Each card committed only after 0 strict review findings (or resolved via revision) and full suite green. Arbitrated untestable items by building reusable engine surfaces (option a) rather than accepting partial coverage, maximizing grader alignment.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Initial task message (quoted verbatim in section 1 above), including the CRITICAL constraint about not modifying `workspace/engine_tests/`.\n   - System reminder: \"/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json was modified, either by the user or by a linter. This change was intentional, so make sure to take it into account as you proceed (ie. don't revert