n on a deterministic draw-time test. I have confirmed test-files.txt contents (`/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md` capturing the miracle-pipeline design (matching the RUN_DECISIONS.md decision just recorded), then invoke the Implementer subagent to implement Lorehold and the additive miracle engine support, then re-invoke the Tester once for the deterministic draw-time miracle test, per the just-recorded decision: \"Spend the single Tester re-invocation on a deterministic draw-time test (first-card draw with Lorehold out → offered → yes casts for {2}, pool −2, card leaves hand; decline keeps it; non-first-card draw doesn't offer).\" This directly continues the sos_201 work (card 7 of 10) before proceeding to sos_226, sos_245, sos_257.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/node/.claude/projects/-workspace/7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"ad65eff2-e71a-4acb-8309-e9ee459e32e3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:21:10.096Z","isSynthetic":true}
