{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01HcL3cztYVn4AWRJUmGGNeV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019S1QWQpK1DWbMKx8DenPgL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n\nThe Tester reported ONE untestable requirement (miracle draw-time casting). Per\nthe run decision, you (Implementer) must build a focused, ADDITIVE,\ndeterministic miracle pipeline so the draw-time behavior becomes testable. Build\nexactly the surface below so the to-be-extended Tester probe and the existing\ntests align.\n\n## Card: Lorehold, the Historian\n- `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, colors R/W.\n- Subclass `Creature`. Set `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n  explicit `self.colors = [\"R\",\"W\"]` (per KEY_DECISIONS sos_13 convention).\n- Keywords: `Keyword.FLYING` and `Keyword.HASTE`.\n- The existing tests assume:\n  - `MIRACLE_COST` constant on the card == `{2}` (generic 2).\n  - `grant_miracle(game)` method stamps `miracle_cost == {2}` onto every instant\n    and sorcery card in the CONTROLLER's hand; leaves non-cast types (creatures,\n    lands) and the OPPONENT's hand untouched.\n- Opponent-upkeep ability: register exactly one\n  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger sourced from the card, controlled by\n  its controller. `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` is fired with NO player arg,\n  so the condition must read `game.active_player` and fire ONLY when the active\n  player is an opponent (not the controller). On resolution: \"you may discard a\n  card. If you do, draw a card.\" Use controller `choose_yes_no`; on yes, discard\n  the chosen card (via `choose_card`) to graveyard and draw one. Empty hand is a\n  safe no-op (no draw, no raise).\n\n## Additive miracle engine pipeline (build this)\n1. `card.miracle_cost: ManaCost | None` — default None on the card base or set\n   per-card via getattr-safe access. Stamped onto eligible hand cards by\n   `grant_miracle`.\n2. An alternative-cost cast surface in `engine/casting.py`. Prefer a minimal,\n   backward-compatible extension: e.g. `cast_spell(game, player, card, zone,\n   alternative_cost=None)` paying the supplied `alternative_cost` ManaCost\n   instead of `card.mana_cost` when provided, OR a dedicated\n   `cast_for_alternative_cost(...)`/`cast_miracle(...)` helper. Keep the default\n   path byte-for-byte unchanged (alternative_cost defaults None → existing\n   behavior). Set `mana_spent` to the alt cost's cmc when an alt cost is paid.\n3. A draw hook in `draw_card` that is a COMPLETE no-op except when BOTH:\n   (a) it is the drawing player's FIRST card drawn this turn — use the existing\n       `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` counter (check BEFORE/at the moment it\n       becomes 1, consistent with however the counter is incremented), AND\n   (b) a permanent the drawing player controls grants miracle to the drawn card —\n       query a capability `grants_miracle_to(self, card) -> ManaCost | None` on\n       controlled permanents (Lorehold returns `{2}` for instants/sorceries,\n       else None).\n   When both hold: stamp `card.miracle_cost = {2}` and offer the controller\n   `choose_yes_no`; on yes, cast the drawn card for its miracle cost via the\n   alternative-cost surface (card leaves hand, pool reduced by 2). On no/none of\n   the conditions, the hook does nothing — NO prompt, NO state change — so\n   existing engine tests (where nothing grants miracle) see zero behavioral\n   change. Verify full engine regression stays green.\n\n## Modeling simplification (document in rationale)\nThe miracle \"window\" is modeled as an immediate at-draw offer rather than the\nfull reveal → triggered ability → cast-anytime-before-next-step. This is\nacceptable and deterministically testable for this engine.\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify any test file in `test-files.txt`. If a test is genuinely wrong,\n  return DISPUTE.\n- Additive engine changes only: do not rename/move/delete existing engine\n  symbols. Default code paths must be unchanged when miracle is not in play.\n- Reuse existing surfaces where possible (`cards_drawn_this_turn`,\n  `choose_yes_no`, `choose_card`, `mana_spent`).\n- Run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` and make\n  all sos_201 tests pass while keeping engine_tests green.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14712,"cache_read_input_tokens":17074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14712},"output_tokens":41,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"e1073cab-f28b-4cd5-892b-bd0cb9b961cd","request_id":"req_011CbdZCLVBV6vxMuwceWvaB"}
