{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ADj3iVkX2g4t5fMikApEos","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_201 (Lorehold, the Historian)\n2\t\n3\tThe Tester reported ONE untestable requirement (miracle draw-time casting). Per\n4\tthe run decision, you (Implementer) must build a focused, ADDITIVE,\n5\tdeterministic miracle pipeline so the draw-time behavior becomes testable. Build\n6\texactly the surface below so the to-be-extended Tester probe and the existing\n7\ttests align.\n8\t\n9\t## Card: Lorehold, the Historian\n10\t- `{3}{R}{W}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, colors R/W.\n11\t- Subclass `Creature`. Set `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n12\t  explicit `self.colors = [\"R\",\"W\"]` (per KEY_DECISIONS sos_13 convention).\n13\t- Keywords: `Keyword.FLYING` and `Keyword.HASTE`.\n14\t- The existing tests assume:\n15\t  - `MIRACLE_COST` constant on the card == `{2}` (generic 2).\n16\t  - `grant_miracle(game)` method stamps `miracle_cost == {2}` onto every instant\n17\t    and sorcery card in the CONTROLLER's hand; leaves non-cast types (creatures,\n18\t    lands) and the OPPONENT's hand untouched.\n19\t- Opponent-upkeep ability: register exactly one\n20\t  `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` trigger sourced from the card, controlled by\n21\t  its controller. `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent` is fired with NO player arg,\n22\t  so the condition must read `game.active_player` and fire ONLY when the active\n23\t  player is an opponent (not the controller). On resolution: \"you may discard a\n24\t  card. If you do, draw a card.\" Use controller `choose_yes_no`; on yes, discard\n25\t  the chosen card (via `choose_card`) to graveyard and draw one. Empty hand is a\n26\t  safe no-op (no draw, no raise).\n27\t\n28\t## Additive miracle engine pipeline (build this)\n29\t1. `card.miracle_cost: ManaCost | None` — default None on the card base or set\n30\t   per-card via getattr-safe access. Stamped onto eligible hand cards by\n31\t   `grant_miracle`.\n32\t2. An alternative-cost cast surface in `engine/casting.py`. Prefer a minimal,\n33\t   backward-compatible extension: e.g. `cast_spell(game, player, card, zone,\n34\t   alternative_cost=None)` paying the supplied `alternative_cost` ManaCost\n35\t   instead of `card.mana_cost` when provided, OR a dedicated\n36\t   `cast_for_alternative_cost(...)`/`cast_miracle(...)` helper. Keep the default\n37\t   path byte-for-byte unchanged (alternative_cost defaults None → existing\n38\t   behavior). Set `mana_spent` to the alt cost's cmc when an alt cost is paid.\n39\t3. A draw hook in `draw_card` that is a COMPLETE no-op except when BOTH:\n40\t   (a) it is the drawing player's FIRST card drawn this turn — use the existing\n41\t       `player.cards_drawn_this_turn` counter (check BEFORE/at the moment it\n42\t       becomes 1, consistent with however the counter is incremented), AND\n43\t   (b) a permanent the drawing player controls grants miracle to the drawn card —\n44\t       query a capability `grants_miracle_to(self, card) -> ManaCost | None` on\n45\t       controlled permanents (Lorehold returns `{2}` for instants/sorceries,\n46\t       else None).\n47\t   When both hold: stamp `card.miracle_cost = {2}` and offer the controller\n48\t   `choose_yes_no`; on yes, cast the drawn card for its miracle cost via the\n49\t   alternative-cost surface (card leaves hand, pool reduced by 2). On no/none of\n50\t   the conditions, the hook does nothing — NO prompt, NO state change — so\n51\t   existing engine tests (where nothing grants miracle) see zero behavioral\n52\t   change. Verify full engine regression stays green.\n53\t\n54\t## Modeling simplification (document in rationale)\n55\tThe miracle \"window\" is modeled as an immediate at-draw offer rather than the\n56\tfull reveal → triggered ability → cast-anytime-before-next-step. This is\n57\tacceptable and deterministically testable for this engine.\n58\t\n59\t## Constraints\n60\t- DO NOT modify any test file in `test-files.txt`. If a test is genuinely wrong,\n61\t  return DISPUTE.\n62\t- Additive engine changes only: do not rename/move/delete existing engine\n63\t  symbols. Default code paths must be unchanged when miracle is not in play.\n64\t- Reuse existing surfaces where possible (`cards_drawn_this_turn`,\n65\t  `choose_yes_no`, `choose_card`, `mana_spent`).\n66\t- Run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` and make\n67\t  all sos_201 tests pass while keeping engine_tests green.\n68\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UtpCPeDJRZ23MXUB9icVCk","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"0b2ddbba-2f14-47be-a761-da4472401984","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:22:01.352Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201 Lorehold + miracle"}
