{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DtVTYL4JnViEnTMR9Reou9","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t- **Decision: option (a) — direct the Implementer to use the sos_1\n101\t  `choose_yes_no`-per-eligible-spell convention** for the multi-select free cast,\n102\t  so the existing positive cast tests pass as-is. No Tester re-invocation needed\n103\t  (the tests already assume this convention).\n104\t- Also note: Paradigm recurs (\"at the beginning of EACH of your first main\n105\t  phases\"). sos_57's `schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect` is ONE-SHOT, so the\n106\t  Paradigm callback must RE-SCHEDULE itself each time it fires (recurring), which\n107\t  the existing engine surface supports without new engine code. The Tester's\n108\t  `test_paradigm_copy_offer_recurs_each_precombat_main_phase` enforces this.\n109\t- Reuses sos_1 `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` for Paradigm self-exile and sos_57\n110\t  delayed-main-phase trigger surface — no new engine surface expected.\n111\t\n112\t## Untestable resolution: sos_201 (Lorehold — miracle draw-time casting)\n113\tOne untestable item: miracle's draw-time cast (\"cast for its miracle cost when\n114\tyou draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn\"). No engine miracle /\n115\talternative-cost / draw-reveal pipeline exists. The Tester covered the observable\n116\tgranting (`MIRACLE_COST` constant + `grant_miracle(game)` stamping `miracle_cost`\n117\ton controller's hand instants/sorceries), flying/haste combat, and the\n118\topponent-upkeep rummage.\n119\t- **Decision: option (a) — build a focused, additive, deterministic miracle\n120\t  pipeline.**\n121\t  - `card.miracle_cost: ManaCost | None` (default None).\n122\t  - Alternative-cost cast surface (e.g. `cast_spell(..., alternative_cost=...)`\n123\t    or a `cast_miracle`/`cast_for_alternative_cost` helper) paying the alt cost\n124\t    instead of mana_cost.\n125\t  - Draw hook in `draw_card`: ONLY acts when (a) it is the drawing player's FIRST\n126\t    card this turn (use existing `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`) AND (b) a\n127\t    permanent the player controls grants miracle to that card (a\n128\t    `grants_miracle_to(card) -> ManaCost|None` capability on Lorehold). When\n129\t    both hold, stamp `miracle_cost` and offer the controller `choose_yes_no` to\n130\t    cast it for the miracle cost. In all other cases the hook is a COMPLETE\n131\t    no-op (so existing engine tests, where nothing grants miracle, are\n132\t    unaffected — no spurious prompts/regressions).\n133\t  - Modeling simplification (documented): the miracle \"window\" is an immediate\n134\t    at-draw offer rather than the full reveal→triggered-ability→cast-anytime;\n135\t    acceptable and deterministically testable for this engine.\n136\t  - Spend the single Tester re-invocation on a deterministic draw-time test\n137\t    (first-card draw with Lorehold out → offered → yes casts for {2}, pool −2,\n138\t    card leaves hand; decline keeps it; non-first-card draw doesn't offer).\n139\t- Reasoning: miracle is a real, reusable mechanic; the gated draw hook is\n140\t  regression-safe. Implementer must pass full engine regression. If it can't be\n141\t  done cleanly/additively, fall back to partial coverage with an UNVERIFIED\n142\t  marker.\n143\t\n144\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01UtpCPeDJRZ23MXUB9icVCk","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"c0bbb119-4b4e-4bcd-b6b2-914bce0b5215","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:22:24.355Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_201 Lorehold + miracle"}
