{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01H2MBWsG3dkVRbEzNVDiXfJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DP4Xs2cvbpN88ARbBpN9ZM","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Extend sos_201 tests: miracle draw","subagent_type":"Tester","prompt":"This is a SINGLE follow-up invocation for card **sos_201** (Lorehold, the Historian). You previously wrote tests and reported ONE untestable requirement (miracle draw-time casting). The Implementer has now BUILT a deterministic miracle pipeline, so EXTEND the existing test file with hard tests for that behavior. Do NOT rewrite or weaken existing passing tests — only ADD new test(s).\n\n## What was built (now real and importable)\n- `card.miracle_cost: ManaCost | None` and `MIRACLE_COST` ({2}) on Lorehold.\n- `LoreholdTheHistorian.grants_miracle_to(self, card) -> ManaCost | None` — returns `{2}` for instants/sorceries, else None.\n- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell(game, player, card, zone, alternative_cost=None)` — backward-compatible new kwarg paying the supplied ManaCost instead of the card's mana cost.\n- A gated hook inside `engine/game.py::draw_card`: it offers a miracle cast ONLY when BOTH (a) the drawn card is the drawing player's FIRST card this turn (`player.cards_drawn_this_turn`) AND (b) a permanent that player controls returns a non-None cost from `grants_miracle_to(card)`. When both hold it stamps `card.miracle_cost` and asks the controller `choose_yes_no`; on yes it casts the drawn card for that cost (card leaves hand, mana pool reduced by the cost). Otherwise the hook is a complete no-op (no prompt, no state change).\n\nRead `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/coordinator-directives.md` for the full design, and `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md` for the modeling simplification (immediate at-draw offer).\n\n## Test to add (deterministic draw-time miracle)\nAdd to `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py` a focused test class covering:\n1. First-card draw with Lorehold on the controller's battlefield + an instant/sorcery on top of library: the controller is offered (`choose_yes_no` returns yes) → the card is cast for `{2}` (mana pool reduced by 2, card leaves hand / goes to stack or resolves per the engine), and `miracle_cost` was stamped.\n2. Decline path: same setup but `choose_yes_no` returns no → card stays in hand, no mana spent.\n3. Non-first-card draw (draw a card first so `cards_drawn_this_turn` > 0, then draw the instant): NO offer, card simply enters hand.\nOptionally: a draw when no miracle-granting permanent is in play → no offer (regression-safety of the gate).\n\nUse the existing test conventions in the file and in `/workspace/engine_tests/` (look at an example like `engine_tests/test_casting.py`). Drive the real engine (`draw_card`, real `GameState`/players, stub `choose_yes_no`/`choose_card` as the file already does). Tests must PASS against the implemented surface (this is post-implementation hardening, not red-phase).\n\n## Engine discovery\nRead engine source directly: `engine/game.py` (draw_card, cards_drawn_this_turn), `engine/casting.py` (cast_spell alternative_cost), `engine/card.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\n\n## Verify\nRun `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`. ALL tests (old + new) must pass and engine_tests must stay green.\n\n## Output (write to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/)\n- Append/update `test-rationale.md` with a section describing the new draw-time miracle tests (note the untestable item is now covered).\n- Ensure `test-files.txt` still lists `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py`.\n- If after building you find any sub-requirement still genuinely untestable, write/update `untestable.json`; otherwise leave it covered.\n\n## Return a short status summary\nReport: number of tests added, whether all pass, and whether the untestable item is now covered (untestable_count)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2502,"cache_read_input_tokens":33744,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2502},"output_tokens":52,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"fabc6c66-9868-482f-9cef-27361aeca663","request_id":"req_011CbdZbWcmj6v6jNufZ6EVS"}
