{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xe1WqMxMFpUL6qY8wSe7Qe","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian — implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Card (`cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`)\n4\t`LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)` — `{3}{R}{W}`, 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`,\n5\tsubtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE`, explicit\n6\t`self.colors = [\"R\",\"W\"]` (KEY_DECISIONS sos_13 convention).\n7\t\n8\tSurfaces:\n9\t- `MIRACLE_COST = ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")` — class constant, single source of\n10\t  truth for the granted alternative cost.\n11\t- `grants_miracle_to(self, card) -> ManaCost | None` — capability queried by the\n12\t  draw-time miracle pipeline; returns `{2}` for instants/sorceries, else `None`.\n13\t  `grant_miracle(game)` reuses it to stamp `card.miracle_cost` onto every\n14\t  instant/sorcery in the **controller's** hand (non-cast types and other\n15\t  players' hands untouched).\n16\t- `register_triggers` registers exactly one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`\n17\t  trigger (source = card, controller = the card's controller). The event is\n18\t  fired with no player arg, so the condition reads `game.active_player` and\n19\t  fires only when the active player is NOT the controller (\"each opponent's\n20\t  upkeep\"). Effect: `choose_yes_no`; on yes, `choose_card` then discard via\n21\t  `move_to_zone(HAND→GRAVEYARD)` and `draw_card`. Empty hand is a safe no-op\n22\t  (\"if you do\" fails → no draw), matching the rummage tests.\n23\t\n24\t## Additive miracle engine pipeline\n25\t1. **`engine/player.py`** — `Player.cards_drawn_this_turn: int = 0` made an\n26\t   explicit, documented attribute (previously only lazily set inside\n27\t   `draw_card`). Additive default; nothing else reads it differently.\n28\t2. **`engine/turn.py`** — untap step now resets `cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` for\n29\t   all players so \"the first card you drew this turn\" is evaluated per turn.\n30\t3. **`engine/casting.py`** — `cast_spell(game, player, card, alternative_cost=None)`.\n31\t   When `alternative_cost` is supplied it is paid instead of `card.mana_cost`\n32\t   (no cost reduction applied to an alt cost), and `card.mana_spent` is set to\n33\t   the alt cost's `cmc`. The sorcery-speed timing check is bypassed only when an\n34\t   alternative cost is in play (miracle, CR 702.94/118.9, lets you cast the\n35\t   spell as it is drawn regardless of timing). With `alternative_cost=None` the\n36\t   function is byte-for-byte unchanged — the default path is untouched.\n37\t4. **`engine/game.py`** — `draw_card` calls new `_offer_miracle(game, player,\n38\t   card)` after firing the draw event. `_offer_miracle` is a COMPLETE no-op\n39\t   unless BOTH (a) `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` (first card this turn)\n40\t   AND (b) some permanent the player controls returns a non-`None`\n41\t   `grants_miracle_to(card)`. Only then does it stamp `card.miracle_cost` and\n42\t   offer `choose_yes_no`; on yes it casts the card for the miracle cost via the\n43\t   alternative-cost surface (`CastingError` is swallowed so an unpayable miracle\n44\t   simply leaves the card in hand). Because the hook is fully gated, ordinary\n45\t   draws (where nothing grants miracle) issue no prompt and change no state, so\n46\t   full engine regression stays green.\n47\t\n48\t## Modeling simplification (documented)\n49\tThe miracle \"window\" is modelled as an **immediate at-draw offer** rather than\n50\tthe full reveal → triggered ability → cast-anytime-before-next-step sequence.\n51\tThis is deterministic and sufficient for this engine. The first-card detection\n52\tuses `cards_drawn_this_turn`, which is now reset per turn for all players.\n53\t\n54\t## Verification\n55\t`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` → 1168 passed\n56\t(23 sos_201 tests + full engine regression). An additional ad-hoc end-to-end\n57\tcheck confirmed the draw-time pipeline: first-card instant offered → yes casts\n58\tfor `{2}` (pool emptied, `mana_spent == 2`, card leaves hand); decline keeps it\n59\t(with `miracle_cost` stamped); non-first-card and no-grantor draws are no-ops\n60\twith no prompt and no stamp.\n61\t\n62\t## Conventions for future cards\n63\t- Alternative/\"as-you-cast\" costs: pass `alternative_cost=<ManaCost>` to\n64\t  `engine.casting.cast_spell`; it replaces the printed cost, skips reduction and\n65\t  the sorcery-speed timing gate, and records `mana_spent = alt_cost.cmc`.\n66\t- Draw-time \"as you draw\" grants: advertise `grants_miracle_to(card) ->\n67\t  ManaCost | None` on a permanent; `draw_card` offers the first-card cast.\n68\t- `Player.cards_drawn_this_turn` is the canonical per-turn draw counter (reset\n69\t  at untap for all players).\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"b90b1171-120c-4370-8c27-7a37fee58c4f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:32:25.446Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_201/impl-rationale.md","content":"# sos_201 — Lorehold, the Historian — implementation rationale\n\n## Card (`cards/sos/sos_201/card_impl.py`)\n`LoreholdTheHistorian(Creature)` — `{3}{R}{W}`, 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`,\nsubtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.HASTE`, explicit\n`self.colors = [\"R\",\"W\"]` (KEY_DECISIONS sos_13 convention).\n\nSurfaces:\n- `MIRACLE_COST = ManaCost.parse(\"{2}\")` — class constant, single source of\n  truth for the granted alternative cost.\n- `grants_miracle_to(self, card) -> ManaCost | None` — capability queried by the\n  draw-time miracle pipeline; returns `{2}` for instants/sorceries, else `None`.\n  `grant_miracle(game)` reuses it to stamp `card.miracle_cost` onto every\n  instant/sorcery in the **controller's** hand (non-cast types and other\n  players' hands untouched).\n- `register_triggers` registers exactly one `BeginningOfUpkeepTriggeredEvent`\n  trigger (source = card, controller = the card's controller). The event is\n  fired with no player arg, so the condition reads `game.active_player` and\n  fires only when the active player is NOT the controller (\"each opponent's\n  upkeep\"). Effect: `choose_yes_no`; on yes, `choose_card` then discard via\n  `move_to_zone(HAND→GRAVEYARD)` and `draw_card`. Empty hand is a safe no-op\n  (\"if you do\" fails → no draw), matching the rummage tests.\n\n## Additive miracle engine pipeline\n1. **`engine/player.py`** — `Player.cards_drawn_this_turn: int = 0` made an\n   explicit, documented attribute (previously only lazily set inside\n   `draw_card`). Additive default; nothing else reads it differently.\n2. **`engine/turn.py`** — untap step now resets `cards_drawn_this_turn = 0` for\n   all players so \"the first card you drew this turn\" is evaluated per turn.\n3. **`engine/casting.py`** — `cast_spell(game, player, card, alternative_cost=None)`.\n   When `alternative_cost` is supplied it is paid instead of `card.mana_cost`\n   (no cost reduction applied to an alt cost), and `card.mana_spent` is set to\n   the alt cost's `cmc`. The sorcery-speed timing check is bypassed only when an\n   alternative cost is in play (miracle, CR 702.94/118.9, lets you cast the\n   spell as it is drawn regardless of timing). With `alternative_cost=None` the\n   function is byte-for-byte unchanged — the default path is untouched.\n4. **`engine/game.py`** — `draw_card` calls new `_offer_miracle(game, player,\n   card)` after firing the draw event. `_offer_miracle` is a COMPLETE no-op\n   unless BOTH (a) `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` (first card this turn)\n   AND (b) some permanent the player controls returns a non-`None`\n   `grants_miracle_to(card)`. Only then does it stamp `card.miracle_cost` and\n   offer `choose_yes_no`; on yes it casts the card for the miracle cost via the\n   alternative-cost surface (`CastingError` is swallowed so an unpayable miracle\n   simply leaves the card in hand). Because the hook is fully gated, ordinary\n   draws (where nothing grants miracle) issue no prompt and change no state, so\n   full engine regression stays green.\n\n## Modeling simplification (documented)\nThe miracle \"window\" is modelled as an **immediate at-draw offer** rather than\nthe full reveal → triggered ability → cast-anytime-before-next-step sequence.\nThis is deterministic and sufficient for this engine. The first-card detection\nuses `cards_drawn_this_turn`, which is now reset per turn for all players.\n\n## Verification\n`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_201/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` → 1168 passed\n(23 sos_201 tests + full engine regression). An additional ad-hoc end-to-end\ncheck confirmed the draw-time pipeline: first-card instant offered → yes casts\nfor `{2}` (pool emptied, `mana_spent == 2`, card leaves hand); decline keeps it\n(with `miracle_cost` stamped); non-first-card and no-grantor draws are no-ops\nwith no prompt and no stamp.\n\n## Conventions for future cards\n- Alternative/\"as-you-cast\" costs: pass `alternative_cost=<ManaCost>` to\n  `engine.casting.cast_spell`; it replaces the printed cost, skips reduction and\n  the sorcery-speed timing gate, and records `mana_spent = alt_cost.cmc`.\n- Draw-time \"as you draw\" grants: advertise `grants_miracle_to(card) ->\n  ManaCost | None` on a permanent; `draw_card` offers the first-card cast.\n- `Player.cards_drawn_this_turn` is the canonical per-turn draw counter (reset\n  at untap for all players).\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":70}}}
