{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_014VKAtj5d1MpRCmbFuiqKbN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MF7afbxjH829d3HeB3628F","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test rationale — sos_226 Silverquill, the Disputant\n\nCard: `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4.\nOracle: \"Flying, vigilance. Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has\ncasualty 1. (As you cast that spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power 1\nor greater. When you do, copy the spell and you may choose new targets for the\ncopy.)\"\n\nTest file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` (27 tests).\n\n## Assumed API contract (so the Implementer can align)\n\nThe engine has **no native casualty mechanic**, and `engine.casting.cast_spell`\ndoes **not** fire any `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`. Following the established\nproject convention for granted abilities lacking native engine support\n(SOS 201's miracle granting via `grants_miracle_to` / `grant_miracle`, and the\n`copy_spell` surface used by FDN 248), the tests assume the card exposes:\n\n- `SilverquillTheDisputant` subclasses `engine.card.Creature` with:\n  - `name == \"Silverquill, the Disputant\"`, `mana_cost == {2}{W}{B}`,\n    `base_power == 4`, `base_toughness == 4`,\n    `supertypes` ⊇ `{LEGENDARY}`, `subtypes` ⊇ `{\"Elder\", \"Dragon\"}`,\n    `keywords` ⊇ `FLYING | VIGILANCE`, and `self.colors == [\"W\", \"B\"]`\n    (KEY_DECISIONS sos_13 explicit-colors convention).\n- `CASUALTY_AMOUNT` class constant equal to `1` (the granted casualty value).\n- `grants_casualty_to(spell) -> int | None` — returns `1` for an\n  instant/sorcery, `None` otherwise (mirrors `grants_miracle_to`).\n- `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj) -> bool` — the casualty offer. Given a spell\n  already on the stack as a `StackObject` (with `is_spell=True`), it:\n  1. returns `False` (no-op, no prompt) if the spell is not controlled by the\n     dragon's controller, or is not an instant/sorcery, or the controller has\n     no creature with `power >= 1` to sacrifice;\n  2. otherwise asks `choose_yes_no` to pay casualty; on decline returns `False`;\n  3. on accept asks `choose_card` to pick a power>=1 creature to sacrifice\n     (the legal options must exclude power-0 creatures), sacrifices it\n     (battlefield → graveyard), then asks `choose_yes_no` whether to choose new\n     targets for the copy; if yes, `choose_target` provides the new target;\n  4. pushes a `copy_spell(...)` of the spell onto the stack (a distinct object\n     from the original, `is_spell=True`, controlled by the dragon's controller,\n     with either the new targets or the original targets) and returns `True`.\n\nDecision order consumed from the player script in the accept path:\n`choose_yes_no (pay)` → `choose_card (sacrifice)` → `choose_yes_no (new targets?)`\n→ `choose_target (new target, only if yes)`. The Implementer may reorder the\n\"new targets\" question relative to the copy, but the tests script exactly one\nyes/no for it after the sacrifice. This contract was validated end-to-end with a\nthrowaway reference implementation: all 27 tests pass against it, then fail\nagainst the stub (TDD red phase).\n\n## Test groups\n\n### TestSilverquillProperties (7)\nStatic characteristics: is a `Creature`, name, mana cost `{2}{W}{B}`, 4/4,\nLEGENDARY supertype, Elder Dragon subtypes, and `self.colors == {W, B}`.\n\n### TestSilverquillKeywords (6)\n- `test_has_flying_and_vigilance` — both keyword flags present.\n- Flying combat consequences through the real `_can_block`: a ground creature\n  cannot block; a flyer or a reach creature can. The flyer/reach tests guard on\n  `Keyword.FLYING in attacker.keywords` so they only pass when Silverquill truly\n  flies (otherwise they would pass trivially against a non-flying stub).\n- `test_vigilance_does_not_tap_when_attacking` — drives the real\n  `declare_attackers_step`; the dragon is declared as an attacker and must\n  remain untapped (`is_attacking is True`, `is_tapped is False`), exercising the\n  engine's vigilance handling.\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyGrant (5)\nThe granted casualty value and eligibility capability: `CASUALTY_AMOUNT == 1`;\n`grants_casualty_to` returns `1` for an instant and a sorcery, and `None` for a\ncreature spell and a land.\n\n### TestSilverquillCasualtyOffer (9)\nThe core behavior, driving `offer_casualty` against a hand-built spell\n`StackObject`:\n- accept → sacrifice a power>=1 creature and push exactly one distinct copy of\n  the spell;\n- decline → no sacrifice, no copy;\n- no power>=1 creature available → no copy, **and no prompt** (verified via the\n  empty player script: a stray prompt raises `ScriptExhaustedError`);\n- power-0 creature is not a legal sacrifice option (a `choose_card` spy captures\n  the offered options and asserts the 0/4 wall is excluded while the 1/1 is\n  included);\n- choosing new targets points the copy at a different target than the original;\n- declining new targets keeps the copy's original targets;\n- the pushed copy is `is_spell=True` and controlled by the dragon's controller;\n- an opponent-controlled spell on the stack gets no offer (no prompt, no copy) —\n  \"spells *you* cast\";\n- a creature spell on the stack gets no offer — casualty is instant/sorcery only.\n\n### TestSilverquillCastingIntegration (1)\n`test_offer_casualty_on_really_cast_spell` — casts an instant through the REAL\n`engine.casting.cast_spell`, locates the genuine spell `StackObject` the engine\npushed, then drives `offer_casualty` against it and asserts the sacrifice +\nsingle copy. This proves the offer composes with a real cast (not just a\nhand-built StackObject).\n\n## Edge cases covered and why\n- Eligibility filter (power >= 1) — exercised both as a no-op (no eligible\n  creature) and as an option-filtering check (power-0 excluded).\n- \"You cast\" ownership gating (opponent's spell ignored).\n- Card-type gating (creature spell ignored; instant and sorcery both granted).\n- New-targets opt-in vs. opt-out for the copy.\n- Vigilance observed through real combat (no tap), not just the flag.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope / unblockable)\n- **Automatic wiring of the casualty offer into `cast_spell`.** The engine\n  fires no spell-cast event and the granted spell's own `on_cast` is not\n  Silverquill's, so there is no guaranteed automatic hook. The integration test\n  therefore drives `offer_casualty` explicitly against a really-cast spell. The\n  automatic-firing portion is recorded in `untestable.json`.\n- **Resolution of the copy / the copy being put into the graveyard.** The copy's\n  resolution behavior is the underlying spell's, not this card's, and is covered\n  by engine tests / the underlying spell's own contract.\n- **Casualty paid with the dragon itself as the sacrifice.** Legal but a\n  redundant variation of the generic power>=1 sacrifice already covered.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":284,"cache_read_input_tokens":128426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":284,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTAjsfjPH76zUPLLeiM977","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"00b6c3c1-db7c-4e6b-95ac-8b32cdc82ecd","request_id":"req_011CbdaTuBjDLxZMypkSzhMa","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_226"}
