{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RTAjsfjPH76zUPLLeiM977","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Only my new test file is added (and the pre-existing `run_manifest.json` modification, which I did not touch — it was modified at session start). No engine_tests/ or FDN files were edited. The card stub is unchanged.\n\n## Summary\n\nI wrote **27 pytest tests** for **sos_226 Silverquill, the Disputant** at `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`. All 27 **currently fail (red phase)** against the stub — failures are all due to the missing implementation (not a `Creature`, missing `CASUALTY_AMOUNT`, missing `offer_casualty`/`grants_casualty_to`), not test bugs.\n\nI validated the test contract is satisfiable by running them against a throwaway reference implementation: **all 27 passed**, then I restored the stub and confirmed they go back to red.\n\nCoverage:\n- **Static properties (7):** Creature type, name, `{2}{W}{B}` cost, 4/4, LEGENDARY, Elder Dragon subtypes, colors `{W, B}`.\n- **Keywords (6):** flying + vigilance flags; flying combat consequences through the real `_can_block` (ground can't block, flyer/reach can — guarded so they fail if flying is absent); and vigilance verified through the real `declare_attackers_step` (attacker stays untapped).\n- **Casualty granting (5):** `CASUALTY_AMOUNT == 1`; `grants_casualty_to` returns 1 for instant/sorcery, None for creature/land.\n- **Casualty offer (9):** accept (sacrifice power≥1 creature + one distinct copy), decline, no-eligible-creature no-op (no prompt), power-0 not a legal sacrifice option, choose-new-targets vs keep-targets, copy is `is_spell`/correct controller, opponent-spell ignored (\"spells you cast\"), creature-spell ignored.\n- **Integration (1):** drives the real `engine.casting.cast_spell`, then `offer_casualty` against the genuine on-stack spell.\n\nThe tests assume a documented card contract (`CASUALTY_AMOUNT`, `grants_casualty_to`, `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`), mirroring the SOS 201 miracle / FDN 248 `copy_spell` conventions — detailed in `test-rationale.md` for the Implementer.\n\n**untestable_count: 1** — `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json`. The single uncovered piece is the *automatic* firing of the casualty offer during `cast_spell` (the engine fires no spell-cast event and provides no native hook). The full observable casualty behavior is tested via `offer_casualty`; only the at-cast auto-wiring is deferred, with an unblock note (an additive `cast_spell` hook analogous to SOS 201's `draw_card` miracle hook).\n\nOutput files written to `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/`: `test-rationale.md`, `test-files.txt`, `untestable.json`."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a1e4de05939281751 (use SendMessage with to: 'a1e4de05939281751' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 133667\ntool_uses: 50\nduration_ms: 345233</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"07a66aec-0651-45db-961a-b4b1732bd51b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:38:47.925Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write pytest tests (TDD red phase) for card **sos_226**.\n\n## Inputs\n- Spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_spec.json` (read it — do not assume).\n- Stub to be implemented later: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`.\n- Test conventions: study `/workspace/engine_tests/` and an example like `/workspace/engine_tests/test_casting.py`. Match the project's existing test style.\n- FDN reference cards (completed examples): `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_*/` — `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md` lists which ship with `tests.py`. Use them as patterns.\n- Conventions you MUST align to: read `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` (explicit `self.colors`; mana_spent; BeginningOfMainPhase events + delayed/recurring deferred effects; StackObject.is_spell; coin flips/skip-turns; planeswalker conventions; preparation cards; alternative-cost casting + draw-time/miracle pipeline). Reus