{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement card **sos_226** (Silverquill, the Disputant) and the additive engine support it requires (a deterministic, fully-gated casualty cast hook). Make ALL tests in the test file pass without modifying any test file.\n\n## Context / workspace rules\n- Read `/workspace/AGENTS.md` and `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md` for workspace rules and path conventions.\n- Read `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` for established conventions you MUST follow (explicit `self.colors`; mana_spent; BeginningOfMainPhase events; StackObject.is_spell; coin flips/skip-turns; planeswalker conventions; preparation cards; alternative-cost casting + draw-time/miracle pipeline — the casualty hook mirrors that miracle pattern).\n- Read `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` to see prior cards' files (do not undo their changes).\n- CRITICAL: Do NOT modify any file under `/workspace/engine_tests/`. Those are staged for local verification only.\n\n## Card spec & tests\n- Spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_spec.json`\n- Stub to fill in: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py`\n- Test file you must make pass (do NOT edit): listed in `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-files.txt` (it is `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`).\n\n## Coordinator directives (authoritative design for the untestable item)\nRead `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/coordinator-directives.md` in full. It specifies the exact card surface (`CASUALTY_AMOUNT`, `grants_casualty_to`, `offer_casualty`, flying+vigilance, W/B colors, legendary Elder Dragon) AND the additive engine cast hook you must build:\n- In `engine/casting.py::cast_spell`, AFTER pushing the spell StackObject, call a helper that is a COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER controls returns a non-None `grants_casualty_to(spell)`; only then invoke that permanent's `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`. Default cast path must be byte-for-byte unchanged when no grantor is present.\n- Reuse the existing `copy_spell(...)` surface and `StackObject.is_spell`.\n\n## Engine API discovery\nRead engine source directly (rich docstrings): `engine/card.py`, `engine/casting.py`, `engine/events.py`, `engine/triggers.py`, `engine/stack.py`, `engine/zones.py`. The `copy_spell` helper exists (used by FDN cards — check `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_*/card_impl.py` and engine). Reuse it; do not reimplement copying.\n\n## Output (write to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/)\n- `impl.diff` — unified diff of all changes (card_impl.py + engine files).\n- `impl-rationale.md` — design rationale, including the casualty modeling and any engine changes; note any conventions worth reusing.\n- `impl-files.txt` — list of files changed.\n- Upsert this card's entry into `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` (match by `card: \"sos_226\"`, replace in place if it exists). Entry shape:\n  `{ \"card\": \"sos_226\", \"tests\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\"}], \"implementation\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\"}] }`\n\n## Verify\nRun `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`. ALL sos_226 tests must pass and engine_tests must stay green.\n\n## Return status summary (exactly one of)\n```\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: <N>\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: <one-line>\n```\nor\n```\nDISPUTE\ntests_failing: <N>\ndisputed_tests: <list>\ndispute_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-dispute.md\nnotes: <one-line>\n```\nNote: a single Tester re-invocation will run AFTER you finish to add a deterministic auto-fire test against the cast hook, so make `grants_casualty_to`, `offer_casualty`, and the `cast_spell` casualty hook real and importable."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AnMfFdRfg114k3p8WJq1hq","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"2636e825-5ce0-4b95-a3c7-a0bda2b2d47f","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:39:50.661Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226 Silverquill + casualty"}
