{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CLaWdt4J5mvuMuztZS1yQg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant)\n2\t\n3\tThe Tester reported ONE untestable requirement: the AUTOMATIC firing of the\n4\tcasualty offer during `engine.casting.cast_spell`. Per the run decision, build a\n5\tfocused, ADDITIVE, fully-gated cast hook (directly analogous to the sos_201\n6\tdraw-time miracle hook) so the auto-fire becomes testable. Build exactly the\n7\tsurface below so the existing tests and the to-be-added Tester probe align.\n8\t\n9\t## Card: Silverquill, the Disputant\n10\t- `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 4/4, colors W/B.\n11\t- Subclass `Creature`. Set `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n12\t  explicit `self.colors = [\"W\",\"B\"]` (KEY_DECISIONS sos_13 convention).\n13\t- Keywords: `Keyword.FLYING` and `Keyword.VIGILANCE`.\n14\t\n15\t## Card surface the existing tests assume (match exactly)\n16\t- `CASUALTY_AMOUNT` class constant == `1`.\n17\t- `grants_casualty_to(self, spell) -> int | None` — returns `1` for an\n18\t  instant/sorcery spell, `None` otherwise.\n19\t- `offer_casualty(self, game, stack_obj) -> bool` — given a spell already on the\n20\t  stack as a `StackObject` (`is_spell=True`):\n21\t  1. return `False` (no-op, NO prompt) if the spell is not controlled by this\n22\t     dragon's controller, OR is not an instant/sorcery, OR the controller has no\n23\t     creature with `power >= 1` to sacrifice;\n24\t  2. else ask controller `choose_yes_no` to pay casualty; on decline return\n25\t     `False`;\n26\t  3. on accept, ask `choose_card` to pick a creature with `power >= 1` to\n27\t     sacrifice — the legal options MUST EXCLUDE power-0 creatures — sacrifice it\n28\t     (battlefield → graveyard), then ask `choose_yes_no` whether to choose new\n29\t     targets for the copy; if yes, `choose_target` supplies the new target;\n30\t  4. push a `copy_spell(...)` of the spell onto the stack — a DISTINCT object,\n31\t     `is_spell=True`, controlled by the dragon's controller, carrying either the\n32\t     new targets (if chosen) or the original targets — and return `True`.\n33\t  Decision order consumed from the player script (accept path):\n34\t  `choose_yes_no (pay)` → `choose_card (sacrifice)` → `choose_yes_no (new targets?)`\n35\t  → `choose_target (new target, only if yes)`.\n36\t\n37\t## Additive engine cast hook (build this)\n38\tIn `engine/casting.py::cast_spell`, AFTER the spell StackObject is pushed, call a\n39\tnew helper (e.g. `_offer_casualty(game, player, stack_obj)`) that is a COMPLETE\n40\tno-op unless some permanent the CASTER (`player`) controls returns a non-None\n41\t`grants_casualty_to(spell)`. For each such permanent, invoke its\n42\t`offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`. When no controlled permanent grants casualty,\n43\tthe helper does nothing — NO prompt, NO state change — so existing engine tests\n44\t(where nothing grants casualty) see zero behavioral change. Keep the default cast\n45\tpath byte-for-byte unchanged when no grantor is present. Use `getattr`-safe\n46\tcapability checks (not all permanents define `grants_casualty_to`).\n47\t\n48\tReuse the existing `copy_spell(...)` surface (see FDN cards / engine) and\n49\t`StackObject.is_spell` (KEY_DECISIONS sos_57). Do not duplicate copy logic.\n50\t\n51\t## Constraints\n52\t- DO NOT modify any test file in `test-files.txt`. If a test is genuinely wrong,\n53\t  return DISPUTE.\n54\t- Additive engine changes only: no renaming/moving/deleting existing engine\n55\t  symbols; default code paths unchanged when casualty is not in play.\n56\t- Run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`; all\n57\t  sos_226 tests pass and engine_tests stay green.\n58\t- Make `grants_casualty_to`, `offer_casualty`, and the cast hook real/importable\n59\t  — a single Tester re-invocation will add a deterministic auto-fire test next.\n60\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AnMfFdRfg114k3p8WJq1hq","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"ee50439d-5b2c-4f7e-a7c4-8b0ab60af6f3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:39:54.326Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226 Silverquill + casualty"}
