{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a6133a0fb53345423","tool_use_id":"toolu_01AnMfFdRfg114k3p8WJq1hq","description":"Writing /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md","subagent_type":"Implementer","usage":{"total_tokens":92776,"tool_uses":34,"duration_ms":163510},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"313c3833-59f1-455b-a0d0-e78365aa9aee","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011U4vG3FR2JRk74AaV8tA89","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MUSbBqHSNy7H9Y3uCgRvjc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md","content":"# sos_226 — Silverquill, the Disputant — implementation rationale\n\n## Card surface\n`SilverquillTheDisputant(Creature)` mirrors the SOS 201 Elder-Dragon shape:\n`{2}{W}{B}`, 4/4, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n`keywords = Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.VIGILANCE`, and an explicit\n`self.colors = [\"W\",\"B\"]` (KEY_DECISIONS sos_13 convention — engine has no\nnative colors field). Flying/vigilance are evergreen flags already honored by\n`engine/combat.py` (`_can_block`, `declare_attackers_step`), so no combat code\nwas needed.\n\n## Casualty modeling (capability + offer)\nCasualty (CR 702.153) has no native engine pipeline, so — directly analogous to\nthe SOS 201 draw-time miracle granting — the grant is exposed as two surfaces:\n\n- `CASUALTY_AMOUNT = 1` class constant (single source of truth).\n- `grants_casualty_to(spell) -> int | None`: returns `1` for an instant/sorcery\n  (`CardType.INSTANT`/`SORCERY` membership, `getattr`-safe), `None` otherwise.\n  This is the capability the engine cast hook queries.\n- `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj) -> bool`: fully gated. Returns `False` with\n  NO prompt / NO state change unless (a) the spell's controller is this dragon's\n  controller, (b) the spell is an instant/sorcery, and (c) the controller\n  controls a creature with `power >= 1`. The legal sacrifice options are\n  filtered to creatures with `power >= 1` (power-0 walls are excluded), which is\n  what the test spies on via a wrapped `choose_card`. On accept it\n  `move_to_zone(battlefield → graveyard)` the chosen fodder, optionally chooses\n  new targets, then reuses `engine.stack.copy_spell(...)` to push a DISTINCT\n  copy (`is_spell=True`, controlled by the dragon's controller) carrying the new\n  or original targets. Decision order: `choose_yes_no` (pay) → `choose_card`\n  (sacrifice) → `choose_yes_no` (new targets?) → `choose_target` (new target,\n  only if yes).\n\nNew-target selection (`_choose_new_targets`) asks for one new target per\noriginal target from the union of all battlefield permanents and the players,\nkeeping the copy's target count equal to the original's.\n\n## Additive engine cast hook\n`engine/casting.py::cast_spell` gains, AFTER the spell StackObject is pushed, a\ncall to the new `_offer_casualty(game, player, stack_obj)` helper. The helper is\na COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER controls advertises a non-None\n`grants_casualty_to(spell)`; only then is that permanent's\n`offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)` invoked. Capability lookups are `getattr`-safe\n(not all permanents define the method) and the battlefield is snapshotted before\niteration so an offer that copies the spell cannot perturb iteration. With no\ngrantor present the default cast path is byte-for-byte unchanged — confirmed by\nall 1372 engine + other-card tests staying green.\n\n## Deviation worth noting (convention for future cards)\nThe integration test (`test_offer_casualty_on_really_cast_spell`) casts the\nspell for real *while the dragon is on the battlefield*, then manually drives\n`offer_casualty`. Because the auto-fire hook now fires during that real\n`cast_spell`, the dragon's controller is prompted with an empty script. Casualty\nis a \"you may\" ability, so declining is always legal: `offer_casualty` guards\nONLY its first optional `choose_yes_no` (\"pay casualty?\") against\n`ScriptExhaustedError`, treating an exhausted script as a decline (return False,\nno state change). This matches the existing precedent in `engine/turn.py`\n(cleanup discard swallows `ScriptExhaustedError`). Once the player commits to\npaying (scripts `True`), the subsequent prompts are mandatory consequences and\nare NOT swallowed. This makes the hook robust for both the existing manual test\nand the to-be-added deterministic auto-fire probe.\n\n## Reuse\n- `engine.stack.copy_spell(...)` for all copy logic (no duplication).\n- `engine.stack.StackObject.is_spell` (KEY_DECISIONS sos_57) to distinguish a\n  spell from an ability on the stack.\n- Gated-helper pattern lifted from SOS 201's `engine.game._offer_miracle`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":208,"cache_read_input_tokens":92109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":208,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":61,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01AnMfFdRfg114k3p8WJq1hq","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"b77a9053-3ae9-4563-a678-7b1c8c97e061","request_id":"req_011CbdaoMYGe5en174Gbgz7j","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_226 Silverquill + casualty"}
