1d2bd","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:44:52.100Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"This is a SINGLE follow-up invocation for card **sos_226** (Silverquill, the Disputant). You previously wrote tests and reported ONE untestable requirement (automatic firing of the casualty offer during `cast_spell`). The Implementer has now BUILT a fully-gated casualty cast hook, so EXTEND the existing test file with hard test(s) for that behavior. Do NOT rewrite or weaken existing passing tests — only ADD new test(s).\n\n## What was built (now real and importable)\n- `SilverquillTheDisputant.grants_casualty_to(self, spell) -> int | None` — returns `1` for instants/sorceries, else None; `offer_casualty(self, game, stack_obj) -> bool` (sacrifice power>=1 creature, push one `copy_spell`, optional new targets) — already covered by your existing tests.\n- New additive hook inside `engine/casting.py::cast_spell`: AFTER the spell StackObject is pushed, the engine queries each permanent the CASTER controls; if a permanent returns a non-None `grants_casualty_to(spell)`, the engine invokes that permanent's `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)` automatically. When no controlled permanent grants casualty, the hook is a COMPLETE no-op (no prompt, no state change).\n\nRead `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/coordinator-directives.md` for the full design and `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md` for the modeling notes.\n\n## Test to add (deterministic casualty auto-fire)\nAdd a focused test class that drives the REAL `engine.casting.cast_spell` (NOT a manual `offer_casualty` call) and asserts:\n1. Auto-fire YES path: Silverquill on the controller's battlefield + a power>=1 creature available + the controller casts an instant/sorcery through `cast_spell`; with the player script accepting casualty (pay yes, choose the power>=1 creature, decline new targets), the creature is sacrificed (battlefield→graveyard) and exactly ONE distinct copy of the spell is on the stack (copy `is_spell=True`, controlled by the controller) — all WITHOUT any manual `offer_casualty` call.\n2. No-grantor regression: casting an instant through `cast_spell` when NO casualty-granting permanent is in play produces no sacrifice, no copy, and issues no casualty prompt (use an empty/exhausted script to prove no prompt was made).\nOptionally: decline-at-cast (Silverquill out, but `choose_yes_no` says no) → spell on stack, no copy, no sacrifice.\n\nUse the existing test conventions in the file and in `/workspace/engine_tests/`. Tests must PASS against the implemented surface (post-implementation hardening, not red-phase).\n\n## Engine discovery\nRead engine source directly: `engine/casting.py` (cast_spell + the new casualty hook), `engine/stack.py`, `engine/card.py`, `engine/zones.py`.\n\n## Verify\nRun `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`. ALL tests (old + new) must pass and engine_tests must stay green.\n\n## Output (write to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/)\n- Append/update `test-rationale.md` with a section describing the new auto-fire tests (note the untestable item is now covered).\n- Ensure `test-files.txt` still lists `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`.\n- Update `untestable.json` to `[]` if the item is now covered; otherwise explain what remains.\n\n## Return a short status summary\nReport: number of tests added, whether all pass, and `untestable_count: <N>`.","agentId":"afed462065216ee16","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`test-files.txt` already lists the single test file path correctly, so no change needed there. All output files are updated.\n\nTESTS_REWRITTEN\ntest_files: 1\ntest_cases: 30 (3 added)\n\nAll 30 sos_226 tests pass and engine_tests stay green (1175 passed total). The 3 added tests live in the new `TestSilverquillCasualtyAutoFire` class in `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py` and drive the real `engine.casting.cast_spell` with no manual `offer_casualty` call:\n- `test_cast_spell_auto_fires_casualty_and_makes_one_copy` — accept path: fodder moves battlefield→graveyard and exactly one distinct copy (`is_spell=True`, controlled by the caster, same name) is on the stack.\n- `test_cast_spell_no_grantor_does_not_prompt_or_copy` — no casualty-grantor in play: no sacrifice, no copy, and an empty script proves no prompt was issued.\n- `test_cast_spell_decline_casualty_leaves_no_copy` — Silverquill in play but `choose_yes_no` returns False: spell stays on the stack, no copy, no sacrifice.\n\nExisting 27 tests were left untouched.\n\nuntestable_count: 0\nuntestable_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json (now `[]` — the automatic at-cast wiring is now covered)\n\nOutput files updated:\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-rationale.md` (new `TestSilverquillCasualtyAutoFire (3)` section; the formerly-untestable item marked covered)\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/untestable.json` (now `[]`)\n- `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/test-files.txt` (unchanged — still lists `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py`)"}],"totalDurationMs":95916,"totalTokens":63568,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":146,"cache_read_input_tokens":62766,"output_tokens":654,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":146},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":62766,"cache_creation_input_tokens":146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":146,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":11,"searchCount":2,"bashCount":2,"editFileCount":5,"linesAdded":197,"linesRemoved":24,"otherToolCount":0}}}
