{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"aaa82cfc087c6108e","tool_use_id":"toolu_01MRGe1F6PdFr1PWEC1kmbt5","description":"Review sos_226 implementation","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"Review the implementation diff for card **sos_226** (Silverquill, the Disputant — `{2}{W}{B}` Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon 4/4, flying+vigilance, grants casualty 1 to the controller's instants/sorceries). The implementation also adds an additive, fully-gated casualty cast hook to the engine.\n\n## What to review\n- Diff: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl.diff`\n- Rationale (context, incl. modeling): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-rationale.md`\n\n## Review focus\nCorrectness vs. spec intent, real bugs, missed edge cases, and convention violations VISIBLE IN THE DIFF. Specifically scrutinize:\n- The new `cast_spell` casualty hook is a COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER controls returns a non-None `grants_casualty_to(spell)` — i.e. no regression to the default cast path, no spurious prompts when no grantor is present. Verify `getattr`-safe capability checks (not all permanents define `grants_casualty_to`/`offer_casualty`).\n- `offer_casualty` correctly gates on: \"spells you cast\" (controller match), instant/sorcery only, requires a power>=1 creature to sacrifice; power-0 creatures excluded from sacrifice options; pushes exactly ONE distinct copy via `copy_spell` (`is_spell=True`, correct controller); optional new-targets path.\n- `grants_casualty_to` only returns a value for instants/sorceries.\n- Flying/vigilance, legendary, colors (`self.colors == [\"W\",\"B\"]`), Elder Dragon subtypes correctness.\n- Reuses existing `copy_spell` / `StackObject.is_spell` rather than reimplementing copy logic.\n\n## Constraints\n- Read `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` and `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`. Do NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards (listed in FILES_MODIFIED.json) or conventions established in KEY_DECISIONS.md (explicit