{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014ga95VmBeYC8c6FwzpqRPt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 165,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"The casualty sacrifice reimplements sacrifice logic instead of reusing the existing canonical helper engine.game.sacrifice(game, player, permanent). The direct move_to_zone(game, chosen, Zone.BATTLEFIELD, Zone.GRAVEYARD) call passes no replacement_event, so per move_to_zone's documented contract no replacement effects are consulted. That means sacrifice-redirection replacement effects (e.g. 'if a creature you control would die, exile it instead', tokens-to-graveyard, etc.) are silently bypassed for the casualty sacrifice. engine.game.sacrifice already handles this correctly by passing a SacrificeReplacementEvent (and guards bf.contains). The review focus explicitly calls for reusing existing helpers rather than reimplementing; use sacrifice(game, controller, chosen) here. (Tests don't catch this because no test board has a sacrifice replacement effect.)\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 180,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"_choose_new_targets offers the union of all players plus every battlefield permanent as legal new targets, regardless of what the original spell could legally target. CR 707.10c requires each new target be legal for that target's targeting requirement and disallows choosing the same target the copy already has only where prohibited. This is a known modeling simplification (acknowledged in the rationale) and the arbitrated tests accept it, so advisory only; a future refinement could restrict options to the spell's actual legal targets.\"\n13\t  },\n14\t  {\n15\t    \"severity\": \"advisory\",\n16\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_226/card_impl.py\",\n17\t    \"line\": 98,\n18\t    \"comment\": \"Modeling note (not a defect given arbitrated tests): casualty (CR 702.153) is an additional cost paid as you cast the spell, with the copy created by a delayed triggered ability. The implementation fires the offer after the spell StackObject is already pushed (engine hook calls _offer_casualty post-push) and pushes the copy directly rather than via a triggered ability. The push-on-top ordering approximates the delayed trigger resolving first, which is acceptable, but the copy bypasses the normal trigger/priority window. Recording for awareness only.\"\n19\t  }\n20\t]\n21\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FWkbLwQU8VHJEPVBvDNHZC","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"67106ff2-1748-4101-9d32-30792be123d3","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:47:14.475Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_226 per review"}
