{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SJBXcsUASHW1yDLzDNknpX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant) — revision rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Strict finding addressed (review.json index 0)\n4\t\n5\t**Finding:** The casualty sacrifice in `offer_casualty` reimplemented sacrifice\n6\tlogic via a raw `move_to_zone(game, chosen, Zone.BATTLEFIELD, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`\n7\twith no `replacement_event`. Per `move_to_zone`'s documented contract, that path\n8\tconsults no replacement effects, so sacrifice-redirection replacement effects\n9\t(e.g. \"if a creature you control would die, exile it instead\") were silently\n10\tbypassed for the casualty sacrifice.\n11\t\n12\t**Change applied:** Replaced the raw `move_to_zone(...)` call with the canonical\n13\tengine helper `engine.game.sacrifice(game, controller, chosen)`. Confirmed via\n14\t`engine/game.py` (lines 237-264) that `sacrifice(game, player, permanent)`:\n15\t- guards `bf.contains(permanent)` (returns early if not on the battlefield), and\n16\t- passes a `SacrificeReplacementEvent(...)` to `move_to_zone`, so sacrifice\n17\t  replacement effects are correctly consulted.\n18\t\n19\tThis makes the per-card `bf.contains` guard that previously preceded the raw\n20\tmove redundant for the move itself, but I kept the existing\n21\t`if chosen is None or not battlefield.contains(chosen): return False` guard\n22\tabove the call: it still serves to bail out of the whole casualty offer (no copy\n23\tmade) when the chosen creature is invalid, which is distinct from the helper's\n24\tinternal no-op guard.\n25\t\n26\t**Import convention:** `sacrifice` is imported *locally* inside `offer_casualty`\n27\t(`from engine.game import sacrifice`) rather than at module top level. This\n28\tmatches the established SOS convention for `engine.game` helpers — see\n29\t`cards/sos/sos_13` (`exile`, `create_token`), `cards/sos/sos_4`\n30\t(`deal_damage`, `draw_card`), `cards/sos/sos_97` (`discard`, `flip_coins`),\n31\tand `cards/sos/sos_201` (`draw_card`) — and avoids any import-cycle risk, since\n32\t`engine.game` imports `engine.turn`/`engine.game_state` at module load. The\n33\tnow-unused top-level imports `from engine.zones import move_to_zone` and the\n34\t`Zone` member of the `engine.types` import were removed (no other references in\n35\tthe file).\n36\t\n37\t## Advisory findings (recorded, intentionally left as-is)\n38\t\n39\t- **Index 1 (`_choose_new_targets`, broad target set, CR 707.10c):** The helper\n40\t  offers the union of all players plus every battlefield permanent as legal new\n41\t  targets rather than restricting to the original spell's legal targets. This is\n42\t  an accepted modeling simplification noted in the original rationale and\n43\t  accepted by the arbitrated tests. Left unchanged. A future refinement could\n44\t  restrict options to the spell's actual legal targets.\n45\t- **Index 2 (casualty additional-cost / delayed-trigger timing):** Casualty is\n46\t  modeled as an immediate post-push offer (the engine hook calls\n47\t  `_offer_casualty` after the spell StackObject is pushed) and the copy is\n48\t  pushed directly rather than via a delayed triggered ability resolving in its\n49\t  own priority window. The push-on-top ordering approximates the delayed trigger\n50\t  resolving first. Accepted modeling simplification, recorded for awareness.\n51\t  Left unchanged.\n52\t\n53\t## Verification\n54\t\n55\t`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` →\n56\t**1175 passed** (pre-existing cleanup-discard warnings only). All sos_226 tests\n57\tpass; engine_tests stay green. No test files were modified.\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"ec84dd48-a5ae-4f0a-917d-e024b2fc9b7b","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:49:15.184Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_226/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# sos_226 (Silverquill, the Disputant) — revision rationale\n\n## Strict finding addressed (review.json index 0)\n\n**Finding:** The casualty sacrifice in `offer_casualty` reimplemented sacrifice\nlogic via a raw `move_to_zone(game, chosen, Zone.BATTLEFIELD, Zone.GRAVEYARD)`\nwith no `replacement_event`. Per `move_to_zone`'s documented contract, that path\nconsults no replacement effects, so sacrifice-redirection replacement effects\n(e.g. \"if a creature you control would die, exile it instead\") were silently\nbypassed for the casualty sacrifice.\n\n**Change applied:** Replaced the raw `move_to_zone(...)` call with the canonical\nengine helper `engine.game.sacrifice(game, controller, chosen)`. Confirmed via\n`engine/game.py` (lines 237-264) that `sacrifice(game, player, permanent)`:\n- guards `bf.contains(permanent)` (returns early if not on the battlefield), and\n- passes a `SacrificeReplacementEvent(...)` to `move_to_zone`, so sacrifice\n  replacement effects are correctly consulted.\n\nThis makes the per-card `bf.contains` guard that previously preceded the raw\nmove redundant for the move itself, but I kept the existing\n`if chosen is None or not battlefield.contains(chosen): return False` guard\nabove the call: it still serves to bail out of the whole casualty offer (no copy\nmade) when the chosen creature is invalid, which is distinct from the helper's\ninternal no-op guard.\n\n**Import convention:** `sacrifice` is imported *locally* inside `offer_casualty`\n(`from engine.game import sacrifice`) rather than at module top level. This\nmatches the established SOS convention for `engine.game` helpers — see\n`cards/sos/sos_13` (`exile`, `create_token`), `cards/sos/sos_4`\n(`deal_damage`, `draw_card`), `cards/sos/sos_97` (`discard`, `flip_coins`),\nand `cards/sos/sos_201` (`draw_card`) — and avoids any import-cycle risk, since\n`engine.game` imports `engine.turn`/`engine.game_state` at module load. The\nnow-unused top-level imports `from engine.zones import move_to_zone` and the\n`Zone` member of the `engine.types` import were removed (no other references in\nthe file).\n\n## Advisory findings (recorded, intentionally left as-is)\n\n- **Index 1 (`_choose_new_targets`, broad target set, CR 707.10c):** The helper\n  offers the union of all players plus every battlefield permanent as legal new\n  targets rather than restricting to the original spell's legal targets. This is\n  an accepted modeling simplification noted in the original rationale and\n  accepted by the arbitrated tests. Left unchanged. A future refinement could\n  restrict options to the spell's actual legal targets.\n- **Index 2 (casualty additional-cost / delayed-trigger timing):** Casualty is\n  modeled as an immediate post-push offer (the engine hook calls\n  `_offer_casualty` after the spell StackObject is pushed) and the copy is\n  pushed directly rather than via a delayed triggered ability resolving in its\n  own priority window. The push-on-top ordering approximates the delayed trigger\n  resolving first. Accepted modeling simplification, recorded for awareness.\n  Left unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n\n`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_226/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` →\n**1175 passed** (pre-existing cleanup-discard warnings only). All sos_226 tests\npass; engine_tests stay green. No test files were modified.\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}}}
