{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01LDy6Pgv9hKzwSr7RpN4P4E","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015pT3sRm2WTnRJLB5UiwfVy","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)","new_string":"## Engine: casualty / \"as you cast\" cast-trigger hook + use sacrifice() helper (sos_226)\n- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` calls a fully-gated `_offer_casualty(game,\n  player, stack_obj)` helper AFTER pushing the spell StackObject. The helper is a\n  COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER controls returns a non-None\n  `grants_casualty_to(spell)` (getattr-safe — not all permanents define it); only\n  then it invokes that permanent's `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`. Default\n  cast path is byte-for-byte unchanged when no grantor is present. This is the\n  general pattern for \"as you cast a spell, do X\" granted abilities (mirrors the\n  sos_201 draw-time miracle hook). Cards expose `grants_casualty_to(spell) ->\n  int|None` (value for instants/sorceries) + `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`\n  (gates on controller match + instant/sorcery + a power>=1 creature to\n  sacrifice; pushes ONE distinct `copy_spell` with `is_spell=True`; optional new\n  targets via `choose_target`). Reuse `copy_spell(...)` — do NOT reimplement copy\n  logic. Modeling simplifications accepted: copy pushed directly post-push (not a\n  delayed triggered ability in its own priority window); new-target options are a\n  broad set rather than the spell's strict legal targets (CR 707.10c).\n- Convention: for any \"sacrifice a permanent\" effect, use the canonical\n  `engine.game.sacrifice(game, player, permanent)` helper (imported LOCALLY\n  inside the method, per SOS convention) rather than a raw\n  `move_to_zone(..., BATTLEFIELD, GRAVEYARD)`. `sacrifice` guards `bf.contains`\n  and passes a `SacrificeReplacementEvent`, so sacrifice-redirection replacement\n  effects (\"if a creature you control would die, exile it instead\", etc.) are\n  correctly consulted. A raw `move_to_zone` with no `replacement_event` silently\n  bypasses them.\n\n## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1583,"cache_read_input_tokens":64000,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1583},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"a021a2eb-a0e2-47a9-84a5-b0b461294cba","request_id":"req_011CbdbLZXDDWXcHewxwLBNB"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015pT3sRm2WTnRJLB5UiwfVy","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"0a19302f-c4c6-4643-bf17-ab6cba764874","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:49:29.475Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)","newString":"## Engine: casualty / \"as you cast\" cast-trigger hook + use sacrifice() helper (sos_226)\n- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` calls a fully-gated `_offer_casualty(game,\n  player, stack_obj)` helper AFTER pushing the spell StackObject. The helper is a\n  COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER controls returns a non-None\n  `grants_casualty_to(spell)` (getattr-safe — not all permanents define it); only\n  then it invokes that permanent's `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`. Default\n  cast path is byte-for-byte unchanged when no grantor is present. This is the\n  general pattern for \"as you cast a spell, do X\" granted abilities (mirrors the\n  sos_201 draw-time miracle hook). Cards expose `grants_casualty_to(spell) ->\n  int|None` (value for instants/sorceries) + `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`\n  (gates on controller match + instant/sorcery + a power>=1 creature to\n  sacrifice; pushes ONE distinct `copy_spell` with `is_spell=True`; optional new\n  targets via `choose_target`). Reuse `copy_spell(...)` — do NOT reimplement copy\n  logic. Modeling simplifications accepted: copy pushed directly post-push (not a\n  delayed triggered ability in its own priority window); new-target options are a\n  broad set rather than the spell's strict legal targets (CR 707.10c).\n- Convention: for any \"sacrifice a permanent\" effect, use the canonical\n  `engine.game.sacrifice(game, player, permanent)` helper (imported LOCALLY\n  inside the method, per SOS convention) rather than a raw\n  `move_to_zone(..., BATTLEFIELD, GRAVEYARD)`. `sacrifice` guards `bf.contains`\n  and passes a `SacrificeReplacementEvent`, so sacrifice-redirection replacement\n  effects (\"if a creature you control would die, exile it instead\", etc.) are\n  correctly consulted. A raw `move_to_zone` with no `replacement_event` silently\n  bypasses them.\n\n## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)","originalFile":"# Key Decisions\n\nPersistent conventions and decisions across runs. Append-only.\n\n## Engine: \"exile instead of graveyard\" for free-cast spells (sos_1)\nFor a non-permanent spell with \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\nexile it instead\": set `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell\nobject before casting it. `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` honors this opt-in\nflag and routes the resolving instant/sorcery from the stack to `Zone.EXILE`\ninstead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, then clears the flag (one-shot). Additive and\nbackward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /\nimpulse effects with the same rider.\n\n## Convention: recurring main-phase delayed trigger + Paradigm (sos_120)\nThe sos_57 `schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect` mechanism is ONE-SHOT. To make\na \"at the beginning of EACH of your main phases, do X\" recurring effect, have the\nscheduled callback RE-SCHEDULE ITSELF each time it fires. CRITICAL: arm the\nrecurring chain idempotently — exactly ONE chain per controller. Use a\nper-controller \"already armed\" guard (additive flag/set on game state or\ncontroller) so repeated resolutions (and resolved free COPIES, whose own\n`on_resolve` would otherwise re-arm) do not spawn additional chains (which would\nmultiply the offer per main phase). Paradigm keyword (CR 702.192): advertise via\na card marker (`self.paradigm`) / rules_text; \"Then exile this spell\" uses the\nsos_1 `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` opt-in; the recurring free-copy offer uses\nthis idempotent self-rescheduling pattern. Exile-until-threshold loops accumulate\n`mana_cost.cmc`, stop on `>= threshold` (boundary card may exceed; MV-0 doesn't\nstop), and terminate safely on a short/empty library.\n\n## Engine: coin flips + skip-turn support; planeswalker conventions (sos_97)\n- Coin flips: `engine.game.flip_coin(game, player=None) -> bool` (True=heads) and\n  `engine.game.flip_coins(game, n, player=None) -> int` (heads count).\n  Deterministic injection order: (1) `game._forced_coin_flips` (list/deque of\n  booleans, consumed from the FRONT); (2) `game.rng` (random.Random-compatible,\n  `rng.random() < 0.5`); (3) module `random`. Cards record their heads count on\n  an attribute (e.g. `pw._last_heads`) for assertion.\n- Skip turns: `Player.skipped_turns: int` (default 0). Honored by\n  `GameState.advance_phase` via `_select_next_active_player`: while the next\n  player has `skipped_turns > 0`, decrement it, consume the turn slot, and move\n  to the next candidate (bounded guard against infinite skip). `extra_turns`\n  FIFO behavior preserved. Use `target.skipped_turns += X` for \"skips their next\n  X turns\" (CR 614.10).\n- Planeswalkers: subclass `Planeswalker` (engine/card.py); set `starting_loyalty`,\n  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtype, explicit `self.colors`. `get_loyalty_abilities()`\n  returns `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)` closures\n  `(game)->None` reading `pw.controller`. Targeted abilities read\n  `pw._resolve_target` (single) / `pw._resolve_targets` (list). \"You may\" /\n  per-card decisions (e.g. surveil keep/bin) via controller `choose_yes_no`;\n  discards via `choose_card`. (Convention from FDN Kaito/Vivien/Liliana.)\n- Surveil N: look at top N library cards, bin any number (per-card `choose_yes_no`),\n  rest stay on top in order; fewer than N or empty library is a safe no-op.\n\n## Engine: mana-spent tracking, delayed main-phase triggers, spell/ability marker (sos_57)\n- `card.mana_spent: int` — set by `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` to the\n  converted mana actually paid (after cost reduction, `effective_cost.cmc`),\n  analogous to `card.colors_spent`; `cast_spell_free` sets 0. Read via\n  `getattr(card, \"mana_spent\", 0)`. Use for any \"amount of mana spent to cast\"\n  rider. (Known gap: ignores {X} payments — would under-count X-spells.)\n- `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, controller, precombat=True)` in\n  `engine/events.py`, fired by `engine/turn.py` on entering precombat/postcombat\n  main phases. Paired with `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(\n  controller, callback, *, precombat=True)` (registry on GameState; delivery via\n  `engine/deferred.py::deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects`, run SYNCHRONOUSLY\n  inside `TriggerManager.fire_event` for that event type). This is the general\n  \"at the beginning of your next main phase, do X once\" mechanism. A test fires\n  it directly: `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game,\n  BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=ctrl, controller=ctrl, precombat=True))`.\n  Effects are one-shot (removed on delivery).\n- `StackObject.is_spell: bool` (additive, default False) — set True only in the\n  casting pipeline (`cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free`, `copy_spell`). Abilities on\n  the stack reuse their source permanent's `card_types`, so to distinguish a\n  SPELL from an ability on the stack (e.g. for \"counter target spell\"), check\n  `getattr(stack_obj, \"is_spell\", False)` rather than inspecting `card_types`.\n\n## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\nThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n\n## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\nThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\nstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\nidentity must be observable.\n\n## Engine: alternative-cost casting + draw-time grants / miracle (sos_201)\n- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell(game, player, card, alternative_cost=None)` —\n  additive kwarg. When a `ManaCost` is passed it is paid INSTEAD of\n  `card.mana_cost`, cost reduction is NOT applied to the alt cost, the\n  sorcery-speed timing gate is bypassed (miracle/as-you-draw casts ignore\n  timing, CR 702.94/118.9), and `card.mana_spent` is set to the alt cost's\n  `cmc`. With `alternative_cost=None` the function is byte-for-byte unchanged —\n  the default cast path is untouched. Use for any \"you may cast this for its\n  <alternative> cost\" rider (miracle, flashback, evoke, etc.).\n- `Player.cards_drawn_this_turn: int` is the canonical per-turn draw counter,\n  reset to 0 at the untap step for ALL players (`engine/turn.py`). Use it for\n  \"the first card you drew this turn\" conditions.\n- Draw-time \"as you draw\" grants (miracle): advertise a capability\n  `grants_miracle_to(self, card) -> ManaCost | None` on a permanent. After\n  firing the draw event, `engine/game.py::draw_card` calls a fully-gated\n  `_offer_miracle` helper that is a COMPLETE no-op unless BOTH (a)\n  `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND (b) some permanent the player controls\n  returns a non-None `grants_miracle_to(card)`. Only then does it stamp\n  `card.miracle_cost` and offer `choose_yes_no`; on yes it casts the card for\n  the miracle cost via the alternative-cost surface (CastingError swallowed → an\n  unpayable miracle just stays in hand). Cards expose `MIRACLE_COST`\n  (`ManaCost`) and `grant_miracle(game)` to stamp `miracle_cost` onto eligible\n  cards (instants/sorceries) in the CONTROLLER's hand only. Modeling\n  simplification: the miracle window is an immediate at-draw offer (not the full\n  reveal→triggered-ability→cast-anytime sequence); deterministic and sufficient.\n\n## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)\nOverride `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine\nclamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in\n`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so no manual\nclamping is needed. The hook may read `self.controller` (engine sets it before\nquerying).\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":118,"oldLines":6,"newStart":118,"newLines":31,"lines":["   simplification: the miracle window is an immediate at-draw offer (not the full","   reveal→triggered-ability→cast-anytime sequence); deterministic and sufficient."," ","+## Engine: casualty / \"as you cast\" cast-trigger hook + use sacrifice() helper (sos_226)","+- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` calls a fully-gated `_offer_casualty(game,","+  player, stack_obj)` helper AFTER pushing the spell StackObject. The helper is a","+  COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER controls returns a non-None","+  `grants_casualty_to(spell)` (getattr-safe — not all permanents define it); only","+  then it invokes that permanent's `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`. Default","+  cast path is byte-for-byte unchanged when no grantor is present. This is the","+  general pattern for \"as you cast a spell, do X\" granted abilities (mirrors the","+  sos_201 draw-time miracle hook). Cards expose `grants_casualty_to(spell) ->","+  int|None` (value for instants/sorceries) + `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`","+  (gates on controller match + instant/sorcery + a power>=1 creature to","+  sacrifice; pushes ONE distinct `copy_spell` with `is_spell=True`; optional new","+  targets via `choose_target`). Reuse `copy_spell(...)` — do NOT reimplement copy","+  logic. Modeling simplifications accepted: copy pushed directly post-push (not a","+  delayed triggered ability in its own priority window); new-target options are a","+  broad set rather than the spell's strict legal targets (CR 707.10c).","+- Convention: for any \"sacrifice a permanent\" effect, use the canonical","+  `engine.game.sacrifice(game, player, permanent)` helper (imported LOCALLY","+  inside the method, per SOS convention) rather than a raw","+  `move_to_zone(..., BATTLEFIELD, GRAVEYARD)`. `sacrifice` guards `bf.contains`","+  and passes a `SacrificeReplacementEvent`, so sacrifice-redirection replacement","+  effects (\"if a creature you control would die, exile it instead\", etc.) are","+  correctly consulted. A raw `move_to_zone` with no `replacement_event` silently","+  bypasses them.","+"," ## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)"," Override `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine"," clamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
