{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EMHfwUTNaezJwFx3gq5TPi","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AGENTS.md — Workspace Orientation\n2\t\n3\t## Task\n4\t\n5\tYou are implementing SOS card implementations. Each card's implementation class\n6\tmust be placed in its assigned file:\n7\t\n8\t```\n9\tcards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py\n10\t```\n11\t\n12\t## Hard Rules\n13\t\n14\t1. **Card location invariant** — Each card's canonical implementation class must\n15\t   remain in `cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py`. Do not move or rename card\n16\t   directories.\n17\t\n18\t2. **Staged-test integrity** — Treat `engine_tests/` as read-only: do not\n19\t   modify, add to, or delete files in it. Likewise do not modify or delete any\n20\t   existing FDN reference test file at `cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py` (you may read\n21\t   them as examples, but never edit them). These tests are for your local\n22\t   verification and learning only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies\n23\t   for grading. Editing them — including adding new files — will not change\n24\t   your score, it will only mislead you about whether your engine changes are\n25\t   correct. Your own SOS tests belong at `cards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py`.\n26\t\n27\t3. **Additive-only engine modifications** — You may add new methods, classes,\n28\t   helpers, and files inside `engine/`. You may modify the bodies of existing\n29\t   functions to implement card behavior. You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete\n30\t   anything that already exists in `engine/` — no renaming, no refactoring.\n31\t   Restructuring the engine will break the grader's imports and zero your score.\n32\t\n33\tThese rules are derived from the project's Workspace Contract decisions\n34\t(maintained outside this workspace). They ensure deterministic grading.\n35\t\n36\t## Test Commands\n37\t\n38\tRun from the workspace root:\n39\t\n40\t```bash\n41\tpytest\n42\t```\n43\t\n44\tThis discovers:\n45\t- Engine regression tests at `engine_tests/test_*.py`.\n46\t- Per-card FDN reference tests at `cards/fdn/fdn_{collector_number}/tests.py`.\n47\t  Only a handful of FDN cards ship with a `tests.py` — see `PROJECT_MAP.md`\n48\t  for the canonical list, and use them as illustrative per-card test examples.\n49\t- Per-card SOS tests you write at `cards/sos/sos_{collector_number}/tests.py`.\n50\t\n51\tThe workspace `pytest.ini` configures `python_files = test_*.py tests.py` for\n52\tdiscovery of all three patterns and sets a per-test timeout (5 minutes).\n53\t\n54\tStandard imports inside per-card tests:\n55\t\n56\t```python\n57\tfrom cards.sos.sos_<N>.card_impl import <ClassName>\n58\tfrom engine.card import Creature, Instant                  # or whichever base\n59\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone\n60\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t## Engine Extension Scope\n64\t\n65\t- **May**: Add files, methods, classes, and helpers inside `engine/`.\n66\t- **May**: Modify the bodies of existing functions in `engine/`.\n67\t- **Must NOT**: Rename, move, or delete anything existing in `engine/`.\n68\t\n69\t## Rules questions → grep RULEBOOK.txt\n70\t\n71\t`RULEBOOK.txt` (workspace root) is the Magic: The Gathering Comprehensive Rules — the authoritative source for any rules question. **Whenever you're unsure how a mechanic works (keyword behavior, timing, replacement vs trigger ordering, state-based actions, etc.), check the rulebook before guessing in a `card_impl.py` or an `engine/` change.**\n72\t\n73\tThe file is large — don't `cat` or `Read` it whole. See the workspace skill at [`skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`](skills/grep-rulebook/SKILL.md) for grep recipes, the file's structure (numbered rules + glossary), and best practices.\n74\t\n75\t## Tools\n76\t\n77\tGit is available. The workspace is initialized as a git repository at stage time.\n78\t\n79\t## Navigation\n80\t\n81\tSee `PROJECT_MAP.md` for the directory layout.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013iwDt6en97Vyy5npkcLWpu","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"8d7c818a-180c-4b40-bc19-643f3aca73e7","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:49:51.759Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_245"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C8a59xBoskRedFqLqqPn8w","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# PROJECT_MAP.md — Directory Layout\n2\t\n3\t```\n4\tAGENTS.md          — Workspace orientation and rules\n5\tPROJECT_MAP.md     — This file; directory summary\n6\tRULEBOOK.txt       — The entire MTG comprehensive rules. Grep — do not read whole.\n7\tprompt.md          — Per-run task prompt (written at stage time)\n8\trun_manifest.json  — Per-run manifest written by the harness: `{timeout_seconds, deadline_utc}`. Harness-owned — do not edit.\n9\tpytest.ini         — Pytest configuration for the workspace\n10\tconftest.py        — Pytest fixtures shared across the workspace\n11\ttest_utils.py      — Shared test helpers (`create_game`, `set_board_state`, …)\n12\ttest_utils.md      — API reference for `test_utils.py`\n13\t.gitignore         — Git ignore rules\n14\tengine/            — Canonical game engine source. Imported as `engine`.\n15\tengine_tests/      — Engine regression tests (do not modify).\n16\tcards/             — Card implementations.\n17\t  cards/fdn/       — Completed FDN reference cards (do not modify their tests).\n18\t  cards/sos/       — SOS card stubs to implement.\n19\tskills/            — Workspace-local skills (e.g. `grep-rulebook/SKILL.md`).\n20\t```\n21\t\n22\t## Card paths\n23\t\n24\tFor an SOS card with collector number `N`:\n25\t\n26\t```\n27\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/card_spec.json   — card metadata (name, mana_cost, oracle_text, P/T, keywords, …)\n28\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/card_impl.py     — implementation stub you complete\n29\tcards/sos/sos_<N>/tests.py         — your tests for this card (you create this)\n30\t```\n31\t\n32\tFor an FDN reference card:\n33\t\n34\t```\n35\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/card_spec.json   — card metadata\n36\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/card_impl.py     — completed reference implementation (read for examples)\n37\tcards/fdn/fdn_<N>/tests.py         — only present for the cards listed below; read as test examples\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\t### FDN cards that ship with a `tests.py`\n41\t\n42\tThis is the canonical list — agent prompts refer back here instead of duplicating it.\n43\tDiscover the current set at any time with:\n44\t\n45\t```bash\n46\tfind cards/fdn -mindepth 2 -maxdepth 2 -name tests.py -printf '%h\\n' | sort -V\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tAs of the latest workspace stage, the list is: `fdn_13`, `fdn_142`, `fdn_205`, `fdn_215`, `fdn_244`. If you suspect the list has grown, re-run the `find` command above — it is authoritative.\n50\t\n51\t## Imports\n52\t\n53\tThe workspace root is on `sys.path`, so use bare package imports:\n54\t\n55\t```python\n56\tfrom cards.sos.sos_1.card_impl import TheDawningArchaic\n57\tfrom engine.card import CardImpl, Creature, Instant\n58\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Keyword, ManaCost, ManaType, Zone\n59\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n60\t```\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013iwDt6en97Vyy5npkcLWpu","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"c45992a2-49ca-43ba-b0de-9b63b3301bb2","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:49:51.758Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_245"}
