{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BvN8kvXrFiV73wmaKmZDrs","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test Rationale — sos_245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n2\t\n3\tCard spec: `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, colors B/G.\n4\tOracle text:\n5\t- \"Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.)\"\n6\t- \"Flying, deathtouch\"\n7\t- \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n8\t\n9\t## File: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`\n10\t\n11\t30 tests, class-grouped (mirrors the FDN/SOS `tests.py` style). Drives the real\n12\tengine (`GameState`, `engine.casting.cast_spell`, `engine.combat` helpers),\n13\tno mocks of the system under test.\n14\t\n15\t### Assumed API contract (so the Implementer can align)\n16\t- Class `WitherbloomTheBalancer` in `cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`, subclass of\n17\t  `engine.card.Creature`.\n18\t- Static data: `name`, `mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{6}{B}{G}\")`, `base_power == 5`,\n19\t  `base_toughness == 5`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY` in `supertypes`, `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"} <= subtypes`,\n20\t  `self.colors == [\"B\",\"G\"]` (explicit-colors convention, KEY_DECISIONS sos_13),\n21\t  `keywords` containing `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`.\n22\t- Own affinity: override `cost_reduction(game) -> int` returning the number of\n23\t  creatures the controller controls (FDN 6 Claws Out convention; engine clamps to\n24\t  the generic portion in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n25\t- Granted affinity capability (mirrors SOS 226 `grants_casualty_to` / SOS 201\n26\t  `grants_miracle_to`):\n27\t  - `grants_affinity_to(spell) -> bool` — truthy for instant/sorcery spells, falsy otherwise.\n28\t  - `affinity_reduction(game) -> int` — the creature count the controller controls (the\n29\t    reduction value granted to instants/sorceries; also the dragon's own affinity metric).\n30\t- Integration requirement: while Witherbloom is on the battlefield, the controller's\n31\t  instant/sorcery spells must actually be reduced by {1} per creature controlled when\n32\t  cast through `engine.casting.cast_spell`. The default engine `get_cost_reduction`\n33\t  consults only the spell's OWN `cost_reduction` hook, so the Implementer must add an\n34\t  additive, fully-gated cost-reduction hook that consults granting permanents\n35\t  (analogous to the sos_226 `_offer_casualty` cast hook), OR otherwise wire the grant.\n36\t  The tests assert the observable result and are agnostic to the wiring mechanism.\n37\t\n38\t### TestWitherbloomProperties (8 tests)\n39\tStatic characteristics from the spec: is a Creature, name, mana cost, mana value\n40\t(8), 5/5 P/T, Legendary supertype, Elder Dragon subtypes, and B/G colors via\n41\t`self.colors`. Validates the printed-data clauses.\n42\t\n43\t### TestWitherbloomKeywords (7 tests)\n44\t- `test_has_flying_and_deathtouch` — both keyword flags present.\n45\t- `test_does_not_have_unrelated_keywords` — guards against accidental extra\n46\t  evergreen keywords (Affinity is not an engine `Keyword`, so it must not appear\n47\t  as a flag).\n48\t- Flying combat consequences via `engine.combat._can_block`: a ground creature\n49\t  cannot block Witherbloom; flying and reach creatures can. Tests the rule, not\n50\t  the flag.\n51\t- Deathtouch consequence via `engine.combat._get_lethal_damage`: 1 damage is\n52\t  lethal when Witherbloom is the source, even against a 10/10. A non-deathtouch\n53\t  control test anchors that the lethal=1 result is caused by deathtouch.\n54\t\n55\t### TestWitherbloomOwnAffinity (6 tests)\n56\t\"Affinity for creatures\" on the dragon itself:\n57\t- Zero with no creatures; counts creatures you control; ignores opponents'\n58\t  creatures; ignores non-creature permanents (lands).\n59\t- `get_cost_reduction` clamping: with 9 creatures the reduction caps at the {6}\n60\t  generic.\n61\t- End-to-end real cast: with 3 creatures, casting Witherbloom consumes exactly\n62\t  {3}{B}{G} (pool emptied) and `mana_spent == 5`.\n63\t\n64\t### TestWitherbloomGrantedAffinityCapability (5 tests)\n65\t\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" — capability:\n66\t- `grants_affinity_to` truthy for instant and sorcery, falsy for creature spell\n67\t  and land.\n68\t- `affinity_reduction(game)` equals the number of creatures the controller\n69\t  controls (dragon + 2 bears = 3).\n70\t\n71\t### TestWitherbloomGrantedAffinityIntegration (4 tests)\n72\tThe granted ability's true requirement, driven through the real cast pipeline:\n73\t- A {3}{R} instant cast with 3 creatures (incl. Witherbloom) in play succeeds\n74\t  paying only {R} (the {3} generic fully reduced).\n75\t- A {4}{U} sorcery with 2 creatures reduces {4}→{2}, paid as {2}{U}.\n76\t- A creature spell ({3}{G}) is NOT reduced (grant is instant/sorcery only): with\n77\t  only {G} the cast raises `CastingError` and nothing changes. (Negative/control —\n78\t  passes pre-implementation because the feature is absent; remains correct after.)\n79\t- Regression: with Witherbloom NOT in play, a {3}{R} instant is not reduced even\n80\t  with 3 creatures controlled — `CastingError`. (Negative/control — same note.)\n81\t\n82\t## Edge cases covered\n83\t- Generic-clamp boundary (more creatures than reducible generic).\n84\t- Opponent creatures / non-creature permanents excluded from the affinity count.\n85\t- Grant restricted to instant/sorcery (creature spell excluded).\n86\t- Grant requires Witherbloom in play (off-battlefield regression).\n87\t\n88\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n89\t- Legend rule / \"Balancer\" name flavor — Witherbloom's name has no rules effect\n90\t  beyond the Legendary supertype, which is already asserted.\n91\t- Layered interaction of multiple simultaneous cost reducers (Trinisphere et al.)\n92\t  — out of scope per the engine's simplified single-source cost-reduction model\n93\t  (documented in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n94\t- {X} spells under granted affinity — the engine's `mana_spent` model under-counts\n95\t  X (KEY_DECISIONS sos_57), and the card grants no X behavior, so out of scope.\n96\t\n97\t## Red-phase status\n98\tAll card-behavior tests fail against the empty stub (25 of 30 fail). The 5\n99\tcurrently-passing tests are control/negative assertions (engine baseline, a\n100\tdefault-zero cost reduction, and two \"no reduction happens\" regressions) that\n101\tmust continue to hold after implementation; they carry no false-positive risk.\n102\tNo requirement was found untestable, so no `untestable.json` is written.\n103\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"09a61ec2-9302-4b0c-8974-1f7a43514d89","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:53:49.754Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/test-rationale.md","content":"# Test Rationale — sos_245 Witherbloom, the Balancer\n\nCard spec: `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, colors B/G.\nOracle text:\n- \"Affinity for creatures (This spell costs {1} less to cast for each creature you control.)\"\n- \"Flying, deathtouch\"\n- \"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures.\"\n\n## File: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py`\n\n30 tests, class-grouped (mirrors the FDN/SOS `tests.py` style). Drives the real\nengine (`GameState`, `engine.casting.cast_spell`, `engine.combat` helpers),\nno mocks of the system under test.\n\n### Assumed API contract (so the Implementer can align)\n- Class `WitherbloomTheBalancer` in `cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`, subclass of\n  `engine.card.Creature`.\n- Static data: `name`, `mana_cost == ManaCost.parse(\"{6}{B}{G}\")`, `base_power == 5`,\n  `base_toughness == 5`, `Supertype.LEGENDARY` in `supertypes`, `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"} <= subtypes`,\n  `self.colors == [\"B\",\"G\"]` (explicit-colors convention, KEY_DECISIONS sos_13),\n  `keywords` containing `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`.\n- Own affinity: override `cost_reduction(game) -> int` returning the number of\n  creatures the controller controls (FDN 6 Claws Out convention; engine clamps to\n  the generic portion in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n- Granted affinity capability (mirrors SOS 226 `grants_casualty_to` / SOS 201\n  `grants_miracle_to`):\n  - `grants_affinity_to(spell) -> bool` — truthy for instant/sorcery spells, falsy otherwise.\n  - `affinity_reduction(game) -> int` — the creature count the controller controls (the\n    reduction value granted to instants/sorceries; also the dragon's own affinity metric).\n- Integration requirement: while Witherbloom is on the battlefield, the controller's\n  instant/sorcery spells must actually be reduced by {1} per creature controlled when\n  cast through `engine.casting.cast_spell`. The default engine `get_cost_reduction`\n  consults only the spell's OWN `cost_reduction` hook, so the Implementer must add an\n  additive, fully-gated cost-reduction hook that consults granting permanents\n  (analogous to the sos_226 `_offer_casualty` cast hook), OR otherwise wire the grant.\n  The tests assert the observable result and are agnostic to the wiring mechanism.\n\n### TestWitherbloomProperties (8 tests)\nStatic characteristics from the spec: is a Creature, name, mana cost, mana value\n(8), 5/5 P/T, Legendary supertype, Elder Dragon subtypes, and B/G colors via\n`self.colors`. Validates the printed-data clauses.\n\n### TestWitherbloomKeywords (7 tests)\n- `test_has_flying_and_deathtouch` — both keyword flags present.\n- `test_does_not_have_unrelated_keywords` — guards against accidental extra\n  evergreen keywords (Affinity is not an engine `Keyword`, so it must not appear\n  as a flag).\n- Flying combat consequences via `engine.combat._can_block`: a ground creature\n  cannot block Witherbloom; flying and reach creatures can. Tests the rule, not\n  the flag.\n- Deathtouch consequence via `engine.combat._get_lethal_damage`: 1 damage is\n  lethal when Witherbloom is the source, even against a 10/10. A non-deathtouch\n  control test anchors that the lethal=1 result is caused by deathtouch.\n\n### TestWitherbloomOwnAffinity (6 tests)\n\"Affinity for creatures\" on the dragon itself:\n- Zero with no creatures; counts creatures you control; ignores opponents'\n  creatures; ignores non-creature permanents (lands).\n- `get_cost_reduction` clamping: with 9 creatures the reduction caps at the {6}\n  generic.\n- End-to-end real cast: with 3 creatures, casting Witherbloom consumes exactly\n  {3}{B}{G} (pool emptied) and `mana_spent == 5`.\n\n### TestWitherbloomGrantedAffinityCapability (5 tests)\n\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" — capability:\n- `grants_affinity_to` truthy for instant and sorcery, falsy for creature spell\n  and land.\n- `affinity_reduction(game)` equals the number of creatures the controller\n  controls (dragon + 2 bears = 3).\n\n### TestWitherbloomGrantedAffinityIntegration (4 tests)\nThe granted ability's true requirement, driven through the real cast pipeline:\n- A {3}{R} instant cast with 3 creatures (incl. Witherbloom) in play succeeds\n  paying only {R} (the {3} generic fully reduced).\n- A {4}{U} sorcery with 2 creatures reduces {4}→{2}, paid as {2}{U}.\n- A creature spell ({3}{G}) is NOT reduced (grant is instant/sorcery only): with\n  only {G} the cast raises `CastingError` and nothing changes. (Negative/control —\n  passes pre-implementation because the feature is absent; remains correct after.)\n- Regression: with Witherbloom NOT in play, a {3}{R} instant is not reduced even\n  with 3 creatures controlled — `CastingError`. (Negative/control — same note.)\n\n## Edge cases covered\n- Generic-clamp boundary (more creatures than reducible generic).\n- Opponent creatures / non-creature permanents excluded from the affinity count.\n- Grant restricted to instant/sorcery (creature spell excluded).\n- Grant requires Witherbloom in play (off-battlefield regression).\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered\n- Legend rule / \"Balancer\" name flavor — Witherbloom's name has no rules effect\n  beyond the Legendary supertype, which is already asserted.\n- Layered interaction of multiple simultaneous cost reducers (Trinisphere et al.)\n  — out of scope per the engine's simplified single-source cost-reduction model\n  (documented in `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`).\n- {X} spells under granted affinity — the engine's `mana_spent` model under-counts\n  X (KEY_DECISIONS sos_57), and the card grants no X behavior, so out of scope.\n\n## Red-phase status\nAll card-behavior tests fail against the empty stub (25 of 30 fail). The 5\ncurrently-passing tests are control/negative assertions (engine baseline, a\ndefault-zero cost reduction, and two \"no reduction happens\" regressions) that\nmust continue to hold after implementation; they carry no false-positive risk.\nNo requirement was found untestable, so no `untestable.json` is written.\n","numLines":103,"startLine":1,"totalLines":103}}}
