{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0116N3XT6x8TZvPb2dwbhVtt","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_245 (Witherbloom, the Balancer)\n2\t\n3\tNo untestable items (Tester `untestable_count: 0`). The integration tests assert\n4\tobservable results and are agnostic to wiring, but they REQUIRE an additive,\n5\tfully-gated engine change because the default `engine.casting.get_cost_reduction`\n6\tconsults only the spell's OWN `cost_reduction` hook. Build the surface below.\n7\t\n8\t## Card: Witherbloom, the Balancer\n9\t- `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature — Elder Dragon, 5/5, colors B/G.\n10\t- Subclass `Creature`. `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`,\n11\t  explicit `self.colors = [\"B\",\"G\"]`, keywords `Keyword.FLYING |\n12\t  Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`. Affinity is NOT an engine Keyword — do not add it as a flag.\n13\t- Own \"Affinity for creatures\": override `cost_reduction(self, game) -> int`\n14\t  returning the number of creatures the CONTROLLER controls (FDN 6 convention;\n15\t  engine clamps to the generic portion in `get_cost_reduction` — no manual clamp).\n16\t- Granted-affinity capability (mirrors sos_226 `grants_casualty_to` / sos_201\n17\t  `grants_miracle_to`):\n18\t  - `grants_affinity_to(self, spell) -> bool` — truthy for instant/sorcery spells.\n19\t  - `affinity_reduction(self, game) -> int` — creature count the controller\n20\t    controls (the reduction granted to instants/sorceries; also the dragon's own\n21\t    affinity metric — `cost_reduction` may delegate to it).\n22\t\n23\t## Additive engine change: granted cost reduction from other permanents\n24\t\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" means a\n25\tpermanent (Witherbloom) grants a cost reduction to OTHER spells. The default\n26\t`get_cost_reduction` only reads the casting spell's own `cost_reduction`. Extend\n27\t`engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction` (or add a fully-gated helper it calls) so\n28\tit ALSO sums reductions granted by permanents the CASTER controls:\n29\t- For each permanent the caster controls, getattr-safe check\n30\t  `grants_affinity_to(spell)`; if truthy, add `affinity_reduction(game)` to the\n31\t  raw reduction before the existing generic-clamp (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`).\n32\t- This must be COMPLETELY no-op when no controlled permanent grants affinity, so\n33\t  the default reduction path and all engine_tests stay byte-for-byte equivalent.\n34\t  Use getattr-safe capability probing (most permanents lack these methods).\n35\t- Keep the existing single-source clamp semantics; the granted reduction is added\n36\t  into the same raw total and clamped to the generic portion together.\n37\t\n38\tReuse the established grant-capability PATTERN (sos_226 `_offer_casualty`,\n39\tsos_201 miracle). Additive only — no renaming/moving/deleting engine symbols.\n40\t\n41\t## Constraints\n42\t- DO NOT modify any test file in `test-files.txt`. If a test is genuinely wrong,\n43\t  return DISPUTE.\n44\t- Run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`; all\n45\t  sos_245 tests pass and engine_tests stay green.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019PHzm2FDpRXoh6F4NHApme","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"602cbc13-6cd8-45b8-8481-7568e96c4ac9","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:54:32.349Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_245 Witherbloom + affinity"}
