{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UzkegfV7wLGBhmS87g5a65","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SoJV3VsZ5mdzZXcDXNJvbu","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md","content":"# sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer — implementation rationale\n\n## Card (`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`)\n`WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)` — `{6}{B}{G}`, 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`,\nsubtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, explicit\n`self.colors = [\"B\",\"G\"]` (sos_13 convention). Affinity is NOT modeled as an\nengine `Keyword` (the spec lists it but the engine has no such flag and the\ntests guard against extra keywords) — it is purely a cost-reduction mechanic.\n\nThree surfaces:\n\n- `cost_reduction(game) -> int` — \"Affinity for creatures\" for the dragon's own\n  cast. It delegates to `affinity_reduction(game)` so the self-affinity and the\n  granted-affinity metric share one source of truth. No manual clamp: the engine\n  clamps to the generic portion in `get_cost_reduction` (FDN 6 Claws Out\n  convention).\n- `grants_affinity_to(spell) -> bool` — truthy only for instants/sorceries\n  (getattr-safe `card_types` probe), the capability the engine queries.\n- `affinity_reduction(game) -> int` — number of creatures the controller\n  controls; 0 when controller is None.\n\n## Additive engine change (`engine/casting.py`)\n\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" means a\npermanent grants cost reduction to OTHER spells, which the default\n`get_cost_reduction` (self-hook only) cannot express. Following the sos_226\n`_offer_casualty` / sos_201 miracle grant-capability pattern:\n\n- Added a fully-gated helper `_granted_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`\n  that iterates the CASTER's battlefield and, for each permanent, getattr-safe\n  probes `grants_affinity_to(card)`; when truthy it adds that permanent's\n  `affinity_reduction(game)` to a running total.\n- `get_cost_reduction` adds this granted total into the existing `raw` value\n  BEFORE the unchanged single-source clamp `max(0, min(raw, generic))`, so the\n  granted reduction is clamped to the generic portion together with the\n  self-reduction. Clamp semantics are untouched.\n- Complete no-op when no controlled permanent advertises the capability: most\n  permanents define neither method (getattr returns None → `continue`), so the\n  loop adds 0 and the default path / all engine_tests stay byte-for-byte\n  equivalent. A `permanent is card` guard prevents a permanent that grants to\n  itself from double-counting (defensive; the grantor is on the battlefield, the\n  spell on the stack, so they are never the same object in practice).\n\n## Convention worth reusing\nGranted cost reduction = the same getattr-safe capability pattern as casualty\n(sos_226) and miracle (sos_201), but wired into `get_cost_reduction` rather than\n`cast_spell`/`draw_card`. Future \"spells you cast cost less / have affinity\"\ngrantors expose `grants_affinity_to(spell) -> bool` + `affinity_reduction(game)\n-> int` on a permanent; the engine sums them across the caster's battlefield.\n\n## Verification\n`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` → 1175 passed\n(30 sos_245 + all engine_tests green; warnings are pre-existing unrelated\ncleanup-discard warnings).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":192,"cache_read_input_tokens":64881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":192,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":68,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019PHzm2FDpRXoh6F4NHApme","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"4abdba11-7907-4a0f-8a1e-339c2c384d06","request_id":"req_011Cbdbrdj4Ti