{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UcHmPNnCe134nnfm6ZQuRw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_245 — Witherbloom, the Balancer — implementation rationale\n2\t\n3\t## Card (`cards/sos/sos_245/card_impl.py`)\n4\t`WitherbloomTheBalancer(Creature)` — `{6}{B}{G}`, 5/5, `Supertype.LEGENDARY`,\n5\tsubtypes `{\"Elder\",\"Dragon\"}`, `Keyword.FLYING | Keyword.DEATHTOUCH`, explicit\n6\t`self.colors = [\"B\",\"G\"]` (sos_13 convention). Affinity is NOT modeled as an\n7\tengine `Keyword` (the spec lists it but the engine has no such flag and the\n8\ttests guard against extra keywords) — it is purely a cost-reduction mechanic.\n9\t\n10\tThree surfaces:\n11\t\n12\t- `cost_reduction(game) -> int` — \"Affinity for creatures\" for the dragon's own\n13\t  cast. It delegates to `affinity_reduction(game)` so the self-affinity and the\n14\t  granted-affinity metric share one source of truth. No manual clamp: the engine\n15\t  clamps to the generic portion in `get_cost_reduction` (FDN 6 Claws Out\n16\t  convention).\n17\t- `grants_affinity_to(spell) -> bool` — truthy only for instants/sorceries\n18\t  (getattr-safe `card_types` probe), the capability the engine queries.\n19\t- `affinity_reduction(game) -> int` — number of creatures the controller\n20\t  controls; 0 when controller is None.\n21\t\n22\t## Additive engine change (`engine/casting.py`)\n23\t\"Instant and sorcery spells you cast have affinity for creatures\" means a\n24\tpermanent grants cost reduction to OTHER spells, which the default\n25\t`get_cost_reduction` (self-hook only) cannot express. Following the sos_226\n26\t`_offer_casualty` / sos_201 miracle grant-capability pattern:\n27\t\n28\t- Added a fully-gated helper `_granted_cost_reduction(game, card, controller)`\n29\t  that iterates the CASTER's battlefield and, for each permanent, getattr-safe\n30\t  probes `grants_affinity_to(card)`; when truthy it adds that permanent's\n31\t  `affinity_reduction(game)` to a running total.\n32\t- `get_cost_reduction` adds this granted total into the existing `raw` value\n33\t  BEFORE the unchanged single-source clamp `max(0, min(raw, generic))`, so the\n34\t  granted reduction is clamped to the generic portion together with the\n35\t  self-reduction. Clamp semantics are untouched.\n36\t- Complete no-op when no controlled permanent advertises the capability: most\n37\t  permanents define neither method (getattr returns None → `continue`), so the\n38\t  loop adds 0 and the default path / all engine_tests stay byte-for-byte\n39\t  equivalent. A `permanent is card` guard prevents a permanent that grants to\n40\t  itself from double-counting (defensive; the grantor is on the battlefield, the\n41\t  spell on the stack, so they are never the same object in practice).\n42\t\n43\t## Convention worth reusing\n44\tGranted cost reduction = the same getattr-safe capability pattern as casualty\n45\t(sos_226) and miracle (sos_201), but wired into `get_cost_reduction` rather than\n46\t`cast_spell`/`draw_card`. Future \"spells you cast cost less / have affinity\"\n47\tgrantors expose `grants_affinity_to(spell) -> bool` + `affinity_reduction(game)\n48\t-> int` on a permanent; the engine sums them across the caster's battlefield.\n49\t\n50\t## Verification\n51\t`python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_245/tests.py engine_tests/ -q` → 1175 passed\n52\t(30 sos_245 + all engine_tests green; warnings are pre-existing unrelated\n53\tcleanup-discard warnings).\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FhNfUVJpcxNHXwXyrc99xQ","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"c8f61a34-b4d3-4f24-bd03-3f92445ce43e","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:57:04.167Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_245 implementation"}
