{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FhNfUVJpcxNHXwXyrc99xQ","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. I examined the card implementation, the additive `engine/casting.py` change, the test file, the engine APIs (`get_battlefield`, `zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD]`, `Creature` base class, `ZoneContainer.get_all`), the cast pipeline call site, and the existing engine cost-reduction regression tests.\n\nFindings: no strict-severity defects. The engine change is correctly gated (getattr-safe, complete no-op when no controlled permanent advertises the capability, summed into `raw` before the unchanged `max(0, min(raw, generic))` clamp). The card's own affinity counts only the controller's creatures, `grants_affinity_to` is truthy only for instants/sorceries, `affinity_reduction` equals the controller's creature count, and static characteristics (flying+deathtouch, legendary, `[\"B\",\"G\"]` colors, Elder Dragon subtypes, 5/5, `{6}{B}{G}`) are correct. Affinity is not added as a Keyword. The `permanent is card` guard plus the fact that a self-cast Witherbloom is on the stack (not the battlefield) means no double-counting. Two advisory notes recorded about the summing model and the dual controller-source paths.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 2\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: af3264c5a86e5c71e (use SendMessage with to: 'af3264c5a86e5c71e' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 49558\ntool_uses: 17\nduration_ms: 75275</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"9c700ae0-2706-4bfa-b038-f92a51844651","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:58:16.168Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Review the implementation diff for card **sos_245** (Witherbloom, the Balancer — `{6}{B}{G}` Legendary Creature—Elder Dragon 5/5, flying+deathtouch, own \"affinity for creatures\", and grants affinity for creatures to the controller's instant/sorcery spells). The implementation also adds an additive change to the engine's cost-reduction path.\n\n## What to review\n- Diff: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl.diff`\n- Rationale (context): `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/impl-rationale.md`\n\n## Review focus\nCorrectness vs. spec intent, real bugs, missed edge cases, and convention violations VISIBLE IN THE DIFF. Specifically scrutinize:\n- The change to `engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction` (or its helper): it must SUM granted reductions from permanents the CASTER controls via getattr-safe `grants_affinity_to(spell)` + `affinity_reduction(game)`, added into the raw total before the existing generic-clamp `max(0, min(raw, generic))`. It MUST be a COMPLETE no-op when no controlled permanent grants affinity — no regression to the default reduction path, getattr-safe (permanents without these methods must not raise).\n- Own affinity: `cost_reduction(game)` counts only the CONTROLLER's creatures (excludes opponents' creatures and non-creatures); relies on the engine clamp (no manual clamp needed, but a manual clamp is not a bug).\n- `grants_affinity_to` truthy only for instants/sorceries; `affinity_reduction` equals controller's creature count.\n- Flying/deathtouch, legendary, colors (`self.colors == [\"B\",\"G\"]`), Elder Dragon subtypes correctness. Affinity must NOT be added as an engine Keyword flag.\n- Watch for double-counting (e.g. Witherbloom granting affinity to itself as a creature spell, or its own `cost_reduction` being summed twice through the new permanent-scan path).\n\n## Constraints\n- Read `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` and `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`. Do NOT flag patterns introduced by earlier cards or conventions established in KEY_DECISIONS.md (explicit self.colors, mana_spent, cost_reduction hook + clamp, grant-capability pattern, etc.).\n- Do NOT demand test rewrites — tests were already arbitrated. Test-quality issues are `advisory` only.\n\n## Output\nWrite `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json` as a JSON array of objects:\n`{\"severity\": \"strict\"|\"advisory\", \"file\": \"<path>\", \"line\": <n>, \"comment\": \"<text>\"}`. Use `strict` only for real correctness/spec/convention defects that must be fixed; everything else is `advisory`. Empty array `[]` if no findings.\n\n## Return status summary\n```\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: <N>\nadvisory_count: <N>\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json\n```","agentId":"af3264c5a86e5c71e","agentType":"Reviewer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review complete. I examined the card implementation, the additive `engine/casting.py` change, the test file, the engine APIs (`get_battlefield`, `zones[Zone.BATTLEFIELD]`, `Creature` base class, `ZoneContainer.get_all`), the cast pipeline call site, and the existing engine cost-reduction regression tests.\n\nFindings: no strict-severity defects. The engine change is correctly gated (getattr-safe, complete no-op when no controlled permanent advertises the capability, summed into `raw` before the unchanged `max(0, min(raw, generic))` clamp). The card's own affinity counts only the controller's creatures, `grants_affinity_to` is truthy only for instants/sorceries, `affinity_reduction` equals the controller's creature count, and static characteristics (flying+deathtouch, legendary, `[\"B\",\"G\"]` colors, Elder Dragon subtypes, 5/5, `{6}{B}{G}`) are correct. Affinity is not added as a Keyword. The `permanent is card` guard plus the fact that a self-cast Witherbloom is on the stack (not the battlefield) means no double-counting. Two advisory notes recorded about the summing model and the dual controller-source paths.\n\nREVIEW_DONE\nstrict_count: 0\nadvisory_count: 2\nreview_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_245/review.json"}],"totalDurationMs":75275,"totalTokens":49558,"totalToolUseCount":17,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1436,"cache_read_input_tokens":47654,"output_tokens":466,"ser