{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FvsCwbugWsNvHR12ScMZt4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent conventions and decisions across runs. Append-only.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: \"exile instead of graveyard\" for free-cast spells (sos_1)\n6\tFor a non-permanent spell with \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\n7\texile it instead\": set `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell\n8\tobject before casting it. `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` honors this opt-in\n9\tflag and routes the resolving instant/sorcery from the stack to `Zone.EXILE`\n10\tinstead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, then clears the flag (one-shot). Additive and\n11\tbackward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /\n12\timpulse effects with the same rider.\n13\t\n14\t## Convention: recurring main-phase delayed trigger + Paradigm (sos_120)\n15\tThe sos_57 `schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect` mechanism is ONE-SHOT. To make\n16\ta \"at the beginning of EACH of your main phases, do X\" recurring effect, have the\n17\tscheduled callback RE-SCHEDULE ITSELF each time it fires. CRITICAL: arm the\n18\trecurring chain idempotently — exactly ONE chain per controller. Use a\n19\tper-controller \"already armed\" guard (additive flag/set on game state or\n20\tcontroller) so repeated resolutions (and resolved free COPIES, whose own\n21\t`on_resolve` would otherwise re-arm) do not spawn additional chains (which would\n22\tmultiply the offer per main phase). Paradigm keyword (CR 702.192): advertise via\n23\ta card marker (`self.paradigm`) / rules_text; \"Then exile this spell\" uses the\n24\tsos_1 `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` opt-in; the recurring free-copy offer uses\n25\tthis idempotent self-rescheduling pattern. Exile-until-threshold loops accumulate\n26\t`mana_cost.cmc`, stop on `>= threshold` (boundary card may exceed; MV-0 doesn't\n27\tstop), and terminate safely on a short/empty library.\n28\t\n29\t## Engine: coin flips + skip-turn support; planeswalker conventions (sos_97)\n30\t- Coin flips: `engine.game.flip_coin(game, player=None) -> bool` (True=heads) and\n31\t  `engine.game.flip_coins(game, n, player=None) -> int` (heads count).\n32\t  Deterministic injection order: (1) `game._forced_coin_flips` (list/deque of\n33\t  booleans, consumed from the FRONT); (2) `game.rng` (random.Random-compatible,\n34\t  `rng.random() < 0.5`); (3) module `random`. Cards record their heads count on\n35\t  an attribute (e.g. `pw._last_heads`) for assertion.\n36\t- Skip turns: `Player.skipped_turns: int` (default 0). Honored by\n37\t  `GameState.advance_phase` via `_select_next_active_player`: while the next\n38\t  player has `skipped_turns > 0`, decrement it, consume the turn slot, and move\n39\t  to the next candidate (bounded guard against infinite skip). `extra_turns`\n40\t  FIFO behavior preserved. Use `target.skipped_turns += X` for \"skips their next\n41\t  X turns\" (CR 614.10).\n42\t- Planeswalkers: subclass `Planeswalker` (engine/card.py); set `starting_loyalty`,\n43\t  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtype, explicit `self.colors`. `get_loyalty_abilities()`\n44\t  returns `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)` closures\n45\t  `(game)->None` reading `pw.controller`. Targeted abilities read\n46\t  `pw._resolve_target` (single) / `pw._resolve_targets` (list). \"You may\" /\n47\t  per-card decisions (e.g. surveil keep/bin) via controller `choose_yes_no`;\n48\t  discards via `choose_card`. (Convention from FDN Kaito/Vivien/Liliana.)\n49\t- Surveil N: look at top N library cards, bin any number (per-card `choose_yes_no`),\n50\t  rest stay on top in order; fewer than N or empty library is a safe no-op.\n51\t\n52\t## Engine: mana-spent tracking, delayed main-phase triggers, spell/ability marker (sos_57)\n53\t- `card.mana_spent: int` — set by `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` to the\n54\t  converted mana actually paid (after cost reduction, `effective_cost.cmc`),\n55\t  analogous to `card.colors_spent`; `cast_spell_free` sets 0. Read via\n56\t  `getattr(card, \"mana_spent\", 0)`. Use for any \"amount of mana spent to cast\"\n57\t  rider. (Known gap: ignores {X} payments — would under-count X-spells.)\n58\t- `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, controller, precombat=True)` in\n59\t  `engine/events.py`, fired by `engine/turn.py` on entering precombat/postcombat\n60\t  main phases. Paired with `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(\n61\t  controller, callback, *, precombat=True)` (registry on GameState; delivery via\n62\t  `engine/deferred.py::deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects`, run SYNCHRONOUSLY\n63\t  inside `TriggerManager.fire_event` for that event type). This is the general\n64\t  \"at the beginning of your next main phase, do X once\" mechanism. A test fires\n65\t  it directly: `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game,\n66\t  BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=ctrl, controller=ctrl, precombat=True))`.\n67\t  Effects are one-shot (removed on delivery).\n68\t- `StackObject.is_spell: bool` (additive, default False) — set True only in the\n69\t  casting pipeline (`cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free`, `copy_spell`). Abilities on\n70\t  the stack reuse their source permanent's `card_types`, so to distinguish a\n71\t  SPELL from an ability on the stack (e.g. for \"counter target spell\"), check\n72\t  `getattr(stack_obj, \"is_spell\", False)` rather than inspecting `card_types`.\n73\t\n74\t## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\n75\tThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n76\t(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n77\t- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n78\t  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n79\t- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n80\t  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n81\t  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n82\t  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n83\t  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n84\t  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n85\t- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n86\t  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n87\t  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n88\t  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n89\t\n90\t## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\n91\tThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\n92\tstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\n93\tidentity must be observable.\n94\t\n95\t## Engine: alternative-cost casting + draw-time grants / miracle (sos_201)\n96\t- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell(game, player, card, alternative_cost=None)` —\n97\t  additive kwarg. When a `ManaCost` is passed it is paid INSTEAD of\n98\t  `card.mana_cost`, cost reduction is NOT applied to the alt cost, the\n99\t  sorcery-speed timing gate is bypassed (miracle/as-you-draw casts ignore\n100\t  timing, CR 702.94/118.9), and `card.mana_spent` is set to the alt cost's\n101\t  `cmc`. With `alternative_cost=None` the function is byte-for-byte unchanged —\n102\t  the default cast path is untouched. Use for any \"you may cast this for its\n103\t  <alternative> cost\" rider (miracle, flashback, evoke, etc.).\n104\t- `Player.cards_drawn_this_turn: int` is the canonical per-turn draw counter,\n105\t  reset to 0 at the untap step for ALL players (`engine/turn.py`). Use it for\n106\t  \"the first card you drew this turn\" conditions.\n107\t- Draw-time \"as you draw\" grants (miracle): advertise a capability\n108\t  `grants_miracle_to(self, card) -> ManaCost | None` on a permanent. After\n109\t  firing the draw event, `engine/game.py::draw_card` calls a fully-gated\n110\t  `_offer_miracle` helper that is a COMPLETE no-op unless BOTH (a)\n111\t  `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND (b) some permanent the player controls\n112\t  returns a non-None `grants_miracle_to(card)`. Only then does it stamp\n113\t  `card.miracle_cost` and offer `choose_yes_no`; on yes it casts the card for\n114\t  the miracle cost via the alternative-cost surface (CastingError swallowed → an\n115\t  unpayable miracle just stays in hand). Cards expose `MIRACLE_COST`\n116\t  (`ManaCost`) and `grant_miracle(game)` to stamp `miracle_cost` onto eligible\n117\t  cards (instants/sorceries) in the CONTROLLER's hand only. Modeling\n118\t  simplification: the miracle window is an immediate at-draw offer (not the full\n119\t  reveal→triggered-ability→cast-anytime sequence); deterministic and sufficient.\n120\t\n121\t## Engine: casualty / \"as you cast\" cast-trigger hook + use sacrifice() helper (sos_226)\n122\t- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` calls a fully-gated `_offer_casualty(game,\n123\t  player, stack_obj)` helper AFTER pushing the spell StackObject. The helper is a\n124\t  COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER controls returns a non-None\n125\t  `grants_casualty_to(spell)` (getattr-safe — not all permanents define it); only\n126\t  then it invokes that permanent's `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`. Default\n127\t  cast path is byte-for-byte unchanged when no grantor is present. This is the\n128\t  general pattern for \"as you cast a spell, do X\" granted abilities (mirrors the\n129\t  sos_201 draw-time miracle hook). Cards expose `grants_casualty_to(spell) ->\n130\t  int|None` (value for instants/sorceries) + `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`\n131\t  (gates on controller match + instant/sorcery + a power>=1 creature to\n132\t  sacrifice; pushes ONE distinct `copy_spell` with `is_spell=True`; optional new\n133\t  targets via `choose_target`). Reuse `copy_spell(...)` — do NOT reimplement copy\n134\t  logic. Modeling simplifications accepted: copy pushed directly post-push (not a\n135\t  delayed triggered ability in its own priority window); new-target options are a\n136\t  broad set rather than the spell's strict legal targets (CR 707.10c).\n137\t- Convention: for any \"sacrifice a permanent\" effect, use the canonical\n138\t  `engine.game.sacrifice(game, player, permanent)` helper (imported LOCALLY\n139\t  inside the method, per SOS convention) rather than a raw\n140\t  `move_to_zone(..., BATTLEFIELD, GRAVEYARD)`. `sacrifice` guards `bf.contains`\n141\t  and passes a `SacrificeReplacementEvent`, so sacrifice-redirection replacement\n142\t  effects (\"if a creature you control would die, exile it instead\", etc.) are\n143\t  correctly consulted. A raw `move_to_zone` with no `replacement_event` silently\n144\t  bypasses them.\n145\t\n146\t## Engine: granted cost reduction from controlled permanents / affinity grant (sos_245)\n147\t`engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction` now sums, in addition to the casting\n148\tspell's OWN `cost_reduction(game)` hook, reductions GRANTED by permanents the\n149\tCASTER controls. A fully-gated helper `_granted_cost_reduction(game, card,\n150\tcontroller)` iterates the caster's battlefield and getattr-safe probes\n151\t`grants_affinity_to(card)`; when truthy it adds that permanent's\n152\t`affinity_reduction(game)` into the raw total BEFORE the unchanged single-source\n153\tclamp `max(0, min(raw, generic))` (granted reduction clamped to the generic\n154\tportion together with the self-reduction). COMPLETE no-op when no controlled\n155\tpermanent advertises the capability (most permanents define neither method →\n156\tloop adds 0), so the default path + all engine_tests are byte-for-byte\n157\tequivalent. A `permanent is card` guard prevents self-grant double-counting.\n158\tThis is the general \"spells you cast cost less / have affinity for X\" grantor\n159\tpattern: a permanent exposes `grants_affinity_to(spell) -> bool` (truthy for the\n160\tgranted card types) + `affinity_reduction(game) -> int`; a card's own affinity\n161\t(`cost_reduction`) may delegate to `affinity_reduction` for a single source of\n162\ttruth. Affinity is NOT an engine `Keyword` flag — it is purely a cost-reduction\n163\tmechanic. Same getattr-safe capability pattern as casualty (sos_226) / miracle\n164\t(sos_201), wired into `get_cost_reduction` rather than `cast_spell`/`draw_card`.\n165\t\n166\t## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)\n167\tOverride `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine\n168\tclamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in\n169\t`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so no manual\n170\tclamping is needed. The hook may read `self.controller` (engine sets it before\n171\tquerying).\n172\t\n173\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01R1PDxcsG2L2uK3sxmw2D39","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"ef28b15d-fbf1-4f34-9dc7-3893c647c559","timestamp":"2026-06-02T01:59:14.110Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Write tests for sos_257"}
