{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R1PDxcsG2L2uK3sxmw2D39","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 34 tests collect cleanly and the suite is in the correct red phase.\n\n## Status summary\n\n**TESTS_WRITTEN**\n\n- **test_files:** 1 — `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`\n- **test_cases:** 34\n- **Red phase confirmed:** 30 fail, 4 pass. The 4 that \"pass\" are static-identity checks (`no mana cost`, `not a creature initially`, `colorless`, `no pump before animation`) that the empty `CardImpl` stub vacuously satisfies; they encode genuine final-card requirements and stay correct for a correct implementation. The 30 substantive behavioral tests fail because the card class is an unimplemented stub.\n- **rationale_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md`\n- **files_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-files.txt`\n- **untestable_count:** 1\n- **untestable_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json`\n\n### Coverage\nDrove the real engine (`activate_ability`, `ManaAbility.cost/mana_produced`, `TriggerManager.fire_event`) — no mocks of the system under test:\n- **Static identity:** name, Land type, no mana cost, not-a-creature initially, colorless, `can_cast` False, untapped.\n- **`{T}: Add {C}`** mana ability: produces 1 colorless, taps, fails when tapped, no colored mana.\n- **`{T}, Pay 1 life: any color`** mana ability: pays exactly 1 life, taps, adds the chosen color, exactly one mana, cost fails (and life unpaid) when tapped.\n- **`{5}` animation:** one `ActivatedAbility`, cost gate at 5 mana, becomes 2/4 Wizard, stays a Land, end-to-end via `activate_ability`, and the \"isn't a creature\" gate prevents double-animation.\n- **Animated cast trigger:** registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, pumps +1/+0 on the controller's instant/sorcery, ignores creature spells and opponents' spells.\n\n### One untestable requirement\nThe \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\" restriction on the any-color mana — the engine's `ManaPool` is a flat `dict[ManaType, int]` with no restricted-mana surface, so there is nothing observable to assert. The testable subset of that ability (tap + 1 life + correct single mana) is fully covered; details and an unblock path are in `untestable.json`.\n\nNotes: The casting pipeline does not itself fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, so the pump tests fire the event directly (mirroring how `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` fires `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`). The assumed implementer API is documented in `test-rationale.md`, and the any-color description match accepts either `\"life\"` or `\"any color\"` to leave the Implementer wording latitude."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ab1505d5c7dac5d01 (use SendMessage with to: 'ab1505d5c7dac5d01' to continue this agent)\n<usage>total_tokens: 146381\ntool_uses: 50\nduration_ms: 273177</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"ef5ce246-273c-4b30-acaa-2a15e88ba9bc","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:03:43.788Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Write pytest tests (TDD red phase) for card **sos_257**.\n\n## Inputs\n- Spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_spec.json` (read it — do not assume).\n- Stub to be implemented later: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py`.\n- Test conventions: study `/workspace/engine_tests/` and an example like `/workspace/engine_tests/test_casting.py`. Match the project's existing test style.\n- FDN reference cards (completed examples): `/workspace/cards/fdn/fdn_*/` — `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md` lists which ship with `tests.py`. Use them as patterns.\n- Conventions you MUST align to: read `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md` (explicit `self.colors`; mana_spent; BeginningOfMainPhase events + delayed/recurring deferred effects; StackObject.is_spell; coin flips/skip-turns; planeswalker conventions; preparation cards; alternative-cost casting + draw-time/miracle pipeline; casualty/cast-trigger hook + use `engine.game.sacrifice`; granted cost reduction / affinity grant). Reuse these engine surfaces rather than inventing new ones where applicable.\n- Prior cards' files: `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`. Workspace rules: `/workspace/AGENTS.md`, `/workspace/PROJECT_MAP.md`.\n\n## Rules\n- Write tests to `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`. Tests must FAIL before implementation (red phase) — they should import the card and assert real behavior.\n- Drive the REAL engine (real `GameState`/players, real triggers/casting), not mocks of the system under test.\n- CRITICAL: Do NOT modify any file under `/workspace/engine_tests/`.\n- Cover all spec clauses: static characteristics (name, cost, P/T or loyalty, type line, supertypes, subtypes, colors, keywords) AND every ability/triggered/activated/replacement effect, plus edge cases.\n\n## If something is genuinely untestable\nIf a requirement cannot be tested because the engine lacks a surface (and you cannot reasonably drive it), record it in `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json` as a JSON array of objects `{\"requirement\": \"...\", \"reason\": \"...\", \"what_would_unblock\": \"...\"}`. Cover the testable subset robustly regardless.\n\n## Output (write to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/)\n- `test-rationale.md` — what each test covers and why; note any assumed API contract (method/attribute names) so the Implementer can align.\n- `test-files.txt` — absolute path(s) of the test file(s) you wrote (one per line): `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`.\n- `untestable.json` — ONLY if there are uncovered requirements.\n\n## Return a short status summary\nReport: number of tests written, whether they currently fail (red), and `untestable_count: <N>`.","agentId":"ab1505d5c7dac5d01","agentType":"Tester","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 34 tests collect cleanly and the suite is in the correct red phase.\n\n## Status summary\n\n**TESTS_WRITTEN**\n\n- **test_files:** 1 — `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`\n- **test_cases:** 34\n- **Red phase confirmed:** 30 fail, 4 pass. The 4 that \"pass\" are static-identity checks (`no mana cost`, `not a creature initially`, `colorless`, `no pump before animation`) that the empty `CardImpl` stub vacuously satisfies; they encode genuine final-card requirements and stay correct for a correct implementation. The 30 substantive behavioral tests fail because the card class is an unimplemented stub.\n- **rationale_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md`\n- **files_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-files.txt`\n- **untestable_count:** 1\n- **untestable_path:** `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/untestable.json`\n\n### Coverage\nDrove the real engine (`activate_ability`, `ManaAbility.cost/mana_produced`, `TriggerManager.fire_event`) — no mocks of the system under test:\n- **Static identity:** name, Land type, no mana cost, not-a-creature initially, colorless, `can_cast` False, untapped.\n- **`{T}: Add {C}`** mana ability: produces 1 colorless, taps, fails when tapped, no colored mana.\n- **`{T}, Pay 1 life: any color`** mana ability: pays exactly 1 life, taps, adds the chosen color, exactly one mana, cost fails (and life unpaid) when tapped.\n- **`{5}` animation:** one `ActivatedAbility`, cost gate at 5 mana, becomes 2/4 Wizard, stays a Land, end-to-end via `activate_ability`, and the \"isn't a creature\" gate prevents double-animation.\n- **Animated cast trigger:** registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, pumps +1/+0 on the controller's instant/sorcery, ignores creature spells and opponents' spells.\n\n### One untestable requirement\nThe \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\" restriction on the any-color mana — the engine's `ManaPool` is a flat `dict[ManaType, int]` with no restricted-mana surface, so there is nothing observable to assert. The testable subset of that ability (tap + 1 life + correct single mana) is fully covered; details and an unblock path are in `untestable.json`.\n\nNotes: The casting pipeline does not itself fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, so the pump tests fire the event directly (mirroring how `cards/sos/sos_57/tests.py` fires `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent`). The assumed implementer API is documented in `test-rationale.md`, and the any-color description match accepts either `\"life\"` or `\"any color\"` to leave the Implementer wording latitude."}],"totalDurationMs":273177,"totalTokens":146381,"totalToolUseCount":50,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":374,"cache_read_input_tokens":144970,"output_tokens":1035,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":374},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1035,"cache_read_input_tokens":144970,"cache_creation_input_tokens":374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":374,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":30,"searchCount":11,"bashCount":5,"editFileCount":4,"linesAdded":597,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
