{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UzqgvMPM8wwZdMNR2gjv52","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Decision: option (a) — build a restricted-mana surface, with an explicit clean fallback to option (b) (UNVERIFIED marker) if it can't be done additively without regression risk. Restricted mana is a real recurring MTG mechanic and the unblock path is clearly buildable. Recording the decision."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3250,"cache_read_input_tokens":85522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3250},"output_tokens":50,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"438913d0-cdf4-497b-923d-7405a7f90b71","request_id":"req_011CbdcT29t1kip9VXGoEm89"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UzqgvMPM8wwZdMNR2gjv52","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UXKEcS9x4JyZsCfsLK3dVV","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","old_string":"- Reuses sos_201 alternative-cost/draw-hook PATTERN and FDN `copy_spell` surface;\n  reusable for other \"as you cast\"/cast-trigger mechanics. Implementer keeps it\n  additive (default cast path byte-for-byte unchanged when no casualty grantor).","new_string":"- Reuses sos_201 alternative-cost/draw-hook PATTERN and FDN `copy_spell` surface;\n  reusable for other \"as you cast\"/cast-trigger mechanics. Implementer keeps it\n  additive (default cast path byte-for-byte unchanged when no casualty grantor).\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_257 (Great Hall — restricted \"instant/sorcery only\" mana)\nOne untestable item: \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\"\non the pay-1-life any-color mana. The engine `ManaPool` is a flat\n`dict[ManaType,int]` with no restricted-mana surface, so there is nothing\nobservable to assert the restriction. The testable subset (taps, pays exactly 1\nlife, adds exactly one mana of the chosen color) is fully covered.\n- **Decision: option (a) — build an ADDITIVE restricted-mana surface, with a\n  clean fallback to (b) if it can't be done without regression risk.** Restricted\n  mana is a real recurring MTG mechanic and the unblock path is buildable:\n  - `ManaPool` gains an additive way to add RESTRICTED mana tagged with a\n    predicate/string (e.g. restriction `\"instant_sorcery\"`), tracked separately\n    so unrestricted accounting is BYTE-FOR-BYTE unchanged when no restricted mana\n    is added.\n  - `engine.casting` payment consults restrictions: restricted mana may pay only\n    for spells matching its predicate (instants/sorceries); for a non-matching\n    spell it is treated as unavailable (CastingError if it's the only mana).\n  - The card's any-color ability adds mana tagged with the instant/sorcery\n    restriction. Spend the single Tester re-invocation on a deterministic test:\n    restricted mana pays an instant/sorcery (success) but cannot pay a creature\n    spell (CastingError / life-unchanged-but-mana-unusable).\n- **Fallback (b):** if a clean additive restricted-mana surface proves infeasible\n  without engine-test regressions, the Implementer adds the mana unrestricted and\n  marks the gap with `# UNVERIFIED: instant/sorcery-only mana restriction — engine\n  ManaPool has no restricted-mana surface` in `card_impl.py`; log here. No Tester\n  re-invocation in that case.\n- Note: the casting pipeline does NOT itself fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, so\n  the animated land's \"+1/+0 whenever you cast an instant/sorcery\" pump trigger\n  is tested by firing the event directly (sos_57 pattern). The Implementer should\n  register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger gated on controller + i/s."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3250,"cache_read_input_tokens":85522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3250},"output_tokens":50,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"0cc92e2c-4e84-4962-864f-2c771d70b67e","request_id":"req_011CbdcT29t1kip9VXGoEm89"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UXKEcS9x4JyZsCfsLK3dVV","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"435fdbcd-a7dd-4592-bc50-4a531328009a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:04:29.787Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/workspace/RUN_DECISIONS.md","oldString":"- Reuses sos_201 alternative-cost/draw-hook PATTERN and FDN `copy_spell` surface;\n  reusable for other \"as you cast\"/cast-trigger mechanics. Implementer keeps it\n  additive (default cast path byte-for-byte unchanged when no casualty grantor).","newString":"- Reuses sos_201 alternative-cost/draw-hook PATTERN and FDN `copy_spell` surface;\n  reusable for other \"as you cast\"/cast-trigger mechanics. Implementer keeps it\n  additive (default cast path byte-for-byte unchanged when no casualty grantor).\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_257 (Great Hall — restricted \"instant/sorcery only\" mana)\nOne untestable item: \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\"\non the pay-1-life any-color mana. The engine `ManaPool` is a flat\n`dict[ManaType,int]` with no restricted-mana surface, so there is nothing\nobservable to assert the restriction. The testable subset (taps, pays exactly 1\nlife, adds exactly one mana of the chosen color) is fully covered.\n- **Decision: option (a) — build an ADDITIVE restricted-mana surface, with a\n  clean fallback to (b) if it can't be done without regression risk.** Restricted\n  mana is a real recurring MTG mechanic and the unblock path is buildable:\n  - `ManaPool` gains an additive way to add RESTRICTED mana tagged with a\n    predicate/string (e.g. restriction `\"instant_sorcery\"`), tracked separately\n    so unrestricted accounting is BYTE-FOR-BYTE unchanged when no restricted mana\n    is added.\n  - `engine.casting` payment consults restrictions: restricted mana may pay only\n    for spells matching its predicate (instants/sorceries); for a non-matching\n    spell it is treated as unavailable (CastingError if it's the only mana).\n  - The card's any-color ability adds mana tagged with the instant/sorcery\n    restriction. Spend the single Tester re-invocation on a deterministic test:\n    restricted mana pays an instant/sorcery (success) but cannot pay a creature\n    spell (CastingError / life-unchanged-but-mana-unusable).\n- **Fallback (b):** if a clean additive restricted-mana surface proves infeasible\n  without engine-test regressions, the Implementer adds the mana unrestricted and\n  marks the gap with `# UNVERIFIED: instant/sorcery-only mana restriction — engine\n  ManaPool has no restricted-mana surface` in `card_impl.py`; log here. No Tester\n  re-invocation in that case.\n- Note: the casting pipeline does NOT itself fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, so\n  the animated land's \"+1/+0 whenever you cast an instant/sorcery\" pump trigger\n  is tested by firing the event directly (sos_57 pattern). The Implementer should\n  register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger gated on controller + i/s.","originalFile":"# Run Decisions\n\nDecisions made during this run only. Before the run ends, migrate anything worth preserving into `KEY_DECISIONS.md`.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_13 (preparation card, CR 722)\nThe engine has no native preparation-card support. The Tester reported 2\nuntestable requirements:\n1. \"Cast a copy of the prepare spell from exile; doing so unprepares it.\"\n2. The inset Swords to Plowshares effect (only skip-guarded; no mandated factory API).\n- **Decision (both): option (a) — hand back to Implementer with a concrete API gap.**\n  Directing the Implementer to expose a defined preparation surface:\n  - `card.make_prepare_spell(game)` factory returning a castable Swords to\n    Plowshares spell object (matches the Tester's probe so the 4 skip-guarded\n    tests run as hard tests).\n  - `card.prepared` boolean designation (becomes True per the ETB clause).\n  - A method to cast the prepare spell while prepared that requires\n    `prepared is True`, resolves the Swords-to-Plowshares effect (exile target\n    creature; its controller gains life equal to its power), and sets\n    `prepared = False` afterward (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n  After the Implementer adds this surface, re-invoke the Tester ONCE to extend\n  coverage (harden the skip-guarded tests + add an unprepare-on-cast test).\n- Reasoning: both gaps are buildable engine helpers, and a functional\n  preparation implementation maximizes alignment with the grader's authoritative\n  tests vs. accepting partial coverage with UNVERIFIED markers.\n\n## Counting-model correction: sos_13 \"becomes prepared\"\n- The first Implementer pass flagged a counting-model issue. Card text: \"...\n  THEN if an opponent controls more creatures than you, this creature becomes\n  prepared.\" `_fire_etb` puts Emeritus on the controller's battlefield before\n  the check, so under **standard MTG rules the entering Emeritus counts toward\n  \"you\"**, and tokens count for whoever controls them.\n- The Tester's `test_prepared_when_opponent_has_more_creatures` sets opp=2 and\n  targets the token to the CONTROLLER, then asserts prepared. Under standard\n  counting that board is controller=2 (Emeritus+token) vs opp=2 → NOT prepared,\n  so the assertion is wrong. The test comment (\"controller controls only\n  Emeritus (1)\") shows the Tester forgot the controller's token bumps the count.\n  The Tester's *intent* (opp strictly more than you → prepared) matches standard\n  rules; only the board state is buggy.\n- The Implementer's first pass adopted a non-standard \"entering creature doesn't\n  count\" model to satisfy the buggy test. **Decision: reject that model. Use\n  standard MTG counting (entering Emeritus counts; tokens count for their\n  controller).** The grader almost certainly uses standard counting.\n- **Action:** the single Tester re-invocation will also fix the buggy board\n  state of that one test (so the prepared case is genuinely opp-more under\n  standard counting, e.g. target the token to the opponent or give opp 3). The\n  other three becomes-prepared tests already pass under standard counting.\n  Then the Implementer's final pass uses standard counting.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_57 (Mana Sculpt — deferred {C} at next main phase)\nTwo untestable items reported:\n1. Deferred {C} delivery \"at the beginning of your next main phase\" — no engine\n   delayed-trigger nor beginning-of-main-phase event exists.\n2. \"amount of mana spent to cast that spell\" — engine tracks only colors spent\n   (`colors_spent`), not total mana spent.\n- **Decision: option (a) for both — build additive engine surface.**\n  - Item 2: add total-mana-spent tracking during `cast_spell` payment (e.g.\n    `card.mana_spent`, analogous to the existing `colors_spent`). The existing\n    tests already read the recorded pending amount, so they go red→green once\n    the field + card logic exist; no re-invocation needed for item 2.\n  - Item 1: add a `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent` (fired by turn.py on\n    entering precombat main) + a delayed/one-shot deferred-effect mechanism so\n    the card can schedule \"add {C} at controller's next main phase\". Spend the\n    single Tester re-invocation on a DETERMINISTIC delivery test that fires the\n    new event directly via trigger_manager (mirroring the ETB-direct-fire\n    pattern) and asserts the {C} appears once.\n- Reasoning: delayed triggers + beginning-of-main-phase are reusable engine\n  features likely exercised by the grader and other SOS cards; building them\n  beats accepting partial coverage. Implementer must keep changes additive and\n  pass full engine regression.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_97 (Ral Zarek — −7 ultimate)\nTwo untestable items, both in the −7 ultimate:\n1. Coin-flip X (\"flip five coins, X = heads\") — no coin-flip primitive; RNG\n   entry point unknown.\n2. Skip-turn enforcement (\"target opponent skips their next X turns\") — no\n   native skip-turn support (only an `extra_turns` FIFO; skip-turn flagged\n   unhandled in GameState docstring).\n- **Decision: option (a) for both — build additive, deterministic engine support.**\n  - Coin flip: add a coin-flip helper (e.g. `flip_coins(game, n) -> heads`) with\n    an INJECTABLE/deterministic RNG so tests can control results; record the\n    heads count on the card (e.g. `pw._last_heads`) for direct assertion.\n  - Skip-turn: add a per-player skipped-turns counter honored by the turn\n    rotation so the opponent's next X turns are actually skipped, observable by\n    advancing turns.\n  - Spend the single Tester re-invocation to assert X (deterministic flips) and\n    skip-turn enforcement.\n- Planeswalker conventions (FDN Kaito/Vivien/Liliana, assumed by the Tester):\n  `Planeswalker` base, `get_loyalty_abilities()` → 4 `LoyaltyAbility`, targeted\n  abilities read `pw._resolve_target` (single) / `pw._resolve_targets` (list),\n  surveil keep/bin via controller `choose_yes_no`. Implementer must match these\n  names (or DISPUTE if genuinely wrong).\n- Reasoning: coin flips + skip-turns are reusable primitives (Ral is a coin-flip\n  character; other SOS cards may skip turns) and likely grader-tested.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_120 (Improvisation Capstone — multi-select free-cast)\nOne untestable item: the exact \"cast any number of spells from among them\" multi-\nselect selection API. The Tester used the sos_1 `choose_yes_no`-per-eligible-spell\nconvention for the positive cast tests; API-agnostic invariants (decline leaves\ncards in exile; lands never cast; free cast pays no mana) are robustly covered.\n- **Decision: option (a) — direct the Implementer to use the sos_1\n  `choose_yes_no`-per-eligible-spell convention** for the multi-select free cast,\n  so the existing positive cast tests pass as-is. No Tester re-invocation needed\n  (the tests already assume this convention).\n- Also note: Paradigm recurs (\"at the beginning of EACH of your first main\n  phases\"). sos_57's `schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect` is ONE-SHOT, so the\n  Paradigm callback must RE-SCHEDULE itself each time it fires (recurring), which\n  the existing engine surface supports without new engine code. The Tester's\n  `test_paradigm_copy_offer_recurs_each_precombat_main_phase` enforces this.\n- Reuses sos_1 `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` for Paradigm self-exile and sos_57\n  delayed-main-phase trigger surface — no new engine surface expected.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_201 (Lorehold — miracle draw-time casting)\nOne untestable item: miracle's draw-time cast (\"cast for its miracle cost when\nyou draw it if it's the first card you drew this turn\"). No engine miracle /\nalternative-cost / draw-reveal pipeline exists. The Tester covered the observable\ngranting (`MIRACLE_COST` constant + `grant_miracle(game)` stamping `miracle_cost`\non controller's hand instants/sorceries), flying/haste combat, and the\nopponent-upkeep rummage.\n- **Decision: option (a) — build a focused, additive, deterministic miracle\n  pipeline.**\n  - `card.miracle_cost: ManaCost | None` (default None).\n  - Alternative-cost cast surface (e.g. `cast_spell(..., alternative_cost=...)`\n    or a `cast_miracle`/`cast_for_alternative_cost` helper) paying the alt cost\n    instead of mana_cost.\n  - Draw hook in `draw_card`: ONLY acts when (a) it is the drawing player's FIRST\n    card this turn (use existing `player.cards_drawn_this_turn`) AND (b) a\n    permanent the player controls grants miracle to that card (a\n    `grants_miracle_to(card) -> ManaCost|None` capability on Lorehold). When\n    both hold, stamp `miracle_cost` and offer the controller `choose_yes_no` to\n    cast it for the miracle cost. In all other cases the hook is a COMPLETE\n    no-op (so existing engine tests, where nothing grants miracle, are\n    unaffected — no spurious prompts/regressions).\n  - Modeling simplification (documented): the miracle \"window\" is an immediate\n    at-draw offer rather than the full reveal→triggered-ability→cast-anytime;\n    acceptable and deterministically testable for this engine.\n  - Spend the single Tester re-invocation on a deterministic draw-time test\n    (first-card draw with Lorehold out → offered → yes casts for {2}, pool −2,\n    card leaves hand; decline keeps it; non-first-card draw doesn't offer).\n- Reasoning: miracle is a real, reusable mechanic; the gated draw hook is\n  regression-safe. Implementer must pass full engine regression. If it can't be\n  done cleanly/additively, fall back to partial coverage with an UNVERIFIED\n  marker.\n\n## Untestable resolution: sos_226 (Silverquill — casualty auto-fire at cast)\nOne untestable item: the AUTOMATIC firing of the casualty offer during\n`engine.casting.cast_spell`. No spell-cast event/hook exists, so the Tester\ncovered the full observable casualty behavior via an explicit\n`offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)` method (sacrifice power>=1 creature + push one\ncopy + optional new targets; gated by \"spells you cast\" + instant/sorcery), but\nnot the at-cast auto-wiring.\n- **Decision: option (a) — build a focused, additive, fully-gated cast hook**,\n  directly analogous to the sos_201 draw-time miracle hook (`_offer_miracle` in\n  `engine/game.py::draw_card`). After `cast_spell` pushes the spell StackObject,\n  call a helper that is a COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER\n  controls returns a non-None `grants_casualty_to(spell)`; only then invoke that\n  permanent's `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`. When nothing grants casualty the\n  hook does nothing (no prompt, no state change) so full engine regression stays\n  green. Spend the single Tester re-invocation on a deterministic auto-fire test:\n  real `cast_spell` of an instant with Silverquill out + a power>=1 creature + yes\n  → sacrifice happens and exactly one copy appears, with NO manual `offer_casualty`\n  call; and a no-grantor cast is a no-op.\n- Reuses sos_201 alternative-cost/draw-hook PATTERN and FDN `copy_spell` surface;\n  reusable for other \"as you cast\"/cast-trigger mechanics. Implementer keeps it\n  additive (default cast path byte-for-byte unchanged when no casualty grantor).\n\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":163,"oldLines":3,"newStart":163,"newLines":33,"lines":["   reusable for other \"as you cast\"/cast-trigger mechanics. Implementer keeps it","   additive (default cast path byte-for-byte unchanged when no casualty grantor)."," ","+## Untestable resolution: sos_257 (Great Hall — restricted \"instant/sorcery only\" mana)","+One untestable item: \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\"","+on the pay-1-life any-color mana. The engine `ManaPool` is a flat","+`dict[ManaType,int]` with no restricted-mana surface, so there is nothing","+observable to assert the restriction. The testable subset (taps, pays exactly 1","+life, adds exactly one mana of the chosen color) is fully covered.","+- **Decision: option (a) — build an ADDITIVE restricted-mana surface, with a","+  clean fallback to (b) if it can't be done without regression risk.** Restricted","+  mana is a real recurring MTG mechanic and the unblock path is buildable:","+  - `ManaPool` gains an additive way to add RESTRICTED mana tagged with a","+    predicate/string (e.g. restriction `\"instant_sorcery\"`), tracked separately","+    so unrestricted accounting is BYTE-FOR-BYTE unchanged when no restricted mana","+    is added.","+  - `engine.casting` payment consults restrictions: restricted mana may pay only","+    for spells matching its predicate (instants/sorceries); for a non-matching","+    spell it is treated as unavailable (CastingError if it's the only mana).","+  - The card's any-color ability adds mana tagged with the instant/sorcery","+    restriction. Spend the single Tester re-invocation on a deterministic test:","+    restricted mana pays an instant/sorcery (success) but cannot pay a creature","+    spell (CastingError / life-unchanged-but-mana-unusable).","+- **Fallback (b):** if a clean additive restricted-mana surface proves infeasible","+  without engine-test regressions, the Implementer adds the mana unrestricted and","+  marks the gap with `# UNVERIFIED: instant/sorcery-only mana restriction — engine","+  ManaPool has no restricted-mana surface` in `card_impl.py`; log here. No Tester","+  re-invocation in that case.","+- Note: the casting pipeline does NOT itself fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, so","+  the animated land's \"+1/+0 whenever you cast an instant/sorcery\" pump trigger","+  is tested by firing the event directly (sos_57 pattern). The Implementer should","+  register a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger gated on controller + i/s.","+"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01M2dEjPV3Uy3tatJxrUgcXc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AUFFNPcXx7RPnWSGxHyWnj","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/coordinator-directives.md","content":"# Coordinator directives — sos_257 (Great Hall of the Biblioplex)\n\nThe Tester reported ONE untestable requirement: the \"Spend this mana only to\ncast an instant or sorcery spell\" restriction on the pay-1-life any-color mana.\nPer the run decision, build an ADDITIVE restricted-mana surface (with a clean\nfallback to an UNVERIFIED marker if it can't be done without regression).\n\n## Card: Great Hall of the Biblioplex (Land)\n- Subclass `engine.card.Land`. `name == \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"`,\n  `mana_cost == ManaCost()`, `colors == []`, starts untapped, `can_cast(game)`\n  False, not a creature initially.\n- `get_mana_abilities()` returns EXACTLY two `ManaAbility`:\n  1. `{T}: Add {C}` — description contains `\"{C}\"`; `cost(game, source)` taps\n     (returns False if already tapped); `mana_produced(game)` adds exactly one\n     `{C}`.\n  2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an\n     instant or sorcery spell.` — description contains `\"life\"` (and/or\n     `\"any color\"`); `cost(game, source)` taps AND deducts 1 life from the\n     controller (atomic: if tapped, fail and DO NOT deduct life);\n     `mana_produced(game)` adds exactly one mana of the color read from the\n     controller's `choose(...)`, tagged with the instant/sorcery restriction\n     (see below).\n- `get_activated_abilities()` returns EXACTLY one `ActivatedAbility` — the `{5}`\n  animation: `cost(game, source)` pays `{5}` (fails on 4 mana); `effect(game)`,\n  GATED on \"isn't a creature\", turns the land into a 2/4 with subtype `\"Wizard\"`,\n  KEEPING `CardType.LAND` (add `CardType.CREATURE`), `power == 2`,\n  `toughness == 4`. Re-running `effect` while already a creature must NOT stack\n  additional P/T.\n- `register_triggers(game)` registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger that\n  pumps the (animated) land +1/+0 until end of turn ONLY when the CONTROLLER\n  casts an instant or sorcery (ignore creature spells and opponents' spells). Use\n  the standard P/T-modification path so `power`/`toughness` reflect +1/+0. Tests\n  fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` directly (sos_57 pattern), since the casting\n  pipeline does not itself fire it.\n\n## Additive restricted-mana surface (build this; fallback below)\n- Extend `ManaPool` (engine) to optionally hold RESTRICTED mana tagged with a\n  predicate/string restriction (e.g. `\"instant_sorcery\"`). Track restricted mana\n  SEPARATELY from the existing `dict[ManaType,int]` so that when no restricted\n  mana is ever added, the pool's behavior, totals, and existing API are\n  BYTE-FOR-BYTE unchanged (all engine_tests stay green).\n- Add an additive way to add restricted mana (e.g. `add(..., restriction=None)`\n  or `add_restricted(mana_type, amount, restriction)`). The any-color ability\n  uses it with the instant/sorcery restriction.\n- `engine.casting` payment consults restrictions: restricted mana may be spent\n  ONLY on a spell whose type matches the predicate (instant/sorcery). For a\n  non-matching spell (e.g. a creature), restricted mana is treated as unavailable\n  — if it is the only mana that could pay, `cast_spell` raises `CastingError`.\n  Matching spells may freely use restricted mana.\n- Keep the restriction-free path untouched: only the presence of restricted mana\n  changes anything. Restricted mana empties between steps like all mana.\n\n## Fallback (only if a clean additive restricted-mana surface is infeasible\nwithout engine-test regressions)\nAdd the any-color mana UNRESTRICTED, and mark the gap in `card_impl.py` with:\n`# UNVERIFIED: instant/sorcery-only mana restriction — engine ManaPool has no restricted-mana surface`\nNote in `impl-rationale.md` that you took the fallback. (No Tester re-invocation\nin that case.)\n\n## Constraints\n- DO NOT modify any test file in `test-files.txt`. If a test is genuinely wrong,\n  return DISPUTE.\n- Additive engine changes only; default mana/payment paths unchanged when no\n  restricted mana is in play.\n- Run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`; all\n  sos_257 tests pass and engine_tests stay green.\n- If you build the restricted-mana surface, make it real/importable — a single\n  Tester re-invocation will add a deterministic restriction test next. State\n  clearly in your status `notes` whether you built it or took the fallback.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3238,"cache_read_input_tokens":88772,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3238},"output_tokens":54,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"a78bc4c0-baf5-4a6a-99ca-502afb7134f0","request_id":"req_011CbdcVzLKk9VRBDT6deXGS"}
