{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014vMwkWCiCCwerWCKrBMb7s","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coordinator directives — sos_257 (Great Hall of the Biblioplex)\n2\t\n3\tThe Tester reported ONE untestable requirement: the \"Spend this mana only to\n4\tcast an instant or sorcery spell\" restriction on the pay-1-life any-color mana.\n5\tPer the run decision, build an ADDITIVE restricted-mana surface (with a clean\n6\tfallback to an UNVERIFIED marker if it can't be done without regression).\n7\t\n8\t## Card: Great Hall of the Biblioplex (Land)\n9\t- Subclass `engine.card.Land`. `name == \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"`,\n10\t  `mana_cost == ManaCost()`, `colors == []`, starts untapped, `can_cast(game)`\n11\t  False, not a creature initially.\n12\t- `get_mana_abilities()` returns EXACTLY two `ManaAbility`:\n13\t  1. `{T}: Add {C}` — description contains `\"{C}\"`; `cost(game, source)` taps\n14\t     (returns False if already tapped); `mana_produced(game)` adds exactly one\n15\t     `{C}`.\n16\t  2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an\n17\t     instant or sorcery spell.` — description contains `\"life\"` (and/or\n18\t     `\"any color\"`); `cost(game, source)` taps AND deducts 1 life from the\n19\t     controller (atomic: if tapped, fail and DO NOT deduct life);\n20\t     `mana_produced(game)` adds exactly one mana of the color read from the\n21\t     controller's `choose(...)`, tagged with the instant/sorcery restriction\n22\t     (see below).\n23\t- `get_activated_abilities()` returns EXACTLY one `ActivatedAbility` — the `{5}`\n24\t  animation: `cost(game, source)` pays `{5}` (fails on 4 mana); `effect(game)`,\n25\t  GATED on \"isn't a creature\", turns the land into a 2/4 with subtype `\"Wizard\"`,\n26\t  KEEPING `CardType.LAND` (add `CardType.CREATURE`), `power == 2`,\n27\t  `toughness == 4`. Re-running `effect` while already a creature must NOT stack\n28\t  additional P/T.\n29\t- `register_triggers(game)` registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger that\n30\t  pumps the (animated) land +1/+0 until end of turn ONLY when the CONTROLLER\n31\t  casts an instant or sorcery (ignore creature spells and opponents' spells). Use\n32\t  the standard P/T-modification path so `power`/`toughness` reflect +1/+0. Tests\n33\t  fire `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` directly (sos_57 pattern), since the casting\n34\t  pipeline does not itself fire it.\n35\t\n36\t## Additive restricted-mana surface (build this; fallback below)\n37\t- Extend `ManaPool` (engine) to optionally hold RESTRICTED mana tagged with a\n38\t  predicate/string restriction (e.g. `\"instant_sorcery\"`). Track restricted mana\n39\t  SEPARATELY from the existing `dict[ManaType,int]` so that when no restricted\n40\t  mana is ever added, the pool's behavior, totals, and existing API are\n41\t  BYTE-FOR-BYTE unchanged (all engine_tests stay green).\n42\t- Add an additive way to add restricted mana (e.g. `add(..., restriction=None)`\n43\t  or `add_restricted(mana_type, amount, restriction)`). The any-color ability\n44\t  uses it with the instant/sorcery restriction.\n45\t- `engine.casting` payment consults restrictions: restricted mana may be spent\n46\t  ONLY on a spell whose type matches the predicate (instant/sorcery). For a\n47\t  non-matching spell (e.g. a creature), restricted mana is treated as unavailable\n48\t  — if it is the only mana that could pay, `cast_spell` raises `CastingError`.\n49\t  Matching spells may freely use restricted mana.\n50\t- Keep the restriction-free path untouched: only the presence of restricted mana\n51\t  changes anything. Restricted mana empties between steps like all mana.\n52\t\n53\t## Fallback (only if a clean additive restricted-mana surface is infeasible\n54\twithout engine-test regressions)\n55\tAdd the any-color mana UNRESTRICTED, and mark the gap in `card_impl.py` with:\n56\t`# UNVERIFIED: instant/sorcery-only mana restriction — engine ManaPool has no restricted-mana surface`\n57\tNote in `impl-rationale.md` that you took the fallback. (No Tester re-invocation\n58\tin that case.)\n59\t\n60\t## Constraints\n61\t- DO NOT modify any test file in `test-files.txt`. If a test is genuinely wrong,\n62\t  return DISPUTE.\n63\t- Additive engine changes only; default mana/payment paths unchanged when no\n64\t  restricted mana is in play.\n65\t- Run `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`; all\n66\t  sos_257 tests pass and engine_tests stay green.\n67\t- If you build the restricted-mana surface, make it real/importable — a single\n68\t  Tester re-invocation will add a deterministic restriction test next. State\n69\t  clearly in your status `notes` whether you built it or took the fallback.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01YGTm3RKSK2yGeCH6x1tUM8","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"c0a9cad9-66ea-4a57-b0ef-314e3a66feb2","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:05:15.902Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Implement sos_257 Great Hall + restricted mana"}
