or cards' files (do not undo their changes).\n- CRITICAL: Do NOT modify any file under `/workspace/engine_tests/`. Those are staged for local verification only.\n\n## Card spec & tests\n- Spec: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_spec.json`\n- Stub to fill in: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py`\n- Test file you must make pass (do NOT edit): listed in `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-files.txt` (it is `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`).\n\n## Coordinator directives (authoritative design)\nRead `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/coordinator-directives.md` IN FULL. It specifies:\n- The full card surface: two `ManaAbility` ({T}:{C} and {T},Pay 1 life: any color restricted to instant/sorcery), one `{5}` `ActivatedAbility` animation (2/4 Wizard, still a Land, gated on \"isn't a creature\"), and a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` +1/+0 pump trigger gated on controller + instant/sorcery.\n- The additive restricted-mana engine surface to build (ManaPool tracking per-mana spend restrictions tagged e.g. \"instant_sorcery\"; `engine.casting` payment consulting it; BYTE-FOR-BYTE unchanged when no restricted mana is present).\n- A CLEAN FALLBACK: if a clean additive restricted-mana surface proves infeasible without engine-test regressions, add the mana UNRESTRICTED and mark the gap with `# UNVERIFIED: instant/sorcery-only mana restriction — engine ManaPool has no restricted-mana surface` in card_impl.py, and note it in the rationale. State in your status notes which path you took.\n\n## Engine API discovery\nRead engine source directly (rich docstrings): `engine/card.py` (Land, ManaAbility, ActivatedAbility), `engine/abilities.py` (`activate_ability`), `engine/mana.py` or wherever `ManaPool` lives, `engine/casting.py` (payment), `engine/events.py` (`SpellCastTriggeredEvent`), `engine/triggers.py`. Use FDN land/animation cards in `/workspace/cards/fdn/` as examples if present.\n\n## Output (write to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/)\n- `impl.diff` — unified diff of all changes (card_impl.py + engine files).\n- `impl-rationale.md` — design rationale; CLEARLY state whether you built the restricted-mana surface or took the fallback, plus any engine changes and conventions worth reusing.\n- `impl-files.txt` — list of files changed.\n- Upsert this card's entry into `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json` (match by `card: \"sos_257\"`, replace in place if it exists). Entry shape:\n  `{ \"card\": \"sos_257\", \"tests\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\"}], \"implementation\": [{\"path\": \"...\", \"summary\": \"...\"}] }`\n\n## Verify\nRun `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`. ALL sos_257 tests must pass and engine_tests must stay green.\n\n## Return status summary (exactly one of)\n```\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: <N>\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: <one-line — STATE built-restricted-mana vs fallback>\n```\nor\n```\nDISPUTE\ntests_failing: <N>\ndisputed_tests: <list>\ndispute_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-dispute.md\nnotes: <one-line>\n```","agentId":"ae701aa76180e583a","agentType":"Implementer","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All checks pass: 1179 tests (34 sos_257 + 1145 engine_tests) green. Output files written.\n\nI built the additive restricted-mana surface (not the fallback). Implementation files: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py`, `/workspace/engine/mana.py`, `/workspace/engine/casting.py`. The `instant_sorcery`-tagged mana is genuinely enforced — a creature spell cannot spend it, an instant/sorcery can — and the default path is byte-for-byte unchanged when no restricted mana is present (verified across the full 1466-test suite).\n\n```\nIMPL_DONE\nfiles_changed: 3\ntests_passing: all\ndiff_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl.diff\nrationale_path: /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-rationale.md\nnotes: built-restricted-mana — additive ManaPool.add_restricted + restriction_allows t