Pool.add_restricted(...)` — and casts an INSTANT (or sorcery) through the REAL `engine.casting.cast_spell` paying with that restricted mana: the cast SUCCEEDS and the mana is consumed.\n2. With the SAME restricted mana as the only available mana, attempts to cast a CREATURE spell through `cast_spell`: it raises `CastingError` (the restricted mana cannot pay for a non-instant/sorcery), and the pool/board state is unchanged.\nOptionally: a control showing ordinary (unrestricted) mana CAN pay a creature spell, to anchor that the restriction—not some other gap—causes the failure.\n\nUse the real engine and the file's existing conventions (look at `/workspace/engine_tests/test_casting.py` and how the existing sos_257 tests build pools/spells). Read `engine/mana.py` and `engine/casting.py` to use the exact API. Tests must PASS against the implemented surface (post-implementation hardening, not red-phase). Keep within ~30-per-card style; a small focused class (2-3 tests) is right.\n\n## Verify\nRun `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`. ALL tests (old + new) must pass and engine_tests must stay green.\n\n## Output (write to /tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/)\n- Append/update `test-rationale.md` with a section describing the new restricted-mana tests (note the untestable item is now covered).\n- Ensure `test-files.txt` still lists `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`.\n- Update `untestable.json` to `[]` if the item is now covered; otherwise explain what remains.\n\n## Return a short status summary\nReport: number of tests added, whether all pass, and `untestable_count: <N>`.","uuid":"019bfe39-6dd5-4976-a798-80eca46c9bec","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145"}
