{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B9pbhFmnYaH2DN2W1SZtEX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Implementation rationale — sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n2\t\n3\t## Path taken: BUILT the additive restricted-mana surface (not the fallback)\n4\t\n5\tI built a real, importable restricted-mana surface on `engine.mana.ManaPool` and\n6\twired `engine.casting` to consult it. The any-color ability tags its mana with\n7\tthe `instant_sorcery` restriction, and a creature spell genuinely cannot spend\n8\tit (raises `CastingError` if it is the only mana that could pay).\n9\t\n10\t## Card design (`cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py`)\n11\t\n12\t`GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(Land)`:\n13\t- `mana_cost == ManaCost()`, explicit `self.colors == []`\n14\t  (per the KEY_DECISIONS explicit-colors convention), starts untapped,\n15\t  `can_cast` inherited `False` from `Land`.\n16\t- Because it is a `Land` (not a `Creature`), it tracks its own P/T. `power` and\n17\t  `toughness` are read-only properties: `power = _base_power + _power_bonus`,\n18\t  `toughness = _base_toughness`. Before animation `_base_power/_base_toughness`\n19\t  are 0 (tests never read P/T pre-animation).\n20\t- `get_mana_abilities()` returns exactly two `ManaAbility`:\n21\t  1. `{T}: Add {C}` — taps (returns `False` if already tapped), adds one\n22\t     `ManaType.COLORLESS`. Description contains `\"{C}\"`.\n23\t  2. `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color …` — atomic cost: if the land\n24\t     is already tapped it returns `False` WITHOUT deducting life; otherwise taps\n25\t     and deducts 1 life. `mana_produced` reads the color via\n26\t     `controller.choose(...)` and adds it via\n27\t     `add_restricted(chosen, 1, restriction=RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY)`.\n28\t     Description contains both `\"life\"` and `\"any color\"`.\n29\t- `get_activated_abilities()` returns exactly one `ActivatedAbility` (the `{5}`\n30\t  animation). `cost` pays `ManaCost(generic=5)` via the controller's pool\n31\t  (`can_pay` then `pay`), so 4 mana fails and 5 mana empties the pool. `effect`\n32\t  is gated on \"isn't a creature\": it returns early if already animated or\n33\t  already a creature, so a second resolution does not stack P/T. On first\n34\t  resolution it adds `CardType.CREATURE` (keeping `CardType.LAND`), adds subtype\n35\t  `\"Wizard\"`, sets base 2/4, and calls `register_triggers` to wire the pump.\n36\t- `register_triggers(game)` is a no-op until animated (the land has no triggered\n37\t  abilities before it becomes a creature), and idempotent via a guard flag so\n38\t  the test's direct call after `effect()` does not double-register. It registers\n39\t  a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger whose condition gates on (a) the spell's\n40\t  caster being the land's controller (\"Whenever YOU cast\") and (b) the spell\n41\t  being an instant or sorcery. The effect adds +1 to `_power_bonus` so\n42\t  `power` reflects +1/+0 immediately. The casting pipeline does not itself fire\n43\t  `SpellCastTriggeredEvent`, so this is exercised by firing the event directly\n44\t  (sos_57 pattern), matching the tests.\n45\t\n46\t## Engine: additive restricted-mana surface (`engine/mana.py`)\n47\t\n48\t- New module-level `RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY = \"instant_sorcery\"` tag and\n49\t  `restriction_allows(restriction, spell) -> bool`. `None` restriction = always\n50\t  allowed; a `None` spell context (e.g. plain `can_pay`, ability payment) is\n51\t  treated conservatively as NOT allowed for restricted mana (fail-closed so an\n52\t  unverifiable restriction never leaks onto an illegal spell); the\n53\t  `instant_sorcery` tag allows only spells whose `card_types` include INSTANT or\n54\t  SORCERY; unknown tags deny by default.\n55\t- `ManaPool` gains a parallel ledger `self._restricted: dict[ManaType, list[str]]`\n56\t  (empty unless `add_restricted` is ever called). Restricted mana is ALSO stored\n57\t  in the existing `_pool`, so `get`/`total` reflect it; `empty()` clears both.\n58\t- New `add_restricted(mana_type, amount, restriction=None)` mirrors `add` but\n59\t  records restriction tags (with `restriction=None` it is identical to `add`).\n60\t- `can_pay(cost, spell=None)` and `pay(cost, choices=None, spell=None)` gained an\n61\t  optional `spell` parameter. When the pool holds restricted mana, payment runs\n62\t  against a `_spendable_pool(spell)` (the pool minus restricted mana the spell\n63\t  may not use). On commit in the restricted path, the amount spent per type is\n64\t  deducted from the real `_pool` and the restriction ledger is reconciled\n65\t  (spending unrestricted mana before restricted/allowed mana of the same type).\n66\t- **Byte-for-byte guarantee:** when no restricted mana is ever added,\n67\t  `_has_restricted()` is `False`, `can_pay`/`pay` use `self._pool` exactly as\n68\t  before, and the commit takes the original fast path. All 1145 engine_tests\n69\t  stay green, and the full card+engine suite (1466 tests) passes.\n70\t\n71\t## Engine: payment wiring (`engine/casting.py`)\n72\t\n73\t`cast_spell` now passes `spell=card` to `player.mana_pool.can_pay(...)` and\n74\t`player.mana_pool.pay(...)`. With no restricted mana in the pool this is a no-op\n75\t(the `spell` argument is only consulted when `_has_restricted()` is true), so the\n76\tdefault cast path is unchanged.\n77\t\n78\t## Conventions worth reusing\n79\t\n80\t- \"Spend this mana only to …\" riders (CR 106.6): produce mana with\n81\t  `ManaPool.add_restricted(mana_type, amount, restriction=<tag>)` and add a tag\n82\t  matcher in `engine.mana.restriction_allows`. The casting pipeline already\n83\t  forwards the spell, so the restriction is enforced automatically. The matcher\n84\t  fails closed for unknown tags / missing spell context.\n85\t- Animating a non-creature `Land` into a creature while staying a land: subclass\n86\t  `Land`, expose `power`/`toughness` as properties over `_base_*`/`_power_bonus`,\n87\t  add `CardType.CREATURE` (union, keep `CardType.LAND`) under an \"isn't a\n88\t  creature\" gate, and wire the creature's triggers from inside the animation\n89\t  effect (idempotent via a guard).\n90\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018vLFmRjnSPaCfdXiEUZvAu","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"7ea2689b-d64a-4790-82f3-df16165ada94","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:10:33.254Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_257 tests: restricted mana"}
