{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JADaakRnZXkYcmY8nTsoFg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Test rationale — sos_257 Great Hall of the Biblioplex\n2\t\n3\tTest file: `/workspace/cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py`\n4\t\n5\tCard (Land):\n6\t- `{T}: Add {C}.`\n7\t- `{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell.`\n8\t- `{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.`\n9\t\n10\tAll tests drive the REAL engine (real `GameState`/players, real `engine.abilities.activate_ability`, real `TriggerManager.fire_event`). 34 test cases total, currently 30 fail (red phase) — the 4 that pass are vacuously satisfied by the empty `CardImpl` stub but encode genuine final-card requirements and remain correct for a correct implementation.\n11\t\n12\t## Assumed API contract (so the Implementer can align)\n13\t\n14\t- Class `GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex` subclasses `engine.card.Land`.\n15\t- `name == \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"`; `mana_cost == ManaCost()`; `colors == []`; `is_tapped` defaults `False`.\n16\t- `get_mana_abilities()` returns **exactly two** `ManaAbility` objects:\n17\t  - One whose `description` contains `\"{C}\"` — the `{T}: Add {C}` ability.\n18\t  - One whose `description` contains `\"life\"` (or `\"any color\"`) — the pay-1-life any-color ability.\n19\t  - `ManaAbility.cost` is invoked as `cost(game, source)` and taps the land (the life ability also deducts 1 life from the controller); returns `False` if already tapped.\n20\t  - `ManaAbility.mana_produced` is invoked as `mana_produced(game)` and adds exactly one mana to the controller's pool. The any-color ability reads the chosen color from the controller's `choose(...)` (tests script a `ManaType`).\n21\t- `get_activated_abilities()` returns **exactly one** `ActivatedAbility` — the `{5}` animation. `cost(game, source)` pays `{5}` (fails on 4 mana); `effect(game)` turns the land into a 2/4 creature with subtype `\"Wizard\"`, keeping `CardType.LAND`, with `power == 2` / `toughness == 4`. The effect is gated on \"isn't a creature\": calling `effect` again when already a creature does not stack additional P/T.\n22\t- `register_triggers(game)` registers a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger that pumps the (animated) land `+1/+0` until end of turn when the **controller** casts an instant or sorcery. The pump uses the standard P/T-modification path so `power`/`toughness` reflect the +1/+0.\n23\t\n24\t> Note: these are the asserted contract surfaces; if the Implementer chooses a slightly different but equivalent surface (e.g., a different attribute for \"chosen color\"), the disputed tests can be re-spec'd. The any-color tests deliberately accept either a `\"life\"` or `\"any color\"` description so the Implementer has latitude on wording.\n25\t\n26\t## Test cases\n27\t\n28\t### TestGreatHallProperties (static identity)\n29\t- `test_name` — name matches spec.\n30\t- `test_is_a_land` — instance of `Land`, has `CardType.LAND`.\n31\t- `test_has_no_mana_cost` — `mana_cost == ManaCost()` (lands have no cost).\n32\t- `test_is_not_a_creature_initially` — no `CardType.CREATURE` before animation.\n33\t- `test_colorless` — `colors == []`.\n34\t- `test_cannot_be_cast` — `can_cast(game) is False` (lands are played).\n35\t- `test_starts_untapped` — `is_tapped is False`.\n36\t\n37\t### TestColorlessManaAbility (`{T}: Add {C}`)\n38\t- `test_exposes_two_mana_abilities` — `get_mana_abilities()` length 2.\n39\t- `test_mana_abilities_are_mana_ability_instances` — both are `ManaAbility`.\n40\t- `test_colorless_ability_adds_one_colorless` — produces +1 `{C}`.\n41\t- `test_colorless_ability_taps_the_land` — paying the cost taps it.\n42\t- `test_colorless_ability_cost_fails_when_tapped` — tapped land can't pay `{T}`.\n43\t- `test_colorless_ability_only_adds_colorless` — no colored mana produced.\n44\t\n45\t### TestAnyColorManaAbility (`{T}, Pay 1 life: any color`)\n46\t- `test_any_color_ability_exists` — an ability mentions life / any color.\n47\t- `test_any_color_pays_one_life` — controller loses exactly 1 life.\n48\t- `test_any_color_taps_the_land` — taps as part of the cost.\n49\t- `test_any_color_adds_chosen_color` — adds the scripted color (green here).\n50\t- `test_any_color_adds_exactly_one_mana` — pool total is exactly 1.\n51\t- `test_any_color_cost_fails_when_tapped` — tapped land can't pay; life unchanged.\n52\t\n53\t### TestAnimationAbility (`{5}` → 2/4 Wizard, still a land)\n54\t- `test_exposes_one_activated_ability` — `get_activated_abilities()` length 1, an `ActivatedAbility`.\n55\t- `test_animation_requires_five_mana` — cost fails with only 4 mana.\n56\t- `test_animation_pays_five_mana` — paying with 5 empties the pool.\n57\t- `test_becomes_creature` — gains `CardType.CREATURE`.\n58\t- `test_stays_a_land` — keeps `CardType.LAND` (\"It's still a land\").\n59\t- `test_becomes_wizard_subtype` — gains subtype `\"Wizard\"`.\n60\t- `test_power_and_toughness_are_two_four` — `power == 2`, `toughness == 4`.\n61\t- `test_animation_via_engine_activate_ability` — end-to-end through `activate_ability` (non-mana → StackObject → resolve → animated).\n62\t- `test_gate_no_double_animation` — re-running the effect while already a creature doesn't double P/T (the \"isn't a creature\" gate).\n63\t\n64\t### TestCastTriggerPump (animated creature's \"whenever you cast\" +1/+0)\n65\t- `test_registers_spell_cast_trigger_after_animation` — a `SpellCastTriggeredEvent` trigger is registered for the source after animation.\n66\t- `test_pump_applies_on_controller_instant_cast` — controller's instant pumps to 3/4.\n67\t- `test_pump_applies_on_controller_sorcery_cast` — controller's sorcery pumps to 3 power.\n68\t- `test_pump_does_not_apply_for_creature_spell` — a creature spell does not pump (stays 2/4).\n69\t- `test_pump_does_not_apply_for_opponent_spell` — opponent's instant does not pump (\"Whenever YOU cast\").\n70\t- `test_no_pump_trigger_before_animation` — before animating, it is not a creature; registering triggers + firing a cast event leaves it a non-creature land (no pump).\n71\t\n72\t## Edge cases covered and why\n73\t- **Tapped-land cost rejection** for both mana abilities (and the life cost not being paid when tap fails) — verifies costs are atomic.\n74\t- **Animation gate** (\"isn't a creature\") — prevents repeated activations from stacking P/T, a real rules nuance (CR: the effect checks the condition on resolution).\n75\t- **Trigger ownership** — only the controller's instants/sorceries pump; creature spells and opponent spells do not.\n76\t- **\"Still a land\"** — keeps `CardType.LAND` so it can still tap for mana / be a land for other effects.\n77\t\n78\t## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope / engine surface gaps)\n79\t- **\"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\"** restriction on the any-color mana. The engine `ManaPool` tracks only a flat `dict[ManaType, int]` and has no per-mana spending restriction / \"restricted mana\" surface, so there is no observable way to assert that the produced mana may only pay for instants/sorceries. Recorded in `untestable.json`. The tests still verify the mana is produced (correct color, exactly one) and the life is paid.\n80\t- **Summoning sickness / \"can't attack the turn it's animated\"** — depends on land-played-this-turn timing the engine does not track on a permanent that was already on the battlefield; this is generic engine behavior, not specific to this card, and the spec text does not call it out.\n81\t- **Until-end-of-turn cleanup of the +1/+0 pump** — the engine's continuous-effect expiry runs in the cleanup step (`remove_expired`). Asserting the pump wears off would require advancing a full turn through `engine.turn`, which is broad integration territory; the per-cast pump application is the load-bearing behavior and is covered.\n82\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018vLFmRjnSPaCfdXiEUZvAu","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"f256ef5a-e532-4c38-b4d8-c51a301e9933","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:11:47.643Z","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_257 tests: restricted mana"}
