{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01SLoSZUsNshQSLXws48vX2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YN5oX9iskWSL2i5N9e9e4D","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/test-rationale.md","old_string":"## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope / engine surface gaps)\n- **\"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\"** restriction on the any-color mana. The engine `ManaPool` tracks only a flat `dict[ManaType, int]` and has no per-mana spending restriction / \"restricted mana\" surface, so there is no observable way to assert that the produced mana may only pay for instants/sorceries. Recorded in `untestable.json`. The tests still verify the mana is produced (correct color, exactly one) and the life is paid.","new_string":"### TestInstantSorceryRestrictedMana (added post-implementation — restricted-mana enforcement)\nThe previously-untestable \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery\nspell\" rider is now covered. The Implementer built the additive restricted-mana\nsurface (`engine.mana.ManaPool.add_restricted`, the `RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY`\ntag, and `engine.casting.cast_spell` forwarding `spell=card` to\n`can_pay`/`pay`). These tests drive the REAL `engine.casting.cast_spell` and\nassert observable outcomes; they PASS against the implemented surface (hardening,\nnot red-phase).\n- `test_restricted_mana_pays_for_instant_via_cast_spell` — the card's own pay-1-life ability produces a restricted BLUE mana (color scripted via `choose`); casting an instant through `cast_spell` SUCCEEDS (spell on the stack) and the mana is consumed.\n- `test_restricted_mana_pays_for_sorcery_via_cast_spell` — restricted GREEN added directly via `ManaPool.add_restricted(..., RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY)` pays for a SORCERY through `cast_spell`; spell lands on the stack, mana consumed.\n- `test_restricted_mana_cannot_pay_for_creature` — with that restricted mana as the ONLY available mana, casting a CREATURE raises `CastingError`; the restricted mana is NOT spent, the creature stays in hand, and the stack stays empty (clean rollback).\n- `test_unrestricted_mana_can_pay_for_creature_control` — control anchor: ordinary (unrestricted) GREEN mana DOES pay for the same creature via `cast_spell`, proving the restriction — not some unrelated gap — is what blocks the creature cast above.\n\nThese run in player 0's precombat main with an empty stack so sorcery-speed\ntiming is satisfied; the only variable across the creature-block test and its\ncontrol is whether the mana is restricted, isolating the restriction as the\ncause. `untestable.json` is now `[]`.\n\n## Edge cases intentionally NOT covered (out of scope / engine surface gaps)\n- **\"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\"** — NOW COVERED by `TestInstantSorceryRestrictedMana` (see above) after the additive restricted-mana surface was implemented. (Previously recorded in `untestable.json`; that item is resolved and the file is now empty.)"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3870,"cache_read_input_tokens":62245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3870,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018vLFmRjnSPaCfdXiEUZvAu","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"07f8f156-e43d-4a13-9006-07105e0c6f4a","request_id":"req_011Cbdd4K9ZKMv2bxiNpiL3K","subagent_type":"Tester","task_description":"Extend sos_257 tests: restricted mana"}
