{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QXqTyCv5zZRkaPdDXGuzfT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Key Decisions\n2\t\n3\tPersistent conventions and decisions across runs. Append-only.\n4\t\n5\t## Engine: \"exile instead of graveyard\" for free-cast spells (sos_1)\n6\tFor a non-permanent spell with \"if that spell would be put into your graveyard,\n7\texile it instead\": set `card._exile_instead_of_graveyard = True` on the spell\n8\tobject before casting it. `engine/casting.py::_resolve_spell` honors this opt-in\n9\tflag and routes the resolving instant/sorcery from the stack to `Zone.EXILE`\n10\tinstead of `Zone.GRAVEYARD`, then clears the flag (one-shot). Additive and\n11\tbackward-compatible (flag defaults absent). Reuse for cast-from-graveyard /\n12\timpulse effects with the same rider.\n13\t\n14\t## Convention: recurring main-phase delayed trigger + Paradigm (sos_120)\n15\tThe sos_57 `schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect` mechanism is ONE-SHOT. To make\n16\ta \"at the beginning of EACH of your main phases, do X\" recurring effect, have the\n17\tscheduled callback RE-SCHEDULE ITSELF each time it fires. CRITICAL: arm the\n18\trecurring chain idempotently — exactly ONE chain per controller. Use a\n19\tper-controller \"already armed\" guard (additive flag/set on game state or\n20\tcontroller) so repeated resolutions (and resolved free COPIES, whose own\n21\t`on_resolve` would otherwise re-arm) do not spawn additional chains (which would\n22\tmultiply the offer per main phase). Paradigm keyword (CR 702.192): advertise via\n23\ta card marker (`self.paradigm`) / rules_text; \"Then exile this spell\" uses the\n24\tsos_1 `_exile_instead_of_graveyard` opt-in; the recurring free-copy offer uses\n25\tthis idempotent self-rescheduling pattern. Exile-until-threshold loops accumulate\n26\t`mana_cost.cmc`, stop on `>= threshold` (boundary card may exceed; MV-0 doesn't\n27\tstop), and terminate safely on a short/empty library.\n28\t\n29\t## Engine: coin flips + skip-turn support; planeswalker conventions (sos_97)\n30\t- Coin flips: `engine.game.flip_coin(game, player=None) -> bool` (True=heads) and\n31\t  `engine.game.flip_coins(game, n, player=None) -> int` (heads count).\n32\t  Deterministic injection order: (1) `game._forced_coin_flips` (list/deque of\n33\t  booleans, consumed from the FRONT); (2) `game.rng` (random.Random-compatible,\n34\t  `rng.random() < 0.5`); (3) module `random`. Cards record their heads count on\n35\t  an attribute (e.g. `pw._last_heads`) for assertion.\n36\t- Skip turns: `Player.skipped_turns: int` (default 0). Honored by\n37\t  `GameState.advance_phase` via `_select_next_active_player`: while the next\n38\t  player has `skipped_turns > 0`, decrement it, consume the turn slot, and move\n39\t  to the next candidate (bounded guard against infinite skip). `extra_turns`\n40\t  FIFO behavior preserved. Use `target.skipped_turns += X` for \"skips their next\n41\t  X turns\" (CR 614.10).\n42\t- Planeswalkers: subclass `Planeswalker` (engine/card.py); set `starting_loyalty`,\n43\t  `Supertype.LEGENDARY`, subtype, explicit `self.colors`. `get_loyalty_abilities()`\n44\t  returns `LoyaltyAbility(loyalty_cost, effect, description)` closures\n45\t  `(game)->None` reading `pw.controller`. Targeted abilities read\n46\t  `pw._resolve_target` (single) / `pw._resolve_targets` (list). \"You may\" /\n47\t  per-card decisions (e.g. surveil keep/bin) via controller `choose_yes_no`;\n48\t  discards via `choose_card`. (Convention from FDN Kaito/Vivien/Liliana.)\n49\t- Surveil N: look at top N library cards, bin any number (per-card `choose_yes_no`),\n50\t  rest stay on top in order; fewer than N or empty library is a safe no-op.\n51\t\n52\t## Engine: mana-spent tracking, delayed main-phase triggers, spell/ability marker (sos_57)\n53\t- `card.mana_spent: int` — set by `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` to the\n54\t  converted mana actually paid (after cost reduction, `effective_cost.cmc`),\n55\t  analogous to `card.colors_spent`; `cast_spell_free` sets 0. Read via\n56\t  `getattr(card, \"mana_spent\", 0)`. Use for any \"amount of mana spent to cast\"\n57\t  rider. (Known gap: ignores {X} payments — would under-count X-spells.)\n58\t- `BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player, controller, precombat=True)` in\n59\t  `engine/events.py`, fired by `engine/turn.py` on entering precombat/postcombat\n60\t  main phases. Paired with `GameState.schedule_main_phase_deferred_effect(\n61\t  controller, callback, *, precombat=True)` (registry on GameState; delivery via\n62\t  `engine/deferred.py::deliver_main_phase_deferred_effects`, run SYNCHRONOUSLY\n63\t  inside `TriggerManager.fire_event` for that event type). This is the general\n64\t  \"at the beginning of your next main phase, do X once\" mechanism. A test fires\n65\t  it directly: `game.trigger_manager.fire_event(game,\n66\t  BeginningOfMainPhaseTriggeredEvent(player=ctrl, controller=ctrl, precombat=True))`.\n67\t  Effects are one-shot (removed on delivery).\n68\t- `StackObject.is_spell: bool` (additive, default False) — set True only in the\n69\t  casting pipeline (`cast_spell`, `cast_spell_free`, `copy_spell`). Abilities on\n70\t  the stack reuse their source permanent's `card_types`, so to distinguish a\n71\t  SPELL from an ability on the stack (e.g. for \"counter target spell\"), check\n72\t  `getattr(stack_obj, \"is_spell\", False)` rather than inspecting `card_types`.\n73\t\n74\t## Convention: preparation cards (CR 722) (sos_13)\n75\tThe engine has no native preparation-card support. Implement a preparation card\n76\t(two-part: a creature/permanent front face + an inset \"prepare spell\") as:\n77\t- The inset prepare spell is its own `Instant`/`Sorcery` subclass in the same\n78\t  `card_impl.py`, resolving via `chosen_targets`.\n79\t- Front-face card exposes: `prepared: bool` (default False) + `is_prepared`\n80\t  read-only alias property; `make_prepare_spell(self, game)` factory returning a\n81\t  castable inset-spell instance; `cast_prepare_spell(self, game, target=None)`\n82\t  which requires `prepared is True` (raise ValueError otherwise), free-casts a\n83\t  copy of the prepare spell (without paying mana), then sets `prepared = False`\n84\t  (unprepare per CR 722.3c).\n85\t- \"Becomes prepared\" / \"more creatures than you\" comparisons use STANDARD MTG\n86\t  counting: a creature is on the battlefield when its own ETB trigger resolves,\n87\t  so it counts toward \"you\"; tokens count for their controller; \"more than\" is\n88\t  strict `>`. Do NOT subtract the entering creature.\n89\t\n90\t## Convention: explicit colors attribute (sos_13)\n91\tThe engine has no native colors field. Set `self.colors` (list of single-letter\n92\tstrings, e.g. `[\"W\"]` or `[\"W\", \"B\"]`) explicitly on cards and tokens when color\n93\tidentity must be observable.\n94\t\n95\t## Engine: alternative-cost casting + draw-time grants / miracle (sos_201)\n96\t- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell(game, player, card, alternative_cost=None)` —\n97\t  additive kwarg. When a `ManaCost` is passed it is paid INSTEAD of\n98\t  `card.mana_cost`, cost reduction is NOT applied to the alt cost, the\n99\t  sorcery-speed timing gate is bypassed (miracle/as-you-draw casts ignore\n100\t  timing, CR 702.94/118.9), and `card.mana_spent` is set to the alt cost's\n101\t  `cmc`. With `alternative_cost=None` the function is byte-for-byte unchanged —\n102\t  the default cast path is untouched. Use for any \"you may cast this for its\n103\t  <alternative> cost\" rider (miracle, flashback, evoke, etc.).\n104\t- `Player.cards_drawn_this_turn: int` is the canonical per-turn draw counter,\n105\t  reset to 0 at the untap step for ALL players (`engine/turn.py`). Use it for\n106\t  \"the first card you drew this turn\" conditions.\n107\t- Draw-time \"as you draw\" grants (miracle): advertise a capability\n108\t  `grants_miracle_to(self, card) -> ManaCost | None` on a permanent. After\n109\t  firing the draw event, `engine/game.py::draw_card` calls a fully-gated\n110\t  `_offer_miracle` helper that is a COMPLETE no-op unless BOTH (a)\n111\t  `player.cards_drawn_this_turn == 1` AND (b) some permanent the player controls\n112\t  returns a non-None `grants_miracle_to(card)`. Only then does it stamp\n113\t  `card.miracle_cost` and offer `choose_yes_no`; on yes it casts the card for\n114\t  the miracle cost via the alternative-cost surface (CastingError swallowed → an\n115\t  unpayable miracle just stays in hand). Cards expose `MIRACLE_COST`\n116\t  (`ManaCost`) and `grant_miracle(game)` to stamp `miracle_cost` onto eligible\n117\t  cards (instants/sorceries) in the CONTROLLER's hand only. Modeling\n118\t  simplification: the miracle window is an immediate at-draw offer (not the full\n119\t  reveal→triggered-ability→cast-anytime sequence); deterministic and sufficient.\n120\t\n121\t## Engine: casualty / \"as you cast\" cast-trigger hook + use sacrifice() helper (sos_226)\n122\t- `engine/casting.py::cast_spell` calls a fully-gated `_offer_casualty(game,\n123\t  player, stack_obj)` helper AFTER pushing the spell StackObject. The helper is a\n124\t  COMPLETE no-op unless some permanent the CASTER controls returns a non-None\n125\t  `grants_casualty_to(spell)` (getattr-safe — not all permanents define it); only\n126\t  then it invokes that permanent's `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`. Default\n127\t  cast path is byte-for-byte unchanged when no grantor is present. This is the\n128\t  general pattern for \"as you cast a spell, do X\" granted abilities (mirrors the\n129\t  sos_201 draw-time miracle hook). Cards expose `grants_casualty_to(spell) ->\n130\t  int|None` (value for instants/sorceries) + `offer_casualty(game, stack_obj)`\n131\t  (gates on controller match + instant/sorcery + a power>=1 creature to\n132\t  sacrifice; pushes ONE distinct `copy_spell` with `is_spell=True`; optional new\n133\t  targets via `choose_target`). Reuse `copy_spell(...)` — do NOT reimplement copy\n134\t  logic. Modeling simplifications accepted: copy pushed directly post-push (not a\n135\t  delayed triggered ability in its own priority window); new-target options are a\n136\t  broad set rather than the spell's strict legal targets (CR 707.10c).\n137\t- Convention: for any \"sacrifice a permanent\" effect, use the canonical\n138\t  `engine.game.sacrifice(game, player, permanent)` helper (imported LOCALLY\n139\t  inside the method, per SOS convention) rather than a raw\n140\t  `move_to_zone(..., BATTLEFIELD, GRAVEYARD)`. `sacrifice` guards `bf.contains`\n141\t  and passes a `SacrificeReplacementEvent`, so sacrifice-redirection replacement\n142\t  effects (\"if a creature you control would die, exile it instead\", etc.) are\n143\t  correctly consulted. A raw `move_to_zone` with no `replacement_event` silently\n144\t  bypasses them.\n145\t\n146\t## Engine: granted cost reduction from controlled permanents / affinity grant (sos_245)\n147\t`engine/casting.py::get_cost_reduction` now sums, in addition to the casting\n148\tspell's OWN `cost_reduction(game)` hook, reductions GRANTED by permanents the\n149\tCASTER controls. A fully-gated helper `_granted_cost_reduction(game, card,\n150\tcontroller)` iterates the caster's battlefield and getattr-safe probes\n151\t`grants_affinity_to(card)`; when truthy it adds that permanent's\n152\t`affinity_reduction(game)` into the raw total BEFORE the unchanged single-source\n153\tclamp `max(0, min(raw, generic))` (granted reduction clamped to the generic\n154\tportion together with the self-reduction). COMPLETE no-op when no controlled\n155\tpermanent advertises the capability (most permanents define neither method →\n156\tloop adds 0), so the default path + all engine_tests are byte-for-byte\n157\tequivalent. A `permanent is card` guard prevents self-grant double-counting.\n158\tThis is the general \"spells you cast cost less / have affinity for X\" grantor\n159\tpattern: a permanent exposes `grants_affinity_to(spell) -> bool` (truthy for the\n160\tgranted card types) + `affinity_reduction(game) -> int`; a card's own affinity\n161\t(`cost_reduction`) may delegate to `affinity_reduction` for a single source of\n162\ttruth. Affinity is NOT an engine `Keyword` flag — it is purely a cost-reduction\n163\tmechanic. Same getattr-safe capability pattern as casualty (sos_226) / miracle\n164\t(sos_201), wired into `get_cost_reduction` rather than `cast_spell`/`draw_card`.\n165\t\n166\t## Convention: cost_reduction hook reads self.controller (sos_1)\n167\tOverride `CardImpl.cost_reduction(game)` for \"costs {N} less\" effects; the engine\n168\tclamps the reduction to the generic portion of the cost in\n169\t`engine.casting.get_cost_reduction` (`max(0, min(raw, generic))`), so no manual\n170\tclamping is needed. The hook may read `self.controller` (engine sets it before\n171\tquerying).\n172\t\n173\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018fs8roC62U1yCwfJG7Hwxt","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"6942787b-c9e0-46c5-b4f3-f151700d0db0","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:12:43.514Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a3cd706d0603ae0de","tool_use_id":"toolu_018fs8roC62U1yCwfJG7Hwxt","description":"Reading engine/mana.py","subagent_type":"Reviewer","usage":{"total_tokens":34438,"tool_uses":5,"duration_ms":7356},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"bbfeadcd-e4d4-4c2f-b794-ec2e43858e52","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_018rVypNs2yiFayqPUYbVvkR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Mw1a11DmeSAEmyBq2ALnnR","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/mana.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23625,"cache_read_input_tokens":10785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":23625,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018fs8roC62U1yCwfJG7Hwxt","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"e9b090c2-1546-4999-9ede-bd76bd51b0c8","request_id":"req_011Cbdd8NDU2TYTUjTkvib3q","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mw1a11DmeSAEmyBq2ALnnR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Mana pool and cost payment logic.\"\"\"\n2\t\n3\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n4\t\n5\tfrom typing import Any\n6\t\n7\tfrom engine.types import CardType, Color, HybridManaSymbol, ManaCost, ManaType\n8\t\n9\t# Map colored ManaTypes to their corresponding Color enum values.\n10\t_MANA_TO_COLOR: dict[ManaType, Color] = {\n11\t    ManaType.WHITE: Color.WHITE,\n12\t    ManaType.BLUE: Color.BLUE,\n13\t    ManaType.BLACK: Color.BLACK,\n14\t    ManaType.RED: Color.RED,\n15\t    ManaType.GREEN: Color.GREEN,\n16\t}\n17\t\n18\t\n19\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n20\t# Restricted-mana matching\n21\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n22\t\n23\t# Built-in restriction tags. A restriction tag describes WHICH spells a piece\n24\t# of mana may be spent on (CR 106.6 / e.g. \"Spend this mana only to cast an\n25\t# instant or sorcery spell\"). Tags are plain strings so the surface stays\n26\t# additive and easy to extend.\n27\tRESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY = \"instant_sorcery\"\n28\t\n29\t\n30\tdef restriction_allows(restriction: str | None, spell: Any) -> bool:\n31\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if mana tagged with *restriction* may pay for *spell*.\n32\t\n33\t    *restriction* of ``None`` means the mana is unrestricted and always\n34\t    spendable. A *spell* of ``None`` (no spell context — e.g. paying for an\n35\t    ability or a plain ``can_pay`` query) is treated conservatively: restricted\n36\t    mana is considered UNAVAILABLE because the restriction cannot be verified.\n37\t\n38\t    The only built-in tag is :data:`RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY`, which allows\n39\t    spending only on a spell whose ``card_types`` include INSTANT or SORCERY.\n40\t    Unknown tags deny by default (fail-closed) so an unverifiable restriction\n41\t    never silently leaks mana onto an illegal spell.\n42\t    \"\"\"\n43\t    if restriction is None:\n44\t        return True\n45\t    if spell is None:\n46\t        return False\n47\t    if restriction == RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY:\n48\t        card_types = getattr(spell, \"card_types\", set()) or set()\n49\t        return CardType.INSTANT in card_types or CardType.SORCERY in card_types\n50\t    return False\n51\t\n52\t\n53\tclass ManaPool:\n54\t    \"\"\"Tracks available mana for a player.\n55\t\n56\t    Internal storage uses a ``dict[ManaType, int]`` mapping each mana type\n57\t    to its current count.\n58\t    \"\"\"\n59\t\n60\t    def __init__(self) -> None:\n61\t        self._pool: dict[ManaType, int] = {mt: 0 for mt in ManaType}\n62\t        self._last_payment_colors: list[Color] = []\n63\t        # Per-mana-type ledger of spending restrictions. Each entry is a\n64\t        # restriction tag (e.g. \"instant_sorcery\"); the LENGTH of the list for\n65\t        # a type equals how many of that type's mana in ``_pool`` carry that\n66\t        # restriction. Restricted mana counts toward ``_pool`` (so ``get`` /\n67\t        # ``total`` / ``empty`` are unchanged) but may only pay for spells the\n68\t        # restriction allows. Empty unless ``add_restricted`` is ever called —\n69\t        # so a pool that never holds restricted mana is byte-for-byte\n70\t        # equivalent to the pre-restriction implementation.\n71\t        self._restricted: dict[ManaType, list[str]] = {mt: [] for mt in ManaType}\n72\t\n73\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n74\t    # Basic operations\n75\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n76\t\n77\t    def add(self, mana_type: ManaType, amount: int = 1) -> None:\n78\t        \"\"\"Add *amount* mana of the given type to the pool.\n79\t\n80\t        Parameters:\n81\t            mana_type: The type of mana to add.\n82\t            amount: How many mana to add (must be non-negative).\n83\t        \"\"\"\n84\t        if amount < 0:\n85\t            raise ValueError(f\"Cannot add negative mana: {amount}\")\n86\t        self._pool[mana_type] = self._pool.get(mana_type, 0) + amount\n87\t\n88\t    def add_restricted(\n89\t        self, mana_type: ManaType, amount: int = 1, restriction: str | None = None\n90\t    ) -> None:\n91\t        \"\"\"Add *amount* mana of *mana_type* carrying a spending *restriction*.\n92\t\n93\t        Restricted mana behaves exactly like normal mana for the purposes of\n94\t        :meth:`get`, :meth:`total`, and :meth:`empty` (it lives in the same\n95\t        underlying pool), but may only be spent to pay for a spell that the\n96\t        *restriction* tag allows (see :func:`restriction_allows`). When\n97\t        *restriction* is ``None`` this is identical to :meth:`add`.\n98\t\n99\t        Parameters:\n100\t            mana_type: The type of mana to add.\n101\t            amount: How many mana to add (must be non-negative).\n102\t            restriction: The restriction tag (e.g.\n103\t                :data:`RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY`) or ``None`` for\n104\t                unrestricted mana.\n105\t        \"\"\"\n106\t        if amount < 0:\n107\t            raise ValueError(f\"Cannot add negative mana: {amount}\")\n108\t        self._pool[mana_type] = self._pool.get(mana_type, 0) + amount\n109\t        if restriction is not None:\n110\t            self._restricted.setdefault(mana_type, []).extend(\n111\t                [restriction] * amount\n112\t            )\n113\t\n114\t    def empty(self) -> None:\n115\t        \"\"\"Clear the pool — happens at phase/step transitions.\"\"\"\n116\t        for mt in self._pool:\n117\t            self._pool[mt] = 0\n118\t        for mt in self._restricted:\n119\t            self._restricted[mt] = []\n120\t\n121\t    def total(self) -> int:\n122\t        \"\"\"Return the total amount of mana in the pool across all types.\"\"\"\n123\t        return sum(self._pool.values())\n124\t\n125\t    def get(self, mana_type: ManaType) -> int:\n126\t        \"\"\"Return the amount of a specific mana type in the pool.\"\"\"\n127\t        return self._pool.get(mana_type, 0)\n128\t\n129\t    @property\n130\t    def last_payment_colors(self) -> list[Color]:\n131\t        \"\"\"Return the distinct colors of mana spent in the last :meth:`pay` call.\n132\t\n133\t        Colorless mana is not a color and is excluded.  The list is sorted\n134\t        by Color enum order for determinism.  Empty if no payment has been\n135\t        made or if all mana spent was colorless.\n136\t        \"\"\"\n137\t        return list(self._last_payment_colors)\n138\t\n139\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n140\t    # Restricted-mana helpers\n141\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n142\t\n143\t    def _has_restricted(self) -> bool:\n144\t        \"\"\"Return ``True`` if any restricted mana is currently held.\"\"\"\n145\t        return any(self._restricted.get(mt) for mt in self._restricted)\n146\t\n147\t    def _spendable_pool(self, spell: Any) -> dict[ManaType, int]:\n148\t        \"\"\"Return a copy of the pool with *unavailable* restricted mana removed.\n149\t\n150\t        For *spell*, mana whose restriction tag does not allow paying for that\n151\t        spell is subtracted out, so the remaining counts are exactly the mana\n152\t        legally spendable on *spell*. When no restricted mana is held the\n153\t        returned dict equals ``dict(self._pool)``.\n154\t        \"\"\"\n155\t        result: dict[ManaType, int] = dict(self._pool)\n156\t        for mt, tags in self._restricted.items():\n157\t            blocked = sum(1 for tag in tags if not restriction_allows(tag, spell))\n158\t            if blocked:\n159\t                result[mt] = result.get(mt, 0) - blocked\n160\t        return result\n161\t\n162\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n163\t    # Cost payment\n164\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n165\t\n166\t    def can_pay(self, cost: ManaCost, spell: Any = None) -> bool:\n167\t        \"\"\"Check whether the pool can satisfy *cost*.\n168\t\n169\t        Generic mana can be paid by any type.  X is treated as 0 for\n170\t        ``can_pay`` unless explicitly set in the cost's generic component.\n171\t        Hybrid symbols can be paid with either option; this method uses\n172\t        backtracking to find a valid assignment.\n173\t\n174\t        Parameters:\n175\t            spell: Optional spell the mana would be spent on. When the pool\n176\t                holds restricted mana (see :meth:`add_restricted`), mana whose\n177\t                restriction does not allow *spell* is treated as unavailable.\n178\t                When ``None`` or when no restricted mana is held, the full pool\n179\t                is considered (byte-for-byte the original behaviour).\n180\t\n181\t        Returns:\n182\t            True if the pool has enough mana to pay the cost.\n183\t        \"\"\"\n184\t        source_pool = (\n185\t            self._spendable_pool(spell) if self._has_restricted() else self._pool\n186\t        )\n187\t        remaining: dict[ManaType, int] = dict(source_pool)\n188\t\n189\t        # Pay colored/colorless pips first.\n190\t        for mana_type, count in cost.pips.items():\n191\t            if remaining.get(mana_type, 0) < count:\n192\t                return False\n193\t            remaining[mana_type] = remaining.get(mana_type, 0) - count\n194\t\n195\t        # Solve hybrid symbols with backtracking.\n196\t        if cost.hybrid:\n197\t            if not self._can_pay_hybrid(remaining, list(cost.hybrid), 0, cost.generic):\n198\t                return False\n199\t            return True\n200\t\n201\t        # Then check generic — sum of all remaining mana must cover it.\n202\t        return sum(remaining.values()) >= cost.generic\n203\t\n204\t    def pay(\n205\t        self,\n206\t        cost: ManaCost,\n207\t        choices: dict[ManaType, int] | None = None,\n208\t        spell: Any = None,\n209\t    ) -> bool:\n210\t        \"\"\"Deduct mana from the pool to pay *cost*.\n211\t\n212\t        Parameters:\n213\t            cost: The mana cost to pay.\n214\t            choices: How to split the generic portion across mana types.\n215\t                If ``None``, auto-pay greedily: pay colored pips first,\n216\t                then hybrid symbols, then generic using colorless first,\n217\t                then excess colored.\n218\t            spell: Optional spell the mana is being spent on. When the pool\n219\t                holds restricted mana (see :meth:`add_restricted`), only mana\n220\t                whose restriction allows *spell* may be spent; restricted mana\n221\t                that does not match is treated as unavailable. When ``None`` or\n222\t                when no restricted mana is held, the full pool is used\n223\t                (byte-for-byte the original behaviour).\n224\t\n225\t        Returns:\n226\t            True if payment succeeded, False if the pool has insufficient mana.\n227\t        \"\"\"\n228\t        if not self.can_pay(cost, spell):\n229\t            return False\n230\t\n231\t        # Work on a copy so we can roll back on failure. When restricted mana\n232\t        # is present the working copy starts from the *spendable* pool so that\n233\t        # the existing payment algorithm never spends mana the spell may not\n234\t        # use. With no restricted mana this is exactly ``dict(self._pool)``.\n235\t        restricted = self._has_restricted()\n236\t        working: dict[ManaType, int] = dict(\n237\t            self._spendable_pool(spell) if restricted else self._pool\n238\t        )\n239\t\n240\t        # 1. Pay colored/colorless pips.\n241\t        for mana_type, count in cost.pips.items():\n242\t            working[mana_type] -= count\n243\t\n244\t        # 2. When explicit generic choices are provided, reserve that mana\n245\t        #    *before* solving hybrids so the solver doesn't steal it.\n246\t        generic_remaining = cost.generic\n247\t        if generic_remaining > 0 and choices is not None:\n248\t            # Reject negative choice amounts — they would create mana.\n249\t            if any(v < 0 for v in choices.values()):\n250\t                return False\n251\t            # Validate choices sum to generic cost.\n252\t            if sum(choices.values()) != generic_remaining:\n253\t                return False\n254\t            for mana_type, amount in choices.items():\n255\t                if working.get(mana_type, 0) < amount:\n256\t                    return False\n257\t                working[mana_type] -= amount\n258\t\n259\t        # 3. Pay hybrid symbols using backtracking to find a valid assignment.\n260\t        #    Generic choices (if any) have already been reserved above,\n261\t        #    so _solve_hybrid sees only the genuinely available mana.\n262\t        if cost.hybrid:\n263\t            generic_for_solver = generic_remaining if choices is None else 0\n264\t            hybrid_assignment = self._solve_hybrid(\n265\t                working, list(cost.hybrid), 0, generic_for_solver,\n266\t            )\n267\t            if hybrid_assignment is None:\n268\t                return False  # pragma: no cover – should not happen after can_pay\n269\t            for mt in hybrid_assignment:\n270\t                working[mt] = working.get(mt, 0) - 1\n271\t\n272\t        # 4. Pay generic cost (auto-pay path — choices already deducted above).\n273\t        if generic_remaining > 0 and choices is None:\n274\t            generic_remaining = self._auto_pay_generic(working, generic_remaining)\n275\t            if generic_remaining > 0:\n276\t                return False  # pragma: no cover – should not happen after can_pay\n277\t\n278\t        # Commit the payment.\n279\t        if not restricted:\n280\t            # Fast path: ``working`` is a derivative of the full pool, so it can\n281\t            # be committed directly (original behaviour).\n282\t            colors_spent: set[Color] = set()\n283\t            for mt, old_amount in self._pool.items():\n284\t                new_amount = working.get(mt, 0)\n285\t                if new_amount < old_amount and mt in _MANA_TO_COLOR:\n286\t                    colors_spent.add(_MANA_TO_COLOR[mt])\n287\t            self._last_payment_colors = sorted(colors_spent, key=lambda c: c.value)\n288\t            self._pool = working\n289\t            return True\n290\t\n291\t        # Restricted path: ``working`` was derived from the spendable pool, so\n292\t        # compute the amount spent per type and deduct it from the real pool,\n293\t        # then reconcile the restriction ledger. We spend UNrestricted mana of\n294\t        # each type before restricted mana so restricted mana lingers only when\n295\t        # it is genuinely needed (it empties between steps regardless).\n296\t        spendable = self._spendable_pool(spell)\n297\t        colors_spent = set()\n298\t        for mt in ManaType:\n299\t            spent = spendable.get(mt, 0) - working.get(mt, 0)\n300\t            if spent <= 0:\n301\t                continue\n302\t            if mt in _MANA_TO_COLOR:\n303\t                colors_spent.add(_MANA_TO_COLOR[mt])\n304\t            self._pool[mt] = self._pool.get(mt, 0) - spent\n305\t            self._spend_restricted(mt, spent, spell)\n306\t        self._last_payment_colors = sorted(colors_spent, key=lambda c: c.value)\n307\t        return True\n308\t\n309\t    def _spend_restricted(self, mana_type: ManaType, amount: int, spell: Any) -> None:\n310\t        \"\"\"Remove *amount* spent mana's restriction tags for *mana_type*.\n311\t\n312\t        Spends unrestricted mana first, then restricted (allowed) mana, so the\n313\t        restriction ledger stays consistent with the underlying pool counts.\n314\t        \"\"\"\n315\t        tags = self._restricted.get(mana_type)\n316\t        if not tags:\n317\t            return\n318\t        # Number of unrestricted mana of this type currently in the pool\n319\t        # (after the deduction has been applied to ``_pool``).\n320\t        # ``_pool`` already reflects the post-payment count; restricted tags\n321\t        # may now exceed it, so trim the matching tags we actually consumed.\n322\t        allowed_idx = [i for i, t in enumerate(tags) if restriction_allows(t, spell)]\n323\t        pool_count = self._pool.get(mana_type, 0)\n324\t        # Drop allowed restricted tags until the ledger no longer exceeds the\n325\t        # remaining pool count for this type.\n326\t        excess = len(tags) - pool_count\n327\t        if excess <= 0:\n328\t            return\n329\t        to_drop = set()\n330\t        for i in allowed_idx:\n331\t            if len(to_drop) >= excess:\n332\t                break\n333\t            to_drop.add(i)\n334\t        self._restricted[mana_type] = [\n335\t            t for i, t in enumerate(tags) if i not in to_drop\n336\t        ]\n337\t\n338\t    @staticmethod\n339\t    def _can_pay_hybrid(\n340\t        remaining: dict[ManaType, int],\n341\t        hybrids: list[HybridManaSymbol],\n342\t        idx: int,\n343\t        generic: int,\n344\t    ) -> bool:\n345\t        \"\"\"Recursively check if hybrid symbols + generic can be satisfied.\n346\t\n347\t        Uses backtracking: for each hybrid symbol, try option_a then option_b.\n348\t        After all hybrids are assigned, check that remaining mana covers generic.\n349\t        \"\"\"\n350\t        if idx >= len(hybrids):\n351\t            return sum(remaining.values()) >= generic\n352\t\n353\t        sym = hybrids[idx]\n354\t        for option in (sym.option_a, sym.option_b):\n355\t            if remaining.get(option, 0) > 0:\n356\t                remaining[option] -= 1\n357\t                if ManaPool._can_pay_hybrid(remaining, hybrids, idx + 1, generic):\n358\t                    remaining[option] += 1\n359\t                    return True\n360\t                remaining[option] += 1\n361\t        return False\n362\t\n363\t    @staticmethod\n364\t    def _solve_hybrid(\n365\t        remaining: dict[ManaType, int],\n366\t        hybrids: list[HybridManaSymbol],\n367\t        idx: int,\n368\t        generic: int,\n369\t    ) -> list[ManaType] | None:\n370\t        \"\"\"Find a valid assignment for hybrid symbols.\n371\t\n372\t        Returns a list of ManaType choices (one per hybrid symbol) or None\n373\t        if no valid assignment exists.\n374\t        \"\"\"\n375\t        if idx >= len(hybrids):\n376\t            if sum(remaining.values()) >= generic:\n377\t                return []\n378\t            return None\n379\t\n380\t        sym = hybrids[idx]\n381\t        for option in (sym.option_a, sym.option_b):\n382\t            if remaining.get(option, 0) > 0:\n383\t                remaining[option] -= 1\n384\t                result = ManaPool._solve_hybrid(remaining, hybrids, idx + 1, generic)\n385\t                if result is not None:\n386\t                    remaining[option] += 1\n387\t                    return [option] + result\n388\t                remaining[option] += 1\n389\t        return None\n390\t\n391\t    @staticmethod\n392\t    def _auto_pay_generic(working: dict[ManaType, int], amount: int) -> int:\n393\t        \"\"\"Deduct *amount* generic mana from *working*, preferring colorless.\n394\t\n395\t        Returns the remaining unpaid generic amount (0 on success).\n396\t        \"\"\"\n397\t        # Pay with colorless first.\n398\t        if working.get(ManaType.COLORLESS, 0) > 0:\n399\t            take = min(working[ManaType.COLORLESS], amount)\n400\t            working[ManaType.COLORLESS] -= take\n401\t            amount -= take\n402\t\n403\t        # Then pay with each colored type in enum order.\n404\t        for mt in ManaType:\n405\t            if mt is ManaType.COLORLESS:\n406\t                continue\n407\t            if amount <= 0:\n408\t                break\n409\t            if working.get(mt, 0) > 0:\n410\t                take = min(working[mt], amount)\n411\t                working[mt] -= take\n412\t                amount -= take\n413\t\n414\t        return amount\n415\t\n416\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n417\t    # Dunder helpers\n418\t    # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n419\t\n420\t    def __repr__(self) -> str:\n421\t        non_zero = {mt.name: v for mt, v in self._pool.items() if v > 0}\n422\t        return f\"ManaPool({non_zero})\"\n423\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018fs8roC62U1yCwfJG7Hwxt","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"9a3a1bd9-ef2f-4791-b59b-651f2b741f6a","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:12:47.534Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
