{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016oq9TzjNQab1555VdF5goc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Tests for SOS 257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex.\n2\t\n3\tGreat Hall of the Biblioplex — Land:\n4\t\n5\t    {T}: Add {C}.\n6\t    {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color. Spend this mana only to\n7\t        cast an instant or sorcery spell.\n8\t    {5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature\n9\t        with \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, this creature\n10\t        gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\" It's still a land.\n11\t\n12\tThe card has four distinct behavioural clauses:\n13\t\n14\t1. **Static land identity** — a colorless Land with no mana cost; not a\n15\t   creature (no power/toughness) until animated.\n16\t2. **{T}: Add {C}** — a mana ability that taps the land and adds one\n17\t   colorless mana to the controller's pool.\n18\t3. **{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color** — a mana ability that\n19\t   taps the land, pays 1 life, and adds one mana of a chosen color.\n20\t4. **{5}: becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature** — an activated ability gated on\n21\t   \"If this land isn't a creature\": it turns the land into a 2/4 Wizard\n22\t   creature that is still a land and gains the prowess-like cast trigger.\n23\t\n24\tThese tests follow the FDN reference-test style: static-property checks plus\n25\tbehavioural checks that drive the card's public hooks (``get_mana_abilities``\n26\t/ ``get_activated_abilities`` / ``register_triggers``) through the real\n27\tengine ability/trigger surfaces.\n28\t\n29\tCONTRACT NOTES for the Implementer (asserted below):\n30\t- Class name: ``GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex`` subclassing ``engine.card.Land``.\n31\t- ``mana_cost`` is empty (``ManaCost()``); ``colors == []``.\n32\t- ``get_mana_abilities()`` returns exactly two ``ManaAbility`` objects:\n33\t  index 0 is the ``{T}: Add {C}`` ability; index 1 is the\n34\t  ``{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color`` ability. Each\n35\t  ``ManaAbility.cost`` is invoked as ``cost(game, source)`` and taps the\n36\t  land (the life-payment ability also pays 1 life); ``mana_produced`` is\n37\t  invoked as ``mana_produced(game)`` and adds one mana to the controller's\n38\t  pool. The any-color ability reads the chosen color via the controller's\n39\t  ``choose`` method (scripted as a ``ManaType`` in these tests).\n40\t- ``get_activated_abilities()`` returns the ``{5}`` animation ability\n41\t  (an ``ActivatedAbility`` invoked through ``engine.abilities.activate_ability``).\n42\t  After it resolves, the land is also a 2/4 creature with subtype \"Wizard\",\n43\t  ``power == 2`` and ``toughness == 4``, and is still a land. The gate\n44\t  \"if this land isn't a creature\" makes a second activation a no-op for the\n45\t  type/P/T change.\n46\t- The animated land registers a ``SpellCastTriggeredEvent`` trigger\n47\t  (via ``register_triggers``) whose effect pumps the land +1/+0 when its\n48\t  controller casts an instant or sorcery spell.\n49\t\"\"\"\n50\t\n51\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n52\t\n53\timport pytest\n54\t\n55\tfrom engine.abilities import ActivatedAbilityInstance, activate_ability\n56\tfrom engine.card import Land, ManaAbility, ActivatedAbility, Instant, Sorcery, Creature\n57\tfrom engine.casting import CastingError, cast_spell\n58\tfrom engine.events import SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n59\tfrom engine.mana import RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY\n60\tfrom engine.triggers import TriggerRegistration\n61\tfrom engine.types import CardType, ManaCost, ManaType, Phase, Zone\n62\tfrom test_utils import create_game, set_board_state\n63\t\n64\tfrom cards.sos.sos_257.card_impl import GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n68\t# Helpers\n69\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n70\t\n71\tdef _hall_on_battlefield(game, player_index=0):\n72\t    \"\"\"Put a Great Hall on *player_index*'s battlefield and return it.\"\"\"\n73\t    hall = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None)\n74\t    set_board_state(game, player_index, battlefield=[hall])\n75\t    return hall\n76\t\n77\t\n78\tdef _mana_ability_for(hall, *, description_contains):\n79\t    \"\"\"Return the ManaAbility whose description contains *description_contains*.\n80\t\n81\t    Falls back to None when no matching ability is found.\n82\t    \"\"\"\n83\t    for ability in hall.get_mana_abilities():\n84\t        desc = getattr(ability, \"description\", \"\") or \"\"\n85\t        if description_contains in desc:\n86\t            return ability\n87\t    return None\n88\t\n89\t\n90\tdef _animation_ability(hall):\n91\t    \"\"\"Return the single ``{5}`` animation ActivatedAbility.\"\"\"\n92\t    abilities = hall.get_activated_abilities()\n93\t    assert abilities, \"Great Hall should expose at least one activated ability\"\n94\t    return abilities[0]\n95\t\n96\t\n97\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n98\t# Static card properties\n99\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n100\t\n101\tclass TestGreatHallProperties:\n102\t    \"\"\"Static card data should match the SOS 257 spec.\"\"\"\n103\t\n104\t    def test_name(self) -> None:\n105\t        assert GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None).name == \"Great Hall of the Biblioplex\"\n106\t\n107\t    def test_is_a_land(self) -> None:\n108\t        card = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None)\n109\t        assert isinstance(card, Land)\n110\t        assert CardType.LAND in card.card_types\n111\t\n112\t    def test_has_no_mana_cost(self) -> None:\n113\t        \"\"\"Lands have no mana cost.\"\"\"\n114\t        assert GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None).mana_cost == ManaCost()\n115\t\n116\t    def test_is_not_a_creature_initially(self) -> None:\n117\t        \"\"\"Until the {5} ability resolves, it is a plain land, not a creature.\"\"\"\n118\t        card = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None)\n119\t        assert CardType.CREATURE not in card.card_types\n120\t\n121\t    def test_colorless(self) -> None:\n122\t        \"\"\"The card's colors are empty (it is colorless).\"\"\"\n123\t        card = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None)\n124\t        assert list(getattr(card, \"colors\", [])) == []\n125\t\n126\t    def test_cannot_be_cast(self) -> None:\n127\t        \"\"\"Lands are played, not cast — ``can_cast`` is False.\"\"\"\n128\t        game = create_game()\n129\t        card = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=game.players[0])\n130\t        assert card.can_cast(game) is False\n131\t\n132\t    def test_starts_untapped(self) -> None:\n133\t        assert GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None).is_tapped is False\n134\t\n135\t\n136\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n137\t# {T}: Add {C}\n138\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n139\t\n140\tclass TestColorlessManaAbility:\n141\t    \"\"\"{T}: Add {C} — taps the land and adds one colorless mana.\"\"\"\n142\t\n143\t    def test_exposes_two_mana_abilities(self) -> None:\n144\t        \"\"\"The land has two distinct mana abilities ({C} and any-color).\"\"\"\n145\t        hall = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None)\n146\t        assert len(hall.get_mana_abilities()) == 2\n147\t\n148\t    def test_mana_abilities_are_mana_ability_instances(self) -> None:\n149\t        hall = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None)\n150\t        for ability in hall.get_mana_abilities():\n151\t            assert isinstance(ability, ManaAbility)\n152\t\n153\t    def test_colorless_ability_adds_one_colorless(self) -> None:\n154\t        game = create_game()\n155\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n156\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n157\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"{C}\")\n158\t        assert ability is not None, \"Expected a {T}: Add {C} mana ability\"\n159\t\n160\t        before = p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.COLORLESS)\n161\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is True\n162\t        ability.mana_produced(game)\n163\t        assert p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.COLORLESS) == before + 1\n164\t\n165\t    def test_colorless_ability_taps_the_land(self) -> None:\n166\t        game = create_game()\n167\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n168\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"{C}\")\n169\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is True\n170\t        assert hall.is_tapped is True\n171\t\n172\t    def test_colorless_ability_cost_fails_when_tapped(self) -> None:\n173\t        \"\"\"A tapped land cannot pay the {T} cost again.\"\"\"\n174\t        game = create_game()\n175\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n176\t        hall.is_tapped = True\n177\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"{C}\")\n178\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is False\n179\t\n180\t    def test_colorless_ability_only_adds_colorless(self) -> None:\n181\t        \"\"\"The {C} ability must not add any colored mana.\"\"\"\n182\t        game = create_game()\n183\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n184\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n185\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"{C}\")\n186\t        ability.cost(game, hall)\n187\t        ability.mana_produced(game)\n188\t        for mt in (ManaType.WHITE, ManaType.BLUE, ManaType.BLACK,\n189\t                   ManaType.RED, ManaType.GREEN):\n190\t            assert p1.mana_pool.get(mt) == 0\n191\t\n192\t\n193\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n194\t# {T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color\n195\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n196\t\n197\tclass TestAnyColorManaAbility:\n198\t    \"\"\"{T}, Pay 1 life: Add one mana of any color.\"\"\"\n199\t\n200\t    def test_any_color_ability_exists(self) -> None:\n201\t        \"\"\"There is a mana ability that pays life for any color.\"\"\"\n202\t        hall = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None)\n203\t        # The any-color ability is the one that is NOT the plain {C} ability.\n204\t        abilities = hall.get_mana_abilities()\n205\t        descs = [getattr(a, \"description\", \"\") or \"\" for a in abilities]\n206\t        assert any(\"life\" in d.lower() or \"any color\" in d.lower() for d in descs)\n207\t\n208\t    def test_any_color_pays_one_life(self) -> None:\n209\t        \"\"\"Activating the ability deducts exactly 1 life from the controller.\"\"\"\n210\t        game = create_game(scripts=([ManaType.BLUE], []))\n211\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n212\t        p1.life = 20\n213\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n214\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"life\")\n215\t        if ability is None:  # tolerate a description that says \"any color\"\n216\t            ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"any color\")\n217\t        assert ability is not None\n218\t\n219\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is True\n220\t        assert p1.life == 19\n221\t\n222\t    def test_any_color_taps_the_land(self) -> None:\n223\t        game = create_game(scripts=([ManaType.RED], []))\n224\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n225\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"life\") \\\n226\t            or _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"any color\")\n227\t        assert ability is not None\n228\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is True\n229\t        assert hall.is_tapped is True\n230\t\n231\t    def test_any_color_adds_chosen_color(self) -> None:\n232\t        \"\"\"The mana added matches the controller's chosen color.\"\"\"\n233\t        game = create_game(scripts=([ManaType.GREEN], []))\n234\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n235\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n236\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"life\") \\\n237\t            or _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"any color\")\n238\t        assert ability is not None\n239\t\n240\t        before = p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.GREEN)\n241\t        ability.cost(game, hall)\n242\t        ability.mana_produced(game)\n243\t        assert p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.GREEN) == before + 1\n244\t\n245\t    def test_any_color_adds_exactly_one_mana(self) -> None:\n246\t        \"\"\"Only a single mana is produced regardless of color chosen.\"\"\"\n247\t        game = create_game(scripts=([ManaType.WHITE], []))\n248\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n249\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n250\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"life\") \\\n251\t            or _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"any color\")\n252\t        assert ability is not None\n253\t        ability.cost(game, hall)\n254\t        ability.mana_produced(game)\n255\t        assert p1.mana_pool.total() == 1\n256\t\n257\t    def test_any_color_cost_fails_when_tapped(self) -> None:\n258\t        \"\"\"A tapped land cannot pay the {T} portion of the cost.\"\"\"\n259\t        game = create_game(scripts=([ManaType.BLUE], []))\n260\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n261\t        p1.life = 20\n262\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n263\t        hall.is_tapped = True\n264\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"life\") \\\n265\t            or _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"any color\")\n266\t        assert ability is not None\n267\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is False\n268\t        # Life should not have been paid if the tap could not happen.\n269\t        assert p1.life == 20\n270\t\n271\t\n272\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n273\t# {5}: becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature\n274\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n275\t\n276\tclass TestAnimationAbility:\n277\t    \"\"\"{5}: If this land isn't a creature, it becomes a 2/4 Wizard creature\n278\t    that's still a land.\"\"\"\n279\t\n280\t    def test_exposes_one_activated_ability(self) -> None:\n281\t        hall = GreatHallOfTheBiblioplex(owner=None)\n282\t        abilities = hall.get_activated_abilities()\n283\t        assert len(abilities) == 1\n284\t        assert isinstance(abilities[0], ActivatedAbility)\n285\t\n286\t    def test_animation_requires_five_mana(self) -> None:\n287\t        \"\"\"With only 4 mana the {5} cost cannot be paid.\"\"\"\n288\t        game = create_game()\n289\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n290\t        set_board_state(game, 0, mana={ManaType.COLORLESS: 4})\n291\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n292\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is False\n293\t\n294\t    def test_animation_pays_five_mana(self) -> None:\n295\t        \"\"\"Paying {5} deducts five mana from the controller's pool.\"\"\"\n296\t        game = create_game()\n297\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n298\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n299\t        set_board_state(game, 0, mana={ManaType.COLORLESS: 5})\n300\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n301\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is True\n302\t        assert p1.mana_pool.total() == 0\n303\t\n304\t    def test_becomes_creature(self) -> None:\n305\t        \"\"\"After the effect, the land has the CREATURE card type.\"\"\"\n306\t        game = create_game()\n307\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n308\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n309\t        ability.effect(game)\n310\t        assert CardType.CREATURE in hall.card_types\n311\t\n312\t    def test_stays_a_land(self) -> None:\n313\t        \"\"\"It's still a land after animating.\"\"\"\n314\t        game = create_game()\n315\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n316\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n317\t        ability.effect(game)\n318\t        assert CardType.LAND in hall.card_types\n319\t\n320\t    def test_becomes_wizard_subtype(self) -> None:\n321\t        game = create_game()\n322\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n323\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n324\t        ability.effect(game)\n325\t        assert \"Wizard\" in hall.subtypes\n326\t\n327\t    def test_power_and_toughness_are_two_four(self) -> None:\n328\t        \"\"\"The animated creature is 2/4.\"\"\"\n329\t        game = create_game()\n330\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n331\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n332\t        ability.effect(game)\n333\t        assert hall.power == 2\n334\t        assert hall.toughness == 4\n335\t\n336\t    def test_animation_via_engine_activate_ability(self) -> None:\n337\t        \"\"\"End-to-end: activating through engine.abilities.activate_ability\n338\t        animates the land (non-mana ability resolves off the stack).\"\"\"\n339\t        game = create_game()\n340\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n341\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n342\t        set_board_state(game, 0, mana={ManaType.COLORLESS: 5})\n343\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n344\t        instance = ActivatedAbilityInstance(\n345\t            source=hall,\n346\t            controller=p1,\n347\t            cost=ability.cost,\n348\t            effect=ability.effect,\n349\t            is_mana_ability=False,\n350\t            description=getattr(ability, \"description\", \"\"),\n351\t        )\n352\t        activate_ability(game, p1, instance)\n353\t        # Non-mana ability pushes a StackObject; resolve it.\n354\t        assert not game.stack.is_empty()\n355\t        obj = game.stack.pop()\n356\t        obj.on_resolve(game)\n357\t        assert CardType.CREATURE in hall.card_types\n358\t        assert CardType.LAND in hall.card_types\n359\t\n360\t    def test_gate_no_double_animation(self) -> None:\n361\t        \"\"\"'If this land isn't a creature' — re-running the effect while it is\n362\t        already a creature must not stack additional power/toughness.\"\"\"\n363\t        game = create_game()\n364\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n365\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n366\t        ability.effect(game)\n367\t        assert (hall.power, hall.toughness) == (2, 4)\n368\t        # Second resolution is a no-op for the becomes-creature change.\n369\t        ability.effect(game)\n370\t        assert (hall.power, hall.toughness) == (2, 4)\n371\t\n372\t\n373\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n374\t# Animated creature's \"Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery\" pump\n375\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n376\t\n377\tclass TestCastTriggerPump:\n378\t    \"\"\"The animated creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn whenever its\n379\t    controller casts an instant or sorcery spell.\"\"\"\n380\t\n381\t    def _animate(self, game, hall):\n382\t        ability = _animation_ability(hall)\n383\t        ability.effect(game)\n384\t        # Register the source's triggers (engine wires this on ETB; here we\n385\t        # invoke it directly so the cast trigger is live).\n386\t        hall.register_triggers(game)\n387\t\n388\t    def test_registers_spell_cast_trigger_after_animation(self) -> None:\n389\t        \"\"\"Once animated, the land registers a SpellCastTriggeredEvent trigger.\"\"\"\n390\t        game = create_game()\n391\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n392\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n393\t        self._animate(game, hall)\n394\t        regs = game.trigger_manager.get_triggers_for_source(hall)\n395\t        assert any(\n396\t            r.event_type is SpellCastTriggeredEvent\n397\t            or issubclass(SpellCastTriggeredEvent, r.event_type)\n398\t            for r in regs\n399\t        )\n400\t\n401\t    def test_pump_applies_on_controller_instant_cast(self) -> None:\n402\t        \"\"\"Firing a SpellCastTriggeredEvent for an instant the controller cast\n403\t        pumps the animated land +1/+0 (to 3/4).\"\"\"\n404\t        game = create_game()\n405\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n406\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n407\t        self._animate(game, hall)\n408\t        assert (hall.power, hall.toughness) == (2, 4)\n409\t\n410\t        bolt = Instant(name=\"Bolt\", mana_cost=ManaCost(pips={ManaType.RED: 1}),\n411\t                       owner=p1, controller=p1)\n412\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n413\t            game,\n414\t            SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=bolt, card=bolt,\n415\t                                    player=p1, controller=p1),\n416\t        )\n417\t        # Resolve any triggered abilities that were pushed.\n418\t        while not game.stack.is_empty():\n419\t            game.stack.pop().on_resolve(game)\n420\t\n421\t        assert hall.power == 3\n422\t        assert hall.toughness == 4\n423\t\n424\t    def test_pump_applies_on_controller_sorcery_cast(self) -> None:\n425\t        \"\"\"A sorcery also triggers the +1/+0 pump.\"\"\"\n426\t        game = create_game()\n427\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n428\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n429\t        self._animate(game, hall)\n430\t\n431\t        sorc = Sorcery(name=\"Divination\",\n432\t                       mana_cost=ManaCost(generic=2, pips={ManaType.BLUE: 1}),\n433\t                       owner=p1, controller=p1)\n434\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n435\t            game,\n436\t            SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=sorc, card=sorc,\n437\t                                    player=p1, controller=p1),\n438\t        )\n439\t        while not game.stack.is_empty():\n440\t            game.stack.pop().on_resolve(game)\n441\t\n442\t        assert hall.power == 3\n443\t\n444\t    def test_pump_does_not_apply_for_creature_spell(self) -> None:\n445\t        \"\"\"Casting a creature spell does NOT pump the animated land.\"\"\"\n446\t        game = create_game()\n447\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n448\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n449\t        self._animate(game, hall)\n450\t\n451\t        bear = Creature(name=\"Bear\",\n452\t                        mana_cost=ManaCost(generic=1, pips={ManaType.GREEN: 1}),\n453\t                        base_power=2, base_toughness=2,\n454\t                        owner=p1, controller=p1)\n455\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n456\t            game,\n457\t            SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=bear, card=bear,\n458\t                                    player=p1, controller=p1),\n459\t        )\n460\t        while not game.stack.is_empty():\n461\t            game.stack.pop().on_resolve(game)\n462\t\n463\t        assert hall.power == 2\n464\t        assert hall.toughness == 4\n465\t\n466\t    def test_pump_does_not_apply_for_opponent_spell(self) -> None:\n467\t        \"\"\"'Whenever YOU cast' — an opponent's instant must not pump it.\"\"\"\n468\t        game = create_game()\n469\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n470\t        p2 = game.players[1]\n471\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n472\t        self._animate(game, hall)\n473\t\n474\t        bolt = Instant(name=\"Opp Bolt\", mana_cost=ManaCost(pips={ManaType.RED: 1}),\n475\t                       owner=p2, controller=p2)\n476\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n477\t            game,\n478\t            SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=bolt, card=bolt,\n479\t                                    player=p2, controller=p2),\n480\t        )\n481\t        while not game.stack.is_empty():\n482\t            game.stack.pop().on_resolve(game)\n483\t\n484\t        assert hall.power == 2\n485\t\n486\t    def test_no_pump_trigger_before_animation(self) -> None:\n487\t        \"\"\"Before animating, casting an instant must not pump it (it is not\n488\t        even a creature). No SpellCast trigger should be registered yet.\"\"\"\n489\t        game = create_game()\n490\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n491\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n492\t        # Register triggers WITHOUT animating first.\n493\t        hall.register_triggers(game)\n494\t\n495\t        bolt = Instant(name=\"Bolt\", mana_cost=ManaCost(pips={ManaType.RED: 1}),\n496\t                       owner=p1, controller=p1)\n497\t        game.trigger_manager.fire_event(\n498\t            game,\n499\t            SpellCastTriggeredEvent(spell=bolt, card=bolt,\n500\t                                    player=p1, controller=p1),\n501\t        )\n502\t        while not game.stack.is_empty():\n503\t            game.stack.pop().on_resolve(game)\n504\t\n505\t        # Still not a creature, and no power to speak of.\n506\t        assert CardType.CREATURE not in hall.card_types\n507\t\n508\t\n509\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n510\t# \"Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell\" restriction\n511\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n512\t\n513\tclass TestInstantSorceryRestrictedMana:\n514\t    \"\"\"The any-color mana from the {T}, Pay 1 life ability carries the\n515\t    'Spend this mana only to cast an instant or sorcery spell' rider\n516\t    (CR 106.6). These tests drive the REAL ``engine.casting.cast_spell``\n517\t    payment path to prove the restriction is enforced: restricted mana pays\n518\t    for an instant/sorcery, but is treated as unavailable for a creature.\n519\t\n520\t    This covers the requirement previously reported as untestable (the engine\n521\t    now exposes ``ManaPool.add_restricted`` and ``cast_spell`` consults it).\n522\t    \"\"\"\n523\t\n524\t    def _main_phase_game(self, *, scripts=None):\n525\t        \"\"\"A two-player game in player 0's precombat main with an empty stack,\n526\t        so sorcery-speed timing is satisfied for sorceries/creatures.\"\"\"\n527\t        game = create_game(scripts=scripts)\n528\t        game.phase = Phase.PRECOMBAT_MAIN\n529\t        return game\n530\t\n531\t    def test_restricted_mana_pays_for_instant_via_cast_spell(self) -> None:\n532\t        \"\"\"Mana produced by the pay-1-life ability (tagged instant/sorcery)\n533\t        successfully pays for an INSTANT through the real cast_spell, and the\n534\t        mana is consumed.\"\"\"\n535\t        # Script the color choice (BLUE) for the any-color ability.\n536\t        game = self._main_phase_game(scripts=([ManaType.BLUE], []))\n537\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n538\t        hall = _hall_on_battlefield(game, 0)\n539\t\n540\t        # Produce the restricted any-color mana via the card's own ability.\n541\t        ability = _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"life\") \\\n542\t            or _mana_ability_for(hall, description_contains=\"any color\")\n543\t        assert ability is not None\n544\t        assert ability.cost(game, hall) is True\n545\t        ability.mana_produced(game)\n546\t        assert p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.BLUE) == 1\n547\t\n548\t        bolt = Instant(name=\"Blue Bolt\",\n549\t                       mana_cost=ManaCost(pips={ManaType.BLUE: 1}),\n550\t                       owner=p1, controller=p1)\n551\t        game.get_hand(p1).add(bolt)\n552\t\n553\t        # The restricted mana is allowed to pay for an instant.\n554\t        cast_spell(game, p1, bolt)\n555\t\n556\t        assert not game.stack.is_empty()\n557\t        assert game.stack.peek().source is bolt\n558\t        # Mana was consumed by the cast.\n559\t        assert p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.BLUE) == 0\n560\t\n561\t    def test_restricted_mana_pays_for_sorcery_via_cast_spell(self) -> None:\n562\t        \"\"\"Restricted mana added directly via ManaPool.add_restricted pays for\n563\t        a SORCERY through cast_spell.\"\"\"\n564\t        game = self._main_phase_game()\n565\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n566\t        p1.mana_pool.empty()\n567\t        p1.mana_pool.add_restricted(\n568\t            ManaType.GREEN, 1, restriction=RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY\n569\t        )\n570\t\n571\t        sorc = Sorcery(name=\"Green Ritual\",\n572\t                       mana_cost=ManaCost(pips={ManaType.GREEN: 1}),\n573\t                       owner=p1, controller=p1)\n574\t        game.get_hand(p1).add(sorc)\n575\t\n576\t        cast_spell(game, p1, sorc)\n577\t\n578\t        assert not game.stack.is_empty()\n579\t        assert game.stack.peek().source is sorc\n580\t        assert p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.GREEN) == 0\n581\t\n582\t    def test_restricted_mana_cannot_pay_for_creature(self) -> None:\n583\t        \"\"\"With instant/sorcery-restricted mana as the ONLY available mana,\n584\t        casting a CREATURE raises CastingError and nothing changes: the spell\n585\t        stays in hand, the stack stays empty, and the mana is untouched.\"\"\"\n586\t        game = self._main_phase_game()\n587\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n588\t        p1.mana_pool.empty()\n589\t        p1.mana_pool.add_restricted(\n590\t            ManaType.GREEN, 1, restriction=RESTRICTION_INSTANT_SORCERY\n591\t        )\n592\t\n593\t        bear = Creature(name=\"Bear\",\n594\t                        mana_cost=ManaCost(pips={ManaType.GREEN: 1}),\n595\t                        base_power=2, base_toughness=2,\n596\t                        owner=p1, controller=p1)\n597\t        game.get_hand(p1).add(bear)\n598\t\n599\t        with pytest.raises(CastingError):\n600\t            cast_spell(game, p1, bear)\n601\t\n602\t        # Restricted mana was NOT spent on the illegal creature spell.\n603\t        assert p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.GREEN) == 1\n604\t        # Rolled back: the creature is still in hand and not on the stack.\n605\t        assert game.get_hand(p1).contains(bear)\n606\t        assert game.stack.is_empty()\n607\t\n608\t    def test_unrestricted_mana_can_pay_for_creature_control(self) -> None:\n609\t        \"\"\"Control: ordinary (unrestricted) GREEN mana DOES pay for the same\n610\t        creature spell, proving it is the restriction — not some other gap —\n611\t        that blocks the creature cast above.\"\"\"\n612\t        game = self._main_phase_game()\n613\t        p1 = game.players[0]\n614\t        set_board_state(game, 0, mana={ManaType.GREEN: 1})\n615\t\n616\t        bear = Creature(name=\"Bear\",\n617\t                        mana_cost=ManaCost(pips={ManaType.GREEN: 1}),\n618\t                        base_power=2, base_toughness=2,\n619\t                        owner=p1, controller=p1)\n620\t        game.get_hand(p1).add(bear)\n621\t\n622\t        cast_spell(game, p1, bear)\n623\t\n624\t        assert not game.stack.is_empty()\n625\t        assert game.stack.peek().source is bear\n626\t        assert p1.mana_pool.get(ManaType.GREEN) == 0\n627\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018fs8roC62U1yCwfJG7Hwxt","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"792bd0c1-cb9e-4a8f-adaf-2befcd60ca00","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:13:06.107Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a3cd706d0603ae0de","tool_use_id":"toolu_018fs8roC62U1yCwfJG7Hwxt","description":"Reading engine/abilities.py","subagent_type":"Reviewer","usage":{"total_tokens":60073,"tool_uses":15,"duration_ms":42269},"last_tool_name":"Read","uuid":"e425d08c-db9a-44ec-8e47-16e603820b57","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CoEgdAxpKfN9niCK9Wzymz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R2ik7jmck5sGzAp66dcvki","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/workspace/engine/abilities.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11669,"cache_read_input_tokens":48158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":11669,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018fs8roC62U1yCwfJG7Hwxt","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"342f3cc4-92ee-4664-a8bf-df774b4c29e1","request_id":"req_011CbddA2cok4ZKDrWPcbuyy","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R2ik7jmck5sGzAp66dcvki","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"Activated abilities system — tap-for-mana, loyalty abilities, and general\n2\tactivated abilities that go on the stack (or resolve immediately for mana\n3\tabilities).\n4\t\n5\tProvides:\n6\t\n7\t- :func:`activate_ability` — verify timing → pay costs → resolve immediately\n8\t  (mana abilities) or push to the stack (non-mana abilities).\n9\t- :func:`tap_cost` — generic tap-cost helper: checks ``not source.is_tapped``\n10\t  and taps the source.\n11\t- :class:`ActivatedAbilityInstance` — a runtime representation of an activated\n12\t  ability with source, controller, cost/effect callables, and metadata.\n13\t- :class:`LoyaltyAbilityInstance` — activated ability variant for planeswalker\n14\t  loyalty abilities with per-turn restriction and loyalty-counter cost.\n15\t\"\"\"\n16\t\n17\tfrom __future__ import annotations\n18\t\n19\tfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\n20\tfrom typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Any, Callable\n21\t\n22\tfrom engine.casting import is_sorcery_speed\n23\tfrom engine.stack import StackObject\n24\t\n25\tif TYPE_CHECKING:\n26\t    from engine.game_state import GameState\n27\t    from engine.player import Player\n28\t\n29\t\n30\tclass AbilityError(Exception):\n31\t    \"\"\"Raised when an ability activation is illegal.\"\"\"\n32\t\n33\t\n34\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n35\t# Runtime ability representations\n36\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n37\t\n38\t@dataclass\n39\tclass ActivatedAbilityInstance:\n40\t    \"\"\"Runtime representation of an activated ability.\n41\t\n42\t    This captures everything needed to activate and resolve an ability:\n43\t    the source permanent, the controlling player, cost/effect callables,\n44\t    and whether the ability is a mana ability.\n45\t\n46\t    Attributes:\n47\t        source: The permanent that has this ability.\n48\t        controller: The player who controls the source.\n49\t        cost: A callable ``(game, source) -> bool`` that checks and pays\n50\t            the cost. Returns ``True`` if the cost was successfully paid,\n51\t            ``False`` otherwise.\n52\t        effect: A callable ``(game) -> None`` that applies the ability's\n53\t            effect when it resolves.\n54\t        is_mana_ability: Whether this is a mana ability (resolves\n55\t            immediately without using the stack).\n56\t        description: Human-readable description of the ability.\n57\t    \"\"\"\n58\t\n59\t    source: Any\n60\t    controller: Any  # Player\n61\t    cost: Callable[..., bool]\n62\t    effect: Callable[..., None]\n63\t    is_mana_ability: bool = False\n64\t    description: str = \"\"\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t@dataclass\n68\tclass LoyaltyAbilityInstance:\n69\t    \"\"\"Runtime representation of a planeswalker loyalty ability.\n70\t\n71\t    Loyalty abilities are activated abilities with special restrictions:\n72\t    they may only be activated at sorcery speed, and only once per turn\n73\t    per source (tracked via ``_activated_this_turn``).\n74\t\n75\t    The cost adjusts the loyalty counters on the source planeswalker.\n76\t\n77\t    Attributes:\n78\t        source: The planeswalker permanent.\n79\t        controller: The player who controls the planeswalker.\n80\t        loyalty_cost: The loyalty adjustment (positive for ``+N``,\n81\t            negative for ``−N``, zero for ``0``).\n82\t        effect: A callable ``(game) -> None`` for the ability's effect.\n83\t        description: Human-readable description.\n84\t    \"\"\"\n85\t\n86\t    source: Any\n87\t    controller: Any  # Player\n88\t    loyalty_cost: int = 0\n89\t    effect: Callable[..., None] = field(default=lambda _game: None)\n90\t    description: str = \"\"\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n94\t# Per-turn loyalty tracking\n95\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n96\t\n97\t# Set of (object_id, turn_number) pairs that have already activated a\n98\t# loyalty ability this turn.  Callers should call\n99\t# ``clear_loyalty_tracking()`` at the start of each turn or manage the\n100\t# set externally.\n101\t_loyalty_activated_this_turn: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n102\t\n103\t\n104\tdef clear_loyalty_tracking() -> None:\n105\t    \"\"\"Clear the loyalty-activated-this-turn tracker.\n106\t\n107\t    Should be called at the start of each turn so that planeswalkers may\n108\t    activate loyalty abilities again.\n109\t    \"\"\"\n110\t    _loyalty_activated_this_turn.clear()\n111\t\n112\t\n113\tdef _has_activated_loyalty_this_turn(source: Any, turn_number: int) -> bool:\n114\t    \"\"\"Return ``True`` if *source* already used a loyalty ability this turn.\"\"\"\n115\t    obj_id = getattr(source, \"object_id\", id(source))\n116\t    return (obj_id, turn_number) in _loyalty_activated_this_turn\n117\t\n118\t\n119\tdef _mark_loyalty_activated(source: Any, turn_number: int) -> None:\n120\t    \"\"\"Record that *source* used a loyalty ability this turn.\"\"\"\n121\t    obj_id = getattr(source, \"object_id\", id(source))\n122\t    _loyalty_activated_this_turn.add((obj_id, turn_number))\n123\t\n124\t\n125\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n126\t# Tap cost helper\n127\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n128\t\n129\tdef tap_cost(game: GameState, source: Any) -> bool:\n130\t    \"\"\"Generic tap-cost function.\n131\t\n132\t    Checks that the source is not already tapped.  If untapped, taps it\n133\t    (sets ``source.is_tapped = True``) and returns ``True``.  If already\n134\t    tapped, returns ``False`` (cost cannot be paid).\n135\t\n136\t    Parameters:\n137\t        game: The current game state (unused here but kept for a\n138\t            consistent ``(game, source) -> bool`` cost signature).\n139\t        source: The permanent to tap.\n140\t\n141\t    Returns:\n142\t        ``True`` if the cost was successfully paid (source was untapped\n143\t        and is now tapped), ``False`` otherwise.\n144\t    \"\"\"\n145\t    if getattr(source, \"is_tapped\", False):\n146\t        return False\n147\t    source.is_tapped = True\n148\t    return True\n149\t\n150\t\n151\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n152\t# Activate ability — main entry point\n153\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n154\t\n155\tdef activate_ability(\n156\t    game: GameState,\n157\t    player: Any,  # Player\n158\t    ability: ActivatedAbilityInstance | LoyaltyAbilityInstance,\n159\t) -> None:\n160\t    \"\"\"Activate an ability.\n161\t\n162\t    Pipeline\n163\t    --------\n164\t    1. **Timing check** — mana abilities bypass timing entirely and\n165\t       resolve immediately.  Regular (non-mana) activated abilities\n166\t       can be activated whenever a player has priority (instant speed);\n167\t       priority enforcement is handled externally by\n168\t       ``priority_loop``, not here.  **Only loyalty abilities** carry\n169\t       a sorcery-speed restriction.\n170\t    2. **Pay costs** — invoke the ability's cost callable.  For loyalty\n171\t       abilities, adjust loyalty counters and enforce once-per-turn.\n172\t    3. **Resolve or push to stack** — mana abilities resolve\n173\t       immediately; all other abilities are pushed onto the game stack\n174\t       as :class:`StackObject` instances.\n175\t\n176\t    Parameters:\n177\t        game: The current game state.\n178\t        player: The player activating the ability.\n179\t        ability: The ability to activate (an\n180\t            :class:`ActivatedAbilityInstance` or\n181\t            :class:`LoyaltyAbilityInstance`).\n182\t\n183\t    Raises:\n184\t        AbilityError: If the activation is illegal (timing, cost, or\n185\t            once-per-turn restriction).\n186\t    \"\"\"\n187\t    if isinstance(ability, LoyaltyAbilityInstance):\n188\t        _activate_loyalty_ability(game, player, ability)\n189\t    elif isinstance(ability, ActivatedAbilityInstance):\n190\t        _activate_regular_ability(game, player, ability)\n191\t    else:\n192\t        raise AbilityError(f\"Unknown ability type: {type(ability)}\")\n193\t\n194\t\n195\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n196\t# Internal helpers\n197\t# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n198\t\n199\tdef _activate_regular_ability(\n200\t    game: GameState,\n201\t    player: Any,\n202\t    ability: ActivatedAbilityInstance,\n203\t) -> None:\n204\t    \"\"\"Activate a regular (non-loyalty) activated ability.\"\"\"\n205\t    # 1. Check \"can't activate\" restriction (e.g. Arrest).\n206\t    if getattr(ability.source, \"_cant_activate\", False):\n207\t        raise AbilityError(\n208\t            \"Cannot activate ability — source's activated abilities are suppressed\"\n209\t        )\n210\t\n211\t    # 2. Pay costs\n212\t    cost_paid = ability.cost(game, ability.source)\n213\t    if not cost_paid:\n214\t        raise AbilityError(\"Cannot activate ability — cost could not be paid\")\n215\t\n216\t    # 3. Resolve or push\n217\t    if ability.is_mana_ability:\n218\t        # Mana abilities resolve immediately without using the stack.\n219\t        ability.effect(game)\n220\t    else:\n221\t        # Push to stack for resolution.\n222\t        stack_obj = StackObject(\n223\t            source=ability.source,\n224\t            controller=player,\n225\t            on_resolve=ability.effect,\n226\t            is_mana_ability=False,\n227\t        )\n228\t        game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n229\t\n230\t\n231\tdef _activate_loyalty_ability(\n232\t    game: GameState,\n233\t    player: Any,\n234\t    ability: LoyaltyAbilityInstance,\n235\t) -> None:\n236\t    \"\"\"Activate a planeswalker loyalty ability.\"\"\"\n237\t    source = ability.source\n238\t\n239\t    # 1. Timing — loyalty abilities are sorcery speed only.\n240\t    if not is_sorcery_speed(game, player):\n241\t        raise AbilityError(\n242\t            \"Cannot activate loyalty ability — sorcery-speed timing not met\"\n243\t        )\n244\t\n245\t    # 2. Once-per-turn restriction.\n246\t    turn_number = getattr(game, \"turn_number\", 0)\n247\t    if _has_activated_loyalty_this_turn(source, turn_number):\n248\t        raise AbilityError(\n249\t            \"Cannot activate loyalty ability — already activated this turn\"\n250\t        )\n251\t\n252\t    # 3. Pay loyalty cost.\n253\t    current_loyalty = getattr(source, \"loyalty\", 0)\n254\t    new_loyalty = current_loyalty + ability.loyalty_cost\n255\t    if new_loyalty < 0:\n256\t        raise AbilityError(\n257\t            f\"Cannot activate loyalty ability — insufficient loyalty \"\n258\t            f\"(have {current_loyalty}, need {-ability.loyalty_cost})\"\n259\t        )\n260\t    source.loyalty = new_loyalty\n261\t\n262\t    # 4. Mark as activated this turn.\n263\t    _mark_loyalty_activated(source, turn_number)\n264\t\n265\t    # 5. Push to stack.\n266\t    stack_obj = StackObject(\n267\t        source=source,\n268\t        controller=player,\n269\t        on_resolve=ability.effect,\n270\t        is_mana_ability=False,\n271\t    )\n272\t    game.stack.push(stack_obj)\n273\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018fs8roC62U1yCwfJG7Hwxt","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"e9193ca4-6484-4155-a319-c6574d41ab83","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:13:22.444Z","subagent_type":"Reviewer","task_description":"Review sos_257 implementation"}
