{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01JT4TYF46EKMDPCSW7LRNbH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hp6qb1u1az9unTEe9d7eJj","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Revise sos_257 per review","subagent_type":"Implementer","prompt":"Revise the implementation of card **sos_257** (Great Hall of the Biblioplex) to address TWO strict review findings. Do NOT modify any test file.\n\n## Inputs\n- Current diff: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl.diff`\n- Review findings: `/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/review.json`\n- Conventions: `/workspace/KEY_DECISIONS.md`; prior cards: `/workspace/FILES_MODIFIED.json`.\n- CRITICAL: Do NOT modify any file under `/workspace/engine_tests/`.\n\n## Required changes (both strict — MUST apply). Read `engine/continuous_effects.py` and the FDN P/T-effect examples `cards/fdn/fdn_69/card_impl.py` and `cards/fdn/fdn_71/card_impl.py` to use the established `ContinuousEffect` convention.\n\n1. **Animation must be a continuous effect, not direct mutation.** The `{5}` effect currently mutates `source.card_types`/`_base_power`/`_base_toughness` directly. `EffectManager.apply_all` calls `_reset_characteristics()` (which resets `card_types` to `_original_card_types`), so the becomes-a-creature change is STRIPPED on the next continuous-effect recalc (cleanup/SBA), leaving a permanently non-creature land. Model the animation as a `ContinuousEffect` added to `game.effect_manager`: a `Layer.TYPE` effect that ADDS `CardType.CREATURE` (and the `\"Wizard\"` subtype) while keeping `CardType.LAND`, plus a `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` SET_PT effect setting 2/4. Ensure the existing arbitrated tests still pass: immediately after `effect(game)` the land must read `CardType.CREATURE` present, `CardType.LAND` present, subtype `\"Wizard\"`, `power == 2`, `toughness == 4` (call/trigger `apply_all` as needed so characteristics reflect the effect right away), and re-running the effect must NOT double the P/T (