{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Zq7aqmqkUFQL2LtxEwMiT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n4\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n5\t    \"line\": 173,\n6\t    \"comment\": \"Animation defect: the {5} effect mutates `source.card_types` (and `_base_power`/`_base_toughness`) directly instead of registering a continuous effect. `CardImpl.__init__` snapshots `_original_card_types = frozenset({CardType.LAND})` BEFORE animation, and `EffectManager.apply_all` (engine/continuous_effects.py) calls `_reset_characteristics()` on every battlefield object, which does `self.card_types = set(self._original_card_types)`. So the very next continuous-effect recalculation (cleanup step calls `effect_manager.remove_expired` + `apply_all`; SBA passes also trigger recalc) STRIPS CardType.CREATURE back off the land — the becomes-a-creature change does not survive. `_is_animated` stays True so the gate then blocks re-animating, leaving a permanently non-creature land. The tests pass only because none of them run `apply_all`/cleanup after animating. A becomes-a-creature (animation) effect must be modeled as a `ContinuousEffect` (Layer.TYPE for the type add + Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS SET_PT for the 2/4) added to `game.effect_manager`, mirroring the established P/T-effect convention in cards/fdn/fdn_69 / fdn_71.\"\n7\t  },\n8\t  {\n9\t    \"severity\": \"strict\",\n10\t    \"file\": \"cards/sos/sos_257/card_impl.py\",\n11\t    \"line\": 221,\n12\t    \"comment\": \"\\\"+1/+0 until end of turn\\\" is not honored: the cast-trigger pump does `source._power_bonus += 1` on a plain instance attribute that nothing ever resets. The engine's end-of-turn cleanup only removes until-EOT effects registered in `game.effect_manager` (turn.py step 2 -> `remove_expired`/`apply_all`), and `apply_all`'s `_reset_characteristics` does not touch this card's `_power_bonus`/`_base_power` (the card exposes `power` as a property over its own fields). So each instant/sorcery cast permanently raises power and it never decays at end of turn. The pump should be applied via the standard P/T-modification path — register a `ContinuousEffect(layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=MODIFY_PT, duration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN)` per cast (see cards/fdn/fdn_69 / fdn_71 for the convention) so the +1/+0 expires correctly.\"\n13\t  }\n14\t]\n15\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hp6qb1u1az9unTEe9d7eJj","session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"2d7720f8-6d15-4099-bf7e-0e66f98486c8","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:15:30.012Z","subagent_type":"Implementer","task_description":"Revise sos_257 per review"}
