{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Td6fUkekQUgnbBAvSQXPoa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — revision rationale\n2\t\n3\tBoth strict review findings were applied. The restricted-mana surface in\n4\t`engine/mana.py` / `engine/casting.py` (built in the prior round) is unchanged.\n5\t\n6\t## Finding 1 — Animation must be a continuous effect, not direct mutation\n7\t\n8\t**Before:** the `{5}` effect set `source.card_types |= {CREATURE}`,\n9\t`source.subtypes |= {\"Wizard\"}`, and `_base_power/_base_toughness` directly.\n10\t`EffectManager.apply_all` (cleanup step, SBA recalcs) calls\n11\t`_reset_characteristics()` on every battlefield object, which resets\n12\t`card_types` to `_original_card_types` (`{LAND}` only). The very next recalc\n13\tstripped `CardType.CREATURE` back off — and `_is_animated` stayed `True`, so\n14\tthe gate then blocked re-animating, leaving a permanently non-creature land.\n15\t\n16\t**After:** animation is modelled as two `ContinuousEffect`s added to\n17\t`game.effect_manager`, both `DURATION_PERMANENT`:\n18\t\n19\t- `Layer.TYPE` — ADDS `CardType.CREATURE` and the `\"Wizard\"` subtype on top of\n20\t  the reset baseline (`CardType.LAND` is in `_original_card_types`, so it is\n21\t  preserved automatically).\n22\t- `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` / `SubLayer.SET_PT` — sets the land to 2/4.\n23\t\n24\tThe card now exposes `power`/`toughness` over `modified_power`/`modified_toughness`\n25\t(mirroring `Creature`), and overrides `_reset_characteristics()` to reset\n26\t`subtypes` to a snapshot `_original_subtypes` and `modified_power/toughness` to\n27\tthe non-creature baseline 0/0. Each `apply_all` therefore re-adds CREATURE /\n28\tWizard / 2/4 on top of the reset, so the animation survives indefinitely.\n29\t\n30\t`_animate` calls `game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)` right after registering\n31\tthe effects so the land reads as a 2/4 creature immediately (tests check\n32\t`hall.power == 2` directly after `effect(game)` without driving a recalc).\n33\t\n34\t## Finding 2 — +1/+0 pump must be an until-end-of-turn continuous effect\n35\t\n36\t**Before:** the cast-trigger did `source._power_bonus += 1` on a plain\n37\tattribute nothing ever reset, so each instant/sorcery permanently raised power.\n38\t\n39\t**After:** the trigger registers a per-cast\n40\t`ContinuousEffect(layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=MODIFY_PT,\n41\tduration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN)` granting +1/+0 (matching fdn_69 / fdn_71), then\n42\tcalls `apply_all` so the bump is visible immediately. Cleanup step\n43\t(`remove_expired` + `apply_all`) sweeps it away at end of turn. The condition\n44\tstill gates on the controller casting an instant/sorcery only, so opponents'\n45\tspells and creature spells do not pump it.\n46\t\n47\tSublayer ordering guarantees correctness on recalc: 7b (SET_PT, set 2/4) runs\n48\tbefore 7c (MODIFY_PT, +1/+0), yielding 3/4 while the pump is live and 2/4 after\n49\tit expires.\n50\t\n51\t## Idempotency / gate\n52\t\n53\tThe \"If this land isn't a creature\" gate is enforced by `_animation_effects_added`\n54\t(and `_is_animated`): a second `effect(game)` is a no-op for the type/P/T change\n55\t(no duplicate effects), so re-running it keeps the land at 2/4.\n56\t\n57\t## Design decisions / conventions for future cards\n58\t\n59\t- A non-`Creature` permanent that \"becomes a creature\" should adopt the\n60\t  `Creature`-style `modified_power`/`modified_toughness` fields and override\n61\t  `_reset_characteristics()` to reset them to the permanent's non-creature\n62\t  baseline, then model the animation as `Layer.TYPE` + `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`\n63\t  `SET_PT` continuous effects (`DURATION_PERMANENT`). Direct attribute mutation\n64\t  does NOT survive `EffectManager.apply_all`'s reset pass.\n65\t- Snapshot `_original_subtypes` (alongside the base class's `_original_card_types`)\n66\t  when a continuous effect grants a subtype, so the reset strips it cleanly.\n67\t- Animation/pump effect callbacks call `game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)`\n68\t  after `add(...)` so characteristics reflect immediately (tests and any caller\n69\t  that does not drive its own recalc see the change at once).\n70\t\n71\t## Verification\n72\t\n73\t- `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`\n74\t  → 38 sos_257 tests pass; 1145 engine tests pass.\n75\t- Manual sanity loop: animate -> `apply_all` recalc keeps it a 2/4 creature+land;\n76\t  cast trigger -> 3/4; end-of-turn `remove_expired`+`apply_all` -> back to 2/4,\n77\t  still a creature.\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c2fbc8b-9529-4254-888d-bbf9dd1c7145","uuid":"d399f036-b168-4ad8-8444-b097c1022a32","timestamp":"2026-06-02T02:18:51.074Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/coordinator-run/sos_257/impl-revised-rationale.md","content":"# sos_257 — Great Hall of the Biblioplex — revision rationale\n\nBoth strict review findings were applied. The restricted-mana surface in\n`engine/mana.py` / `engine/casting.py` (built in the prior round) is unchanged.\n\n## Finding 1 — Animation must be a continuous effect, not direct mutation\n\n**Before:** the `{5}` effect set `source.card_types |= {CREATURE}`,\n`source.subtypes |= {\"Wizard\"}`, and `_base_power/_base_toughness` directly.\n`EffectManager.apply_all` (cleanup step, SBA recalcs) calls\n`_reset_characteristics()` on every battlefield object, which resets\n`card_types` to `_original_card_types` (`{LAND}` only). The very next recalc\nstripped `CardType.CREATURE` back off — and `_is_animated` stayed `True`, so\nthe gate then blocked re-animating, leaving a permanently non-creature land.\n\n**After:** animation is modelled as two `ContinuousEffect`s added to\n`game.effect_manager`, both `DURATION_PERMANENT`:\n\n- `Layer.TYPE` — ADDS `CardType.CREATURE` and the `\"Wizard\"` subtype on top of\n  the reset baseline (`CardType.LAND` is in `_original_card_types`, so it is\n  preserved automatically).\n- `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS` / `SubLayer.SET_PT` — sets the land to 2/4.\n\nThe card now exposes `power`/`toughness` over `modified_power`/`modified_toughness`\n(mirroring `Creature`), and overrides `_reset_characteristics()` to reset\n`subtypes` to a snapshot `_original_subtypes` and `modified_power/toughness` to\nthe non-creature baseline 0/0. Each `apply_all` therefore re-adds CREATURE /\nWizard / 2/4 on top of the reset, so the animation survives indefinitely.\n\n`_animate` calls `game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)` right after registering\nthe effects so the land reads as a 2/4 creature immediately (tests check\n`hall.power == 2` directly after `effect(game)` without driving a recalc).\n\n## Finding 2 — +1/+0 pump must be an until-end-of-turn continuous effect\n\n**Before:** the cast-trigger did `source._power_bonus += 1` on a plain\nattribute nothing ever reset, so each instant/sorcery permanently raised power.\n\n**After:** the trigger registers a per-cast\n`ContinuousEffect(layer=POWER_TOUGHNESS, sublayer=MODIFY_PT,\nduration=DURATION_END_OF_TURN)` granting +1/+0 (matching fdn_69 / fdn_71), then\ncalls `apply_all` so the bump is visible immediately. Cleanup step\n(`remove_expired` + `apply_all`) sweeps it away at end of turn. The condition\nstill gates on the controller casting an instant/sorcery only, so opponents'\nspells and creature spells do not pump it.\n\nSublayer ordering guarantees correctness on recalc: 7b (SET_PT, set 2/4) runs\nbefore 7c (MODIFY_PT, +1/+0), yielding 3/4 while the pump is live and 2/4 after\nit expires.\n\n## Idempotency / gate\n\nThe \"If this land isn't a creature\" gate is enforced by `_animation_effects_added`\n(and `_is_animated`): a second `effect(game)` is a no-op for the type/P/T change\n(no duplicate effects), so re-running it keeps the land at 2/4.\n\n## Design decisions / conventions for future cards\n\n- A non-`Creature` permanent that \"becomes a creature\" should adopt the\n  `Creature`-style `modified_power`/`modified_toughness` fields and override\n  `_reset_characteristics()` to reset them to the permanent's non-creature\n  baseline, then model the animation as `Layer.TYPE` + `Layer.POWER_TOUGHNESS`\n  `SET_PT` continuous effects (`DURATION_PERMANENT`). Direct attribute mutation\n  does NOT survive `EffectManager.apply_all`'s reset pass.\n- Snapshot `_original_subtypes` (alongside the base class's `_original_card_types`)\n  when a continuous effect grants a subtype, so the reset strips it cleanly.\n- Animation/pump effect callbacks call `game.effect_manager.apply_all(game)`\n  after `add(...)` so characteristics reflect immediately (tests and any caller\n  that does not drive its own recalc see the change at once).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `python3 -m pytest cards/sos/sos_257/tests.py engine_tests/ -q`\n  → 38 sos_257 tests pass; 1145 engine tests pass.\n- Manual sanity loop: animate -> `apply_all` recalc keeps it a 2/4 creature+land;\n  cast trigger -> 3/4; end-of-turn `remove_expired`+`apply_all` -> back to 2/4,\n  still a creature.\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
